i.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove no-op f-string prefixes to satisfy Ruff F541.**\n\nThese strings have no interpolation and can fail lint gates.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✗ aborted — keeping yours\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✗ aborted — keeping yours\\n\")\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✗ aborted — skipping insert\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✗ aborted — skipping insert\\n\")\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✓ manually edited\\n\")\n-                            sys.stderr.write(f\"        ✗ aborted — keeping yours\\n\")\n+                            sys.stderr.write(\"        ✗ aborted — keeping yours\\n\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.15.2)</summary>\n\n[error] 1906-1906: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n---\n\n[error] 1908-1908: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n---\n\n[error] 1922-1922: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n---\n\n[error] 1924-1924: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n---\n\n[error] 1939-1939: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n---\n\n[error] 1941-1941: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n1906 - 1941, Several sys.stderr.write calls use unnecessary f-strings (no\ninterpolation) which triggers Ruff F541; replace those f\"...\" strings with plain\nstring literals. In the blocks handling report.get(\"inserted\"),\nreport[\"skipped\"], and the updates loop (references: declined_update,\ndeclined_insert, accepted_force, modify_overrides) and helper calls\n(_open_editor_for_marker, _prompt_confirm, _show_marker_content,\n_show_marker_diff), change lines like sys.stderr.write(f\"    + {k} — new\nmarker\\n\") only when they contain no { } interpolation to non-f-string\nequivalents (e.g. \"        ✓ manually edited\\n\" -> \"        ✓ manually\nedited\\n\"), leaving f-strings that do include variables intact.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856055","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856055"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856055"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856055/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1906,"original_start_line":1906,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1941,"original_line":1941,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":591,"position":591,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856064","pull_request_review_id":3884370982,"id":2879856064,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rpx3A","diff_hunk":"@@ -1894,11 +2152,84 @@ def cmd_kit_migrate(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n     if args.dry_run:\n         output[\"dry_run\"] = True\n \n-    print(json.dumps(output, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n+    ui.result(output, human_fn=lambda d: _human_kit_migrate(d))\n     return 0\n     # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-blueprint-system-kit-migrate:p1:inst-return-migrate-ok\n \n \n+def _human_kit_migrate(data: dict) -> None:\n+    status = data.get(\"status\", \"\")\n+    dry = data.get(\"dry_run\", False)\n+\n+    ui.header(\"Kit Migrate\" + (\" (dry run)\" if dry else \"\"))\n+    ui.detail(\"Migrated\", str(data.get(\"kits_migrated\", 0)))\n+    ui.detail(\"Current\", str(data.get(\"kits_current\", 0)))\n+    if data.get(\"kits_aborted\"):\n+        ui.detail(\"Aborted\", str(data[\"kits_aborted\"]))\n+\n+    for r in data.get(\"results\", []):\n+        kit_slug = r.get(\"kit\", \"?\")\n+        rs = r.get(\"status\", \"?\")\n+        from_v = r.get(\"from_version\")\n+        to_v = r.get(\"to_version\")\n+        ver_str = \"\"\n+        if from_v is not None and to_v is not None:\n+            ver_str = f\" v{from_v} → v{to_v}\"\n+\n+        if rs == \"migrated\":\n+            ui.step(f\"{kit_slug}: migrated{ver_str}\")\n+            regen = r.get(\"regenerated\", {})\n+            if regen:\n+                fw = regen.get(\"files_written\", 0)\n+                ww = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                err = regen.get(\"error\")\n+                if err:\n+                    ui.warn(f\"  Regen failed: {err}\")\n+                else:\n+                    ui.substep(f\"  Regenerated: {fw} files, {ww} workflows\")\n+            # Show merge details\n+            merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", [])\n+            for mb in merged:\n+                bp_name = mb.get(\"blueprint\", \"?\")","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py","commit_id":"c96e799b6972bcebfa743b5bec1bdee2b7c00f2d","original_commit_id":"c12140acedca8584696f503d87054fc2fb3ee036","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`_human_kit_migrate` is reading fields that current migrate results do not emit.**\n\nThe formatter expects `from_version` / `to_version` and `merged_blueprints`, but `migrate_kit` currently returns `kit_version` and `blueprints`. This drops version/merge detail in real output, and `workflows_written` may print as a raw list instead of a count.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        from_v = r.get(\"from_version\")\n-        to_v = r.get(\"to_version\")\n-        ver_str = \"\"\n-        if from_v is not None and to_v is not None:\n-            ver_str = f\" v{from_v} → v{to_v}\"\n+        ver_str = \"\"\n+        kit_version = r.get(\"kit_version\")\n+        if kit_version:\n+            ver_str = f\" {kit_version}\"\n+        else:\n+            from_v = r.get(\"from_version\")\n+            to_v = r.get(\"to_version\")\n+            if from_v is not None and to_v is not None:\n+                ver_str = f\" v{from_v} → v{to_v}\"\n\n         if rs == \"migrated\":\n             ui.step(f\"{kit_slug}: migrated{ver_str}\")\n             regen = r.get(\"regenerated\", {})\n             if regen:\n                 fw = regen.get(\"files_written\", 0)\n-                ww = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                ww_raw = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                ww = len(ww_raw) if isinstance(ww_raw, list) else int(ww_raw or 0)\n                 err = regen.get(\"error\")\n                 if err:\n                     ui.warn(f\"  Regen failed: {err}\")\n                 else:\n                     ui.substep(f\"  Regenerated: {fw} files, {ww} workflows\")\n             # Show merge details\n-            merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", [])\n+            merged = r.get(\"blueprints\", r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", []))\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n        ver_str = \"\"\n        kit_version = r.get(\"kit_version\")\n        if kit_version:\n            ver_str = f\" {kit_version}\"\n        else:\n            from_v = r.get(\"from_version\")\n            to_v = r.get(\"to_version\")\n            if from_v is not None and to_v is not None:\n                ver_str = f\" v{from_v} → v{to_v}\"\n\n        if rs == \"migrated\":\n            ui.step(f\"{kit_slug}: migrated{ver_str}\")\n            regen = r.get(\"regenerated\", {})\n            if regen:\n                fw = regen.get(\"files_written\", 0)\n                ww_raw = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n                ww = len(ww_raw) if isinstance(ww_raw, list) else int(ww_raw or 0)\n                err = regen.get(\"error\")\n                if err:\n                    ui.warn(f\"  Regen failed: {err}\")\n                else:\n                    ui.substep(f\"  Regenerated: {fw} files, {ww} workflows\")\n            # Show merge details\n            merged = r.get(\"blueprints\", r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", []))\n            for mb in merged:\n                bp_name = mb.get(\"blueprint\", \"?\")\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n2173 - 2193, _human_kit_migrate is reading keys that migrate_kit no longer\nemits; update it to accept both shapes: read from_version/to_version but fall\nback to the single kit_version (e.g., if from_version/to_version are missing use\nr.get(\"kit_version\")), and read merged_blueprints but fall back to blueprints\n(e.g., merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", r.get(\"blueprints\", []))). Also\nnormalize regenerated counts: when reading regen.get(\"files_written\") and\nregen.get(\"workflows_written\") coerce lists to counts (use len() when the value\nis a list) and handle missing values with 0 so the UI prints numeric counts\ninstead of raw lists or None; update _human_kit_migrate to use these fallbacks\nand normalizations.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856064","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856064"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856064"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":2173,"original_start_line":2173,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":2193,"original_line":2193,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":699,"position":699,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856070","pull_request_review_id":3884370982,"id":2879856070,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rpx3G","diff_hunk":"@@ -982,29 +990,272 @@ def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n         else:\n             cfg = {\"version\": 1, \"agents\": {a: {\"workflows\": {}, \"skills\": {}} for a in agents_to_process}}\n \n+    return args, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, copy_report, cfg_path, cfg\n+\n+\n+def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Read-only command: list generated agent integration files.\"\"\"\n+    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(argv, prog=\"agents\", description=\"Show generated agent integration files\")\n+    if ctx is None:\n+        return 1\n+    args, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, copy_report, cfg_path, cfg = ctx\n+","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py","commit_id":"c96e799b6972bcebfa743b5bec1bdee2b7c00f2d","original_commit_id":"c12140acedca8584696f503d87054fc2fb3ee036","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`cmd_agents` is read-only but can still mutate project state.**\n\n`cmd_agents` uses the shared resolver, which may copy Cypilot into the project when external roots are detected. That is unexpected side-effect for a listing command.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-def _resolve_agents_context(argv: List[str], prog: str, description: str, *, allow_yes: bool = False) -> Optional[tuple]:\n+def _resolve_agents_context(\n+    argv: List[str],\n+    prog: str,\n+    description: str,\n+    *,\n+    allow_yes: bool = False,\n+    read_only: bool = False,\n+) -> Optional[tuple]:\n@@\n-    cypilot_root, copy_report = _ensure_cypilot_local(cypilot_root, project_root, args.dry_run)\n+    cypilot_root, copy_report = _ensure_cypilot_local(\n+        cypilot_root, project_root, True if read_only else args.dry_run\n+    )\n@@\n-    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(argv, prog=\"agents\", description=\"Show generated agent integration files\")\n+    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(\n+        argv,\n+        prog=\"agents\",\n+        description=\"Show generated agent integration files\",\n+        read_only=True,\n+    )\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.15.2)</summary>\n\n[warning] 1001-1001: Unpacked variable `args` is never used\n\nPrefix it with an underscore or any other dummy variable pattern\n\n(RUF059)\n\n---\n\n[warning] 1001-1001: Unpacked variable `copy_report` is never used\n\nPrefix it with an underscore or any other dummy variable pattern\n\n(RUF059)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py` around lines 996 - 1002,\nThe cmd_agents function is intended to be read-only but currently calls\n_resolve_agents_context which may copy Cypilot into the project (mutating\nstate); update the resolver call or resolver to avoid side effects: add a\nread_only or disable_copy parameter to _resolve_agents_context (or an equivalent\nflag like allow_copy=False) and pass it from cmd_agents so that when cmd_agents\ncalls _resolve_agents_context it never performs any project-copying or writes\n(ensure any code paths that set copy_report, perform copying, or mutate\nproject_root/cypilot_root are skipped when the flag is false); keep symbol names\nconsistent with cmd_agents and _resolve_agents_context so the change is easy to\nlocate.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856070","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856070"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856070"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":996,"original_start_line":996,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1002,"original_line":1002,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":161,"position":161,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856072","pull_request_review_id":3884370982,"id":2879856072,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rpx3I","diff_hunk":"@@ -982,29 +990,272 @@ def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n         else:\n             cfg = {\"version\": 1, \"agents\": {a: {\"workflows\": {}, \"skills\": {}} for a in agents_to_process}}\n \n+    return args, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, copy_report, cfg_path, cfg\n+\n+\n+def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Read-only command: list generated agent integration files.\"\"\"\n+    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(argv, prog=\"agents\", description=\"Show generated agent integration files\")\n+    if ctx is None:\n+        return 1\n+    args, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, copy_report, cfg_path, cfg = ctx\n+\n+    # Scan for existing agent files (dry-run to see what exists)\n+    results: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n+    for agent in agents_to_process:\n+        result = _process_single_agent(agent, project_root, cypilot_root, cfg, cfg_path, dry_run=True)\n+        results[agent] = result\n+\n+    ui.result(\n+        {\n+            \"status\": \"OK\",\n+            \"agents\": list(agents_to_process),\n+            \"project_root\": project_root.as_posix(),\n+            \"cypilot_root\": cypilot_root.as_posix(),\n+            \"results\": results,\n+        },\n+        human_fn=lambda d: _human_agents_list(d, agents_to_process, results, project_root),\n+    )\n+    return 0\n+\n+\n+def cmd_generate_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Generate/update agent-specific workflow proxies and skill outputs.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-user-agents\n+    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(\n+        argv, prog=\"generate-agents\",\n+        description=\"Generate/update agent-specific workflow proxies and skill outputs\",\n+        allow_yes=True,\n+    )\n+    if ctx is None:\n+        return 1\n+    args, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, copy_report, cfg_path, cfg = ctx\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-user-agents\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-resolve-project\n+    # Resolved in _resolve_agents_context: project_root via find_project_root,\n+    # cypilot_root via AGENTS.md cypilot_path variable or __file__ ancestry.\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-resolve-project\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-ensure-local\n+    # Handled in _resolve_agents_context via _ensure_cypilot_local:\n+    # copies cypilot files into project when cypilot_root is external.\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-ensure-local\n+\n+    # Step 1: Dry run to preview changes\n     # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-agent-integration-generate:p1:inst-for-each-agent\n+    preview_results: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n+    for agent in agents_to_process:\n+        preview_results[agent] = _process_single_agent(agent, project_root, cypilot_root, cfg, cfg_path, dry_run=True)\n+\n+    # Compute total changes\n+    total_create = 0\n+    total_update = 0\n+    for r in preview_results.values():\n+        wf = r.get(\"workflows\", {})\n+        sk = r.get(\"skills\", {})\n+        total_create += len(wf.get(\"created\", [])) + len(sk.get(\"created\", []))\n+        total_update += len(wf.get(\"updated\", [])) + len(sk.get(\"updated\", []))\n+\n+    if args.dry_run:\n+        # Just show the preview and exit\n+        agents_result = _build_result(preview_results, agents_to_process, project_root, cypilot_root, cfg_path, copy_report, dry_run=True)\n+        ui.result(agents_result, human_fn=lambda d: _human_generate_agents_ok(d, agents_to_process, preview_results, dry_run=True))\n+        return 0\n+\n+    # Step 2: Show preview and ask for confirmation (interactive)\n+    if total_create == 0 and total_update == 0:\n+        ui.info(\"No changes needed — agent files are up to date.\")\n+    else:","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py","commit_id":"c96e799b6972bcebfa743b5bec1bdee2b7c00f2d","original_commit_id":"c12140acedca8584696f503d87054fc2fb3ee036","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Preview change detection ignores rename/delete operations.**\n\nThe confirmation gate only counts created/updated files. Renames/deletes can still execute afterward even when preview says “No changes needed.”\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     total_create = 0\n     total_update = 0\n+    total_rename = 0\n+    total_delete = 0\n     for r in preview_results.values():\n         wf = r.get(\"workflows\", {})\n         sk = r.get(\"skills\", {})\n         total_create += len(wf.get(\"created\", [])) + len(sk.get(\"created\", []))\n         total_update += len(wf.get(\"updated\", [])) + len(sk.get(\"updated\", []))\n+        total_rename += len(wf.get(\"renamed\", []))\n+        total_delete += len(wf.get(\"deleted\", []))\n@@\n-    if total_create == 0 and total_update == 0:\n+    if total_create == 0 and total_update == 0 and total_rename == 0 and total_delete == 0:\n         ui.info(\"No changes needed — agent files are up to date.\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py` around lines 1050 - 1068,\nThe preview totals only sum created/updated items, so rename/delete operations\nin preview_results are ignored and can still run after a \"No changes needed\"\nmessage; update the aggregation that computes total_create/total_update (and/or\nintroduce total_delete/total_rename) to also include len(wf.get(\"deleted\", [])),\nlen(sk.get(\"deleted\", [])), and len(wf.get(\"renamed\", []))/len(sk.get(\"renamed\",\n[])) from preview_results, then use those totals in the interactive confirmation\nbranch (the same logic around args.dry_run, _build_result,\n_human_generate_agents_ok, and the ui.info check) so the confirmation gate\ntreats deletions/renames as changes requiring confirmation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856072","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856072"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856072"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1050,"original_start_line":1050,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1068,"original_line":1068,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":227,"position":227,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856076","pull_request_review_id":3884370982,"id":2879856076,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rpx3M","diff_hunk":"@@ -1114,6 +1336,12 @@ def _three_way_merge_blueprint(\n         old_raw = old_map.get(key)\n         new_raw = new_map.get(key)\n \n+        # Manual editor override takes precedence over all other logic\n+        if key in modify_overrides:\n+            merged_parts.append((modify_overrides[key], key))\n+            modified.append(key)\n+            continue","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py","commit_id":"c96e799b6972bcebfa743b5bec1bdee2b7c00f2d","original_commit_id":"c12140acedca8584696f503d87054fc2fb3ee036","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Include manually modified markers in insertion anchoring.**\n\nMarkers that hit `modify_overrides` short-circuit before `updated/skipped/kept`, so they are excluded from `seen_keys` and can break insertion placement for nearby new markers.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    seen_keys = set(updated) | set(skipped) | set(kept)\n+    seen_keys = set(updated) | set(skipped) | set(kept) | set(modified)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py` around lines 1339 - 1343, The\nmanual override branch that appends to merged_parts and modified when a key is\nin modify_overrides short-circuits and never marks that key as seen, which\nbreaks insertion anchoring later; update the block handling modify_overrides\n(the code that appends to merged_parts and modified) to also add the key to the\nseen_keys set (the same set used by the updated/skipped/kept logic) so\noverridden markers are treated the same as updated/skipped/kept for insertion\nplacement and anchoring.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:25:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856076","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856076"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/86#discussion_r2879856076"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/86"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1339,"original_start_line":1339,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1343,"original_line":1343,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":509,"position":509,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2879856080","pull_request_review_id":3884370982,"id":2879856080,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rpx3Q","diff_hunk":"@@ -1894,11 +2152,84 @@ def cmd_kit_migrate(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n     if args.dry_run:\n         output[\"dry_run\"] = True\n \n-    print(json.dumps(output, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n+    ui.result(output, human_fn=lambda d: _human_kit_migrate(d))\n     return 0\n     # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-blueprint-system-kit-migrate:p1:inst-return-migrate-ok\n \n \n+def _human_kit_migrate(data: dict) -> None:\n+    status = data.get(\"status\", \"\")\n+    dry = data.get(\"dry_run\", Fal