t and\nany location metadata, or invoke the UI's show/display method right after\nui.result so the content is rendered in human mode.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py-141-146 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`141-146`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Reset JSON mode deterministically on every invocation.**\n\nLine 145 only sets JSON mode to `True` when `--json` is present; it never resets to `False` when absent. In repeated in-process calls to `main()`, output mode can leak between invocations.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if \"--json\" in argv_list:\n-        argv_list.remove(\"--json\")\n-        set_json_mode(True)\n+    json_mode = \"--json\" in argv_list\n+    argv_list = [a for a in argv_list if a != \"--json\"]\n+    set_json_mode(json_mode)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py around lines 141 -\n146, The code currently sets JSON mode to True when \"--json\" is present but\nnever resets it to False, causing mode to leak between repeated in-process runs;\nupdate the pre-dispatch logic in cli.py so set_json_mode is always called\ndeterministically (e.g., call set_json_mode(\"--json\" in argv_list) or use an\nif/else where argv_list.remove(\"--json\") and set_json_mode(True) when present,\notherwise set_json_mode(False)) so that argv_list and JSON mode are correctly\nhandled on every invocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/toc.py-121-148 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`121-148`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add `@cpt-*` traceability markers for `_human_toc`.**\n\nThe newly added formatter block should be traceability-wrapped like the rest of the command flow.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested wrapper</summary>\n\n```diff\n+# `@cpt-begin`:cpt-cypilot-flow-developer-experience-toc:p1:inst-human-render\n def _human_toc(data: dict) -> None:\n     ui.header(\"Table of Contents\")\n     ...\n     ui.blank()\n+# `@cpt-end`:cpt-cypilot-flow-developer-experience-toc:p1:inst-human-render\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines `Implement code-artifact traceability using `@cpt-`* markers to link code to artifacts`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/toc.py around lines\n121 - 148, Add `@cpt-`* traceability markers around the newly added human-readable\nTOC formatter by wrapping the _human_toc function's entry and exit points with\nthe project's code-artifact traceability markers (e.g. add an opening marker\nlike \"@cpt-start:toc\" immediately before the first ui.header(...) call and a\nclosing marker like \"@cpt-end:toc\" just before ui.blank()), and ensure any\nimportant subsections (status handling, validation handling, final summary)\ninclude inline `@cpt-`* markers as appropriate to match the other command flow\nwrappers so the entire _human_toc block is traceability-wrapped.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/spec_coverage.py-148-165 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`148-165`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add `@cpt-*` traceability wrappers around the new human formatter.**\n\nThe new `_human_spec_coverage` block is currently unwrapped, which weakens artifact-to-code traceability for this behavior.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested wrapper</summary>\n\n```diff\n+# `@cpt-begin`:cpt-cypilot-flow-spec-coverage-report:p1:inst-human-render\n def _human_spec_coverage(data: dict) -> None:\n     summary = data.get(\"summary\", {})\n     status = data.get(\"status\", \"\")\n     ui.header(\"Spec Coverage\")\n     ui.detail(\"Files\", f\"{summary.get('covered_files', 0)}/{summary.get('total_files', 0)} covered\")\n     ui.detail(\"Coverage\", f\"{summary.get('coverage_pct', 0):.1f}%\")\n     ui.detail(\"Granularity\", f\"{summary.get('granularity_score', 0):.4f}\")\n     failures = data.get(\"threshold_failures\", [])\n     if failures:\n         for f in failures:\n             ui.warn(f)\n     if status == \"PASS\":\n         ui.success(\"All thresholds met.\")\n     elif status == \"FAIL\":\n         ui.error(\"Threshold check failed.\")\n     else:\n         ui.info(f\"Status: {status}\")\n     ui.blank()\n+# `@cpt-end`:cpt-cypilot-flow-spec-coverage-report:p1:inst-human-render\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines `Implement code-artifact traceability using `@cpt-`* markers to link code to artifacts`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/spec_coverage.py\naround lines 148 - 165, Wrap the new human formatter function\n_human_spec_coverage with the required traceability comment markers by adding an\nopening marker before the function (e.g. a comment starting with\n`@cpt-spec_coverage-start` or similar project convention) and a closing marker\nafter the function (e.g. `@cpt-spec_coverage-end`); ensure the markers use the\n`@cpt-`* pattern and clearly identify the artifact \"spec_coverage human formatter\"\nso tools can map the function _human_spec_coverage to the artifact and leave the\nfunction body unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py-768-822 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`768-822`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Wrap `_human_validate` with `@cpt-*` traceability markers.**\n\nThe newly introduced human formatter is outside traceabilit