act` flows, plus `_human_get_content` branches (ERROR/NOT_FOUND/FOUND with and without metadata).\n> \n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 50-100, 104-157\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/get_content.py` around lines 24 - 47,\n> Test coverage is below threshold because the get_content command's --code and\n> --artifact execution paths and the various branches of _human_get_content\n> (ERROR, NOT_FOUND, FOUND with and without metadata) are not exercised; add\n> unit/integration tests that simulate: a) valid --code flow by creating a\n> temporary file and calling CodeFile.from_path, then exercising cf.get_by_inst\n> and cf.get to return content and asserting ui.result outputs FOUND with correct\n> id/inst/text and human_fn formatting; b) failure cases where CodeFile.from_path\n> returns errs or None to trigger ERROR, and missing content to trigger NOT_FOUND;\n> c) the --artifact flow equivalently; ensure tests cover metadata present and\n> absent for _human_get_content formatting and assert exit codes (0/1/2) and\n> returned ui.result payloads.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `394-647`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Add targeted tests for new update helpers and formatter branches.**\n> \n> CI shows per-file coverage at 75.91% (below 90%). The newly added `_maybe_regenerate_agents` and `_human_update_ok` branches need direct unit coverage.\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> I can generate a test matrix for: core/kit change triggers, no-change no-op, per-agent error handling, and human summary rendering branches.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py` around lines 394 - 647,\n> Add unit tests covering the new branches in _maybe_regenerate_agents and\n> _human_update_ok: for _maybe_regenerate_agents, write tests that simulate (1) no\n> core/kits changes returns empty list, (2) core_changed or kits_changed but no\n> existing skill output files skips agents, and (3) regeneration path by\n> monkeypatching _ALL_RECOGNIZED_AGENTS, _default_agents_config (to include a\n> skill output path), and _process_single_agent to return dicts with\n> created/updated workflows/skills so the function returns the regenerated agent\n> names and triggers ui.step/substep; also test handling when\n> _process_single_agent reports zero changes. For _human_update_ok, create tests\n> feeding different data shapes to exercise created/updated/unchanged file lists,\n> core_update dict branch, kits dict branch (with ver/ref/gen combos), the\n> agents_regenerated list branch, errors as dict and string, warnings list, and\n> the dry/status branches (dry_run True, status \"PASS\", and non-PASS), capturing\n> ui outputs (or monkeypatching ui methods) and ensuring correct branches are hit;\n> include a non-interactive path for _show_core_whatsnew as needed. Use targeted\n> monkeypatching of functions named _maybe_regenerate_agents,\n> _default_agents_config, _process_single_agent, _ALL_RECOGNIZED_AGENTS, and call\n> _human_update_ok directly to assert behavior.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🟠 Major comments (30)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_id_kinds.py-175-215 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`175-215`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add `@cpt` markers for the new human formatter.**\n\n`_human_list_id_kinds` is a new behavior block but currently not traceability-marked.\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines, \"Implement code-artifact traceability using `@cpt-`* markers to link code to artifacts\".\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_id_kinds.py` around lines 175 -\n215, The new human formatter function _human_list_id_kinds lacks the required\ncode-artifact traceability markers; add appropriate `@cpt-`* markers (e.g.,\n`@cpt-begin` / `@cpt-end` or `@cpt-function`) around the behavior block so the\nformatter is traceable, placing the markers in the _human_list_id_kinds\ndefinition near the ui.header(\"ID Kinds\") start and before the final ui.blank()\nend; ensure any new UI sections (e.g., the table creation using ui.table, the\nreverse mapping using t2k and ui.substep) include inline `@cpt` references as\nneeded to map those artifacts to their design IDs per the project's marker\nconvention.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py-235-281 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`235-281`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Traceability markers are missing on the new list-ids formatter.**\n\nPlease wrap `_human_list_ids` with `@cpt-*` markers.\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines, \"Implement code-artifact traceability using `@cpt-`* markers to link code to artifacts\".\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 235 - 281,\nThe _human_list_ids formatter is missing code-artifact traceability markers;\nupdate the function to emit `@cpt-`* markers: add an overall start marker (e.g.,\n\"@cpt-start\") near the top of _human_list_ids and a matching end marker (e.g.,\n\"@cpt-end\") before the final ui.blank(), and annotate each reported ID line by\nemitting a per-item marker containing the id (for example \"@cpt-id:<id>\") when\ncalling ui.substep (the ui.substep call inside the loop over items in\n_human_list_ids should include the per-item `@cpt-id` marker alongside the\nexisting message). Ensure markers are plain text strings included in the output\nwhere ui.substep/ui.step/ui.detail are invoked so traceability links to\nartifacts are created.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py-311-318 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`311-318`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Agent regeneration failures can be silently dropped from the final update status.**\n\n`_maybe_regenerate_agents` only returns agent names; it does not propagate per-agent failures, and caller does not merge regeneration failures into `errors`. This can report a successful update while regeneration actually failed.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n-    if not args.dry_run:\n-        agents_regen = _maybe_regenerate_agents(\n+    if not args.dry_run:\n+        agents_regen, regen_errors = _maybe_regenerate_agents(\n             copy_results, kit_results, project_root, cypilot_dir,\n         )\n         if agents_regen:\n             actions[\"agents_regenerated\"] = agents_regen\n+        if regen_errors:\n+            errors.extend(regen_errors)\n@@\n-def _maybe_regenerate_agents(\n+def _maybe_regenerate_agents(\n     copy_results: Dict[str, str],\n     kit_results: Dict[str, Any],\n     project_root: Path,\n     cypilot_dir: Path,\n-) -> List[str]:\n+) -> Tuple[List[str], List[Dict[str, str]]]:\n@@\n-    regenerated: List[str] = []\n+    regenerated: List[str] = []\n+    regen_errors: List[Dict[str, str]] = []\n@@\n-        result = _process_single_agent(\n-            agent, project_root, cypilot_dir, cfg, None, dry_run=False,\n-        )\n+        try:\n+            result = _process_single_agent(\n+                agent, project_root, cypilot_dir, cfg, None, dry_run=False,\n+            )\n+        except Exception as exc:\n+            regen_errors.append({\"path\": agent, \"error\": f\"agent regeneration failed: {exc}\"})\n+            continue\n+        if result.get(\"status\") != \"PASS\":\n+            msgs = result.get(\"errors\") or [\"agent regeneration failed\"]\n+            regen_errors.append({\"path\": agent, \"error\": \"; \".join(str(m) for m in msgs)})\n+            continue\n@@\n-    return regenerated\n+    return regenerated, regen_errors\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 394-458\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py around\nlines 311 - 318, The call to _maybe_regenerate_agents only returns names and\ncurrently its failures are not merged into the overall errors, so update the\ninvocation sites (the block using agents_regen and the similar block around\nlines 394-458) to: capture both successful names and any per-agent failure\ndetails from _maybe_regenerate_agents (or change it to return a structure like\n{\"succeeded\": [...], \"failed\": {agent: error}}), merge any failures into the\nexisting errors collection, and include both succeeded and failed info in\nactions (e.g., actions[\"agents_regenerated\"] = {...}) so that regeneration\nfailures are reflected in the final update status; reference the function\n_maybe_regenerate_agents, the local variable agents_regen, and the\nactions[\"agents_regenerated\"]/errors variables when making the changes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py-529-647 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`529-647`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**New update UI formatter path needs `@cpt` traceability markers.**\n\nThe added human-rendering section is not wrapped with `@cpt-*` markers.\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines, \"Implement code-artifact traceability using `@cpt-`* markers to lin