n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                ww = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                ww_raw = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", [])\n+                ww = len(ww_raw) if isinstance(ww_raw, list) else int(ww_raw or 0)\n@@\n-            merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", [])\n+            merged = r.get(\"blueprints\", [])\n             for mb in merged:\n                 bp_name = mb.get(\"blueprint\", \"?\")\n-                accepted = mb.get(\"accepted\", 0)\n-                declined = mb.get(\"declined\", 0)\n-                inserted = mb.get(\"inserted\", 0)\n-                deleted = mb.get(\"deleted\", 0)\n+                accepted = len(mb.get(\"markers_updated\", []))\n+                declined = len(mb.get(\"markers_skipped\", []))\n+                inserted = len(mb.get(\"markers_inserted\", []))\n+                deleted = len(mb.get(\"markers_deleted\", []))\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py` around lines 2176 - 2203, The\ncode in _human_kit_migrate is using the wrong result schema: replace references\nto \"merged_blueprints\" with the actual \"blueprints\" key returned by migrate_kit\nand treat \"workflows_written\" as a list (use len(r.get(\"workflows_written\",\n[]))) rather than a numeric count; update the loop that builds parts (currently\niterating mb from merged) to iterate over each blueprint entry in\nr.get(\"blueprints\", []) and read the correct fields on each blueprint object,\nthen call ui.substep/ui.warn as before so migration details are displayed\ncorrectly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py-439-452 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`439-452`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Don’t silently swallow agent-regeneration failures.**\n\nThis path only tracks changed-file counts. If `_process_single_agent` returns `PARTIAL`/errors with zero writes, update still looks successful and the user gets no corrective guidance.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         result = _process_single_agent(\n             agent, project_root, cypilot_dir, cfg, None, dry_run=False,\n         )\n+        if result.get(\"status\") != \"PASS\":\n+            ui.warn(f\"{agent}: regeneration returned {result.get('status')}\")\n+            for err in (result.get(\"errors\") or []):\n+                ui.substep(f\"  {err}\")\n+            ui.hint(\"Run /cypilot to reinitialize missing core skill/workflow files.\")\n+            continue\n         wf = result.get(\"workflows\", {})\n         sk = result.get(\"skills\", {})\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on learnings, \"If a critical Cypilot dependency is missing (SKILL.md, workflow), inform the user and suggest running `/cypilot` to reinitialize\".\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py` around lines 439 - 452,\nThe current update logic only checks changed-file counts from\n_process_single_agent and can miss PARTIAL/error cases; modify the handling\nafter calling _process_single_agent so you detect and handle non-success results\n(e.g., a status field like \"PARTIAL\" or an error indicator in result) in\naddition to n_changed: if result indicates PARTIAL or contains errors (even when\nwf/sk change lists are empty), add the agent to a failing list (or to\nregenerated with a flag) and log a clear message directing the user to run the\nreinitialization command (/cypilot) to restore missing critical artifacts\n(SKILL.md, workflow); update any return/exit behavior so the CLI reports these\nfailures instead of silently succeeding.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py-997-1003 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`997-1003`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`cmd_agents` should not trigger file-copy side effects.**\n\nLine 999 routes through `_resolve_agents_context`, which can call `_ensure_cypilot_local(..., dry_run=False)` by default. That makes this “read-only” command potentially write into the project.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-def _resolve_agents_context(argv: List[str], prog: str, description: str, *, allow_yes: bool = False) -> Optional[tuple]:\n+def _resolve_agents_context(\n+    argv: List[str],\n+    prog: str,\n+    description: str,\n+    *,\n+    allow_yes: bool = False,\n+    ensure_local: bool = True,\n+) -> Optional[tuple]:\n@@\n-    cypilot_root, copy_report = _ensure_cypilot_local(cypilot_root, project_root, args.dry_run)\n+    if ensure_local:\n+        cypilot_root, copy_report = _ensure_cypilot_local(cypilot_root, project_root, args.dry_run)\n+    else:\n+        copy_report = {\"action\": \"none\"}\n@@\n-def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n+def cmd_agents(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n@@\n-    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(argv, prog=\"agents\", description=\"Show generated agent integration files\")\n+    ctx = _resolve_agents_context(\n+        argv,\n+        prog=\"agents\",\n+        description=\"Show generated agent integration files\",\n+        ensure_local=False,\n+    )\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/agents.py` around lines 997 - 1003,\ncmd_agents currently calls _resolve_agents_context which by default may invoke\n_ensure_cypilot_local with dry_run=False and cause file-copy side effects;\nchange the call path so cmd_agents requests a read-only context (e.g., pass\ndry_run=True through _resolve_agents_context or otherwise ensure\n_ensure_cypilot_local is invoked with dry_run=True) so no files are written when\nlisting agents; update the invocation in cmd_agents and any signature usage of\n_resolve_agents_context to accept and forward the dry_run flag, and ensure\n_ensure_cypilot_local is only called with dry_run=True for this command.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py-1201-1221 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1201-1221`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Guard cleanup against uninitialized `tmp_path`.**\n\nIf temp-file creation fails before `tmp_path` is assigned, the `finally` block can raise `UnboundLocalError` and hide the real editor failure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _open_editor_for_marker(\n@@\n-    editor = _get_editor()\n+    editor = _get_editor()\n+    tmp_path: Optional[str] = None\n     try:\n@@\n-            tmp_path = tmp.name\n+            tmp_path = tmp.name\n@@\n     finally:\n         try:\n-            os.unlink(tmp_path)\n+            if tmp_path:\n+                os.unlink(tmp_path)\n         except OSError:\n             pass\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py` around lines 1201 - 1221, The\nfinally block can raise UnboundLocalError if tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile fails\nbefore tmp_path is assigned; initialize tmp_path = None before the try that\ncreates the temp file and in the finally guard the cleanup (os.unlink) with a\nconditional check like \"if tmp_path is not None and os.path.exists(tmp_path):\"\nand catch/log OSError there so cleanup won't mask the original exception; update\nthe cleanup logic around the tmp_path variable in the same scope where\nNamedTemporaryFile, tmp.write, subprocess.check_call, and open(tmp_path, ...)\nare used.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<su