kquote>\n\n`1200-1222`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Guard temp-file cleanup when `tmp_path` was never assigned.**\n\nIf temp file creation fails before assignment, Line 1220 can raise `UnboundLocalError` and mask the original failure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _open_editor_for_marker(\n@@\n-    try:\n+    tmp_path: Optional[str] = None\n+    try:\n         with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(\n@@\n             tmp.write(content)\n             tmp_path = tmp.name\n@@\n     finally:\n-        try:\n-            os.unlink(tmp_path)\n-        except OSError:\n-            pass\n+        if tmp_path:\n+            try:\n+                os.unlink(tmp_path)\n+            except OSError:\n+                pass\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n1200 - 1222, The finally block assumes tmp_path exists and can raise\nUnboundLocalError if temp file creation failed; initialize tmp_path = None\nbefore the try (or check with \"if tmp_path:\" / \"if tmp_path is not None\" inside\nthe finally) and only call os.unlink(tmp_path) when tmp_path is set; update the\ncleanup in the try/except/finally around the tempfile creation and\nsubprocess/edit/read steps (the block using tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile,\nsubprocess.check_call, and open to read edited) to guard removal so the original\nexception isn't masked.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py-2155-2204 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2155-2204`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`_human_kit_migrate` is reading fields that `migrate_kit` never returns.**\n\nThe renderer expects `from_version`/`to_version` and `merged_blueprints`, but migration results provide `kit_version` and `blueprints`. As written, version/merge summaries are silently dropped in human mode.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        from_v = r.get(\"from_version\")\n-        to_v = r.get(\"to_version\")\n-        ver_str = \"\"\n-        if from_v is not None and to_v is not None:\n-            ver_str = f\" v{from_v} → v{to_v}\"\n+        kit_version = r.get(\"kit_version\", \"\")\n+        ver_str = f\" ({kit_version})\" if kit_version else \"\"\n@@\n-            regen = r.get(\"regenerated\", {})\n+            regen = r.get(\"regenerated\", {})\n             if regen:\n                 fw = regen.get(\"files_written\", 0)\n-                ww = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                ww_raw = regen.get(\"workflows_written\", 0)\n+                ww = len(ww_raw) if isinstance(ww_raw, list) else int(ww_raw or 0)\n                 err = regen.get(\"error\")\n@@\n-            # Show merge details\n-            merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", [])\n+            # Show merge details\n+            merged = r.get(\"blueprints\", [])\n             for mb in merged:\n                 bp_name = mb.get(\"blueprint\", \"?\")\n-                accepted = mb.get(\"accepted\", 0)\n-                declined = mb.get(\"declined\", 0)\n-                inserted = mb.get(\"inserted\", 0)\n-                deleted = mb.get(\"deleted\", 0)\n+                updated = len(mb.get(\"markers_updated\", []))\n+                skipped = len(mb.get(\"markers_skipped\", []))\n+                inserted = len(mb.get(\"markers_inserted\", []))\n+                modified = len(mb.get(\"markers_modified\", []))\n                 parts = []\n-                if accepted:\n-                    parts.append(f\"{accepted} accepted\")\n-                if declined:\n-                    parts.append(f\"{declined} declined\")\n+                if updated:\n+                    parts.append(f\"{updated} updated\")\n+                if skipped:\n+                    parts.append(f\"{skipped} skipped\")\n                 if inserted:\n                     parts.append(f\"{inserted} inserted\")\n-                if deleted:\n-                    parts.append(f\"{deleted} deleted\")\n+                if modified:\n+                    parts.append(f\"{modified} modified\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n2155 - 2204, _human_kit_migrate currently reads from_version/to_version and\nmerged_blueprints which migrate_kit doesn't return; update the renderer to look\nfor \"kit_version\" (fall back to existing from_version/to_version if present) and\nbuild ver_str from kit_version (handle either a dict with \"from\"/\"to\" or a\nsingle version string), and replace uses of \"merged_blueprints\" with\n\"blueprints\" (iterate each blueprint entry to extract \"blueprint\", \"accepted\",\n\"declined\", \"inserted\", \"deleted\"). Keep the existing regen/error handling and\nui calls but source version and merge data from r.get(\"kit_version\") and\nr.get(\"blueprints\") so version/merge summaries are shown.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py-1199-1212 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1199-1212`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Parse `$VISUAL/$EDITOR` as argv before launching subprocess.**\n\nLine 1210 passes the entire editor string as a single token to `subprocess.check_call()`. Common values like `code --wait` will fail because the subprocess module expects separate argv tokens, not a shell command string. Use `shlex.split()` to tokenize the environment variable, matching standard practice in git and other tools.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+import shlex\n...\n def _open_editor_for_marker(\n     key: str,\n     user_raw: str,\n     new_raw: str,\n ) -> Optional[str]:\n     \"\"\"Open user's default editor for manual marker merge, git-style.\n     \"\"\"\n     editor = _get_editor()\n+    editor_argv = shlex.split(editor)\n+    if not editor_argv:\n+        sys.stderr.write(\"        editor failed: empty editor command\\n\")\n+        return None\n     try:\n         with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(\n             mode=\"w\",\n             suffix=\".md\",\n             prefix=f\"cypilot-migrate-{key.replace(':', '-').replace('#', '-')}-\",\n             delete=False,\n             encoding=\"utf-8\",\n         ) as tmp:\n             tmp.write(content)\n             tmp_path = tmp.name\n \n-        subprocess.check_call([editor, tmp_path])\n+        subprocess.check_call([*editor_argv, tmp_path])\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n1199 - 1212, The editor command string returned by _get_editor() is being passed\nas a single token to subprocess.check_call([editor, tmp_path]), which fails for\nmulti-argument editors like \"code --wait\"; split the editor string into argv\ntokens with shlex.split(editor) and pass the resulting list plus tmp_path to\nsubprocess.check_call (e.g. argv = shlex.split(editor) + [tmp_path]) so\nsubprocess receives separate arguments; ensure you import shlex at the top of\nthe module.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`123-129`: **Consider extracting `_rel` helper to the shared UI module.**\n\nThis helper function is duplicated verbatim in `list_ids.py`, `where_used.py`, and `where_defined.py`. Extracting it to `ui.py` (e.g., as `