D\" update the warn call to\nremove the unnecessary f-string prefix on the \"Aborted\" literal: change\nf\"Aborted\" to a plain \"Aborted\" while keeping the inner f-string (f\":\n{message}\") for the message interpolation; this touches the warn(...) expression\nin that aborted-status branch.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`229-229`: **Simplify lambda to direct function reference.**\n\nThe lambda wrapper is unnecessary since `_human_list_ids` already matches the expected signature.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    ui.result(result, human_fn=lambda d: _human_list_ids(d))\n+    ui.result(result, human_fn=_human_list_ids)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py at line\n229, The ui.result call uses an unnecessary lambda wrapper around\n_human_list_ids; update the call in list_ids.py to pass the function reference\ndirectly by replacing human_fn=lambda d: _human_list_ids(d) with\nhuman_fn=_human_list_ids so ui.result uses _human_list_ids directly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`121-121`: **Remove extraneous f-string prefix.**\n\nThis f-string has no placeholders, so the `f` prefix is unnecessary.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        ui.warn(f\"ID not found in any artifact.\")\n+        ui.warn(\"ID not found in any artifact.\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py at\nline 121, Remove the unnecessary f-string prefix from the ui.warn call so the\nliteral isn't treated as an f-string; replace ui.warn(f\"ID not found in any\nartifact.\") with ui.warn(\"ID not found in any artifact.\") in the\nwhere_defined.py code (the ui.warn invocation shown).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`79-79`: **Include explicit `status` in `ui.result` payloads for outcome clarity.**\n\nThese result payloads omit `status`, which makes command outcomes less consistent for consumers and human-mode status handling.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        ui.result({\"id\": target_id, \"artifacts_scanned\": 0, \"count\": 0, \"references\": []}, human_fn=lambda d: _human_where_used(d))\n+        ui.result({\"status\": \"NOT_FOUND\", \"id\": target_id, \"artifacts_scanned\": 0, \"count\": 0, \"references\": []}, human_fn=lambda d: _human_where_used(d))\n@@\n-    ui.result({\"id\": target_id, \"artifacts_scanned\": len(artifacts_to_scan), \"count\": len(references), \"references\": references}, human_fn=lambda d: _human_where_used(d))\n+    ui.result({\n+        \"status\": \"FOUND\" if references else \"NOT_FOUND\",\n+        \"id\": target_id,\n+        \"artifacts_scanned\": len(artifacts_to_scan),\n+        \"count\": len(references),\n+        \"references\": references,\n+    }, human_fn=lambda d: _human_where_used(d))\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 105-105\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py` at line 79, Update the\nui.result payloads in where_used.py (the ui.result call at the shown diff and\nthe similar call around the later occurrence) to include an explicit \"status\"\nfield; set status to \"not_found\" when artifacts_scanned/count are 0 and to\n\"success\" when references were found (or otherwise use the same status\nconvention used by other commands), and ensure the human_fn/_human_where_used\nbehavior remains unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py:\n- Around line 1906-1941: Several sys.stderr.write calls use unnecessary\nf-strings (no interpolation) which triggers Ruff F541; replace those f\"...\"\nstrings with plain string literals. In the blocks handling\nreport.get(\"inserted\"), report[\"skipped\"], and the updates loop (references:\ndeclined_update, declined_insert, accepted_force, modify_overrides) and helper\ncalls (_open_editor_for_marker, _prompt_confirm, _show_marker_content,\n_show_marker_diff), change lines like sys.stderr.write(f\"    + {k} — new\nmarker\\n\") only when they contain no { } interpolation to non-f-string\nequivalents (e.g. \"        ✓ manually edited\\n\" -> \"        ✓ manually\nedited\\n\"), leaving f-strings that do include variables intact.\n- Around line 2173-2193: _human_kit_migrate is reading keys that migrate_kit no\nlonger emits; update it to accept both shapes: read from_version/to_version but\nfall back to the single kit_version (e.g., if from_version/to_version are\nmissing use r.get(\"kit_version\")), and read merged_blueprints but fall back to\nblueprints (e.g., merged = r.get(\"merged_blueprints\", r.get(\"blueprints\", []))).\nAlso normalize regenerated counts: when reading regen.get(\"files_written\") and\nregen.get(\"workflows_written\") coerce lists to counts (use len() when the value\nis a list) and handle missing values with 0 so the UI prints numeric counts\ninstead of raw lists or None; update _human_kit_migrate to use these fallbacks\nand normaliz