_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T22:58:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T10:06:40Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> ## Rate limit exceeded\n> \n> `@ainetx` has exceeded the limit for the number of commits that can be reviewed per hour. Please wait **13 minutes and 23 seconds** before requesting another review.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⌛ How to resolve this issue?</summary>\n> \n> After the wait time has elapsed, a review can be triggered using the `@coderabbitai review` command as a PR comment. Alternatively, push new commits to this PR.\n> \n> We recommend that you space out your commits to avoid hitting the rate limit.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🚦 How do rate limits work?</summary>\n> \n> CodeRabbit enforces hourly rate limits for each developer per organization.\n> \n> Our paid plans have higher rate limits than the trial, open-source and free plans. In all cases, we re-allow further reviews after a brief timeout.\n> \n> Please see our [FAQ](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/faq) for further information.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n> \n> Reviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 480af09978d3376e6a7e5ce643b09f094586deff and 642f958467c7bbe6eb9a941f7e48c7f83420ac5e.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n> \n> * `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py`\n> * `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/toc.py`\n> * `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py`\n> * `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/toc.py`\n> * `tests/test_kit.py`\n> * `tests/test_toc.py`\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThe PR adds dual marker syntax (named TYPE:ID + legacy TYPE), a stable marker identity resolution order (explicit ID → TOML-derived → positional fallback), identity-key-based parsing and three-way merges with legacy-to-named upgrades, anchor-relative insertion, interactive/auto migration controls, and widespread blueprint marker renaming to explicit scoped identifiers.\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Architecture & Specs** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/architecture/DESIGN.md`, `.bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/blueprint-system.md`, `.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/kit/blueprint.md`, `.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/kit/examples/blueprint-structure.md`|Design and spec docs updated to define dual marker syntaxes, marker identity resolution order, identity-key-centric parsing/three-way merge, anchor insertion rules, deprecation/upgrade behavior, and new marker categories (system-prompt, workflow).|\n|**CLI Merge & Migration** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py`, `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py`|Implements identity-aware three-way merge, legacy→named normalization/upgrades, anchor-relative insertion, interactive migration UX and auto-approve flags; adds helpers (`_derive_marker_id`, `_normalize_legacy_to_named`, `_upgrade_legacy_tags`, `_read_whatsnew`, `_show_whatsnew`) and updates `update_kit`/`migrate_kit` signatures.|\n|**Blueprint Parser & Utilities** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/blueprint.py`, `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/codebase.py`, `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/toc.py`|Parser accepts optional `:ID`, records `explicit_id`, adds `_SINGLETON_MARKERS`, warns on legacy non-singleton markers, extracts system-prompt/workflow blocks; `cross_validate_code` accepts `artifact_instances_all`; TOC parsing made fence-aware.|\n|**Validation & Update CLI** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py`|Collects full artifact instances (`artifact_instances_all`) for broader cross-validation; `cmd_update` adds `--no-interactive` and `-y/--yes`, surfaces core whatsnew before core replacement, and passes interactive/auto flags to kit updates.|\n|**Blueprint Content (mass renames)** <br> `.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/*.md`, `.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/blueprints/*.md` (ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-*, PRD, etc.)|Large, systematic refactor replacing generic markers (`@cpt:rule`, `@cpt:heading`, `@cpt:prompt`, `@cpt:check`, etc.) with explicit scoped variants (`@cpt:rule:<id>`, `@cpt:heading:<id>`, etc.) to align with identity-based parsing and deterministic artifact generation.|\n|**Kit Metadata & Versioning** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/__init__.py`, `.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/conf.toml`|Bumped package version `v3.0.6-beta` → `v3.0.7-beta`; kit version incremented (2 → 4).|\n|**Guidance & Generated Artifacts** <br> `.bootstrap/config/AGENTS.md`, `.bootstrap/.gen/kits/sdlc/codebase/rules.md`|Editorial guidance additions and stricter traceability rules requiring per-instruction begin/end markers with placement examples.|\n|**WhatsNew Ledger** <br> `.bootstrap/.core/whatsnew.toml`|Added whatsnew entries documenting core versions, migration notes, three-way merge, and interactive migration features.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User as User\n    participant CLI as CLI\n    participant Parser as Parser\n    participant Normalizer as Normalizer\n    participant Merger as Merger\n    participant Upgrader as Upgrader\n    participant Output as Output\n\n    User->>CLI: kit update / migrate (interactive / auto_approve)\n    CLI->>Parser: parse_blueprint(user_blueprint)\n    Parser->>Parser: extract segments (type, explicit_id, identity_key)\n    Parser-->>CLI: user_segments\n\n    CLI->>Parser: parse_blueprint(old_reference)\n    Parser-->>CLI: old_segments\n    CLI->>Parser: parse_blueprint(new_reference)\n    Parser-->>CLI: new_segments\n\n    alt legacy markers present\n        CLI->>Normalizer: _normalize_legacy_to_named(user_text, reference_text)\n        Normalizer->>Normalizer: derive IDs from heading/TOML/position\n        Normalizer-->>CLI: normalized_user_text\n    end\n\n    CLI->>Merger: _three_way_merge_blueprint(old, new, user, force/restore/remove)\n    Merger->>Merger: match markers by identity_key\n    Merger->>Merger: apply merge rules (preserve user edits, anchor inserts, respect deletions)\n    Merger->>Upgrader: _upgrade_legacy_tags(merged_parts)\n    Upgrader->>Upgrader: convert unnamed → named using derived IDs\n    Upgrader-->>Merger: upgraded_result\n\n    alt interactive\n        Merger->>User: show per-marker diffs / prompts\n        User->>Merger: approve / reject\n    else auto-approve\n        Merger->>Merger: apply changes automatically\n    end\n\n    Merger-->>Output: merged_and_upgraded_blueprint\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- cyberfabric/cyber-pilot#82: Overlaps marker-identity, three-way blueprint merge, and kit migration codepaths — strong code-level connection.  \n- cyberfabric/cyber-pilot#83: Related updates to kit update/migrate flows and version bump that intersect with CLI/metadata changes.  \n- cyberfabric/cyber-pilot#64: Related blueprint/template token changes for PR review/status workflows and template identifiers.\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 In burrows of code the markers hide,  \n> > From nameless whispers to IDs with pride,  \n> > Three-way hops and gentle merges play,  \n> > Legacy to named — a carrot-lit way,  \n> > The rabbit cheers: \"Blueprints spring to life today!\"\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n### ❌ Failed checks (1