hout an explicit `strict=` parameter\n\nAdd explicit value for parameter `strict=`\n\n(B905)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py around lines\n936 - 943, The loop currently skips types when len(t_segs) != len(r_segs), which\ndrops possible identity mappings; instead of continuing, for each mtype build a\nlookup of reference segments with explicit_id (from ref_by_type) and then for\neach t_seg in text_by_type[mtype] that lacks explicit_id attempt to find an\nunmatched r_seg with explicit_id and map upgrade_map[id(t_seg)] = (mtype,\nr_seg.explicit_id); ensure you mark r_segs as consumed to avoid duplicate\nmapping and still skip types only when no explicit-id mappings can be\nestablished. Use the existing variables t_segs, r_segs, upgrade_map, t_seg,\nr_seg and the explicit_id attribute to locate and perform the mappings.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-02T23:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T23:03:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133294","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/85","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133294"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133294"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/85"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":952,"original_start_line":936,"start_side":"RIGHT","line