eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Fence parsing is still incorrect for mixed fence lengths/types.**\n\nAt Line 199 and Line 200, fence state flips on any ` ``` ` / `~~~` match. That misparses valid Markdown where a longer opener contains shorter fence text, causing false TOC boundaries and heading detection downstream.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix (track fence char + minimum closing length)</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _next_heading_or_separator(\n     lines: List[str], start: int,\n ) -> Optional[int]:\n     \"\"\"Return index of next heading or ``---`` separator, skipping fenced blocks.\"\"\"\n-    in_fence = False\n+    in_fence = False\n+    fence_char = \"\"\n+    fence_len = 0\n     for j in range(start, len(lines)):\n-        if _FENCE_RE.match(lines[j].strip()):\n-            in_fence = not in_fence\n+        stripped = lines[j].strip()\n+        m = re.match(r\"^([`~]{3,})\", stripped)\n+        if m:\n+            token = m.group(1)\n+            token_char = token[0]\n+            token_len = len(token)\n+            if not in_fence:\n+                in_fence = True\n+                fence_char = token_char\n+                fence_len = token_len\n+            elif token_char == fence_char and token_len >= fence_len:\n+                in_fence = False\n+                fence_char = \"\"\n+                fence_len = 0\n             continue\n         if in_fence:\n             continue\n         if re.match(r\"^#{1,6}\\s\", lines[j]) or lines[j].strip() == \"---\":\n             return j\n     return None\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/toc.py around lines\n193 - 206, The fence parsing in _next_heading_or_separator flips in_fence on any\n_FENCE_RE match which misdetects fences of different types/lengths; change the\nlogic to record the fence delimiter char and the opener length when entering a\nfence (e.g., store fence_char and fence_len) and only exit the fence when a\nmatching fence delimiter with the same char is seen whose length is at least the\nopener length; update the matching logic that currently toggles in_fence to\nset/clear these fence variables and ensure headings/separators are skipped only\nwhile fence_char is set, leaving the rest of the function (heading detection via\nre.match and '---' check) unchanged so _next_heading_or_separator, in_fence, and\n_FENCE_RE references remain consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 0e1e4ef to 21c8888","created_at":"2026-03-02T23:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T23:17:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133347","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/85","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133347"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133347"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/85"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":225,"original_start_line":193,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":239,"original_line":206,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":17,"position":77,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133358","pull_request_review_id":3879230695,"id":2875133358,"