dule-specific non-functional requirements and explicit exclusions.\n+```\n+`@/cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on learnings: Apply deterministic validation for structure, cross-references, and traceability in artifacts.\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n`@cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/PRD.md at line 3239, There is an\nunmatched closing prompt marker (`@/cpt:prompt`) that breaks the template;\nreplace that orphan closing tag with the correct named prompt marker (for\nexample `@/cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`) or remove it entirely so the prompt block is\nproperly opened/closed; ensure the surrounding prompt block uses the matching\nnamed marker (`@/cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`) for module-specific NFRs and exclusions\nand validate adjacent prompt markers for symmetry.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 0e1e4ef to 21c8888","created_at":"2026-03-02T23:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T23:17:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133358","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/85","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2875133358"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/85#discussion_r2875133358"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.g