ails live in FEATURE artifacts instead, and add a clarifying\n> note in the template (or link) indicating where authors must place API schemas\n> (FEATURE) to prevent impossible validation; search for occurrences of \"API\n> endpoint\", \"API request/response\", and the rule ID DECOMP-NO-001 within\n> DECOMPOSITION.md and the referenced ranges (1478-1485, 1792-1990, 1993-2110) to\n> remove or move those sections accordingly.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> \n> `1464-1512`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Define all checklist domains used by checks (`DECOMP`, `FMT`) in the checklist skeleton.**\n> \n> `@cpt:check` entries use `domain = \"DECOMP\"` and `domain = \"FMT\"`, but those domains are not declared in `[[domain]]` and are also absent from `review.priority`. This can make these checks ungrouped/unordered or fail deterministic validation.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  [review]\n> -priority = [\"COV\", \"EXC\", \"ATTR\", \"LEV\", \"CFG\", \"TRC\", \"DEP\", \"CHK\", \"DOC\"]\n> +priority = [\"COV\", \"EXC\", \"ATTR\", \"LEV\", \"CFG\", \"TRC\", \"DEP\", \"CHK\", \"DOC\", \"DECOMP\", \"FMT\"]\n> \n>  [[domain]]\n>  abbr = \"DOC\"\n>  name = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS\"\n>  header = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS (DOC)\"\n>  standards = []\n> \n> +[[domain]]\n> +abbr = \"DECOMP\"\n> +name = \"DECOMPOSITION BOUNDARIES\"\n> +header = \"DECOMPOSITION BOUNDARIES (DECOMP)\"\n> +standards = []\n> +\n> +[[domain]]\n> +abbr = \"FMT\"\n> +name = \"FORMAT VALIDATION\"\n> +header = \"FORMAT VALIDATION (FMT)\"\n> +standards = []\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 1541-1608, 688-749\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DECOMPOSITION.md around lines 1464 -\n> 1512, Add missing domain declarations and review ordering for the domains\n> referenced by `@cp