matches the existing opening \"`@cpt:prompt:adr-traceability`\" semantics\n> and that all backtick-wrapped markers are correctly balanced.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/FEATURE.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1824-1824`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Use canonical severity values only (`CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW`).**\n> \n> At Line 1824, Line 1899, Line 1924, Line 1949, Line 2222, Line 2247, and Line 2299, severity includes extra text (e.g., `\"HIGH (if applicable)\"`). This can break deterministic severity sorting/reporting. Keep applicability in checklist text, not in the severity token.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🛠️ Suggested normalization pattern</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> - severity = \"HIGH (if applicable)\"\n> + severity = \"HIGH\"\n> ```\n> \n> Apply the same normalization to other non-canonical severity values.\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 1899-1899, 1924-1924, 1949-1949, 2222-2222, 2247-2247, 2299-2299\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/FEATURE.md at line 1824, Replace\n> non-canonical severity tokens (e.g., severity = \"HIGH (if applicable)\") with the\n> canonical values CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW (for this instance change\n> severity = \"HIGH (if applicable)\" to severity = \"HIGH\"); keep any\n> explanatory/applicability text in the checklist or comment text rather than\n> inside the severity token so deterministic sorting/reporting works; apply the\n> same normalization to the other occurrences of non-canonical tokens (the other\n> severity = \"… (if applicable)\" instances) in FEATURE.md.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> \n> `3106-3106`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **`algo` ID heading binding points to the wrong section.**\n> \n> At Line 3106, `