rkflows.extend(_collect_workflow_blocks(bp))\n> +        for wf in _collect_workflow_blocks(bp):\n> +            wf_name = wf.get(\"name\", \"\")\n> +            if wf_name in seen_workflow_names:\n> +                errors.append(\n> +                    f\"Duplicate workflow name '{wf_name}' found in {bp.path}\"\n> +                )\n> +                continue\n> +            seen_workflow_names.add(wf_name)\n> +            all_workflows.append(wf)\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DECOMPOSITION.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `686-749`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n> \n> **Declare `DECOMP`/`FMT` domains (or remap checks) to avoid validation failure.**\n> \n> Checks now reference `domain = \"DECOMP\"` and `domain = \"FMT\"`, but those domains are not declared in the checklist skeleton. This will break domain-reference validation for `@cpt:check`.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested patch (add missing domains and review order)</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  [review]\n> -priority = [\"COV\", \"EXC\", \"ATTR\", \"LEV\", \"CFG\", \"TRC\", \"DEP\", \"CHK\", \"DOC\"]\n> +priority = [\"COV\", \"EXC\", \"ATTR\", \"LEV\", \"CFG\", \"TRC\", \"DEP\", \"CHK\", \"FMT\", \"DECOMP\", \"DOC\"]\n> @@\n>  [[domain]]\n>  abbr = \"CHK\"\n>  name = \"CHECKBOX CONSISTENCY\"\n>  header = \"CHECKBOX CONSISTENCY (CHK)\"\n>  standards = []\n>  \n> +[[domain]]\n> +abbr = \"FMT\"\n> +name = \"FORMAT VALIDATION\"\n> +header = \"FORMAT VALIDATION (FMT)\"\n> +standards = []\n> +\n> +[[domain]]\n> +abbr = \"DECOMP\"\n> +name = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS (DECOMPOSITION)\"\n> +header = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS (DECOMP)\"\n> +standards = []\n> +\n>  [[domain]]\n>  abbr = \"DOC\"\n>  name = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS\"\n>  header = \"DELIBERATE OMISSIONS (DOC)\"\n>  standards = []\n> ```\n> </details>\n> Based on learnings: Apply deterministic validation for structure, cross-references, and traceability in artifacts.