n enum fields.\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 1889-1889, 2159-2159, 2183-2183\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DESIGN.md at line 1814, Replace the\n> non-enum severity strings like `severity = \"HIGH (if database schemas are\n> documented)\"` with a valid enum value (e.g., `severity = \"HIGH\"`) in the\n> DESIGN.md entries and remove the parenthetical applicability phrase from the\n> enum field; instead, append that applicability note to the check description\n> text (the human-readable check/comment associated with the same entry). Do this\n> for the occurrences matching the exact phrase `severity = \"HIGH (if database\n> schemas are documented)\"` and the other listed instances (around the same\n> pattern at the other occurrences) so all severity fields conform to the declared\n> severity enum and applicability remains in the descriptive text.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> \n> `220-230`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Replace non-standard `SPEC` artifact references with supported artifact types.**\n> \n> This blueprint instructs users to move content to `SPEC` / `Spec DESIGN`, but that artifact type is not part of the SDLC standard set used elsewhere. This creates workflow and traceability ambiguity.\n> \n> \n> Based on learnings: Use standard artifact types in the Cypilot kit SDLC: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD.\n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 2291-2292, 2373-2374\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DESIGN.md around lines 220 - 230, The\n> blueprint uses a non-standard artifact name \"SPEC\" (and occurrences of \"Spec\n> DESIGN\") which is not part of the kit's SDLC vocabulary; update every reference\n> of \"SPEC\" / \"Spec DESIGN\" in this document (including the \"NOT DESIGN-worthy\"\n> list and the relationship notes) to one of the supported artifact types (e.g.,\n> replace with DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, PRD, ADR, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE,\n> PR-REVIEW, or PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE as appropriate for the context) so\n> traceability follows the standard set and ensure the replacement preserves the\n> intended meaning (use DESIGN for high-level implementation intent or\n> DECOMPOSITION for implementation-detail instructions).\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/codebase.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`382-399`: **Consider renaming `_all` to avoid shadowing the built-in `all()`.**\n\nThe variable `_all` shadows Python's built-in `all()` function. While this doesn't cause a bug here since `all()` isn't used in this scope, it's a minor readability concern and can confuse readers or static analysis tools.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Suggested rename</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            _all = artifact_instances_all or artifact_instances\n-            if _all and fid in _all:\n-                art_insts = _all[fid]\n+            inst_source = artifact_instances_all or artifact_instances\n+            if inst_source and fid in inst_source:\n+                art_insts = inst_source[fid]\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/codebase.py around\nlines 382 - 399, The local variable named `_all` shadows Python's built-in\nall(); rename it to a clearer non-shadowing name (e.g., inst_map,\nartifact_inst_map, or art_insts_lookup) and update its usage in the block that\ncomputes art_insts and compares against _code_inst_lookup (referencing the\nvariables artifact_instances_all, artifact_instances, and the local `_all`),\nensuring the new name replaces `_all` in the conditional `if _all and fid in\n_all:` and the subsequent `art_insts = _all[fid]` so logic remains identical but\nno built-in is shadowed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`58-61`: **Clarify precedence between `--no-interactive` and `--yes`.**\n\nAt Line 58 and Line 60, both flags can be enabled together, and both are forwarded at Line 148-149. Consider making them mutually exclusive (or explicitly defining precedence) to avoid ambiguous behavior.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested CLI guard</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    p.add_argument(\"--no-interactive\", action=\"store_true\",\n-                   help=\"Disable interactive prompts (auto-skip customized markers)\")\n-    p.add_argument(\"-y\", \"--yes\", action=\"store_true\",\n-                   help=\"Auto-approve all prompts (no interaction)\")\n+    mode = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n+    mode.add_argument(\"--no-interactive\", action=\"store_true\",\n+                      help=\"Disable interactive prompts (auto-skip customized markers)\")\n+    mode.add_argument(\"-y\", \"--yes\", action=\"store_true\",\n+                      help=\"Auto-approve all prompts (no interaction)\")\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 148-149\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py around\nlines 58 - 61, The two CLI flags --no-interactive (added via p.add_argument) and\n-y/--yes are ambiguous when both set and are later forwarded; make them mutually\nexclusive by creating an argparse mutually exclusive group (via\np.add_mutually_exclusive_group()) and adding both flags to that group so\nargparse enforces exclusivity, or alternatively add a runtime check after\nparsing (e.g., in the function that forwards these flags) that calls\nparser.error or raises a clear error if both args.no_interactive and args.yes\nare True and document the chosen precedence; update the code paths that forward\nthese flags to reflect the enforced exclusivity (references: p.add_argument for\n--no-interactive and -y/--yes and the forwarding site where both flags are\npassed).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/kit/blueprint.md:\n- Around line 27-40: The table of contents contains invalid fragment links\n(e.g., \"PRD Commands\", \"PRD Workflows\", \"cpt:system-prompt\", \"cpt:workflow\")\ncausing broken in-page navigation and MD051; update the TOC to match actual\nheadings or remove/update the offending entries: either rename the TOC entries\nto the exact heading text/anchors present in the document or add the\ncorresponding headings (e.g., create \"PRD Commands\" and \"PRD Workflows\"\nsections) so anchors resolve; target the TOC block that lists \"[PRD\nCommands](`#prd-commands`)\" and similar entries and make the link text/fragment\nidentifiers match the real headings such as the existing \"Prerequisites\",\n\"Steps\", and the cpt:... anchors.\n- Around line 837-845: The fenced code block that starts with\n\"{cypilot_path}/kits/{slug}/.prev/  ── old reference (saved before update)\" is\nmissing a language tag and triggers MD040; fix it by adding a language\nidentifier (use \"text\") immediately after the opening triple backticks (so the\nblock becomes \"```text ... ```\") and keep the content and closing fence\nunchanged.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py:\n- Line 1538: The user-facing write call using sys.stderr.write in the kit.py\nsnippet prints a Unicode minus '−' which causes lint/terminal issues; change the\nf-string in that removal message (the sys.stderr.write call that currently\ncontains \"    − {k} — removed from reference (will be deleted from config)\\n\")\nto use the ASCII hyphen-minus '-' (and also replace the long dash '—' with '-'\nor a consistent ASCII hyphen if desired) so the output uses only ASCII\ncharacters; update the string in that sys.stderr.write invocation and run\nlint/tests to confirm the warning is resolved.\n- Around line 1510-1513: The local variable del_details is assigned from\nreport.get(\"deleted_details\", {}) in the update-report handling block but never\nused, causing a lint/CI failure; remove the unused assignment (del_details =\nreport.get(\"deleted_details\", {})) from the function where kit_slug and bp_name\nare used (the block that also assigns upd_details and skip_details and calls\nsys.stderr.write) so only necessary locals remain.\n- Around line 936-943: The loop currently skips types when len(t_segs) !=\nlen(r_segs), which drops possible identity mappings; instead of continuing, for\neach mtype build a lookup of reference segments with explicit_id (from\nref_by_type) and then for each t_seg in text_by_type[mtype] that lacks\nexplicit_id attempt to find an unmatched r_seg with explicit_id and map\nupgrade_map[id(t_seg)] = (mtype, r_seg.explicit_id); ensure you mark r_segs as\nconsumed to avoid duplicate mapping and still skip types only when no\nexplicit-id mappings can be established. Use the existing variables t_segs,\nr_segs, upgrade_map, t_seg, r_seg and the explicit_id attribute to locate and\nperform the mappings.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/blueprint.py:\n- Around line 108-109: The unclosed-marker error message should include the\nexplicit marker ID when present: 