remain\nconsistent.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/PRD.md:\n- Line 3239: There is an unmatched closing prompt marker (`@/cpt:prompt`) that\nbreaks the template; replace that orphan closing tag with the correct named\nprompt marker (for example `@/cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`) or remove it entirely so the\nprompt block is properly opened/closed; ensure the surrounding prompt block uses\nthe matching named marker (`@/cpt:prompt:prd-nfr`) for module-specific NFRs and\nexclusions and validate adjacent prompt markers for symmetry.\n\n---\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/ADR.md:\n- Around line 2770-2784: There is an unmatched closing marker \"`@/cpt:example`\"\nat the end of the ADR section that breaks marker parsing; fix by either removing\nthat standalone closing marker or by adding the corresponding opening marker for\nthe intended example block (e.g., add a matching \"`@cpt:example`\" or a named\nexample like \"`@cpt:example:adr-traceability`\" before the traceability content),\nmaking sure the pair matches the existing opening\n\"`@cpt:prompt:adr-traceability`\" semantics and that all backtick-wrapped markers\nare correctly balanced.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DECOMPOSITION.md:\n- Around line 1478-1485: The DECOMPOSITION template conflicts with the\nvalidation rule DECOMP-NO-001 by including API endpoint and API request/response\nschema sections; update the DECOMPOSITION.md template to remove or relocate any\nexplicit \"API endpoint\" and \"API request/response schemas\" sections so\nimplementation details live in FEATURE artifacts instead, and add a clarifying\nnote in the template (or link) indicating where authors must place API schemas\n(FEATURE) to prevent impossible validation; search for occurrences of \"API\nendpoint\", \"API request/response\", and the rule ID DECOMP-NO-001 within\nDECOMPOSITION.md and the referenced ranges (1478-1485, 1792-1990, 1993-2110) to\nremove or move those sections accordingly.\n- Around line 1464-1512: Add missing domain declarations and review ordering for\nthe domains referenced by `@cpt`:check entries: locate the checklist skeleton in\nDECOMPOSITION.md where domains are declared and add [[domain]] entries for\n\"DECOMP\" and \"FMT\" (so checks like id = \"DECOMP-NO-001\" and id = \"DECOMP-NO-002\"\nhave a matching domain). Also add \"DECOMP\" and \"FMT\" to the review.priority list\nso these checks are grouped and ordered deterministically; ensure the domain\nnames exactly match the domain = \"…\" values used by `@cpt`:check entries.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DESIGN.md:\n- Line 1814: Replace the non-enum severity strings like `severity = \"HIGH (if\ndatabase schemas are documented)\"` with a valid enum value (e.g., `severity =\n\"HIGH\"`) in the DESIGN.md entries and remove the parenthetical applicability\nphrase from the enum field; instead, append that applicability note to the check\ndescription text (the human-readable check/comment associated with the same\nentry). Do this for the occurrences matching the exact phrase `severity = \"HIGH\n(if database schemas are documented)\"` and the other listed instances (around\nthe same pattern at the other occurrences) so all severity fields conform to the\ndeclared severity enum and applicability remains in the descriptive text.\n- Around line 220-230: The blueprint uses a non-standard artifact name \"SPEC\"\n(and occurrences of \"Spec DESIGN\") which is not part of the kit's SDLC\nvocabulary; update every reference of \"SPEC\" / \"Spec DESIGN\" in this document\n(including the \"NOT DESIGN-worthy\" list and the relationship notes) to one of\nthe supported artifact types (e.g., replace with DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, PRD,\nADR, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, or PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE\nas appropriate for the context) so traceability follows the standard set and\nensure the replacement preserves the intended meaning (use DESIGN for high-level\nimplementation intent or DECOMPOSITION for implementation-detail instructions).\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/FEATURE.md:\n- Line 1824: Replace non-canonical severity tokens (e.g., severity = \"HIGH (if\napplicable)\") with the canonical values CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW (for this\ninstance change severity = \"HIGH (if applicable)\" to severity = \"HIGH\"); keep\nany explanatory/applicability text in the checklist or comment text rather than\ninside the severity token so deterministic sorting/reporting works; apply the\nsame normalization to the other occurrences of non-canonical tokens (the other\nseverity = \"… (if applicable)\" instances) in FEATURE.md.\n- Line 3106: The heading binding is incorrect: change headings =\n[\"feature-processes\"] to match the actual algo ID section where algo IDs are\ndeclared (the `@cpt`:prompt:feature-process block). Update headings to\n[\"prompt:feature-process\"] (or the exact constraint ID used in the `@cpt`\ndeclaration) so the heading-scope validation points to the correct section, and\napply the same correction for the other occurrences around the 3115-3118 range.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/config/kits/sdlc/blueprints/PRD.md:\n- Around line 587-593: The rule block tagged\n`@cpt:rule:error_handling-missing_config` uses section = \"missing_config\" which\ndoesn't match the error_handling.sections skeleton; fix by making the keys\ncanonical: either change the rule's section value to \"missing_adapter\" so it\nmatches the skeleton, or alternatively add \"missing_config\" to the\nerror_handling.sections list in the skeleton — update whichever place you choose\n(the rule block `@cpt:rule:error_handling-missing_config` or the skeleton\n`error_handling.sections`) so both use the same canonical key.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/blueprints/DECOMPOSITION.md:\n- Around line 686-749: The checklist references domains \"DECOMP\" and \"FMT\" but\nonly COV/EXC/ATTR/LEV/CFG/TRC/DEP/CHK/DOC are declared; add missing domain\ndeclarations with a