scriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/issues/comments/3983286262","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/82#issuecomment-3983286262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/issues/82","id":3983286262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQ7VXwc7tbB_2","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T09:49:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T09:49:16Z","body":"<h3>Review Summary by Qodo</h3>\n\nKit migration with marker-level three-way merge, TOML versioning, and v2→v3 config migration\n\n<code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code>🐞 Bug fix</code> <code>🧪 Tests</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>Walkthroughs</h3>\n\n<details open>\n<summary>Description</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>\n• Implemented marker-level three-way merge system for intelligent blueprint updates that preserves\n  user customizations while updating unchanged markers\n• Added <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function orchestrating full kit update cycle: snapshot, reference copy,\n  migration, script copy, and <b><i>.gen/</i></b> regeneration\n• Added <b><i>migrate_kit()</i></b> with version drift detection and automatic blueprint migration via\n  <b><i>cmd_kit_migrate()</i></b> subcommand\n• Changed kit metadata extraction from blueprint parsing to <b><i>conf.toml</i></b> as single source of truth\n  for versioning\n• Added <b><i>_seed_kit_config_files()</i></b> to copy default <b><i>.toml</i></b> configs from kit scripts to <b><i>config/</i></b>\n  directory on first install\n• Refactored <b><i>cmd_update()</i></b> to use dedicated <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function, removing manual kit processing\n  logic\n• Implemented v2→v3 migration for kit configs with <b><i>_regenerate_gen_from_config()</i></b> and\n  <b><i>_migrate_adapter_json_configs()</i></b> for JSON-to-TOML conversion\n• Added TOML support to PR config loading with legacy JSON fallback in <b><i>pr.py</i></b> scripts across all\n  kit variants\n• Fixed <b><i>process_kit()</i></b> to use caller-provided <b><i>kit_slug</i></b> instead of relying on blueprint TOML\n  parsing\n• Fixed cache update skip logic for <b><i>--help</i></b> flag in update command\n• Added comprehensive test coverage for three-way merge, kit migration, pr-review normalization, and\n  JSON config migration\n• Added new SDLC kit blueprints (ADR, CODEBASE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE,\n  PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE) with marker-based organization\n• Updated PR-REVIEW blueprint and workflows to use TOML config format with artifact metadata\n• Bumped version to v3.0.4-beta\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Kit Update Trigger\"] --> B[\"update_kit()\"]\n  B --> C[\"Create .prev Snapshot\"]\n  C --> D[\"Copy Reference Kit\"]\n  D --> E[\"migrate_kit()\"]\n  E --> F[\"Three-Way Merge<br/>Blueprints\"]\n  F --> G[\"Copy Scripts\"]\n  G --> H[\"Regenerate .gen/\"]\n  H --> I[\"Updated Kit\"]\n  \n  J[\"conf.toml\"] --> K[\"Version Tracking\"]\n  K --> L[\"Migration Detection\"]\n  L --> E\n  \n  M[\"JSON Configs\"] --> N[\"_migrate_adapter_json_configs()\"]\n  N --> O[\"TOML Configs\"]\n  O --> P[\"pr.py TOML Support\"]\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +652/-9 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Kit migration with marker-level three-way merge and conf.toml versioning\n><pre>\n>• Added <b><i>_seed_kit_config_files()</i></b> to copy default <b><i>.toml</i></b> configs from kit scripts to <b><i>config/</i></b>\n>  directory on first install\n>• Implemented marker-level three-way merge system with <b><i>_parse_segments()</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>_marker_identity_key()</i></b>, and <b><i>_three_way_merge_blueprint()</i></b> for intelligent blueprint updates\n>• Added <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function orchestrating full kit update cycle: snapshot, reference copy,\n>  migration, script copy, and <b><i>.gen/</i></b> regeneration\n>• Added <b><i>migrate_kit()</i></b> and <b><i>cmd_kit_migrate()</i></b> for automatic blueprint migration with version drift\n>  detection and user customization preservation\n>• Changed kit metadata extraction from blueprint parsing to <b><i>conf.toml</i></b> as single source of truth\n>• Updated <b><i>cmd_kit()</i></b> dispatcher to support new <b><i>migrate</i></b> subcommand\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-b8897eb8dd4855e58b1f687d9a75e679ceccaddf1ee38b456a08ecde9c162c36'> .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +652/-9 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Kit migration with marker-level three-way merge and conf.toml versioning\n><pre>\n>• Added <b><i>_seed_kit_config_files()</i></b> to copy default <b><i>.toml</i></b> configs from kit scripts to <b><i>config/</i></b>\n>  directory on first install\n>• Implemented marker-level three-way merge system with <b><i>_parse_segments()</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>_marker_identity_key()</i></b>, and <b><i>_three_way_merge_blueprint()</i></b> for intelligent blueprint updates\n>• Added <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function orchestrating full kit update cycle: snapshot, reference copy,\n>  migration, script copy, and <b><i>.gen/</i></b> regeneration\n>• Added <b><i>migrate_kit()</i></b> and <b><i>cmd_kit_migrate()</i></b> for automatic blueprint migration with version drift\n>  detection and user customization preservation\n>• Changed kit metadata extraction from blueprint parsing to <b><i>conf.toml</i></b> as single source of truth\n>• Updated <b><i>cmd_kit()</i></b> dispatcher to support new <b><i>migrate</i></b> subcommand\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-bf5deba71465cc75af506fddf66814d28892347ccf5948f8a04a8ac2a55297ab'> skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. tests/test_kit.py\n <code>🧪 Tests</code> <code> +360/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Comprehensive tests for kit migration and three-way merge\n><pre>\n>• Added comprehensive test suite for <b><i>_parse_segments()</i></b> covering text-only, single markers,\n>  workflow/heading identity keys, and unclosed marker handling\n>• Added <b><i>TestThreeWayMerge</i></b> class with 6 tests validating marker update logic: unchanged markers\n>  updated, customized markers skipped, deleted markers not re-added, mixed scenarios\n>• Added <b><i>TestMigrateKit</i></b> class with 8 tests for <b><i>migrate_kit()</i></b> function including version drift,\n>  <b><i>.prev/</i></b> snapshot handling, conf.toml updates, and dry-run mode\n>• Added <b><i>TestCmdKitMigrate</i></b> class testing CLI command dispatch and error handling for missing\n>  project root and kits\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-b3958ae2feb00d9e16b26db0a3af497629df71b4db8d583f8178a4c74fa901d3'> tests/test_kit.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (77)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py\n <code> Refactoring </code> <code> +62/-241 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Refactor kit update to use dedicated update_kit function\n><pre>\n>• Refactored kit update logic from <b><i>cmd_update()</i></b> into dedicated <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function call,\n>  simplifying the update command\n>• Removed manual kit reference copying, version comparison, and <b><i>.gen/</i></b> regeneration code (now in\n>  <b><i>update_kit()</i></b>)\n>• Consolidated kit processing into single loop with cleaner progress reporting for created,\n>  migrated, and current kits\n>• Removed helper functions <b><i>_read_conf_section()</i></b> and <b><i>_compare_conf_versions()</i></b> (replaced by\n>  migration logic)\n>• Re-exported <b><i>_read_conf_version()</i></b> from <b><i>kit.py</i></b> for backward compatibility\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-38400ff287c9895ed785f4276c8b14f55bdffa9b9f603325d4004e42dfaed321'> .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py\n <code> Refactoring </code> <code> +62/-241 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Refactor kit update to use dedicated update_kit function\n><pre>\n>• Refactored kit update logic from <b><i>cmd_update()</i></b> into dedicated <b><i>update_kit()</i></b> function call,\n>  simplifying the update command\n>• Removed manual kit reference copying, version comparison, and <b><i>.gen/</i></b> regeneration code (now in\n>  <b><i>update_kit()</i></b>)\n>• Consolidated kit processing into single loop with cleaner progress reporting for created,\n>  migrated, and current kits\n>• Removed helper functions <b><i>_read_conf_section()</i></b> and <b><i>_compare_conf_versions()</i></b> (replaced by\n>  migration logic)\n>• Re-exported <b><i>_read_conf_version()</i></b> from <b><i>kit.py</i></b> for backward compatibility\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-8dea9b920d6f894d5774d9288b55700605a11d2b61e8784bbde89407ce2072dc'> skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/migrate.py\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +167/-2 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add v2→v3 migration for kit configs and .gen regeneration\n><pre>\n>• Added <b><i>_regenerate_gen_from_config()</i></b> to process migrated blueprints and populate <b><i>.gen/kits/</i></b>\n>  during v2→v3 migration\n>• Added <b><i>_migrate_adapter_json_configs()</i></b> to convert remaining adapter JSON configs to TOML with\n>  file-specific normalization\n>• Added <b><i>_normalize_pr_review_data()</i></b> and <b><i>_normalize_pr_review_entry()</i></b> to handle <b><i>pr-review.json</i></b>\n>  key renaming (camelCase→snake_case) and path rewriting\n>• Integrated <b><i>_regenerate_gen_from_config()</i></b> call before AGENTS.md generation to ensure workflow\n>  proxies resolve correctly\n>• Integrated <b><i>_migrate_adapter_json_configs()</i></b> call before adapter cleanup to preserve kit-specific\n>  configs\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-196f7ea52124f52c9c182b27e413c02b442549e2b313986a366eea956a251d0f'> .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/migrate.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. .bootstrap/.gen/kits/sdlc/scripts/pr.py\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +35/-17 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add TOML support to PR config loading with legacy fallback\n><pre>\n>• Added <b><i>tomllib</i></b> import with fallback to <b><i>tomli</i></b> for Python &lt; 3.11 compatibility\n>• Updated <b><i>_load_pr_config()</i></b> to support TOML format with resolution order: user config TOML, kit\n>  default TOML, legacy JSON configs\n>• Changed <b><i>dataDir</i></b> key access to check both snake_case (<b><i>data_dir</i></b>) and legacy camelCase\n>  (<b><i>dataDir</i></b>) for backward compatibility\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-364e62ef8585738a08d124073736933a5ef3e05c682408c3313649babbc087e2'> .bootstrap/.gen/kits/sdlc/scripts/pr.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>8. tests/test_agents_coverage.py\n <code>🧪 Tests</code> <code> +19/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Expand test coverage for agents.py edge cases\n><pre>\n>• Added <b><i>TestTargetPathFromRoot</i></b> class to cover <b><i>_target_path_from_root()</i></b> with <b><i>cypilot_root=None</i></b>\n>  parameter\n>• Added test case for <b><i>_load_json_file()</i></b> with nonexistent file returning <b><i>None</i></b>\n>• Updated docstring for <b><i>TestLoadJsonFileNonDict</i></b> to reflect expanded coverage\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-a8e7dacefd3c6de27c58b7c5f78bbee0716a9f9b7d56607a763cdec43ff0bc23'> tests/test_agents_coverage.py\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>9. .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/blueprint.py\n <code>🐞 Bug fix</code> <code> +1/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Use caller-provided kit slug in process_kit\n><pre>\n>• Modified <b><i>process_kit()</i></b> to set <b><i>bp.kit_slug</i></b> from caller parameter instead of relying on\n>  blueprint TOML parsing, ensuring consistent kit identification\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot/pull/82/files#diff-bac8eba31a410cb97bbc5721c8d5a6f4cde943f88deed2b5a00cbeb59