st the previous staged pipeline. Please align Section “Update Pipeline” with the new delegated lifecycle.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested patch</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### Update Pipeline\n@@\n-1. - `p1` - Replace `.core/` from cache - `inst-replace-core-algo`\n-2. - `p1` - Update kit reference copies from cache - `inst-update-refs-algo`\n-3. - `p1` - Compare blueprint versions using `_read_blueprint_versions()` and `_compare_versions()` - `inst-compare-algo`\n-4. - `p1` - Regenerate `.gen/` from user blueprints - `inst-regen-algo`\n-5. - `p1` - Ensure config scaffold - `inst-scaffold-algo`\n+1. - `p1` - Replace `.core/` from cache - `inst-replace-core-algo`\n+2. - `p1` - For each cached kit, delegate full lifecycle to `update_kit()` (`.prev` snapshot, ref copy, first-install/migrate, scripts sync, `.gen` regeneration) - `inst-update-kits-algo`\n+3. - `p1` - Ensure config scaffold files exist (create only if missing) - `inst-scaffold-algo`\n+4. - `p1` - Regenerate agent entry points - `inst-regenerate-agents-algo`\n+5. - `p1` - **RETURN** update report with actions taken - `inst-return-report-algo`\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 104-109\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/version-config.md around lines 77 -\n80, The \"Update Pipeline\" algorithm is out of sync: replace the old staged\npipeline (lines referenced) with the new delegated lifecycle that delegates\nper-kit work to update_kit() and uses the inst-* steps; update the section to\nlist the new flow: inst-update-kits (per-kit: save .prev, copy ref,\nfirst-install/migrate, copy scripts, regen .gen/), inst-ensure-scaffold,\ninst-regenerate-agents, and inst-return-report; ensure any mentions of the prior\nstaged pipeline are removed or rewritten to reference update_kit() orchestration\nand the inst-* step names so the document reflects the new control flow.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/.prev/blueprints/PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE.md-127-127 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`127-127`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix command typo in Notes section.**\n\nLine 127 uses `/cypilotpr-review`, which is inconsistent with Line 24 and likely invalid.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested patch</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- `{placeholders}` are filled by the LLM during the `/cypilotpr-review` workflow.\n+- `{placeholders}` are filled by the LLM during the `/cypilot-pr-review` workflow.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/.prev/blueprints/PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE.md at line\n127, Replace the incorrect command token \"/cypilotpr-review\" used in the Notes\nsentence that describes `{placeholders}` with the correct command\n\"/copilotpr-review\" so it matches the earlier occurrence and is valid; update\nthe string token in that markdown sentence (the one containing `{placeholders}`)\nto use \"/copilotpr-review\" and scan for any other occurrences of\n\"/cypilotpr-review\" to correct them as well.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.gen/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/prd-review.md-9-11 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-11`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Placeholders reference optional fields that are commented out by default.**\n\nLines 10-11 use `{project_domain}` and `{existing_artifacts}` placeholders, but these fields are commented out in the default `pr-review.toml` for the PRD Review entry. If the user doesn't configure these fields, the prompt will contain unresolved placeholders.\n\nConsider either:\n1. Making these fields required in the PRD Review config entry\n2. Adding conditional logic in the workflow to skip these lines if fields are not configured\n3. Providing sensible defaults in the TOML config\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.gen/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/prd-review.md around lines 9 -\n11, The prompt template prd-review.md contains unresolved placeholders\n`{project_domain}` and `{existing_artifacts}` that are commented out by default\nin the PRD Review entry of pr-review.toml; update either the PRD Review config\nor the template so these lines never emit unresolved placeholders: modify the\nPRD Review config to make `project_domain` and `existing_artifacts` required, or\nadd conditional rendering logic in the template generator to omit the two lines\nwhen those TOML fields are empty, or supply sensible defaults in pr-review.toml\nfor `project_domain` and `existing_artifacts` so the `{project_domain}` and\n`{existing_artifacts}` tokens are always resolved.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/.prev/blueprints/CODEBASE.md-727-731 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`727-731`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix domain enum hint to include `SEM` for consistency.**\n\nLine 729’s allowed-domain hint omits `SEM`, but Line 730 sets `domain = \"SEM\"`. This contradictory guidance can cause authoring mistakes for future checks.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/kits/sdlc/.prev/blueprints/CODEBASE.md around lines 727 - 731,\nUpdate the allowed-domain hint to include \"SEM\" so it matches the actual domain\nused (domain = \"SEM\") for the check id = \"SEM-CODE-001\"; locate the\nallowed-domain enumeration/hint near the top of this blueprint and add \"SEM\" to\nthe list of permitted values to ensure consistency with the domain assignment.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>architecture/features/version-config.md-77-80 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`77-80`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Align actor-flow step IDs with the updated per-kit orchestration model.**\n\nLine 77 introduces `inst-update-kits`, but the “Update Pipeline” algorithm section still reflects the old top-level ref/compare/regen split. This weakens flow-to-algorithm traceability.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested doc alignment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-2. - `p1` - Update kit reference copies from cache - `inst-update-refs-algo`\n-3. - `p1` - Compare blueprint versions using `_read_blueprint_versions()` and `_compare_versions()` - `inst-compare-algo`\n-4. - `p1` - Regenerate `.gen/` from user blueprints - `inst-regen-algo`\n-5. - `p1` - Ensure config scaffold - `inst-scaffold-algo`\n+2. - `p1` - For each kit in cache, delegate full lifecycle to `update_kit()` (snapshot/ref copy/first-install or migrate/script copy/regenerate) - `inst-update-kits-algo`\n+3. - `p1` - Ensure config scaffold - `inst-scaffold-algo`\n+4. - `p1` - Regenerate agent entry points - `inst-regenerate-agents-algo`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@architecture/features/version-config.md` around lines 77 - 80, Update the\n\"Update Pipeline\" algorithm to match the new per-kit orchestration by replacing\nthe old top-level ref/compare/regen steps with the per-kit steps referenced by\nthe actor-flow IDs (e.g., inst-update-kits, inst-ensure-scaffold,\ninst-regenerate-agents, inst-return-report); specifically, document that\ninst-update-kits delegates to update_kit() for each cached kit (save .prev, copy\nref, handle first-install/migrate, copy scripts, regen .gen/), ensure\ninst-ensure-scaffold creates missing scaffold files only, inst-regenerate-agents\nregenerates agent entry points, and inst-return-report returns the consolidated\nupdate report so the algorithm and actor-flow IDs are fully aligned.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>tests/test_kit.py-735-735 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`735-735`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix unused variable linting violations in tests/test_kit.py.**\n\nRuff detects 5 unused variable violations. The comment correctly identifies three at lines 735 (RUF059), 766 (RUF059), and 870 (F841), but verification also uncovered additional violations at lines 276 and 295 (both F841 for `adapter`).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\nLine 276:\n-            adapter = _bootstrap_project(root)\n+            _ = _bootstrap_project(root)\n\nLine 295:\n-            adapter = _bootstrap_project(root)\n+            _ = _bootstrap_project(root)\n\nLine 735:\n-        merged, report = _three_way_merge_blueprint(old_ref, new_ref, user)\n+        merged, _report = _three_way_merge_blueprint(old_ref, new_ref, user)\n\nLine 766:\n-        merged, report = _three_way_merge_blueprint(same, same, same)\n+        _merged, report = _three_way_merge_blueprint(same, same, same)\n\nLine 870:\n-            result = migrate_kit(\"sdlc\", ref_dir, config_kit, gen_kits, dry_run=True)\n+            _ = migrate_kit(\"sdlc\", ref_dir, config_kit, gen_kits, dry_run=True)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_kit.py` at line 735, Several test functions declare variables that\nare never used (merged, report, adapter), causing unused-variable lint errors;\nupdate those declarations to mark them as intentionally unused by renaming to\nunderscore-prefixed names or discarding them (e.g., use _, _merged, _report or\n_adapter) or assign to a single underscore when only one value is unused;\nspecifically update the call sites such as _three_way_merge_blueprint(old_ref,\nnew_ref, user) to capture unused returns as _merged, _report (or _), and replace\noccurrences of adapter declarations with _adapter (or use del adapter) so\nRuff/F841 and RUF059 violations are resolved while preserving test behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py-340-341 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`340-341`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add `@cpt-*` traceability markers for this changed segment.**\n\nThe re-export change is currently untracked by markers in the bootstrap copy.\n\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines, `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/update.py around\nlines 340 - 341, Add the required `@cpt-`* traceability markers around the\nre-exported symbol to mark this change for traceability: modify the re-export\nline in update.py that references _read_conf_version (the statement \"from .kit\nimport _read_conf_version as _read_conf_version\") to include the appropriate\n`@cpt-`... marker comments before and/or after the line following the project's\nmarker convention so the bootstrap copy is tracked; ensure the marker references\nthe same artifact identifier used elsewhere for kit.py changes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py-36-53 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`36-53`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add `@cpt-*` markers around newly introduced helper/migration blocks.**\n\nThese added sections are not currently traceable via repository marker conventions.\n\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines, `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n\nAlso applies to: 580-1179\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the