ound lines 1164 - 1170, The\ncode calls process_kit(kit_slug, bp_dir, gen_kits_dir, dry_run=False) and\ndiscards the returned _errors, so kit migration can report success despite\nregeneration errors; update the handler around process_kit (the invocation that\nassigns summary, _errors) to capture and propagate or record _errors into the\nmigration result (e.g., add an \"errors\" or \"regeneration_errors\" field alongside\nresult[\"regenerated\"] or set an overall failure flag) and ensure any non-empty\n_errors causes the command to surface failure/status rather than silently\nsucceed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/kit.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1164-1170`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Handle returned `process_kit` errors as migration failures.**\n\nLine 1164 captures `_errors` but ignores them, so a failed regeneration can still be reported as migrated/PASS.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                    summary, _errors = process_kit(\n+                    summary, regen_errors = process_kit(\n                         kit_slug, bp_dir, gen_kits_dir, dry_run=False,\n                     )\n-                    result[\"regenerated\"] = {\n-                        \"files_written\": summary.get(\"files_written\", 0),\n-                        \"artifact_kinds\": summary.get(\"artifact_kinds\", []),\n-                    }\n+                    result[\"regenerated\"] = {\n+                        \"files_written\": summary.get(\"files_written\", 0),\n+                        \"artifact_kinds\": summary.get(\"artifact_kinds\", []),\n+                    }\n+                    if regen_errors:\n+                        result[\"status\"] = \"FAIL\"\n+                        result[\"regenerated\"][\"errors\"] = regen_errors\n+                        print(\n+                            f\"kit-migrate: regen reported errors 