o include the --adapter <path> flag (i.e., python3\n{cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add-inline --name\n<name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path]]), ensuring the command\nlines and surrounding docs reflect these supported options.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 6028a4d","created_at":"2026-02-27T12:11:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T10:25:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2864045534","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2864045534"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2864045534"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2864045534/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":295,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":310,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":47,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2871221335","pull_request_review_id":3874833064,"id":2871221335,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6rI1xX","diff_hunk":"@@ -466,8 +466,94 @@ Syntax highlighting:\n \n ---\n \n+## Workspace Commands (v1.2+)\n+\n+```\n+COMMAND workspace-init\n+SYNOPSIS: cypilot workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--dry-run]\n+DESCRIPTION: Initialize a multi-repo workspace by scanning sibling directories for repos with adapters.\n+\n+OPTIONS:\n+  --root     path   [default: parent of project root]  Directory to scan for sibling repos\n+  --output   path   [default: scan root]  Where to write .cypilot-workspace.json\n+  --inline   boolean  Write workspace inline into current repo's .cypilot-config.json\n+  --dry-run  boolean  Print what would be generated without writing files\n+\n+EXIT CODES:\n+  0  Success (workspace created or dry-run complete)\n+  1  Error (no project root found)\n+\n+EXAMPLE:\n+  $ cypilot workspace-init --dry-run\n+  $ cypilot workspace-init --inline\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+```\n+COMMAND workspace-add\n+SYNOPSIS: cypilot workspace-add --name <name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]\n+DESCRIPTION: Add a source to an existing standalone .cypilot-workspace.json.\n+\n+OPTIONS:\n+  --name     string   required  Human-readable source name\n+  --path     path     required  Path to source repo (relative to workspace file)\n+  --role     string   [default: full]  Source role: artifacts, codebase, kits, full\n+  --adapter  path     Path to adapter dir within source\n+\n+EXIT CODES:\n+  0  Success (source added)\n+  1  Error (no workspace found or save failed)\n+\n+EXAMPLE:\n+  $ cypilot workspace-add --name hyperspot --path ../hyperspot --role full --adapter .cypilot-adapter\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+```\n+COMMAND workspace-add-inline\n+SYNOPSIS: cypilot workspace-add-inline --name <name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]\n+DESCRIPTION: Add a source inline to the current repo's .cypilot-config.json workspace section.\n+\n+OPTIONS:\n+  --name     string   required  Human-readable source name\n+  --path     path     required  Path to source repo (relative to project root)\n+  --role     string   [default: full]  Source role: artifacts, codebase, kits, full\n+  --adapter  path     Path to adapter dir within source\n+\n+EXIT CODES:\n+  0  Success (source added inline)\n+  1  Error (no project root or external workspace ref)\n+\n+EXAMPLE:\n+  $ cypilot workspace-add-inline --name docs --path ../docs-repo --role artifacts\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+```\n+COMMAND workspace-info\n+SYNOPSIS: cypilot workspace-info\n+DESCRIPTION: Display workspace configuration, list sources, show per-source status.\n+\n+EXIT CODES:\n+  0  Success (workspace info displayed, or no workspace found)\n+  1  Error (no project root)\n+\n+EXAMPLE:\n+  $ cypilot workspace-info\n+```","path":".bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/CLISPEC.md","commit_id":"53f02bf53c8ce1e623af29c9a9c1eef2ae425835","original_commit_id":"b795cd63e4747d8cff82916aee4a9c1408946fbf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Normalize workspace command blocks to valid CLISPEC grammar.**\n\nThese command entries diverge from the spec defined earlier in this same document: types should be `<path>/<string>/<boolean>`, and required sections (`ARGUMENTS`, even if empty) should be present. Current formatting can break CLISPEC parsers.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed doc fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n COMMAND workspace-init\n SYNOPSIS: cypilot workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--dry-run]\n DESCRIPTION: Initialize a multi-repo workspace by scanning sibling directories for repos with adapters.\n \n+ARGUMENTS:\n+  (none)\n+\n OPTIONS:\n-  --root     path   [default: parent of project root]  Directory to scan for sibling repos\n-  --output   path   [default: scan root]  Where to write .cypilot-workspace.json\n-  --inline   boolean  Write workspace inline into current repo's .cypilot-config.json\n-  --dry-run  boolean  Print what would be generated without writing files\n+  --root     <path>   [default: parent of project root]  Directory to scan for sibling repos\n+  --output   <path>   [default: scan root]  Where to write .cypilot-workspace.json\n+  --inline   <boolean>  Write workspace inline into current repo's .cypilot-config.json\n+  --dry-run  <boolean>  Print what would be generated without writing files\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/CLISPEC.md around lines 469 - 546, The\ncommand blocks for workspace-init, workspace-add, workspace-add-inline and\nworkspace-info in CLISPEC.md must be normalized to the CLISPEC grammar: replace\noption type words like \"path/string/boolean\" with explicit angle-bracket types\n(<path>, <string>, <boolean>), ensure every COMMAND block includes the required\nARGUMENTS section (use \"ARGUMENTS: (none)\" if there are none), and make OPTIONS\nentries use the exact type tokens (e.g., --path <path>, --name <string>,\n--inline <boolean>) and indicate required/defaults consistently; update the four\ncommand sections (workspace-init, workspace-add, workspace-add-inline,\nworkspace-info) to follow that pattern so CLISPEC parsers can consume them.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->"