fore committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    if not args.local_only:\n        from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\n        if isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext) and ctx.sources and ctx.cross_repo and ctx.resolve_remote_ids:\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 408 - 410,\nThe current conditional lets remote ID expansion run whenever ctx.cross_repo is\ntrue even if the workspace disables remote ID resolution; update the guard in\nthe validate flow so remote expansion only runs when not args.local_only AND\nremote ID resolution is enabled in the workspace config. Edit the conditional\nthat uses WorkspaceContext / ctx.sources / ctx.cross_repo to also check the\nworkspace flag (e.g. ctx.resolve_remote_ids or ctx.sources.resolve_remote_ids\nvia getattr to handle absence) so the whole clause becomes: if not\nargs.local_only and getattr(ctx, \"resolve_remote_ids\", True) and isinstance(ctx,\nWorkspaceContext) and ctx.sources and ctx.cross_repo.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-02T10:32:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T19:52:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2871652971","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2871652971"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2871652971"},"pull_re