e mode.**\n\nAfter the warning at Line 81, the code still goes through the source-filter branch, so non-workspace runs return zero artifacts instead of normal results.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if args.source and not is_workspace:\n             import sys\n             print(f\"Warning: --source filter '{args.source}' ignored (not in workspace mode)\", file=sys.stderr)\n+            args.source = None\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 79 - 86,\nThe warning about \"--source\" being ignored (when is_workspace is False) is\nprinted but the code still enters the else branch and applies the source filter;\nto fix, after printing the warning in the list_ids flow, ensure the code treats\nthe run as if no source was provided — e.g., set args.source = None or jump to\nthe same path used when not args.source so collect_artifacts_to_scan(ctx) is\ninvoked; update the block around the args.source / is_workspace check so that\nwhen is_workspace is False the source-filter branch is not executed and\nartifacts_to_scan is populated via collect_artifacts_to_scan(ctx).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit b456721","created_at":"2026-03-02T11:31:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T20:31:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2871927943","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2871927943"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2871927943"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/c