ions skip `--json`, and they also stop putting it first. An agent following them literally will get human-formatted output instead of the stable JSON required by the Agent-Safe Invocation section above.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--force] [--dry-run]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace init`\n+ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--force] [--dry-run]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace init`\n\n-ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add --name <name> (--path <path> | --url <url>) [--branch <branch>] [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace add <name> <path>` — auto-detects inline workspace and routes accordingly (no `--inline` flag needed when inline workspace already exists)\n+ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-add --name <name> (--path <path> | --url <url>) [--branch <branch>] [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace add <name> <path>` — auto-detects inline workspace and routes accordingly (no `--inline` flag needed when inline workspace already exists)\n\n-ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add --inline --name <name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace add --inline <name> <path>` — forces inline add; Git URL sources not supported in inline mode\n+ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-add --inline --name <name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace add --inline <name> <path>` — forces inline add; Git URL sources not supported in inline mode\n\n-ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-info` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace info`\n+ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-info` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace info`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/SKILL.md around lines 167 - 173, Update the\nworkspace command examples in SKILL.md so they use agent-safe JSON output: add\nthe --json flag (and place it first) to each \"ALWAYS run `python3\n{cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py ...\" invocation\nreferenced (workspace-init, workspace-add variants, and workspace-info) so the\nexamples read like `--json ... workspace-init`, `--json ... workspace-add ...`,\n`--json ... workspace-add --inline ...`, and `--json ... workspace-info`,\nensuring the agent receives stable machine-readable output.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-11T11:58:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T19:53:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2917910950","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2917910950"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2917910950"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2917910950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1"