  artifacts_to_validate.append((artifact_path, template_path, artifact_meta.kind, artifact_meta.traceability, system_node.kit))","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py","commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","original_commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Workspace `validate` still ignores remote source registries for artifact cross-checks.**\n\nThese loops only walk `meta.iter_all_artifacts()` from the primary context. Remote sources are only folded in later via `artifact_ids`, so artifact-to-artifact reference validation still misses definitions that live only in `SourceContext.meta`. Whole-workspace `validate` will keep flagging cross-repo refs unless those remote artifacts are duplicated in the primary registry.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 355-372, 452-456\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py around\nlines 185 - 197, The validate loop only collects artifacts from the primary meta\n(meta.iter_all_artifacts()) and thus misses artifacts that live in remote source\ncontexts; when ctx is a WorkspaceContext, also iterate each source context's\nmeta (e.g., for source_ctx in ctx.get_source_contexts(): for artifact_meta,\nsystem_node in source_ctx.meta.iter_all_artifacts()) and append those resolved\nartifact tuples into artifacts_to_validate using the same resolution logic\n(template_path, artifact_path, artifact_meta.kind, artifact_meta.traceability,\nsystem_node.kit) so cross-repo references from SourceContext.meta are included\nrather than relying solely on artifact_ids later.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-11T12:23:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T19:53:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031671","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031671"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031671"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":185,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":197,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":94,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031675","pull_request_review_id":3929233886,"id":2918031675,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6t7aE7","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,231 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-add: Add a source to workspace config (standalone or inline).\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+\n+import argparse\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import List\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+from ..utils.workspace import WorkspaceConfig\n+\n+\n+def _add_to_standalone(args: argparse.Namespace, ws_cfg: WorkspaceConfig) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Add source to an existing standalone .cypilot-workspace.toml.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-source\n+    replaced = args.name in ws_cfg.sources\n+    ws_cfg.add_source(args.name, args.path, role=args.role, adapter=args.adapter, url=args.url, branch=args.branch)\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-source\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-save\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-update-standalone\n+    save_err = ws_cfg.save()\n+    if save_err:\n+        ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": save_err})\n+        return 1\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-update-standalone\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-save\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-return-ok\n+    source_info: dict = {\n+        \"name\": args.name,\n+        \"path\": args.path,\n+        \"role\": args.role,\n+        \"adapter\": args.adapter,\n+    }\n+    if args.url:\n+        source_info[\"url\"] = args.url\n+    if args.branch:\n+        source_info[\"branch\"] = args.branch\n+    verb = \"updated in\" if replaced else \"added to\"\n+    result: dict = {\n+        \"status\": \"ADDED\",\n+        \"message\": f\"Source '{args.name}' {verb} workspace\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(ws_cfg.workspace_file),\n+        \"source\": source_info,\n+    }\n+    if replaced:\n+        result[\"replaced\"] = True\n+    ui.result(result, human_fn=_human_workspace_add)\n+    return 0\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-add:p1:inst-add-return-ok\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-update-inline\n+def _add_to_inline(args: argparse.Namespace, project_root: Path) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Add source inline to the current repo's config/core.toml.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-update-inline\n+    from ..utils.workspace import _load_inline_config\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    config_path, existing, err = _load_inline_config(project_root)\n+    if err:\n+        ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": err})\n+        return 1\n+\n+    # Get or create inline workspace\n+    ws = existing.get(\"workspace\")\n+    if isinstance(ws, str):\n+        ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": \"Workspace is defined as external file reference. Run without --inline to add to standalone file.\"})\n+        return 1\n+\n+    if ws is not None and not isinstance(ws, dict):\n+        ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Malformed 'workspace' in config: expected table, got {type(ws).__name__}\"})\n+        return 1\n+    if ws is None:\n+        ws = {\"version\": \"1.0\", \"sources\": {}}\n+    if not isinstance(ws.get(\"sources\"), dict):\n+        ws[\"sources\"] = {}","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py","commit_id":"63b1e3edbd685cedf29e15256c45fe0d61839b87","original_commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Don't erase malformed `workspace.sources`.**\n\nThis copy has the same problem as the main command file: a non-table `workspace.sources` value gets replaced with `{}` and then persisted, which can wipe all previously configured sources. Fail fast here instead.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if not isinstance(ws.get(\"sources\"), dict):\n-        ws[\"sources\"] = {}\n+    sources = ws.get(\"sources\")\n+    if sources is None:\n+        ws[\"sources\"] = {}\n+    elif not isinstance(sources, dict):\n+        ui.result({\n+            \"status\": \"ERROR\",\n+            \"message\": f\"Malformed 'workspace.sources' in {config_path}: expected table, got {type(sources).__name__}\",\n+        })\n+        return 1\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py\naround lines 72 - 78, The current code silently replaces a non-dict\nworkspace[\"sources\"] with an empty dict and may wipe persisted sources; modify\nthe checks in workspace_add.py so that after handling ws (the existing workspace\nvariable) you verify if \"sources\" exists and if it is present but not a dict\nthen return an error via ui.result (same error pattern used for malformed\n'workspace') instead of overwriting it; only set ws[\"sources\"] = {} when\n\"sources\" is completely missing (ws.get(\"sources\") is None), keeping the\nui.result call and return value for error cases.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-11T12:23:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T19:53:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031675","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031675"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031675"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031675/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":72,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":78,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031681","pull_request_review_id":3929233886,"id":2918031681,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6t7aFB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,235 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-info: Display workspace configuration and per-source status.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+\n+import argparse\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import List, Optional\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+from ..utils.workspace import WorkspaceConfig\n+\n+\n+def _probe_source_adapter(resolved: Path, explicit_adapter: Optional[Path]) -> Optional[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter directory for a reachable source.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory\n+\n+    found = find_cypilot_directory(resolved)\n+    if found is None and explicit_adapter is not None:\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n+            found = explicit_adapter\n+    return found","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py","commit_id":"63b1e3edbd685cedf29e15256c45fe0d61839b87","original_commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Avoid a second source resolution when probing adapters.**\n\n`resolve_source_adapter(name)` re-runs `resolve_source_path(name)`, so `workspace-info` can clone/fetch URL sources twice per entry. The explicit fallback also checks for `AGENTS.md`, which is stricter than the adapter discovery used by `workspace-init`. Reuse the already-resolved root and validate the explicit adapter by its real config layout instead.\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _probe_source_adapter(resolved: Path, explicit_adapter: Optional[Path]) -> Optional[Path]:\n     \"\"\"Find the adapter directory for a reachable source.\"\"\"\n     from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory\n\n     found = find_cypilot_directory(resolved)\n     if found is None and explicit_adapter is not None:\n-        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"config\").is_dir():\n             found = explicit_adapter\n     return found\n@@\n-    found_adapter = _probe_source_adapter(resolved, ws_cfg.resolve_source_adapter(name))\n+    explicit_adapter = (resolved / src.adapter).resolve() if src.adapter else None\n+    found_adapter = _probe_source_adapter(resolved, explicit_adapter)\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 48-49\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py\naround lines 14 - 22, The current _probe_source_adapter/resolve_source_adapter\nlogic re-resolves sources (calling resolve_source_path) causing double\nclone/fetch and the explicit_adapter fallback checks only for AGENTS.md which is\nstricter than workspace-init; fix by reusing the already-resolved root passed\ninto _probe_source_adapter (do not call resolve_source_path again from\nresolve_source_adapter), run find_cypilot_directory(resolved) on that root, and\nwhen validating explicit_adapter use the same adapter discovery rules as\nworkspace-init (check the real adapter config/layout files used by\nworkspace-init rather than only AGENTS.md) so resolution uses the provided\nresolved Path and consistent adapter validation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 94b7e25 to 63b1e3e","created_at":"2026-03-11T12:23:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T20:14:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031681","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031681"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031681"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":14,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":22,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":22,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031684","pull_request_review_id":3929233886,"id":2918031684,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6t7aFE","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,368 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-init: Initialize a new workspace by scanning nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+\n+import argparse\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+\n+\n+def _is_project_dir(entry: Path) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Check if a directory looks like a project (has .git or AGENTS.md with marker).\"\"\"\n+    if (entry / \".git\").exists():\n+        return True\n+    agents_file = entry / \"AGENTS.md\"\n+    if not agents_file.is_file():\n+        return False\n+    try:\n+        head = agents_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")[:512]\n+        return \"<!-- @cpt:root-agents -->\" in head\n+    except OSError:\n+        return False\n+\n+\n+def _find_adapter_path(entry: Path) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter path for a project directory.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory, _read_cypilot_var\n+\n+    # v3 discovery: read cypilot_path variable from AGENTS.md\n+    cypilot_rel = _read_cypilot_var(entry)\n+    if cypilot_rel:\n+        candidate = (entry / cypilot_rel).resolve()\n+        if candidate.is_dir() and (candidate / \"config\").is_dir():\n+            return cypilot_rel\n+\n+    # Fallback: try find_cypilot_directory for recursive search\n+    found_dir = find_cypilot_directory(entry)\n+    if found_dir is not None:\n+        try:\n+            return str(found_dir.relative_to(entry))\n+        except ValueError:\n+            return str(found_dir)\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _compute_source_path(entry: Path, output_dir: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Compute relative source path from the output location.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        return str(entry.relative_to(output_dir).as_posix())\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return str(entry.as_posix())\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1\n+def _infer_role(repo_path: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Best-effort role inference from directory contents.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    has_src = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"src\", \"lib\", \"app\", \"pkg\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    has_docs = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"docs\", \"architecture\", \"requirements\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+    has_kits = (repo_path / \"kits\").is_dir()\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    if has_kits and not has_src:\n+        return \"kits\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    if has_docs and not has_src:\n+        return \"artifacts\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    if has_src and not has_docs:\n+        return \"codebase\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+    return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1\n+def _scan_nested_repos(\n+    scan_root: Path,\n+    output_dir: Path,\n+) -> Dict[str, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Scan nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\"\"\"\n+    discovered: Dict[str, dict] = {}\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+    try:\n+        entries = sorted(scan_root.iterdir(), key=lambda p: p.name)\n+    except OSError:\n+        entries = []\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+    for entry in entries:\n+        if not entry.is_dir() or entry.name.startswith(\".\"):\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+        if not _is_project_dir(entry):\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+            # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+            continue\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        adapter_path = _find_adapter_path(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        if not adapter_path:\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        info: dict = {\"path\": _compute_source_path(entry, output_dir), \"adapter\": adapter_path}\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        info[\"role\"] = _infer_role(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+        discovered[entry.name] = info\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+    return discovered\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+def _write_inline(\n+    project_root: Path,\n+    workspace_data: dict,\n+) -> Tuple[int, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Write workspace config inline into core.toml. Returns (exit_code, result_dict).\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+    from ..utils.workspace import _load_inline_config\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    config_path, existing, err = _load_inline_config(project_root)\n+    if err:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": err}\n+\n+    existing[\"workspace\"] = workspace_data\n+    try:\n+        toml_utils.dump(existing, config_path)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Failed to write workspace to {config_path}: {e}\"}\n+\n+    return 0, {\n+        \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n+        \"message\": \"Workspace added inline to core.toml\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(config_path),\n+        \"sources_count\": len(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {})),\n+        \"sources\": list(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {}).keys()),\n+    }\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-standalone\n+def _write_standalone(\n+    output_path: Path,\n+    workspace_data: dict,\n+) -> Tuple[int, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Write standalone .cypilot-workspace.toml. Returns (exit_code, result_dict).\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-standalone\n+    from ..constants import WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    if output_path.is_dir():\n+        output_path = output_path / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+\n+    try:\n+        toml_utils.dump(workspace_data, output_path)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Failed to write workspace config to {output_path}: {e}\"}\n+\n+    return 0, {\n+        \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n+        \"message\": f\"Workspace config created at {output_path}\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(output_path),\n+        \"sources_count\": len(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {})),\n+        \"sources\": list(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {}).keys()),\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def _resolve_output_dir(args: argparse.Namespace, scan_root: Path, project_root: Path) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"Compute the output directory used for relative path computation.\"\"\"\n+    if args.inline:\n+        return project_root\n+    if args.output:\n+        _out_resolved = Path(args.output).resolve()\n+        return _out_resolved if _out_resolved.is_dir() else _out_resolved.parent\n+    return scan_root\n+\n+\n+def _check_existing_workspace(project_root: Path, *, inline: bool, force: bool) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Check for existing workspace config conflicts. Returns error message or None.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.workspace import find_workspace_config as _find_ws\n+\n+    existing_ws, _ = _find_ws(project_root)\n+    if existing_ws is None:\n+        return None","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Don't treat parse failures as “no workspace”.**\n\n`find_workspace_config()` returns `(None, error)` for malformed inline/standalone configs. Ignoring that here lets `workspace-init` overwrite a broken config without surfacing the problem first.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py\naround lines 200 - 206, The helper _check_existing_workspace currently ignores\nparse failures from find_workspace_config (imported as _find_ws) and treats a\nreturned (None, error) as \"no workspace\"; change it to inspect the second tuple\nelement and, if an error is present, return that error string (or a wrapped\ndescriptive message) instead of None so workspace-init won't overwrite a\nmalformed inline/standalone config; update logic around existing_ws and the\nerror tuple returned by _find_ws to short-circuit on parse errors and surface\nthem to the caller.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-11T12:23:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T19:53:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031684","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031684"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918031684"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":259,"original_start_line":200,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":267,"original_line":206,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":206,"position":267,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918031690","pull_request_review_id":3929233886,"id":2918031690,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6t7aFK","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,368 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-init: Initialize a new workspace by scanning nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+\n+import argparse\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+\n+\n+def _is_project_dir(entry: Path) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Check if a directory looks like a project (has .git or AGENTS.md with marker).\"\"\"\n+    if (entry / \".git\").exists():\n+        return True\n+    agents_file = entry / \"AGENTS.md\"\n+    if not agents_file.is_file():\n+        return False\n+    try:\n+        head = agents_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")[:512]\n+        return \"<!-- @cpt:root-agents -->\" in head\n+    except OSError:\n+        return False\n+\n+\n+def _find_adapter_path(entry: Path) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter path for a project directory.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory, _read_cypilot_var\n+\n+    # v3 discovery: read cypilot_path variable from AGENTS.md\n+    cypilot_rel = _read_cypilot_var(entry)\n+    if cypilot_rel:\n+        candidate = (entry / cypilot_rel).resolve()\n+        if candidate.is_dir() and (candidate / \"config\").is_dir():\n+            return cypilot_rel\n+\n+    # Fallback: try find_cypilot_directory for recursive search\n+    found_dir = find_cypilot_directory(entry)\n+    if found_dir is not None:\n+        try:\n+            return str(found_dir.relative_to(entry))\n+        except ValueError:\n+            return str(found_dir)\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _compute_source_path(entry: Path, output_dir: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Compute relative source path from the output location.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        return str(entry.relative_to(output_dir).as_posix())\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return str(entry.as_posix())\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1\n+def _infer_role(repo_path: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Best-effort role inference from directory contents.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    has_src = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"src\", \"lib\", \"app\", \"pkg\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    has_docs = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"docs\", \"architecture\", \"requirements\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+    has_kits = (repo_path / \"kits\").is_dir()\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    if has_kits and not has_src:\n+        return \"kits\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    if has_docs and not has_src:\n+        return \"artifacts\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    if has_src and not has_docs:\n+        return \"codebase\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+    return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1\n+def _scan_nested_repos(\n+    scan_root: Path,\n+    output_dir: Path,\n+) -> Dict[str, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Scan nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\"\"\"\n+    discovered: Dict[str, dict] = {}\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+    try:\n+        entries = sorted(scan_root.iterdir(), key=lambda p: p.name)\n+    except OSError:\n+        entries = []\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+    for entry in entries:\n+        if not entry.is_dir() or entry.name.startswith(\".\"):\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+        if not _is_project_dir(entry):\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+            # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+            continue\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        adapter_path = _find_adapter_path(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        if not adapter_path:\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        info: dict = {\"path\": _compute_source_path(entry, output_dir), \"adapter\": adapter_path}\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        info[\"role\"] = _infer_role(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+        discovered[entry.name] = info\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+    return discovered\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+def _write_inline(\n+    project_root: Path,\n+    workspace_data: dict,\n+) -> Tuple[int, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Write workspace config inline into core.toml. Returns (exit_code, result_dict).\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+    from ..utils.workspace import _load_inline_config\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    config_path, existing, err = _load_inline_config(project_root)\n+    if err:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": err}\n+\n+    existing[\"workspace\"] = workspace_data\n+    try:\n+        toml_utils.dump(existing, config_path)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Failed to write workspace to {config_path}: {e}\"}\n+\n+    return 0, {\n+        \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n+        \"message\": \"Workspace added inline to core.toml\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(config_path),\n+        \"sources_count\": len(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {})),\n+        \"sources\": list(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {}).keys()),\n+    }\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-standalone\n+def _write_standalone(\n+    output_path: Path,\n+    workspace_data: dict,\n+) -> Tuple[int, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Write standalone .cypilot-workspace.toml. Returns (exit_code, result_dict).\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-standalone\n+    from ..constants import WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    if output_path.is_dir():\n+        output_path = output_path / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+\n+    try:\n+        toml_utils.dump(workspace_data, output_path)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Failed to write workspace config to {output_path}: {e}\"}\n+\n+    return 0, {\n+        \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n+        \"message\": f\"Workspace config created at {output_path}\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(output_path),\n+        \"sources_count\": len(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {})),\n+        \"sources\": list(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {}).keys()),\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def _resolve_output_dir(args: argparse.Namespace, scan_root: Path, project_root: Path) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"Compute the output directory used for relative path computation.\"\"\"\n+    if args.inline:\n+        return project_root\n+    if args.output:\n+        _out_resolved = Path(args.output).resolve()\n+        return _out_resolved if _out_resolved.is_dir() else _out_resolved.parent\n+    return scan_root\n+\n+\n+def _check_existing_workspace(project_root: Path, *, inline: bool, force: bool) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Check for existing workspace config conflicts. Returns error message or None.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.workspace import find_workspace_config as _find_ws\n+\n+    existing_ws, _ = _find_ws(project_root)\n+    if existing_ws is None:\n+        return None\n+\n+    if inline and not existing_ws.is_inline:\n+        return (\n+            f\"Standalone workspace already exists at {existing_ws.workspace_file}. \"\n+            \"Cannot create inline workspace — this would create parallel configs. \"\n+            \"Delete the standalone file first, then retry with --inline.\"\n+        )\n+    if not inline and existing_ws.is_inline:\n+        return (\n+            \"Inline workspace already exists in core.toml. \"\n+            \"Cannot create standalone workspace — this would create parallel configs. \"\n+            \"Remove the [workspace] section from core.toml first, then retry.\"\n+        )\n+    if not force:\n+        config_loc = \"core.toml\" if existing_ws.is_inline else str(existing_ws.workspace_file)\n+        return (\n+            f\"Workspace already exists ({config_loc}). \"\n+            \"Use --force to reinitialize (this will overwrite existing workspace config).\"\n+        )\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-flow:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-init:p1\n+# @cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-init:p1\n+def cmd_workspace_init(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Initialize a multi-repo workspace.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-init:p1:inst-user-workspace-init\n+    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n+        prog=\"workspace-init\",\n+        description=\"Initialize a new workspace: scan nested sub-dirs for repos with adapters, generate .cypilot-workspace.toml\",\n+    )\n+    p.add_argument(\n+        \"--root\", default=None,\n+        help=\"Directory to scan for nested repo sub-dirs (default: current project root)\",\n+    )\n+    p.add_argument(\n+        \"--output\", default=None,\n+        help=\"Where to write .cypilot-workspace.toml (default: scan root)\",\n+    )","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"bbd9d67bfb716d0d6a2f03b0f3a46917a407740e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Non-default `--output` paths are never wired into discovery.**\n\nIf the standalone file is written anywhere except `{project_root}/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, later commands will not find it unless `core.toml` gets a `workspace = \"...\"` pointer. Right now this writes the file and returns `CREATED`, but the workspace stays undiscoverable. Based on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` only auto-discovers standalone workspace files at `project_root`; any other location must be referenced via the `workspace` key in `core.toml`.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 321-322\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eaf5018","created_at":"2026-03-11T12:23:32Z","updat