mote Git repository URL, an optional branch or ref, and namespace resolution rules that map the URL to a local working directory path (e.g., `gitlab.com/org/project.git` → `org/project`). The workspace MUST support a configurable working directory (defaulting to the current directory) under which cloned repos are resolved via namespace rules. Git URL sources MUST NOT be supported in inline workspace configuration (`config/core.toml`) — inline mode remains local-paths-only. The system MUST clone or fetch sources as needed and cache them locally. Branch configuration MUST allow workspace-level defaults and per-source overrides.","path":"architecture/PRD.md","commit_id":"b456721ad17005d5a2044968932b3bf30224e561","original_commit_id":"b456721ad17005d5a2044968932b3bf30224e561","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, thanks for the confirmation! I'll keep an eye out for that fix in the next PR. Just to make sure it's captured clearly: the PRD line currently reads \"defaulting to the current directory\" and should be updated to \"defaulting to `.workspace-sources`\" to match the `ResolveConfig` default in the code.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:06.396Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py:93-96\nTimestamp: 2026-03-09T12:52:43.966Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`, the `try/except OSError` around `scan_root.iterdir()` in `_scan_nested_repos` (around lines 93–96) intentionally swallows the error and falls back to `entries = []`. This is by design for graceful degradation: an inaccessible scan root is treated as \"no sources found\" rather than a hard ERROR. Do not flag this as a bug or suggest propagating the OSError.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-11T14:27:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T14:27:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918737807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918737807"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2918737807"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918737807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":344,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":348,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2907856911,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2918742749","pull_request_review_id":3930020317,"id":2918742749,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6t-Hrd","diff_hunk":"@@ -336,6 +337,23 @@ The system MUST provide a unique ID system for all design elements using structu\n **Actors**:\n `cpt-cypilot-actor-user`, `cpt-cypilot-actor-ai-agent`, `cpt-cypilot-actor-ci-pipeline`\n \n+#### Multi-Repo Workspace Federation\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`\n+\n+The system MUST support multi-repo workspace federation — discovering repositories in nested sub-directories, configuring sources, and enabling cross-repo artifact traceability without merging adapters. Workspace configuration MUST support two modes: standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` file and inline `[workspace]` section in `config/core.toml`. The system MUST discover workspace config by first checking the project's `core.toml` for a `workspace` key (string path or inline dict), then falling back to well-known standalone file `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at the project root — no implicit parent directory traversal. Each named source MUST map to a local filesystem path with optional adapter location and role (`artifacts`, `codebase`, `kits`, `full`). Source path resolution MUST be relative to the workspace file's parent directory (standalone) or project root (inline). The system MUST provide CLI commands: `workspace-init` (scan nested sub-directories for repos with `.git` or `AGENTS.md` marker, infer roles, generate config), `workspace-add` with `--inline` flag (add sources to standalone or inline config), `workspace-info` (display workspace status with per-source reachability). Cross-repo traceability MUST be controllable via `cross_repo` and `resolve_remote_ids` settings. The system MUST provide `--local-only` flag for `validate` to skip cross-repo resolution, and `--source` filter for `list-ids`. The system MUST degrade gracefully when sources are unreachable — emit warnings to stderr and continue with available sources. The system MUST be fully backward compatible — projects without workspace config operate in single-repo mode with zero behavioral changes.\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace-git-sources`\n+\n+The system MUST support Git URL sources in standalone workspace configuration (`.cypilot-workspace.toml`). Each Git URL source MUST specify: a remote Git repository URL, an optional branch or ref, and namespace resolution rules that map the URL to a local working directory path (e.g., `gitlab.com/org/project.git` → `org/project`). The workspace MUST support a configurable working directory (defaulting to the current directory) under which cloned repos are resolved via namespace rules. Git URL sources MUST NOT be supported in inline workspace configuration (`config/core.toml`) — inline mode remains local-paths-only. The system MUST clone or fetch sources as needed and cache them locally. Branch configuration MUST allow workspace-level defaults and per-source overrides.","path":"architecture/PRD.md","commit_id":"b456721ad17005d5a2044968932b3bf30224e561","original_commit_id":"b456721ad17005d5a2044968932b3bf30224e561","user":{"login":"nonameffh",