_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--source` enforcement is incomplete for primary-context matches.**\n\nLines 199–205 only reject mismatches when `matched_sc` is not `None`. If the artifact resolves to primary, validation can proceed outside the selected source.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🎯 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if ws_ctx is not None:\n+            selected_root = getattr(ctx, \"project_root\", None) if args.source else None\n             matched_sc, matched_ctx = determine_target_source(artifact_path, ws_ctx)\n             if matched_ctx is None:\n                 ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Cannot resolve context for artifact: {artifact_path}\"})\n                 return 1\n-            if args.source and matched_sc is not None and matched_sc.name != args.source:\n-                ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": (\n-                    f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{matched_sc.name}', \"\n-                    f\"not '{args.source}'.\"\n-                )})\n-                return 1\n+            if args.source:\n+                if selected_root is None or getattr(matched_ctx, \"project_root\", None) != selected_root:\n+                    actual = matched_sc.name if matched_sc is not None else \"primary\"\n+                    ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": (\n+                        f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{actual}', \"\n+                        f\"not '{args.source}'.\"\n+                    )})\n+                    return 1\n             ctx = matched_ctx\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 194 - 205,\nThe code only enforces args.source when matched_sc is not None, allowing\nartifacts that resolve to the workspace primary context to bypass --source;\nupdate the check after determine_target_source to enforce --source for both\nexplicit and primary matches by: if args.source is set then compute the\neffective source name (use matched_sc.name when matched_sc is not None,\notherwise use the workspace primary source name via ws_ctx.primary_source.name\nor equivalent) and compare it to args.source, returning the same error when they\ndiffer; keep the existing ui.result error message and the ctx = matched_ctx\nassignment unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T10:45:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T10:45:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935108881","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935108881"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935108881"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935108881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":194,"original_start_line":194,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":205,"original_line":205,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":135,"position":135,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935108882","pull_request_review_id":3948636542,"id":2935108882,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u8jUS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,271 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-add: Add a source to workspace config (standalone or inline).\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+\n+import argparse\n+import re\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import List\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+from ..utils.workspace import WorkspaceConfig\n+\n+# SCP-style SSH: git@host:org/repo or user@host:path\n+_SCP_SSH_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+@[A-Za-z0-9._-]+:.+\")\n+\n+\n+def _is_scp_style_ssh(url: str) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Return True if *url* looks like an SCP-style SSH remote (git@host:path).\"\"\"\n+    return _SCP_SSH_RE.match(url) is not None\n+\n+\n+def _validate_add_args(args: argparse.Namespace) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"Validate parsed workspace-add args. Return error message or None.\"\"\"\n+    if args.inline and args.url:\n+        return \"Git URL sources are not supported in inline workspace config. Remove --inline to add to a standalone workspace file.\"\n+    if args.branch and args.path:\n+        return \"--branch is only valid with --url sources. Path sources do not use branch.\"\n+    if args.url:\n+        url = args.url\n+        if not (url.startswith(\"https://\") or url.startswith(\"ssh://\") or _is_scp_style_ssh(url)):\n+            return \"Unsupported URL scheme — only HTTPS and SSH are allowed.\"\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _resolve_inline_workspace(existing: dict) -> tuple[dict, str | None]:\n+    \"\"\"Validate and return the inline workspace dict from a parsed core.toml.\n+\n+    Returns (workspace_dict, None) on success or ({}, error_message) on failure.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    ws = existing.get(\"workspace\")\n+    if isinstance(ws, str):\n+        return {}, \"Workspace is defined as external file reference. Run without --inline to add to standalone file.\"\n+    if ws is not None and not isinstance(ws, dict):\n+        return {}, f\"Malformed 'workspace' in config: expected table, got {type(ws).__name__}\"\n+    if ws is None:\n+        ws = {\"version\": \"1.0\", \"sources\": {}}\n+    sources = ws.get(\"sources\")\n+    if sources is not None and not isinstance(sources, dict):\n+        return {}, f\"Malformed 'workspace.sources' in config: expected table, got {type(sources).__name__}\"\n+    if sources is None:\n+        ws[\"sources\"] = {}\n+    return ws, None\n+\n+\n+def _emit_add_result(args: argparse.Namespace, replaced: bool, config_path: str, message: str) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Build and emit the workspace-add result dict.\"\"\"\n+    source_info: dict = {\"name\": args.name, \"role\": args.role}\n+    if args.path:\n+        source_info[\"path\"] = args.path\n+    if args.adapter:\n+        source_info[\"adapter\"] = args.adapter\n+    url = getattr(args, \"url\", None)\n+    if url:\n+        source_info[\"url\"] = url","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py","commit_id":"df262014f90b54c41e1e1689de3aeca14ca0cd39","original_commit_id":"0cedd3e652071742f6515aae6d74dbba9b7307f2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Redact Git credentials before echoing the source URL.**\n\n`args.url` is copied straight into the result payload here, so `workspace-add --url https://user:token@host/repo.git` leaks credentials in both JSON output and the human formatter. Keep the raw URL in persisted config, but only emit a redacted form from this response path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py` around lines 63 -\n65, The code copies args.url directly into source_info which can leak embedded\nGit credentials; instead, keep the raw URL in the persisted config but emit a\nredacted version in the response: parse args.url (e.g. with\nurllib.parse.urlparse), strip or replace urlparse.username and urlparse.password\nwith placeholders, rebuild a redacted_url and assign source_info[\"url\"] =\nredacted_url for the output path, while storing the original args.url only in\nthe persisted config/save routine used by the workspace-add command.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits ea38fb8 to 76e1b86","created_at":"2026-03-14T10:45:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T17:45:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935108882","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935108882"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935108882"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935108882/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":63,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"origi