ce_init.py\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot\n\nLength of output: 1600\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg \"try|except\" skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot\n\nLength of output: 920\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py | sed -n '140,165p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot\n\nLength of output: 1848\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py | sed -n '165,180p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot\n\nLength of output: 1223\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py | sed -n '100,145p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot\n\nLength of output: 2082\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Guard `os.path.relpath()` for cross-drive Windows paths.**\n\nLine 167 calls `_compute_source_path(entry, output_dir)` without error handling. On Windows, `os.path.relpath()` raises `ValueError` when `entry` and `output_dir` are on different drives (e.g., `workspace-init --output D:\\...` scanning a repo on `C:`), crashing before discovery completes. Wrap the call in a try/except to fall back to an absolute POSIX path when relative computation fails.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 50 -\n52, _os.path.relpath() can raise ValueError on cross-drive Windows paths causing\n_compute_source_path to crash; update the _compute_source_path(entry: Path,\noutput_dir: Path) function to catch ValueError from os.path.relpath(entry,\noutput_dir) and in the except branch return the absolute POSIX path (e.g.,\nentry.resolve().as_posix() or Path(entry).as_posix()) so callers of\n_compute_source_path won't fail when entry 