ata)\n     if output_arg and exit_code == 0:\n-        rel = output_path.relative_to(project_root) if output_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else output_path\n+        written_path = Path(data[\"config_path\"])\n+        rel = written_path.relative_to(project_root) if written_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else written_path\n         data[\"hint\"] = (\n             f\"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n             f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n         )\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 304 -\n310, The hint currently suggests the directory when --output points to a\ndirectory, but _write_standalone actually writes WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\ninside that directory; update the logic around output_path and the hint so it\nuses the actual manifest file path (e.g. compute manifest_path = output_path if\noutput_arg points to a file else output_path / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME prior\nto calling _write_standalone, or derive the written file path from the value\nreturned by _write_standalone) and then build rel =\nmanifest_path.relative_to(project_root) (or leave manifest_path) so data[\"hint\"]\npoints to the real written file; adjust references to output_path/manifest_path\nand keep WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME, _write_standalone, output_arg, project_root\nand scan_root in mind.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits ea38fb8 to 890e99b","created_at":"2026-03-14T10:45:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T10:47:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935108885","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/