5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, you're correct — I apologize for the noise. Looking at the full file content, the `@cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-core-infra-route-command:p1:inst-route-helpers` marker opens at the top of the file (before the imports) and the matching `@cpt-end` closes after `_cmd_workspace_sync`. The new workspace helpers are already within that block and are fully covered by the existing `inst-route-helpers` traceability marker. My suggestion was mistaken.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Applies to **/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php,rs,kt,swift,scala} : Use cpt-* markers for establishing code↔artifact traceability\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: ainetx\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 102\nFile: tests/test_resolve_vars.py:1-693\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T10:25:53.450Z\nLearning: In the cyberfabric/cyber-pilot repository, `cpt-*` trace markers are NOT added to test files. The annotation convention applies only to production source files (e.g., `*.py`, `*.ts`, etc.), not to test suites.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T11:08:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T11:08:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935127249","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935127249"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935127249"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.gi