lse},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Use error-level rendering for `status == \"ERROR\"`.**\n\nThis path currently prints as a warning, even though command status and exit code are errors.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        ui.warn(f\"Error: {data.get('message', 'unknown error')}\")\n+        ui.error(f\"Error: {data.get('message', 'unknown error')}\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    if status == \"ERROR\":\n        ui.header(\"Where Defined\")\n        ui.blank()\n        ui.error(f\"Error: {data.get('message', 'unknown error')}\")\n        ui.blank()\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py` around lines 66 -\n70, The error branch currently renders errors as warnings; update the status ==\n\"ERROR\" path in where_defined.py to use the UI's error-level renderer (replace\nui.warn(...) with ui.error(...)) so the message is shown as an error; also\nensure the surrounding block in the same function that sets status/exit behavior\npreserves returning or exiting with a non-zero code when status is \"ERROR\" so\noutput and exit semantics remain error-level.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 68de967","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:30:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616387","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616387"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616387"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":66,"original_start_line":66,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":70,"original_line":70,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":119,"position":119,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616392","pull_request_review_id":3949119923,"id":2935616392,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-fOI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,253 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-info: Display workspace configuration and per-source status.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-info:p1:inst-info-helpers\n+import argparse\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import List, Optional\n+\n+from ..utils.git_utils import _redact_url\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+from ..utils.workspace import WorkspaceConfig\n+\n+\n+def _probe_source_adapter(resolved: Path, explicit_adapter: Optional[Path]) -> Optional[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter directory for a reachable source.\n+\n+    Prioritizes the explicit adapter path from workspace config over\n+    auto-discovery to avoid finding a wrong nested adapter.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if explicit_adapter is not None:\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n+            return explicit_adapter\n+        return None  # explicit path declared but invalid","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Use the same explicit-adapter validity check as workspace discovery.**\n\n`workspace-init` records an adapter as soon as the directory exists and contains `config/`, but this branch only accepts an explicit adapter when it has a top-level `AGENTS.md`. A source discovered by `workspace-init` can therefore show `adapter_found: false` and lose artifact/system counts in `workspace-info` unless that extra file happens to exist.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 21 -\n24, The explicit-adapter branch in workspace_info.py currently accepts only\nadapters containing a top-level \"AGENTS.md\", causing mismatch with workspace\ndiscovery; change the validity check for explicit_adapter to mirror\nworkspace-init by testing that explicit_adapter.is_dir() and that\nexplicit_adapter / \"config\" is a directory (or exists) instead of checking for\n\"AGENTS.md\", keeping the same return behavior when invalid so workspace-info\nreports adapter_found consistently and preserves artifact/system counts.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 68de967","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:30:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616392","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616392"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616392"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":21,"original_start_line":21,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":24,"original_line":24,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":24,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616393","pull_request_review_id":3949119923,"id":2935616393,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-fOJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,463 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-init: Initialize a new workspace by scanning nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-helpers\n+import argparse\n+import os\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+\n+\n+def _is_project_dir(entry: Path) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Check if a directory looks like a project (has .git or AGENTS.md with marker).\"\"\"\n+    if (entry / \".git\").exists():\n+        return True\n+    agents_file = entry / \"AGENTS.md\"\n+    if not agents_file.is_file():\n+        return False\n+    try:\n+        head = agents_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")[:512]\n+        return \"<!-- @cpt:root-agents -->\" in head\n+    except OSError:\n+        return False\n+\n+\n+def _find_adapter_path(entry: Path) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter path for a project directory.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory, _read_cypilot_var\n+\n+    # v3 discovery: read cypilot_path variable from AGENTS.md\n+    cypilot_rel = _read_cypilot_var(entry)\n+    if cypilot_rel:\n+        candidate = (entry / cypilot_rel).resolve()\n+        if candidate.is_dir() and (candidate / \"config\").is_dir():\n+            return cypilot_rel\n+\n+    # Fallback: try find_cypilot_directory for recursive search\n+    found_dir = find_cypilot_directory(entry)\n+    if found_dir is not None:\n+        try:\n+            return str(found_dir.relative_to(entry))\n+        except ValueError:\n+            return str(found_dir)\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _compute_source_path(entry: Path, output_dir: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Compute relative source path from the output location.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        return Path(os.path.relpath(entry, output_dir)).as_posix()\n+    except ValueError:\n+        # Windows: entry and output_dir are on different drives\n+        return entry.resolve().as_posix()\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-helpers\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1\n+def _infer_role(repo_path: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Best-effort role inference from directory contents.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    has_src = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"src\", \"lib\", \"app\", \"pkg\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    has_docs = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"docs\", \"architecture\", \"requirements\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+    has_kits = (repo_path / \"kits\").is_dir()\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-multi\n+    capabilities = sum((has_src, has_docs, has_kits))\n+    if capabilities > 1:\n+        return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-multi\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    if has_kits:\n+        return \"kits\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    if has_docs:\n+        return \"artifacts\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    if has_src:\n+        return \"codebase\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+    return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+\n+\n+def _sanitize_source_name(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Sanitize an auto-discovered source name to safe characters.\"\"\"\n+    import re\n+    # Replace unsafe characters with hyphens\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]\", \"-\", name)\n+    # Strip leading non-alphanumeric characters\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"^[^A-Za-z0-9]+\", \"\", sanitized)\n+    # Collapse consecutive hyphens\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"-{2,}\", \"-\", sanitized)\n+    return sanitized or \"source\"\n+\n+\n+def _dedup_source_key(key: str, existing: Dict[str, dict], new_path: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Return a unique source key, warning on collision.\"\"\"\n+    key = _sanitize_source_name(key)\n+    if key not in existing:\n+        return key\n+    n = 2\n+    while f\"{key}-{n}\" in existing:\n+        n += 1\n+    new_key = f\"{key}-{n}\"\n+    print(\n+        f\"Warning: source name '{key}' collision — \"\n+        f\"'{new_path}' conflicts with '{existing[key].get('path', '?')}'; \"\n+        f\"renaming to '{new_key}'\",\n+        file=sys.stderr,\n+    )\n+    return new_key\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1\n+def _scan_nested_repos(\n+    scan_root: Path,\n+    output_dir: Path,\n+    max_depth: int = 3,\n+    _current_depth: int = 1,\n+) -> Dict[str, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Scan nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\"\"\"\n+    discovered: Dict[str, dict] = {}\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-depth\n+    if _current_depth > max_depth:\n+        return discovered\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-depth\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+    try:\n+        entries = sorted(scan_root.iterdir(), key=lambda p: p.name)\n+    except OSError as exc:\n+        print(f\"Warning: cannot scan {scan_root}: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        entries = []\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+    for entry in entries:\n+        if not entry.is_dir() or entry.name.startswith(\".\") or entry.is_symlink():\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+        if not _is_project_dir(entry):\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+            # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+            # Not a project — recurse into subdirectory\n+            nested = _scan_nested_repos(entry, output_dir, max_depth, _current_depth + 1)\n+            for nkey, ninfo in nested.items():\n+                nkey = _dedup_source_key(nkey, discovered, ninfo.get(\"path\", \"?\"))\n+                discovered[nkey] = ninfo\n+            continue\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        adapter_path = _find_adapter_path(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        if not adapter_path:\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        info: dict = {\"path\": _compute_source_path(entry, output_dir), \"adapter\": adapter_path}\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-compute-path\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        info[\"role\"] = _infer_role(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-infer-role\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+        key = _dedup_source_key(entry.name, discovered, info.get(\"path\", \"?\"))\n+        discovered[key] = info\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-add-source\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+    return discovered\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-return\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+def _write_inline(\n+    project_root: Path,\n+    workspace_data: dict,\n+) -> Tuple[int, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Write workspace config inline into core.toml. Returns (exit_code, result_dict).\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-create-inline\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-init:p1:inst-write-inline-impl\n+    from ..utils.workspace import load_inline_config\n+    from ..utils import toml_utils\n+\n+    config_path, existing, err = load_inline_config(project_root)\n+    if err:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": err}\n+\n+    existing[\"workspace\"] = workspace_data\n+    try:\n+        toml_utils.dump(existing, config_path)\n+    except OSError as e:\n+        return 1, {\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Failed to write workspace to {config_path}: {e}\"}\n+\n+    return 0, {\n+        \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n+        \"message\": \"Workspace added inline to core.toml\",\n+        \"config_path\": str(config_path),\n+        \"sources_count\": len(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {})),\n+        \"sources\": list(workspace_data.get(\"sources\", {}).keys()),\n+    }","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Don't fabricate type/source details from a partial `CREATED` payload.**\n\n`_write_inline()` doesn't set `is_inline`, and neither write path includes `workspace.sources`. `_human_workspace_init()` therefore prints `Type: standalone` for `workspace-init --inline`, and every created source falls back to `(full)` with an empty path. Either include those fields in the `CREATED` payload or make the formatter show only source names when full metadata is absent.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 236-242, 426-448\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 207 -\n213, The CREATED payload returned by _write_inline() is missing fields like\nis_inline and workspace.sources, causing _human_workspace_init() to misrender\ntype and source paths; fix by either (A) updating _write_inline() to populate\nthe returned dict with \"is_inline\": True and include a minimal \"workspace\":\n{\"sources\": {<name>: {\"type\": ..., \"path\": ...} }} (only include type/path when\navailable) so downstream formatting has metadata, or (B) modify\n_human_workspace_init() to defensively detect missing workspace/sources metadata\nand only display source names (omit type/path or show a placeholder) when those\nfields are absent; reference the CREATED payload, _write_inline(), and\n_human_workspace_init() when making the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 68de967","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:30:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616393","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616393"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616393"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":207,"original_start_line":207,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":214,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":213,"position":214,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616396","pull_request_review_id":3949119923,"id":2935616396,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-fOM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,352 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+Git utilities for workspace source resolution.\n+\n+Handles parsing Git URLs, namespace mapping, clone operations,\n+and explicit sync operations using subprocess (stdlib-only constraint).\n+\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-sync-git-source:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-git-url-sources:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-sync:p1\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+import re\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+if TYPE_CHECKING:\n+    from .workspace import NamespaceRule, ResolveConfig, SourceEntry\n+\n+# Patterns for parsing Git URLs\n+# HTTPS: https://gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_HTTPS_RE = re.compile(r\"^https://([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH shorthand: git@gitlab.com:org/repo.git\n+_SSH_SHORT_RE = re.compile(r\"^[\\w.-]+@([^:]+):(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH URL: ssh://git@gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_SSH_URL_RE = re.compile(r\"^ssh://[\\w.-]+@([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+\n+_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120  # seconds\n+\n+\n+def _redact_url(url: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Strip credentials from a Git URL before displaying it.\"\"\"\n+    # SCP-style SSH: user@host:path — redact the user part\n+    if \"://\" not in url and \"@\" in url and \":\" in url:\n+        at_idx = url.index(\"@\")\n+        return f\"***{url[at_idx:]}\"\n+    # Standard URLs: https://user:pass@host/path\n+    from urllib.parse import urlsplit, urlunsplit\n+    parts = urlsplit(url)\n+    if parts.username or parts.password:\n+        netloc = parts.hostname or \"\"\n+        if parts.port:\n+            netloc += f\":{parts.port}\"\n+        return urlunsplit((parts.scheme, netloc, parts.path, parts.query, parts.fragment))\n+    return url\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+def _parse_git_url(url: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, str, str]]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse a Git URL into (host, org, repo) components.\n+\n+    Supports HTTPS, SSH shorthand (git@host:path), and ssh:// URLs.\n+    Returns None if the URL cannot be parsed.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    for pattern in (_HTTPS_RE, _SSH_URL_RE, _SSH_SHORT_RE):\n+        m = pattern.match(url.strip())\n+        if m:\n+            host = m.group(1)\n+            path_part = m.group(2).strip(\"/\")\n+            # Split path into org (everything before last /) and repo (last segment)\n+            parts = path_part.rsplit(\"/\", 1)\n+            if len(parts) == 2:\n+                return (host, parts[0], parts[1])\n+            # Single segment: no org, just repo\n+            return (host, \"\", parts[0])\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+def _lookup_namespace(host: str, rules: list) -> \"Optional[NamespaceRule]\":\n+    \"\"\"Find a namespace rule matching the given host by exact match.\"\"\"\n+    for rule in rules:\n+        if rule.host == host:\n+            return rule\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+def _apply_template(template: str, org: str, repo: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Apply {org}/{repo} substitution to a namespace template.\n+\n+    Raises ValueError if the result is an absolute path or contains '..'\n+    segments that could escape the workspace directory.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    result = template.replace(\"{org}\", org).replace(\"{repo}\", repo)\n+    # Strip leading slash that appears when org is empty (\"{org}/{repo}\" → \"/repo\")\n+    result = result.lstrip(\"/\")\n+    # Reject path traversal: absolute paths or \"..\" segments\n+    if not result or result.startswith(\"/\") or \"..\" in Path(result).parts:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Unsafe path template result: {result!r}\")\n+    return result\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-clone-or-fetch\n+def _clone_if_missing(url: str, local_path: Path, branch: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Clone a git repo or return existing local path.\n+\n+    For existing repos, returns local_path without network operations.\n+    Use sync_git_source() to fetch and update worktrees explicitly.\n+    Returns local_path on success, None on clone failure.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if _parse_git_url(url) is None:\n+        print(f\"Warning: refusing to clone unrecognized URL: {_redact_url(url)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    if local_path.is_dir() and (local_path / \".git\").exists():\n+        return local_path\n+    # Clone\n+    clone_args = [\"clone\", \"--quiet\"]\n+    if branch != \"HEAD\":\n+        clone_args.extend([\"--branch\", branch])\n+    clone_args.extend([url, str(local_path)])\n+    rc, _out, err = _run_git(clone_args)\n+    if rc != 0:\n+        print(f\"Warning: git clone failed for {_redact_url(url)}: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    return local_path","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Verify `origin` before reusing an existing checkout.**\n\n`_clone_if_missing()` accepts any existing `.git` directory at `local_path` as the requested source. With the default `{org}/{repo}` mapping, two URLs on different hosts can collide onto the same path, and the second source will silently resolve to the first repo.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     if local_path.is_dir() and (local_path / \".git\").exists():\n-        return local_path\n+        rc, out, _err = _run_git([\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"], cwd=local_path)\n+        existing = out.strip() if rc == 0 else \"\"\n+        if existing and _parse_git_url(existing) == _parse_git_url(url):\n+            return local_path\n+        print(\n+            f\"Warning: existing checkout at {local_path} points to \"\n+            f\"{_redact_url(existing) if existing else 'an unknown remote'}; \"\n+            f\"expected {_redact_url(url)}\",\n+            file=sys.stderr,\n+        )\n+        return None\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py` around lines 109 - 123, In\n_clone_if_missing: don’t assume any existing .git at local_path is the requested\nrepo—query and verify the origin remote before reusing it. If\nlocal_path.is_dir() and (local_path / \".git\").exists(), run git -C <local_path>\nremote get-url origin (via _run_git), parse both the requested url and the\nreturned origin with _parse_git_url and compare normalized values; only return\nlocal_path when they match. If the git command errors or the origin does not\nmatch, print a warning using _redact_url(url) and proceed to attempt the clone\n(or return None on failure) rather than silently reusing the checkout.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T18:26:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616396","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616396"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616396"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":109,"original_start_line":109,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":123,"original_line":123,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":123,"position":123,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616399","pull_request_review_id":3949119923,"id":2935616399,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-fOP","diff_hunk":"@@ -202,18 +202,27 @@ ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json generate-agents --agent <name>` directly WHEN user\n \n ALWAYS open and follow `{cypilot_path}/.core/workflows/generate.md` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot auto-config` or `cypilot configure` — generate.md will trigger the auto-config methodology\n \n+ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--force] [--max-depth <N>] [--dry-run]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace init`\n+\n+ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-add --name <name> (--path <path> | --url <url>) [--branch <branch>] [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>] [--inline] [--force]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace add` — auto-detects inline workspace and routes accordingly when `--inline` is not specified. Use `--inline` to force adding to `config/core.toml` (Git URL sources not supported in inline mode). Returns error if source name already exists unless `--force` is specified.\n+\n+ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-info` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace info`\n+\n+ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-sync [--source <name>] [--dry-run] [--force]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace sync` — **WARNING: `--force` is DESTRUCTIVE** — it discards uncommitted changes and may lose local commits\n ---","path":"skills/cypilot/SKILL.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Insert a blank line before this thematic break.**\n\nWithout it, markdownlint reads the previous line as a setext heading and keeps MD003 noisy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-sync [--source <name>] [--dry-run] [--force]` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot workspace sync` — **WARNING: `--force` is DESTRUCTIVE** — it discards uncommitted changes and may lose local commits\n+\n ---\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.21.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 211-211: Heading style\nExpected: atx; Actual: setext\n\n(MD003, heading-style)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/SKILL.md` around lines 211 - 212, Add a single blank line\nimmediately before the thematic break (the line with '---') that follows the\n\"ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-sync ...`\" sentence so the previous line\nis not treated as a setext heading by markdownlint; locate the paragraph\ncontaining \"ALWAYS run `{cpt_cmd} --json workspace-sync [--source <name>]\n[--dry-run] [--force]`...\" and insert one blank line directly above the '---'\ndivider.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 68de967","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:30:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616399","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616399"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935616399"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935616399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":211,"original_start_line":211,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":213,"original_line":212,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":11,"position":12,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935622666","pull_request_review_id":3949124437,"id":2935622666,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-gwK","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,352 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+Git utilities for workspace source resolution.\n+\n+Handles parsing Git URLs, namespace mapping, clone operations,\n+and explicit sync operations using subprocess (stdlib-only constraint).\n+\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-sync-git-source:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-git-url-sources:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-sync:p1\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+import re\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+if TYPE_CHECKING:\n+    from .workspace import NamespaceRule, ResolveConfig, SourceEntry\n+\n+# Patterns for parsing Git URLs\n+# HTTPS: https://gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_HTTPS_RE = re.compile(r\"^https://([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH shorthand: git@gitlab.com:org/repo.git\n+_SSH_SHORT_RE = re.compile(r\"^[\\w.-]+@([^:]+):(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH URL: ssh://git@gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_SSH_URL_RE = re.compile(r\"^ssh://[\\w.-]+@([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+\n+_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120  # seconds\n+\n+\n+def _redact_url(url: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Strip credentials from a Git URL before displaying it.\"\"\"\n+    # SCP-style SSH: user@host:path — redact the user part\n+    if \"://\" not in url and \"@\" in url and \":\" in url:\n+        at_idx = url.index(\"@\")\n+        return f\"***{url[at_idx:]}\"\n+    # Standard URLs: https://user:pass@host/path\n+    from urllib.parse import urlsplit, urlunsplit\n+    parts = urlsplit(url)\n+    if parts.username or parts.password:\n+        netloc = parts.hostname or \"\"\n+        if parts.port:\n+            netloc += f\":{parts.port}\"\n+        return urlunsplit((parts.scheme, netloc, parts.path, parts.query, parts.fragment))\n+    return url\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+def _parse_git_url(url: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, str, str]]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse a Git URL into (host, org, repo) components.\n+\n+    Supports HTTPS, SSH shorthand (git@host:path), and ssh:// URLs.\n+    Returns None if the URL cannot be parsed.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    for pattern in (_HTTPS_RE, _SSH_URL_RE, _SSH_SHORT_RE):\n+        m = pattern.match(url.strip())\n+        if m:\n+            host = m.group(1)\n+            path_part = m.group(2).strip(\"/\")\n+            # Split path into org (everything before last /) and repo (last segment)\n+            parts = path_part.rsplit(\"/\", 1)\n+            if len(parts) == 2:\n+                return (host, parts[0], parts[1])\n+            # Single segment: no org, just repo\n+            return (host, \"\", parts[0])\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+def _lookup_namespace(host: str, rules: list) -> \"Optional[NamespaceRule]\":\n+    \"\"\"Find a namespace rule matching the given host by exact match.\"\"\"\n+    for rule in rules:\n+        if rule.host == host:\n+            return rule\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+def _apply_template(template: str, org: str, repo: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Apply {org}/{repo} substitution to a namespace template.\n+\n+    Raises ValueError if the result is an absolute path or contains '..'\n+    segments that could escape the workspace directory.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    result = template.replace(\"{org}\", org).replace(\"{repo}\", repo)\n+    # Strip leading slash that appears when org is empty (\"{org}/{repo}\" → \"/repo\")\n+    result = result.lstrip(\"/\")\n+    # Reject path traversal: absolute paths or \"..\" segments\n+    if not result or result.startswith(\"/\") or \"..\" in Path(result).parts:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Unsafe path template result: {result!r}\")\n+    return result\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-clone-or-fetch\n+def _clone_if_missing(url: str, local_path: Path, branch: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Clone a git repo or return existing local path.\n+\n+    For existing repos, returns local_path without network operations.\n+    Use sync_git_source() to fetch and update worktrees explicitly.\n+    Returns local_path on success, None on clone failure.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if _parse_git_url(url) is None:\n+        print(f\"Warning: refusing to clone unrecognized URL: {_redact_url(url)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    if local_path.is_dir() and (local_path / \".git\").exists():\n+        return local_path\n+    # Clone\n+    clone_args = [\"clone\", \"--quiet\"]\n+    if branch != \"HEAD\":\n+        clone_args.extend([\"--branch\", branch])\n+    clone_args.extend([url, str(local_path)])\n+    rc, _out, err = _run_git(clone_args)\n+    if rc != 0:\n+        print(f\"Warning: git clone failed for {_redact_url(url)}: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    return local_path","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":" The local path is computed deterministically from the URL via _compute_local_path (URL → _parse_git_url → (host, org, repo) → template → path), so two different URLs can only collide if they produce the same normalized (host, org, repo) tuple — which means they point to the same repository. A runtime git remote get-url origin check would add a subprocess call on every resolve for existing repos, breaking the current no-I/O contract of _clone_if_missing for the existing-repo path, with no practical benefit.","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:26:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T18:26:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935622666","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935622666"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935622666"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935622666/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":109,"original_start_line":109,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":123,"original_line":123,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616396,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":123,"position":123,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935623288","pull_request_review_id":3949124872,"id":2935623288,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-g54","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,352 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+Git utilities for workspace source resolution.\n+\n+Handles parsing Git URLs, namespace mapping, clone operations,\n+and explicit sync operations using subprocess (stdlib-only constraint).\n+\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1\n+@cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-sync-git-source:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-git-url-sources:p1\n+@cpt-dod:cpt-cypilot-dod-workspace-sync:p1\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+import re\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+if TYPE_CHECKING:\n+    from .workspace import NamespaceRule, ResolveConfig, SourceEntry\n+\n+# Patterns for parsing Git URLs\n+# HTTPS: https://gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_HTTPS_RE = re.compile(r\"^https://([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH shorthand: git@gitlab.com:org/repo.git\n+_SSH_SHORT_RE = re.compile(r\"^[\\w.-]+@([^:]+):(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+# SSH URL: ssh://git@gitlab.com/org/repo.git\n+_SSH_URL_RE = re.compile(r\"^ssh://[\\w.-]+@([^/]+)/(.+?)(?:\\.git)?$\")\n+\n+_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120  # seconds\n+\n+\n+def _redact_url(url: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Strip credentials from a Git URL before displaying it.\"\"\"\n+    # SCP-style SSH: user@host:path — redact the user part\n+    if \"://\" not in url and \"@\" in url and \":\" in url:\n+        at_idx = url.index(\"@\")\n+        return f\"***{url[at_idx:]}\"\n+    # Standard URLs: https://user:pass@host/path\n+    from urllib.parse import urlsplit, urlunsplit\n+    parts = urlsplit(url)\n+    if parts.username or parts.password:\n+        netloc = parts.hostname or \"\"\n+        if parts.port:\n+            netloc += f\":{parts.port}\"\n+        return urlunsplit((parts.scheme, netloc, parts.path, parts.query, parts.fragment))\n+    return url\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+def _parse_git_url(url: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, str, str]]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse a Git URL into (host, org, repo) components.\n+\n+    Supports HTTPS, SSH shorthand (git@host:path), and ssh:// URLs.\n+    Returns None if the URL cannot be parsed.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    for pattern in (_HTTPS_RE, _SSH_URL_RE, _SSH_SHORT_RE):\n+        m = pattern.match(url.strip())\n+        if m:\n+            host = m.group(1)\n+            path_part = m.group(2).strip(\"/\")\n+            # Split path into org (everything before last /) and repo (last segment)\n+            parts = path_part.rsplit(\"/\", 1)\n+            if len(parts) == 2:\n+                return (host, parts[0], parts[1])\n+            # Single segment: no org, just repo\n+            return (host, \"\", parts[0])\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-parse-url\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+def _lookup_namespace(host: str, rules: list) -> \"Optional[NamespaceRule]\":\n+    \"\"\"Find a namespace rule matching the given host by exact match.\"\"\"\n+    for rule in rules:\n+        if rule.host == host:\n+            return rule\n+    return None\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-lookup-namespace\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+def _apply_template(template: str, org: str, repo: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Apply {org}/{repo} substitution to a namespace template.\n+\n+    Raises ValueError if the result is an absolute path or contains '..'\n+    segments that could escape the workspace directory.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    result = template.replace(\"{org}\", org).replace(\"{repo}\", repo)\n+    # Strip leading slash that appears when org is empty (\"{org}/{repo}\" → \"/repo\")\n+    result = result.lstrip(\"/\")\n+    # Reject path traversal: absolute paths or \"..\" segments\n+    if not result or result.startswith(\"/\") or \"..\" in Path(result).parts:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Unsafe path template result: {result!r}\")\n+    return result\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-apply-template\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-clone-or-fetch\n+def _clone_if_missing(url: str, local_path: Path, branch: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+    \"\"\"Clone a git repo or return existing local path.\n+\n+    For existing repos, returns local_path without network operations.\n+    Use sync_git_source() to fetch and update worktrees explicitly.\n+    Returns local_path on success, None on clone failure.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if _parse_git_url(url) is None:\n+        print(f\"Warning: refusing to clone unrecognized URL: {_redact_url(url)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    if local_path.is_dir() and (local_path / \".git\").exists():\n+        return local_path\n+    # Clone\n+    clone_args = [\"clone\", \"--quiet\"]\n+    if branch != \"HEAD\":\n+        clone_args.extend([\"--branch\", branch])\n+    clone_args.extend([url, str(local_path)])\n+    rc, _out, err = _run_git(clone_args)\n+    if rc != 0:\n+        print(f\"Warning: git clone failed for {_redact_url(url)}: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n+    return local_path","path":"skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, that's a well-reasoned explanation — you're right. Since `_compute_local_path` is the authoritative source of the filesystem path and it's derived deterministically from the parsed `(host, org, repo)` triple, a path collision can only occur when two URLs resolve to the same triple, which by definition means they point to the same repository. The origin-verification check is therefore redundant, and removing the no-I/O fast path for the common case would be an unnecessary regression. I've withdrawn the concern.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py:109-123\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T18:26:28.128Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py`, `_clone_if_missing()` intentionally accepts any existing `.git` directory at `local_path` without verifying the `origin` remote. The local path is computed deterministically by `_compute_local_path()` via URL → `_parse_git_url()` → (host, org, repo) → namespace template → path, so two different URLs can only collide onto the same path if they produce the same normalized (host, org, repo) tuple, meaning they point to the same repository. A runtime `git remote get-url origin` check is redundant and would break the no-I/O contract of the existing-repo fast path. Do not flag this as a missing verification.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py:187-193\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T11:25:08.406Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py`, the `_compute_local_path()` function intentionally trusts `resolve_config.workdir` as-is (including absolute paths or paths with `..`), because it is a direct user configuration value. The `local_path.relative_to(expected_base)` containment check is there to guard against malicious `org`/`repo` segments derived from parsed Git URLs, not against the user's own workspace layout. Do not suggest validating or sanitizing `workdir` for path traversal — it is the intended configuration mechanism.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py:48-51\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T17:01:08.042Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py`, the `if not reachable:` block in `_build_source_info` (lines 49–56) already handles both URL-only and path-only sources: URL sources display a redacted URL with a 'workspace-sync' hint via `_redact_url(src.url)`; path-only sources use `identifier = src.path or name` to prevent None in the warning. `checkout_path` does not exist on `SourceEntry`. Do not flag the warning message as potentially showing \"None\".\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py:93-96\nTimestamp: 2026-03-09T12:52:53.548Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`, the `try/except OSError` around `scan_root.iterdir()` in `_scan_nested_repos` (around lines 93–96) intentionally swallows the error and falls back to `entries = []`. This is by design for graceful degradation: an inaccessible scan root is treated as \"no sources found\" rather than a hard ERROR. Do not flag this as a bug or suggest propagating the OSError.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T18:26:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T18:26:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935623288","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935623288"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935623288"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935623288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":109,"original_start_line":109,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":123,"original_line":123,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616396,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":123,"position":123,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935709274","pull_request_review_id":3949191909,"id":2935709274,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-15a","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"https://example.com/cypilot/workspace.schema.json\",\n+  \"title\": \"Cypilot Workspace Configuration (.cypilot-workspace.toml)\",\n+  \"description\": \"Federation layer for multi-repo workspace support. Maps named sources (repos) to local paths with roles. Standalone file uses TOML format.\",\n+  \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n+  \"required\": [\"version\", \"sources\"],\n+  \"examples\": [\n+    {\n+      \"version\": \"1.0\",\n+      \"sources\": {\n+        \"docs-repo\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../docs-repo\",\n+          \"adapter\": \".bootstrap\",\n+          \"role\": \"artifacts\"\n+        },\n+        \"code-repo\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../code-repo\",\n+          \"adapter\": \".bootstrap\",\n+          \"role\": \"codebase\"\n+        },\n+        \"shared-kits\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../shared-kits\",\n+          \"role\": \"kits\"\n+        },\n+        \"remote-lib\": {\n+          \"url\": \"https://gitlab.com/team/lib.git\",\n+          \"branch\": \"main\",\n+          \"role\": \"codebase\"\n+        }\n+      },\n+      \"traceability\": {\n+        \"cross_repo\": true,\n+        \"resolve_remote_ids\": true\n+      },\n+      \"resolve\": {\n+        \"workdir\": \".workspace-sources\",\n+        \"namespace\": {\n+          \"gitlab.com\": \"{org}/{repo}\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"properties\": {\n+    \"version\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"minLength\": 1,\n+      \"description\": \"Schema version (currently '1.0')\"\n+    },\n+    \"sources\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Named source repositories in the workspace. Keys are human-readable names.\",\n+      \"additionalProperties\": {\n+        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/source_entry\"\n+      }\n+    },\n+    \"traceability\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/traceability_config\"\n+    },\n+    \"resolve\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/resolve_config\"\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"$defs\": {\n+    \"source_entry\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n+      \"oneOf\": [\n+        {\n+          \"required\": [\"path\"],\n+          \"not\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"required\": [\"url\"]}, {\"required\": [\"branch\"]}]}\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"required\": [\"url\"],\n+          \"not\": {\"required\": [\"path\"]}\n+        }\n+      ],\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"path\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Local filesystem path to the source repo. Resolved relative to workspace file location.\"\n+        },\n+        \"adapter\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Path to adapter directory within the source repo (e.g., '.bootstrap'). Omit if repo has no adapter.\"\n+        },\n+        \"role\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"enum\": [\"artifacts\", \"codebase\", \"kits\", \"full\"],\n+          \"default\": \"full\",\n+          \"description\": \"Constrains what the source contributes. 'artifacts' = only artifacts, 'codebase' = only code, 'kits' = only kits, 'full' = everything.\"\n+        },\n+        \"url\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Git remote URL (HTTPS or SSH). Only supported in standalone workspace files, not inline config.\"\n+        },\n+        \"branch\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Git branch or ref to checkout. Defaults to HEAD when not specified.\"\n+        }","path":"schemas/workspace.schema.json","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The schema, spec, and code are all consistent. The workspace feature spec (workspace.md line 386) explicitly states: \"Determine branch: source branch field if set, else \"HEAD\"\". The code uses \"HEAD\" as an internal sentinel (git_utils.py:232) — when branch == \"HEAD\", git clone runs without --branch, which clones the remote's default branch. The schema description accurately reflects this behavior.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:14:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:14:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935709274","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935709274"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935709274"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935709274/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":101,"original_start_line":101,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":105,"original_line":105,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616383,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":105,"position":105,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710109","pull_request_review_id":3949192790,"id":2935710109,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-2Gd","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"https://example.com/cypilot/workspace.schema.json\",\n+  \"title\": \"Cypilot Workspace Configuration (.cypilot-workspace.toml)\",\n+  \"description\": \"Federation layer for multi-repo workspace support. Maps named sources (repos) to local paths with roles. Standalone file uses TOML format.\",\n+  \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n+  \"required\": [\"version\", \"sources\"],\n+  \"examples\": [\n+    {\n+      \"version\": \"1.0\",\n+      \"sources\": {\n+        \"docs-repo\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../docs-repo\",\n+          \"adapter\": \".bootstrap\",\n+          \"role\": \"artifacts\"\n+        },\n+        \"code-repo\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../code-repo\",\n+          \"adapter\": \".bootstrap\",\n+          \"role\": \"codebase\"\n+        },\n+        \"shared-kits\": {\n+          \"path\": \"../shared-kits\",\n+          \"role\": \"kits\"\n+        },\n+        \"remote-lib\": {\n+          \"url\": \"https://gitlab.com/team/lib.git\",\n+          \"branch\": \"main\",\n+          \"role\": \"codebase\"\n+        }\n+      },\n+      \"traceability\": {\n+        \"cross_repo\": true,\n+        \"resolve_remote_ids\": true\n+      },\n+      \"resolve\": {\n+        \"workdir\": \".workspace-sources\",\n+        \"namespace\": {\n+          \"gitlab.com\": \"{org}/{repo}\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"properties\": {\n+    \"version\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"minLength\": 1,\n+      \"description\": \"Schema version (currently '1.0')\"\n+    },\n+    \"sources\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Named source repositories in the workspace. Keys are human-readable names.\",\n+      \"additionalProperties\": {\n+        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/source_entry\"\n+      }\n+    },\n+    \"traceability\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/traceability_config\"\n+    },\n+    \"resolve\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/resolve_config\"\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"$defs\": {\n+    \"source_entry\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n+      \"oneOf\": [\n+        {\n+          \"required\": [\"path\"],\n+          \"not\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"required\": [\"url\"]}, {\"required\": [\"branch\"]}]}\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"required\": [\"url\"],\n+          \"not\": {\"required\": [\"path\"]}\n+        }\n+      ],\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"path\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Local filesystem path to the source repo. Resolved relative to workspace file location.\"\n+        },\n+        \"adapter\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Path to adapter directory within the source repo (e.g., '.bootstrap'). Omit if repo has no adapter.\"\n+        },\n+        \"role\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"enum\": [\"artifacts\", \"codebase\", \"kits\", \"full\"],\n+          \"default\": \"full\",\n+          \"description\": \"Constrains what the source contributes. 'artifacts' = only artifacts, 'codebase' = only code, 'kits' = only kits, 'full' = everything.\"\n+        },\n+        \"url\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Git remote URL (HTTPS or SSH). Only supported in standalone workspace files, not inline config.\"\n+        },\n+        \"branch\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1,\n+          \"description\": \"Git branch or ref to checkout. Defaults to HEAD when not specified.\"\n+        }","path":"schemas/workspace.schema.json","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, thank you for the detailed explanation — that's clear and makes sense. The `\"HEAD\"` sentinel is the correct and intentional value: `git_utils.py` uses it to detect \"no branch specified\" and omits `--branch` from the clone command, deferring to the remote's default branch. The schema description accurately reflects this internal behavior. My concern was mistaken.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: schemas/workspace.schema.json:101-105\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T19:15:04.072Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py` (around line 232), the string `\"HEAD\"` is used as an internal sentinel for the `branch` field on `SourceEntry`. When `branch == \"HEAD\"`, the git clone command runs without `--branch`, which causes git to clone the remote repository's default branch. This is the intended behavior when no branch is explicitly specified. The workspace feature spec (workspace.md line 386) documents this as: \"Determine branch: source branch field if set, else 'HEAD'\". The JSON schema description \"Defaults to HEAD when not specified\" in `schemas/workspace.schema.json` is correct and intentional — do not suggest changing it to \"remote repository's default branch\".\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935710109","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710109"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935710109"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710109/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":101,"original_start_line":101,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":105,"original_line":105,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616383,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":105,"position":105,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710754","pull_request_review_id":3949193558,"id":2935710754,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-2Qi","diff_hunk":"@@ -928,6 +974,142 @@ The plugin MUST delegate all validation logic to the installed Cypilot CLI to en\n \n ---\n \n+### UC-014 Initialize Multi-Repo Workspace\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cypilot-usecase-workspace-init`\n+\n+**Actors**:\n+`cpt-cypilot-actor-user`, `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Cypilot initialized in project; one or more sibling repositories exist in nested sub-directories\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+\n+1. User runs `workspace-init [--root DIR] [--output PATH] [--inline] [--force] [--max-depth N] [--dry-run]` from project root\n+2. Tool scans nested sub-directories (up to `--max-depth` levels, default 3) for repos with `.git` or `AGENTS.md` with `@cpt:root-agents` marker (uses capability `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`)\n+3. Tool infers source roles (`artifacts`, `codebase`, `kits`, `full`) based on adapter contents\n+4. Tool checks for existing workspace config conflicts (cross-type or same-type without `--force`)\n+5. Tool writes workspace config with discovered sources and default traceability settings: standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` by default, or inline `[workspace]` in `config/core.toml` when `--inline` is specified\n+\n+**Alternative Flows**:\n+- **No nested repos found**: Tool creates an empty workspace config; user can add sources incrementally via `workspace-add`.\n+- **Workspace config already exists**: Tool rejects unless `--force` is specified.\n+- **`--dry-run` specified**: Tool displays discovered sources without writing files.","path":"architecture/PRD.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The precondition \"one or more sibling repositories exist\" describes the expected state for the main flow. The alternative flow \"No nested repos found\" explicitly covers the case when this precondition is not met — that's standard use-case modeling (preconditions define the happy path; alternative flows handle deviations). Changing to \"zero or more\" would make the precondition vacuous and the \"No nested repos found\" alternative flow logically redundant.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935710754","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710754"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935710754"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935710754/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":984,"original_start_line":984,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":997,"original_line":997,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616382,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":91,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935711249","pull_request_review_id":3949194126,"id":2935711249,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-2YR","diff_hunk":"@@ -928,6 +974,142 @@ The plugin MUST delegate all validation logic to the installed Cypilot CLI to en\n \n ---\n \n+### UC-014 Initialize Multi-Repo Workspace\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cypilot-usecase-workspace-init`\n+\n+**Actors**:\n+`cpt-cypilot-actor-user`, `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Cypilot initialized in project; one or more sibling repositories exist in nested sub-directories\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+\n+1. User runs `workspace-init [--root DIR] [--output PATH] [--inline] [--force] [--max-depth N] [--dry-run]` from project root\n+2. Tool scans nested sub-directories (up to `--max-depth` levels, default 3) for repos with `.git` or `AGENTS.md` with `@cpt:root-agents` marker (uses capability `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`)\n+3. Tool infers source roles (`artifacts`, `codebase`, `kits`, `full`) based on adapter contents\n+4. Tool checks for existing workspace config conflicts (cross-type or same-type without `--force`)\n+5. Tool writes workspace config with discovered sources and default traceability settings: standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` by default, or inline `[workspace]` in `config/core.toml` when `--inline` is specified\n+\n+**Alternative Flows**:\n+- **No nested repos found**: Tool creates an empty workspace config; user can add sources incrementally via `workspace-add`.\n+- **Workspace config already exists**: Tool rejects unless `--force` is specified.\n+- **`--dry-run` specified**: Tool displays discovered sources without writing files.","path":"architecture/PRD.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, you're absolutely right — that's a correct application of standard use-case modeling conventions. Preconditions define the expected state for the main (happy) flow, and alternative flows are precisely the mechanism to handle deviations from those conditions. Keeping \"one or more sibling repositories exist\" as the precondition gives the \"No nested repos found\" alternative flow its purpose and meaning. My concern was misplaced.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: When a critical Cypilot dependency is missing (SKILL.md or workflow files), inform the user and suggest running `/cypilot` to reinitialize rather than failing silently\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py:93-96\nTimestamp: 2026-03-09T12:52:53.548Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`, the `try/except OSError` around `scan_root.iterdir()` in `_scan_nested_repos` (around lines 93–96) intentionally swallows the error and falls back to `entries = []`. This is by design for graceful degradation: an inaccessible scan root is treated as \"no sources found\" rather than a hard ERROR. Do not flag this as a bug or suggest propagating the OSError.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:15:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935711249","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935711249"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935711249"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935711249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":984,"original_start_line":984,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":997,"original_line":997,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616382,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":91,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935712764","pull_request_review_id":3949195553,"id":2935712764,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-2v8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,675 @@\n+# Feature: Multi-Repo Workspace Federation\n+\n+\n+<!-- toc -->\n+\n+- [1. Feature Context](#1-feature-context)\n+  - [1. Overview](#1-overview)\n+  - [2. Purpose](#2-purpose)\n+  - [3. Actors](#3-actors)\n+  - [4. References](#4-references)\n+  - [5. Non-Applicability](#5-non-applicability)\n+  - [6. Out of Scope](#6-out-of-scope)\n+- [2. Actor Flows (CDSL)](#2-actor-flows-cdsl)\n+  - [Workspace Initialization](#workspace-initialization)\n+  - [Workspace Source Management](#workspace-source-management)\n+  - [Workspace Info Display](#workspace-info-display)\n+  - [Workspace Sync](#workspace-sync)\n+- [3. Processes / Business Logic (CDSL)](#3-processes--business-logic-cdsl)\n+  - [Find Workspace Config](#find-workspace-config)\n+  - [Discover Nested Repos](#discover-nested-repos)\n+  - [Resolve Source Path](#resolve-source-path)\n+  - [Infer Source Role](#infer-source-role)\n+  - [Load Workspace Context](#load-workspace-context)\n+  - [Resolve Artifact Path](#resolve-artifact-path)\n+  - [Collect Cross-Repo IDs](#collect-cross-repo-ids)\n+  - [Resolve Git URL Source](#resolve-git-url-source)\n+  - [Sync Git Source](#sync-git-source)\n+  - [Resolve Source Adapter Context](#resolve-source-adapter-context)\n+  - [Determine Target Source](#determine-target-source)\n+- [4. States (CDSL)](#4-states-cdsl)\n+  - [Source Reachability](#source-reachability)\n+  - [Config Lifecycle](#config-lifecycle)\n+- [5. Definitions of Done](#5-definitions-of-done)\n+  - [Workspace Initialization and Config](#workspace-initialization-and-config)\n+  - [Source Management](#source-management)\n+  - [Cross-Repo Traceability](#cross-repo-traceability)\n+  - [Graceful Degradation](#graceful-degradation)\n+  - [Backward Compatibility](#backward-compatibility)\n+  - [Git URL Source Resolution](#git-url-source-resolution)\n+  - [Cross-Repo Editing](#cross-repo-editing)\n+  - [Workspace Sync](#workspace-sync-1)\n+- [6. Implementation Modules](#6-implementation-modules)\n+- [7. Acceptance Criteria](#7-acceptance-criteria)\n+\n+<!-- /toc -->\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-featstatus-workspace`\n+\n+## 1. Feature Context\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - `cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace`\n+\n+### 1. Overview\n+\n+Multi-repo workspace federation enabling nested sub-directory repo discovery, source configuration (standalone or inline), cross-repo artifact traceability, and graceful degradation when sources are unreachable. Projects without workspace config continue operating in single-repo mode with zero behavioral changes.\n+\n+### 2. Purpose\n+\n+Enables teams working across multiple repositories to federate their Cypilot-managed artifacts — discovering repos in nested sub-directories, resolving cross-repo artifact paths, and collecting IDs across workspace boundaries — without merging adapters or modifying individual project configs. Addresses PRD requirement for workspace federation (`cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`) and extends the core traceability system (`cpt-cypilot-fr-core-traceability`) with cross-repo resolution.\n+\n+### 3. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Role in Feature |\n+|-------|-----------------|\n+| `cpt-cypilot-actor-user` | Runs `workspace-init`, `workspace-add` (with `--inline` flag for inline mode), `workspace-info`, `workspace-sync`; uses `validate --local-only` and `list-ids --source` |\n+| `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli` | Discovers workspace config during context loading, resolves cross-repo paths, loads source contexts |\n+\n+### 4. References\n+\n+- **PRD**: [PRD.md](../PRD.md) — `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-traceability`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace-git-sources`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace-cross-repo-editing`\n+- **Design**: [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) — `cpt-cypilot-component-config-manager`, `cpt-cypilot-component-traceability-engine`\n+- **Design Principles**: `cpt-cypilot-principle-traceability-by-design`, `cpt-cypilot-principle-determinism-first`, `cpt-cypilot-principle-zero-harm`\n+- **Design Constraints**: `cpt-cypilot-constraint-python-stdlib`\n+- **CLI Spec**: [cli.md](../specs/cli.md)\n+- **Dependencies**: `cpt-cypilot-feature-core-infra`, `cpt-cypilot-feature-traceability-validation`\n+\n+### 5. Non-Applicability\n+\n+The following quality domains are not applicable to this feature:\n+\n+- **Performance**: Core operations (init, add, info) are local filesystem reads/writes on small TOML configs. Git URL source resolution clones on first access only; subsequent reads reuse the cached checkout without network operations. Explicit updates via `workspace-sync` delegate to the user's git CLI with a 120-second timeout; no custom performance-sensitive code paths beyond subprocess delegation\n+- **Security**: Local-path mode has no network access. Git URL sources perform `git clone` (first access) and `git fetch` (only via explicit `workspace-sync`) using the user's existing Git CLI credentials — no custom authentication or credential handling. CLI arguments parsed by argparse with no untrusted input\n+- **Compliance**: No regulatory, privacy, or audit requirements\n+- **Usability (UI)**: CLI-only interaction with structured JSON output; no graphical UI\n+- **Operations**: No deployment, observability, or infrastructure concerns; standalone CLI commands\n+\n+### 6. Out of Scope\n+\n+- Workspace-level aggregate linting or test orchestration across sources\n+- Remote source authentication beyond Git CLI credentials\n+- Workspace-level dependency resolution between source packages\n+- Live file-watching or automatic re-discovery of sources\n+\n+## 2. Actor Flows (CDSL)\n+\n+### Workspace Initialization\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-init`\n+\n+**Actors**:\n+\n+- `cpt-cypilot-actor-user`\n+- `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli`\n+\n+**Success Scenarios**:\n+- User runs `workspace-init` → nested sub-directories scanned for repos, workspace config generated with discovered sources\n+- User runs `workspace-init --inline` → workspace config written inline into `config/core.toml`\n+- User runs `workspace-init --dry-run` → shows what would be generated without writing\n+\n+**Error Scenarios**:\n+- No project root found → error with instructions\n+- Scan root not found → error with path\n+- No repos discovered in nested sub-directories → creates empty workspace (sources: {})\n+- `--inline` with existing standalone workspace → error (prevents parallel configs)","path":"architecture/features/workspace.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":" The file contains no fenced code blocks (triple backticks) — all code references use inline backticks. MD040 (fenced-code-language) cannot trigger. The two tables (lines 63-66 and 629-638) already have correct padding and consistent column spacing. No changes needed.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:16:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:16:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935712764","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935712764"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935712764"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935712764/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":114,"original_line":114,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616379,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":114,"position":114,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935713964","pull_request_review_id":3949196923,"id":2935713964,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-3Cs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,675 @@\n+# Feature: Multi-Repo Workspace Federation\n+\n+\n+<!-- toc -->\n+\n+- [1. Feature Context](#1-feature-context)\n+  - [1. Overview](#1-overview)\n+  - [2. Purpose](#2-purpose)\n+  - [3. Actors](#3-actors)\n+  - [4. References](#4-references)\n+  - [5. Non-Applicability](#5-non-applicability)\n+  - [6. Out of Scope](#6-out-of-scope)\n+- [2. Actor Flows (CDSL)](#2-actor-flows-cdsl)\n+  - [Workspace Initialization](#workspace-initialization)\n+  - [Workspace Source Management](#workspace-source-management)\n+  - [Workspace Info Display](#workspace-info-display)\n+  - [Workspace Sync](#workspace-sync)\n+- [3. Processes / Business Logic (CDSL)](#3-processes--business-logic-cdsl)\n+  - [Find Workspace Config](#find-workspace-config)\n+  - [Discover Nested Repos](#discover-nested-repos)\n+  - [Resolve Source Path](#resolve-source-path)\n+  - [Infer Source Role](#infer-source-role)\n+  - [Load Workspace Context](#load-workspace-context)\n+  - [Resolve Artifact Path](#resolve-artifact-path)\n+  - [Collect Cross-Repo IDs](#collect-cross-repo-ids)\n+  - [Resolve Git URL Source](#resolve-git-url-source)\n+  - [Sync Git Source](#sync-git-source)\n+  - [Resolve Source Adapter Context](#resolve-source-adapter-context)\n+  - [Determine Target Source](#determine-target-source)\n+- [4. States (CDSL)](#4-states-cdsl)\n+  - [Source Reachability](#source-reachability)\n+  - [Config Lifecycle](#config-lifecycle)\n+- [5. Definitions of Done](#5-definitions-of-done)\n+  - [Workspace Initialization and Config](#workspace-initialization-and-config)\n+  - [Source Management](#source-management)\n+  - [Cross-Repo Traceability](#cross-repo-traceability)\n+  - [Graceful Degradation](#graceful-degradation)\n+  - [Backward Compatibility](#backward-compatibility)\n+  - [Git URL Source Resolution](#git-url-source-resolution)\n+  - [Cross-Repo Editing](#cross-repo-editing)\n+  - [Workspace Sync](#workspace-sync-1)\n+- [6. Implementation Modules](#6-implementation-modules)\n+- [7. Acceptance Criteria](#7-acceptance-criteria)\n+\n+<!-- /toc -->\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-featstatus-workspace`\n+\n+## 1. Feature Context\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - `cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace`\n+\n+### 1. Overview\n+\n+Multi-repo workspace federation enabling nested sub-directory repo discovery, source configuration (standalone or inline), cross-repo artifact traceability, and graceful degradation when sources are unreachable. Projects without workspace config continue operating in single-repo mode with zero behavioral changes.\n+\n+### 2. Purpose\n+\n+Enables teams working across multiple repositories to federate their Cypilot-managed artifacts — discovering repos in nested sub-directories, resolving cross-repo artifact paths, and collecting IDs across workspace boundaries — without merging adapters or modifying individual project configs. Addresses PRD requirement for workspace federation (`cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`) and extends the core traceability system (`cpt-cypilot-fr-core-traceability`) with cross-repo resolution.\n+\n+### 3. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Role in Feature |\n+|-------|-----------------|\n+| `cpt-cypilot-actor-user` | Runs `workspace-init`, `workspace-add` (with `--inline` flag for inline mode), `workspace-info`, `workspace-sync`; uses `validate --local-only` and `list-ids --source` |\n+| `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli` | Discovers workspace config during context loading, resolves cross-repo paths, loads source contexts |\n+\n+### 4. References\n+\n+- **PRD**: [PRD.md](../PRD.md) — `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-traceability`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace-git-sources`, `cpt-cypilot-fr-core-workspace-cross-repo-editing`\n+- **Design**: [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) — `cpt-cypilot-component-config-manager`, `cpt-cypilot-component-traceability-engine`\n+- **Design Principles**: `cpt-cypilot-principle-traceability-by-design`, `cpt-cypilot-principle-determinism-first`, `cpt-cypilot-principle-zero-harm`\n+- **Design Constraints**: `cpt-cypilot-constraint-python-stdlib`\n+- **CLI Spec**: [cli.md](../specs/cli.md)\n+- **Dependencies**: `cpt-cypilot-feature-core-infra`, `cpt-cypilot-feature-traceability-validation`\n+\n+### 5. Non-Applicability\n+\n+The following quality domains are not applicable to this feature:\n+\n+- **Performance**: Core operations (init, add, info) are local filesystem reads/writes on small TOML configs. Git URL source resolution clones on first access only; subsequent reads reuse the cached checkout without network operations. Explicit updates via `workspace-sync` delegate to the user's git CLI with a 120-second timeout; no custom performance-sensitive code paths beyond subprocess delegation\n+- **Security**: Local-path mode has no network access. Git URL sources perform `git clone` (first access) and `git fetch` (only via explicit `workspace-sync`) using the user's existing Git CLI credentials — no custom authentication or credential handling. CLI arguments parsed by argparse with no untrusted input\n+- **Compliance**: No regulatory, privacy, or audit requirements\n+- **Usability (UI)**: CLI-only interaction with structured JSON output; no graphical UI\n+- **Operations**: No deployment, observability, or infrastructure concerns; standalone CLI commands\n+\n+### 6. Out of Scope\n+\n+- Workspace-level aggregate linting or test orchestration across sources\n+- Remote source authentication beyond Git CLI credentials\n+- Workspace-level dependency resolution between source packages\n+- Live file-watching or automatic re-discovery of sources\n+\n+## 2. Actor Flows (CDSL)\n+\n+### Workspace Initialization\n+\n+- [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cypilot-flow-workspace-init`\n+\n+**Actors**:\n+\n+- `cpt-cypilot-actor-user`\n+- `cpt-cypilot-actor-cypilot-cli`\n+\n+**Success Scenarios**:\n+- User runs `workspace-init` → nested sub-directories scanned for repos, workspace config generated with discovered sources\n+- User runs `workspace-init --inline` → workspace config written inline into `config/core.toml`\n+- User runs `workspace-init --dry-run` → shows what would be generated without writing\n+\n+**Error Scenarios**:\n+- No project root found → error with instructions\n+- Scan root not found → error with path\n+- No repos discovered in nested sub-directories → creates empty workspace (sources: {})\n+- `--inline` with existing standalone workspace → error (prevents parallel configs)","path":"architecture/features/workspace.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n````\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check for triple-backtick fenced code blocks in the file\necho \"=== Triple-backtick fenced blocks ===\"\ngrep -n '^\\s*```' architecture/features/workspace.md | head -40\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Table rows (lines with pipe chars) ===\"\ngrep -n '|' architecture/features/workspace.md | head -40\n````\n\nLength of output: 2022\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@nonameffh`, you're right — the script confirms there are zero triple-backtick fenced code blocks in `architecture/features/workspace.md`, and both tables already have correct pipe padding. MD040 cannot apply to this file. My original review comment was incorrect. No changes needed — apologies for the noise!\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:17:33Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:17:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935713964","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935713964"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935713964"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935713964/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":114,"original_line":114,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616379,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":114,"position":114,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935716258","pull_request_review_id":3949199534,"id":2935716258,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-3mi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+# /cypilot-workspace\n+\n+\n+ALWAYS open and follow `{cypilot_path}/.core/workflows/workspace.md`","path":".cursor/commands/cypilot-workspace.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"All sub-workflow Cursor commands (cypilot-analyze, cypilot-generate, cypilot-workspace) follow the same pattern: a single-line redirect to their workflow file, intentionally skipping the full bootstrap. The bootstrap chain (Protocol Guard, AGENTS.md loading, SKILL.md) is the responsibility of the main `/cypilot` entry point. Adding it to every sub-workflow would duplicate logic already in SKILL.md and break consistency with the other commands, none of which include it.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:19:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:19:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935716258","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935716258"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935716258"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935716258/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":4,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616378,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935717160","pull_request_review_id":3949200663,"id":2935717160,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-30o","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+# /cypilot-workspace\n+\n+\n+ALWAYS open and follow `{cypilot_path}/.core/workflows/workspace.md`","path":".cursor/commands/cypilot-workspace.md","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, understood — that's a clear and consistent architectural decision. The single-line redirect pattern for sub-workflow commands is intentional, and the bootstrap responsibility belongs solely to the main `/cypilot` entry point. I'll remember this for future reviews.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .cursor/commands/cypilot-workspace.md:1-4\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T19:19:28.407Z\nLearning: In the cyberfabric/cyber-pilot repository, sub-workflow Cursor commands (e.g., `.cursor/commands/cypilot-analyze.md`, `.cursor/commands/cypilot-generate.md`, `.cursor/commands/cypilot-workspace.md`) intentionally use a single-line redirect to their respective workflow file (e.g., `{cypilot_path}/.core/workflows/workspace.md`). They do NOT include the full bootstrap chain (Protocol Guard, AGENTS.md loading, SKILL.md). The bootstrap chain is the sole responsibility of the main `/cypilot` entry point. Do not flag the absence of bootstrap steps in sub-workflow command files as an issue.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: ALWAYS open and follow `{cypilot_path}/config/AGENTS.md` FIRST when starting any Cypilot work\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:22:37.306Z\nLearning: Always open and follow `{cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/SKILL.md`\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Always open and follow Cypilot skill documentation at {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/SKILL.md\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: ALWAYS open and follow `{cypilot_path}/.gen/AGENTS.md` FIRST when working with Cypilot AI agents\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: ALWAYS invoke `{cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/SKILL.md` WHEN user asks to do something with Cypilot\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Use Cypilot workflow routing for analyzing and validating artifacts, or creating/generating/implementing work through Cypilot workflows\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: When a critical Cypilot dependency is missing (SKILL.md or workflow files), inform the user and suggest running `/cypilot` to reinitialize rather than failing silently\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-11T18:34:15.395Z\nLearning: Store the Cypilot path as a project variable set to `.bootstrap`\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: CLAUDE.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-02T12:29:41.299Z\nLearning: STOP and READ `AGENTS.md` in project root before ANY tool calls or skill invocation\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py:93-96\nTimestamp: 2026-03-09T12:52:53.548Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`, the `try/except OSError` around `scan_root.iterdir()` in `_scan_nested_repos` (around lines 93–96) intentionally swallows the error and falls back to `entries = []`. This is by design for graceful degradation: an inaccessible scan root is treated as \"no sources found\" rather than a hard ERROR. Do not flag this as a bug or suggest propagating the OSError.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:19:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:19:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935717160","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935717160"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935717160"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935717160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":4,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616378,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721087","pull_request_review_id":3949203669,"id":2935721087,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-4x_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,524 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+Cypilot Workspace - Multi-repo federation support.\n+\n+Loads and validates .cypilot-workspace.toml (standalone or inline in core.toml).\n+Each source maps a named repo to a local path, optional adapter location, and a role.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-datamodel\n+from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+import re\n+\n+from ..constants import WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+from . import toml_utils\n+\n+# Valid source roles\n+VALID_ROLES = {\"artifacts\", \"codebase\", \"kits\", \"full\"}\n+\n+# Source name validation: alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores, dots only\n+_SOURCE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$\")\n+\n+\n+def validate_source_name(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Validate a workspace source name. Returns error message or None.\"\"\"\n+    if not name:\n+        return \"Source name cannot be empty\"\n+    if not _SOURCE_NAME_RE.match(name):\n+        return (\n+            f\"Invalid source name '{name}' — \"\n+            \"must start with alphanumeric and contain only [A-Za-z0-9._-]\"\n+        )\n+    if \"..\" in name:\n+        return f\"Invalid source name '{name}' — must not contain '..'\"\n+    return None\n+\n+_CONFIG_FILENAME = \"core.toml\"\n+\n+\n+def _resolve_config_path(project_root: Path, cypilot_rel: str) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"Resolve the config file path, preferring config/ subdirectory.\"\"\"\n+    config_path = (project_root / cypilot_rel / \"config\" / _CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve()\n+    if not config_path.is_file():\n+        config_path = (project_root / cypilot_rel / _CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve()\n+    return config_path\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class SourceEntry:\n+    \"\"\"A named source repo in the workspace.\"\"\"\n+\n+    name: str\n+    path: Optional[str] = None  # Filesystem path (resolved relative to workspace file location)\n+    adapter: Optional[str] = None  # Path to adapter dir within the source, or None\n+    role: str = \"full\"  # \"artifacts\" | \"codebase\" | \"kits\" | \"full\"\n+    url: Optional[str] = None  # Git remote URL (HTTPS or SSH)\n+    branch: Optional[str] = None  # Git branch/ref to checkout\n+\n+    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n+        self.path = (self.path.strip() or None) if self.path else None\n+        self.url = (self.url.strip() or None) if self.url else None\n+        self.branch = (self.branch.strip() or None) if self.branch else None\n+        if self.role not in VALID_ROLES:\n+            raise ValueError(\n+                f\"Source '{self.name}' has invalid role '{self.role}' \"\n+                f\"(valid: {', '.join(sorted(VALID_ROLES))})\"\n+            )\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, name: str, data: dict) -> \"SourceEntry\":\n+        raw_path = str((data or {}).get(\"path\", \"\")).strip() or None\n+        raw_adapter = (data or {}).get(\"adapter\", None)\n+        # Omitted key means no adapter (TOML has no null)\n+        adapter = str(raw_adapter).strip() if isinstance(raw_adapter, str) and str(raw_adapter).strip() else None\n+        raw_role = str((data or {}).get(\"role\", \"full\")).strip().lower()\n+        raw_url = (data or {}).get(\"url\", None)\n+        url = str(raw_url).strip() if isinstance(raw_url, str) and str(raw_url).strip() else None\n+        raw_branch = (data or {}).get(\"branch\", None)\n+        branch = str(raw_branch).strip() if isinstance(raw_branch, str) and str(raw_branch).strip() else None\n+        return cls(name=name, path=raw_path, adapter=adapter, role=raw_role, url=url, branch=branch)\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {}\n+        if self.url is not None:\n+            d[\"url\"] = self.url\n+        if self.branch is not None:\n+            d[\"branch\"] = self.branch\n+        if self.path:\n+            d[\"path\"] = self.path\n+        if self.adapter is not None:\n+            d[\"adapter\"] = self.adapter\n+        if self.role != \"full\":\n+            d[\"role\"] = self.role\n+        return d\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+@dataclass\n+class TraceabilityConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Workspace-level traceability settings.\"\"\"\n+\n+    cross_repo: bool = True\n+    resolve_remote_ids: bool = True\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"TraceabilityConfig\":\n+        return cls(\n+            cross_repo=bool((data or {}).get(\"cross_repo\", True)),\n+            resolve_remote_ids=bool((data or {}).get(\"resolve_remote_ids\", True)),\n+        )\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        return {\n+            \"cross_repo\": self.cross_repo,\n+            \"resolve_remote_ids\": self.resolve_remote_ids,\n+        }\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class NamespaceRule:\n+    \"\"\"Maps a Git host to a local directory template.\"\"\"\n+\n+    host: str  # e.g. \"gitlab.com\"\n+    template: str  # e.g. \"{org}/{repo}\"\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        return {\"host\": self.host, \"template\": self.template}\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class ResolveConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Workspace-level git URL resolution settings.\"\"\"\n+\n+    workdir: str = \".workspace-sources\"\n+    namespace: List[\"NamespaceRule\"] = field(default_factory=list)\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"ResolveConfig\":\n+        workdir = str((data or {}).get(\"workdir\", \".workspace-sources\")).strip()\n+        raw_ns = (data or {}).get(\"namespace\", {})\n+        namespace: List[NamespaceRule] = []\n+        if isinstance(raw_ns, dict):\n+            for host, template in raw_ns.items():\n+                if isinstance(host, str) and isinstance(template, str):\n+                    namespace.append(NamespaceRule(host=host.strip(), template=template.strip()))\n+        return cls(workdir=workdir, namespace=namespace)\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {\"workdir\": self.workdir}\n+        if self.namespace:\n+            d[\"namespace\"] = {r.host: r.template for r in self.namespace}\n+        return d\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-find-config:p1:inst-find-config-datamodel\n+@dataclass\n+class WorkspaceConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Parsed workspace configuration.\"\"\"\n+\n+    version: str = \"1.0\"\n+    sources: Dict[str, SourceEntry] = field(default_factory=dict)\n+    traceability: TraceabilityConfig = field(default_factory=TraceabilityConfig)\n+    resolve: Optional[ResolveConfig] = None  # Git URL resolution config\n+    workspace_file: Optional[Path] = None  # Absolute path to the workspace file\n+    is_inline: bool = False  # True if loaded from core.toml inline workspace\n+    resolution_base: Optional[Path] = None  # Override for source path resolution base directory\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(\n+        cls,\n+        data: dict,\n+        *,\n+        workspace_file: Optional[Path] = None,\n+        is_inline: bool = False,\n+        resolution_base: Optional[Path] = None,\n+    ) -> \"WorkspaceConfig\":\n+        version = str((data or {}).get(\"version\", \"1.0\")).strip()\n+        sources: Dict[str, SourceEntry] = {}\n+        raw_sources = (data or {}).get(\"sources\", {})\n+        if not isinstance(raw_sources, dict):\n+            raise ValueError(\"'sources' must be a mapping\")\n+        for name, src_data in raw_sources.items():\n+            if not isinstance(src_data, dict):\n+                raise ValueError(f\"Source '{name}' must be a table, got {type(src_data).__name__}\")\n+            if isinstance(name, str) and name.strip():\n+                sources[name.strip()] = SourceEntry.from_dict(name.strip(), src_data)\n+\n+        traceability = TraceabilityConfig()\n+        raw_trace = (data or {}).get(\"traceability\", None)\n+        if isinstance(raw_trace, dict):\n+            traceability = TraceabilityConfig.from_dict(raw_trace)\n+\n+        resolve_cfg: Optional[ResolveConfig] = None\n+        raw_resolve = (data or {}).get(\"resolve\", None)\n+        if isinstance(raw_resolve, dict):\n+            resolve_cfg = ResolveConfig.from_dict(raw_resolve)\n+\n+        return cls(\n+            version=version,\n+            sources=sources,\n+            traceability=traceability,\n+            resolve=resolve_cfg,\n+            workspace_file=workspace_file,\n+            is_inline=is_inline,\n+            resolution_base=resolution_base,\n+        )\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {\"version\": self.version}\n+        d[\"sources\"] = {name: src.to_dict() for name, src in self.sources.items()}\n+        trace = self.traceability.to_dict()\n+        if trace != TraceabilityConfig().to_dict():\n+            d[\"traceability\"] = trace\n+        if self.resolve is not None:\n+            d[\"resolve\"] = self.resolve.to_dict()\n+        return d\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def load(cls, workspace_path: Path) -> Tuple[Optional[\"WorkspaceConfig\"], Optional[str]]:\n+        \"\"\"Load workspace config from a TOML file.\n+\n+        Args:\n+            workspace_path: Absolute path to .cypilot-workspace.toml\n+\n+        Returns:\n+            (WorkspaceConfig, None) on success or (None, error_message) on failure.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        if not workspace_path.is_file():\n+            return None, f\"Workspace file not found: {workspace_path}\"\n+        try:\n+            data = toml_utils.load(workspace_path)\n+        except Exception as e:\n+            return None, f\"Failed to read workspace file {workspace_path}: {e}\"\n+        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace file (expected TOML table): {workspace_path}\"\n+        if \"version\" not in data:\n+            return None, f\"Missing required field 'version' in {workspace_path}\"\n+        if \"sources\" not in data:\n+            return None, f\"Missing required field 'sources' in {workspace_path}\"\n+        try:\n+            cfg = cls.from_dict(data, workspace_file=workspace_path.resolve(), is_inline=False)\n+        except ValueError as e:\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace config in {workspace_path}: {e}\"\n+        errs = cfg.validate()\n+        if errs:\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace config in {workspace_path}: {'; '.join(errs)}\"\n+        return cfg, None\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-find-config:p1:inst-find-config-datamodel\n+\n+    # @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1\n+    def resolve_source_path(self, source_name: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+        \"\"\"Resolve the absolute filesystem path for a named source.\n+\n+        For standalone workspace files, paths resolve relative to the file's\n+        parent directory.  For inline workspaces (defined in core.toml),\n+        paths resolve relative to the project root (set via resolution_base).\n+        For git URL sources, delegates to git_utils.resolve_git_source().\n+        \"\"\"\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-lookup\n+        src = self.sources.get(source_name)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-lookup\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-if-not-found\n+        if src is None:\n+            return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-if-not-found\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-determine-base\n+        if self.resolution_base is not None:\n+            base = self.resolution_base\n+        elif self.workspace_file is not None:\n+            base = self.workspace_file.parent\n+        else:\n+            return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-determine-base\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-return\n+        if src.path:\n+            return (base / src.path).resolve()\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-return\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        if src.url:\n+            from .git_utils import resolve_git_source\n+            return resolve_git_source(src, self.resolve or ResolveConfig(), base)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-fallback\n+        return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-fallback\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-methods\n+    def resolve_source_adapter(self, source_name: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+        \"\"\"Resolve the absolute path to a source's adapter directory.\"\"\"\n+        src = self.sources.get(source_name)\n+        if src is None or not src.adapter:\n+            return None\n+        source_root = self.resolve_source_path(source_name)\n+        if source_root is None:\n+            return None\n+        return (source_root / src.adapter).resolve()\n+\n+    def validate(self) -> List[str]:\n+        \"\"\"Validate workspace config and return list of error messages.\"\"\"\n+        errors: List[str] = []\n+        for name, src in self.sources.items():\n+            if src.url and self.is_inline:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has 'url' but inline workspaces only support local paths\")\n+            if src.path and src.url:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has both 'path' and 'url' — they are mutually exclusive\")\n+            if src.path and src.branch:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has both 'path' and 'branch' — branch is only valid with 'url'\")\n+            if not src.path and not src.url:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' must have either 'path' or 'url'\")\n+            if src.role not in VALID_ROLES:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has invalid role '{src.role}' (valid: {', '.join(sorted(VALID_ROLES))})\")\n+        return errors","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Low practical impact. All programmatic entry points already enforce name validity: workspace-add calls `validate_source_name()` before adding, and workspace-init uses `_sanitize_source_name()` to auto-clean discovered names. Invalid names in `WorkspaceConfig.validate()` would only arise from manual TOML file editing, where TOML's own bare-key syntax already constrains most problematic characters. Adding the check to validate() is technically correct but adds complexity for a scenario that doesn't occur through normal usage.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:22:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:22:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935721087","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721087"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935721087"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721087/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":303,"original_start_line":303,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":317,"original_line":317,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616374,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":317,"position":317,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721855","pull_request_review_id":3949204152,"id":2935721855,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-49_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,524 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+Cypilot Workspace - Multi-repo federation support.\n+\n+Loads and validates .cypilot-workspace.toml (standalone or inline in core.toml).\n+Each source maps a named repo to a local path, optional adapter location, and a role.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-datamodel\n+from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+import re\n+\n+from ..constants import WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+from . import toml_utils\n+\n+# Valid source roles\n+VALID_ROLES = {\"artifacts\", \"codebase\", \"kits\", \"full\"}\n+\n+# Source name validation: alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores, dots only\n+_SOURCE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$\")\n+\n+\n+def validate_source_name(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Validate a workspace source name. Returns error message or None.\"\"\"\n+    if not name:\n+        return \"Source name cannot be empty\"\n+    if not _SOURCE_NAME_RE.match(name):\n+        return (\n+            f\"Invalid source name '{name}' — \"\n+            \"must start with alphanumeric and contain only [A-Za-z0-9._-]\"\n+        )\n+    if \"..\" in name:\n+        return f\"Invalid source name '{name}' — must not contain '..'\"\n+    return None\n+\n+_CONFIG_FILENAME = \"core.toml\"\n+\n+\n+def _resolve_config_path(project_root: Path, cypilot_rel: str) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"Resolve the config file path, preferring config/ subdirectory.\"\"\"\n+    config_path = (project_root / cypilot_rel / \"config\" / _CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve()\n+    if not config_path.is_file():\n+        config_path = (project_root / cypilot_rel / _CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve()\n+    return config_path\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class SourceEntry:\n+    \"\"\"A named source repo in the workspace.\"\"\"\n+\n+    name: str\n+    path: Optional[str] = None  # Filesystem path (resolved relative to workspace file location)\n+    adapter: Optional[str] = None  # Path to adapter dir within the source, or None\n+    role: str = \"full\"  # \"artifacts\" | \"codebase\" | \"kits\" | \"full\"\n+    url: Optional[str] = None  # Git remote URL (HTTPS or SSH)\n+    branch: Optional[str] = None  # Git branch/ref to checkout\n+\n+    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n+        self.path = (self.path.strip() or None) if self.path else None\n+        self.url = (self.url.strip() or None) if self.url else None\n+        self.branch = (self.branch.strip() or None) if self.branch else None\n+        if self.role not in VALID_ROLES:\n+            raise ValueError(\n+                f\"Source '{self.name}' has invalid role '{self.role}' \"\n+                f\"(valid: {', '.join(sorted(VALID_ROLES))})\"\n+            )\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, name: str, data: dict) -> \"SourceEntry\":\n+        raw_path = str((data or {}).get(\"path\", \"\")).strip() or None\n+        raw_adapter = (data or {}).get(\"adapter\", None)\n+        # Omitted key means no adapter (TOML has no null)\n+        adapter = str(raw_adapter).strip() if isinstance(raw_adapter, str) and str(raw_adapter).strip() else None\n+        raw_role = str((data or {}).get(\"role\", \"full\")).strip().lower()\n+        raw_url = (data or {}).get(\"url\", None)\n+        url = str(raw_url).strip() if isinstance(raw_url, str) and str(raw_url).strip() else None\n+        raw_branch = (data or {}).get(\"branch\", None)\n+        branch = str(raw_branch).strip() if isinstance(raw_branch, str) and str(raw_branch).strip() else None\n+        return cls(name=name, path=raw_path, adapter=adapter, role=raw_role, url=url, branch=branch)\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {}\n+        if self.url is not None:\n+            d[\"url\"] = self.url\n+        if self.branch is not None:\n+            d[\"branch\"] = self.branch\n+        if self.path:\n+            d[\"path\"] = self.path\n+        if self.adapter is not None:\n+            d[\"adapter\"] = self.adapter\n+        if self.role != \"full\":\n+            d[\"role\"] = self.role\n+        return d\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+@dataclass\n+class TraceabilityConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Workspace-level traceability settings.\"\"\"\n+\n+    cross_repo: bool = True\n+    resolve_remote_ids: bool = True\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"TraceabilityConfig\":\n+        return cls(\n+            cross_repo=bool((data or {}).get(\"cross_repo\", True)),\n+            resolve_remote_ids=bool((data or {}).get(\"resolve_remote_ids\", True)),\n+        )\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        return {\n+            \"cross_repo\": self.cross_repo,\n+            \"resolve_remote_ids\": self.resolve_remote_ids,\n+        }\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class NamespaceRule:\n+    \"\"\"Maps a Git host to a local directory template.\"\"\"\n+\n+    host: str  # e.g. \"gitlab.com\"\n+    template: str  # e.g. \"{org}/{repo}\"\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        return {\"host\": self.host, \"template\": self.template}\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class ResolveConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Workspace-level git URL resolution settings.\"\"\"\n+\n+    workdir: str = \".workspace-sources\"\n+    namespace: List[\"NamespaceRule\"] = field(default_factory=list)\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"ResolveConfig\":\n+        workdir = str((data or {}).get(\"workdir\", \".workspace-sources\")).strip()\n+        raw_ns = (data or {}).get(\"namespace\", {})\n+        namespace: List[NamespaceRule] = []\n+        if isinstance(raw_ns, dict):\n+            for host, template in raw_ns.items():\n+                if isinstance(host, str) and isinstance(template, str):\n+                    namespace.append(NamespaceRule(host=host.strip(), template=template.strip()))\n+        return cls(workdir=workdir, namespace=namespace)\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {\"workdir\": self.workdir}\n+        if self.namespace:\n+            d[\"namespace\"] = {r.host: r.template for r in self.namespace}\n+        return d\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-git-datamodel\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-find-config:p1:inst-find-config-datamodel\n+@dataclass\n+class WorkspaceConfig:\n+    \"\"\"Parsed workspace configuration.\"\"\"\n+\n+    version: str = \"1.0\"\n+    sources: Dict[str, SourceEntry] = field(default_factory=dict)\n+    traceability: TraceabilityConfig = field(default_factory=TraceabilityConfig)\n+    resolve: Optional[ResolveConfig] = None  # Git URL resolution config\n+    workspace_file: Optional[Path] = None  # Absolute path to the workspace file\n+    is_inline: bool = False  # True if loaded from core.toml inline workspace\n+    resolution_base: Optional[Path] = None  # Override for source path resolution base directory\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def from_dict(\n+        cls,\n+        data: dict,\n+        *,\n+        workspace_file: Optional[Path] = None,\n+        is_inline: bool = False,\n+        resolution_base: Optional[Path] = None,\n+    ) -> \"WorkspaceConfig\":\n+        version = str((data or {}).get(\"version\", \"1.0\")).strip()\n+        sources: Dict[str, SourceEntry] = {}\n+        raw_sources = (data or {}).get(\"sources\", {})\n+        if not isinstance(raw_sources, dict):\n+            raise ValueError(\"'sources' must be a mapping\")\n+        for name, src_data in raw_sources.items():\n+            if not isinstance(src_data, dict):\n+                raise ValueError(f\"Source '{name}' must be a table, got {type(src_data).__name__}\")\n+            if isinstance(name, str) and name.strip():\n+                sources[name.strip()] = SourceEntry.from_dict(name.strip(), src_data)\n+\n+        traceability = TraceabilityConfig()\n+        raw_trace = (data or {}).get(\"traceability\", None)\n+        if isinstance(raw_trace, dict):\n+            traceability = TraceabilityConfig.from_dict(raw_trace)\n+\n+        resolve_cfg: Optional[ResolveConfig] = None\n+        raw_resolve = (data or {}).get(\"resolve\", None)\n+        if isinstance(raw_resolve, dict):\n+            resolve_cfg = ResolveConfig.from_dict(raw_resolve)\n+\n+        return cls(\n+            version=version,\n+            sources=sources,\n+            traceability=traceability,\n+            resolve=resolve_cfg,\n+            workspace_file=workspace_file,\n+            is_inline=is_inline,\n+            resolution_base=resolution_base,\n+        )\n+\n+    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n+        d: dict = {\"version\": self.version}\n+        d[\"sources\"] = {name: src.to_dict() for name, src in self.sources.items()}\n+        trace = self.traceability.to_dict()\n+        if trace != TraceabilityConfig().to_dict():\n+            d[\"traceability\"] = trace\n+        if self.resolve is not None:\n+            d[\"resolve\"] = self.resolve.to_dict()\n+        return d\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def load(cls, workspace_path: Path) -> Tuple[Optional[\"WorkspaceConfig\"], Optional[str]]:\n+        \"\"\"Load workspace config from a TOML file.\n+\n+        Args:\n+            workspace_path: Absolute path to .cypilot-workspace.toml\n+\n+        Returns:\n+            (WorkspaceConfig, None) on success or (None, error_message) on failure.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        if not workspace_path.is_file():\n+            return None, f\"Workspace file not found: {workspace_path}\"\n+        try:\n+            data = toml_utils.load(workspace_path)\n+        except Exception as e:\n+            return None, f\"Failed to read workspace file {workspace_path}: {e}\"\n+        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace file (expected TOML table): {workspace_path}\"\n+        if \"version\" not in data:\n+            return None, f\"Missing required field 'version' in {workspace_path}\"\n+        if \"sources\" not in data:\n+            return None, f\"Missing required field 'sources' in {workspace_path}\"\n+        try:\n+            cfg = cls.from_dict(data, workspace_file=workspace_path.resolve(), is_inline=False)\n+        except ValueError as e:\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace config in {workspace_path}: {e}\"\n+        errs = cfg.validate()\n+        if errs:\n+            return None, f\"Invalid workspace config in {workspace_path}: {'; '.join(errs)}\"\n+        return cfg, None\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-find-config:p1:inst-find-config-datamodel\n+\n+    # @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1\n+    def resolve_source_path(self, source_name: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+        \"\"\"Resolve the absolute filesystem path for a named source.\n+\n+        For standalone workspace files, paths resolve relative to the file's\n+        parent directory.  For inline workspaces (defined in core.toml),\n+        paths resolve relative to the project root (set via resolution_base).\n+        For git URL sources, delegates to git_utils.resolve_git_source().\n+        \"\"\"\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-lookup\n+        src = self.sources.get(source_name)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-lookup\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-if-not-found\n+        if src is None:\n+            return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-if-not-found\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-determine-base\n+        if self.resolution_base is not None:\n+            base = self.resolution_base\n+        elif self.workspace_file is not None:\n+            base = self.workspace_file.parent\n+        else:\n+            return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-determine-base\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-return\n+        if src.path:\n+            return (base / src.path).resolve()\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-return\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        if src.url:\n+            from .git_utils import resolve_git_source\n+            return resolve_git_source(src, self.resolve or ResolveConfig(), base)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-git-url:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-git-url-delegate\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-fallback\n+        return None\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-source:p1:inst-resolve-fallback\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-state-workspace-config-lifecycle:p1:inst-config-methods\n+    def resolve_source_adapter(self, source_name: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n+        \"\"\"Resolve the absolute path to a source's adapter directory.\"\"\"\n+        src = self.sources.get(source_name)\n+        if src is None or not src.adapter:\n+            return None\n+        source_root = self.resolve_source_path(source_name)\n+        if source_root is None:\n+            return None\n+        return (source_root / src.adapter).resolve()\n+\n+    def validate(self) -> List[str]:\n+        \"\"\"Validate workspace config and return list of error messages.\"\"\"\n+        errors: List[str] = []\n+        for name, src in self.sources.items():\n+            if src.url and self.is_inline:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has 'url' but inline workspaces only support local paths\")\n+            if src.path and src.url:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has both 'path' and 'url' — they are mutually exclusive\")\n+            if src.path and src.branch:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has both 'path' and 'branch' — branch is only valid with 'url'\")\n+            if not src.path and not src.url:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' must have either 'path' or 'url'\")\n+            if src.role not in VALID_ROLES:\n+                errors.append(f\"Source '{name}' has invalid role '{src.role}' (valid: {', '.join(sorted(VALID_ROLES))})\")\n+        return errors","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, understood — that's a reasonable design choice. Since all programmatic entry points already guard name validity (either via `validate_source_name()` in `workspace-add` or `_sanitize_source_name()` in `workspace-init`), the `validate()` method would only catch names introduced through direct manual TOML edits, which TOML's own key-syntax rules already constrain. The layered enforcement at the entry points is sufficient.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py:303-317\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T19:23:05.638Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py` (and its `.bootstrap` mirror), `WorkspaceConfig.validate()` intentionally does NOT call `validate_source_name()` on source keys. All programmatic entry points already enforce name validity: `workspace-add` calls `validate_source_name()` before insertion, and `workspace-init` uses `_sanitize_source_name()` to auto-clean discovered names. Invalid names in `validate()` would only arise from manual TOML edits, where TOML's bare-key syntax already constrains most problematic characters. Do not flag the absence of `validate_source_name()` inside `WorkspaceConfig.validate()` as a bug.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md:66-70\nTimestamp: 2026-03-10T07:24:10.352Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`, `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order:\n1. Checks for a `workspace` key in `core.toml` (string path to external file, or inline dict).\n2. Falls back to auto-discovering a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` via `_find_standalone_workspace`.\n\nThere is NO parent directory traversal beyond `project_root`. A standalone workspace file placed at `project_root` is auto-discovered without requiring an explicit `workspace` key in `core.toml`. Do not suggest that all workspace locations must be explicitly configured — the project-root fallback is intentional.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py:48-51\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T17:01:08.042Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py`, the `if not reachable:` block in `_build_source_info` (lines 49–56) already handles both URL-only and path-only sources: URL sources display a redacted URL with a 'workspace-sync' hint via `_redact_url(src.url)`; path-only sources use `identifier = src.path or name` to prevent None in the warning. `checkout_path` does not exist on `SourceEntry`. Do not flag the warning message as potentially showing \"None\".\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py:187-193\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T11:25:08.406Z\nLearning: In `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py`, the `_compute_local_path()` function intentionally trusts `resolve_config.workdir` as-is (including absolute paths or paths with `..`), because it is a direct user configuration value. The `local_path.relative_to(expected_base)` containment check is there to guard against malicious `org`/`repo` segments derived from parsed Git URLs, not against the user's own workspace layout. Do not suggest validating or sanitizing `workdir` for path traversal — it is the intended configuration mechanism.\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:23:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:23:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935721855","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721855"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935721855"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935721855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":303,"original_start_line":303,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":317,"original_line":317,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616374,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":317,"position":317,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724537","pull_request_review_id":3949206112,"id":2935724537,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-5n5","diff_hunk":"@@ -1030,6 +1030,28 @@ def headings_info_for_kind(kind: str, heading_ids: Sequence[str]) -> List[Dict[s\n                     refs_by_system_kind.setdefault(system, {}).setdefault(ak, []).append(row)\n     # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-build-index\n \n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-duplicate-defs\n+    # Detect duplicate ID definitions across different artifact files\n+    for did, drows in defs_by_id.items():\n+        if len(drows) < 2:\n+            continue\n+        # Group by artifact path — same ID in the same file is not a cross-file collision\n+        paths = {str(d.get(\"artifact_path\", \"\")) for d in drows}\n+        if len(paths) < 2:\n+            continue\n+        sorted_paths = sorted(paths)\n+        for d in drows:\n+            other_paths = [p for p in sorted_paths if p != str(d.get(\"artifact_path\", \"\"))]\n+            errors.append(error(\n+                \"structure\",\n+                f\"Duplicate definition of `{did}` — also defined in: {', '.join(other_paths)}\",\n+                code=EC.DUPLICATE_DEFINITION,\n+                path=d.get(\"artifact_path\"),\n+                line=int(d.get(\"line\", 1) or 1),\n+                id=did,\n+            ))\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-duplicate-defs","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/constraints.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is standard cascading-error behavior for validators. The follow-on checks (`REF_DONE_DEF_NOT_DONE`, `DEF_DONE_REF_NOT_DONE`) are technically correct even with duplicates — they iterate all definitions and the done-status logic handles multi-def cases by design. Filtering duplicate IDs from subsequent passes would suppress validation of done-status consistency for those IDs entirely, potentially hiding real issues. The `DUPLICATE_DEFINITION` error surfaces first and signals the user to fix that before interpreting follow-on results — same pattern as compilers reporting cascading errors.","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:25:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:25:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935724537","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724537"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935724537"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724537/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":1033,"original_start_line":1033,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1053,"original_line":1053,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616373,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":24,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724969","pull_request_review_id":3949206488,"id":2935724969,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u-5up","diff_hunk":"@@ -1030,6 +1030,28 @@ def headings_info_for_kind(kind: str, heading_ids: Sequence[str]) -> List[Dict[s\n                     refs_by_system_kind.setdefault(system, {}).setdefault(ak, []).append(row)\n     # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-build-index\n \n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-duplicate-defs\n+    # Detect duplicate ID definitions across different artifact files\n+    for did, drows in defs_by_id.items():\n+        if len(drows) < 2:\n+            continue\n+        # Group by artifact path — same ID in the same file is not a cross-file collision\n+        paths = {str(d.get(\"artifact_path\", \"\")) for d in drows}\n+        if len(paths) < 2:\n+            continue\n+        sorted_paths = sorted(paths)\n+        for d in drows:\n+            other_paths = [p for p in sorted_paths if p != str(d.get(\"artifact_path\", \"\"))]\n+            errors.append(error(\n+                \"structure\",\n+                f\"Duplicate definition of `{did}` — also defined in: {', '.join(other_paths)}\",\n+                code=EC.DUPLICATE_DEFINITION,\n+                path=d.get(\"artifact_path\"),\n+                line=int(d.get(\"line\", 1) or 1),\n+                id=did,\n+            ))\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-traceability-validation-cross-validate:p1:inst-duplicate-defs","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/constraints.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nonameffh`, that's a fair and clear rationale — the cascading-error model is well-established in validators and compilers (GCC, clang, tsc all exhibit this), and preserving done-status checks on duplicate-defined IDs does leave the user with actionable signal rather than silently dropping those checks. The `DUPLICATE_DEFINITION` entry acting as a sentinel to contextualize follow-on results makes sense in that framing. I'll defer to your judgment here.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: nonameffh\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 81\nFile: .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/constraints.py:1033-1053\nTimestamp: 2026-03-14T19:25:54.113Z\nLearning: In `cross_validate_artifacts()` in `.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/constraints.py`, duplicate-definition detection (DUPLICATE_DEFINITION) intentionally uses a cascading-error pattern: follow-on checks like `REF_DONE_DEF_NOT_DONE` and `DEF_DONE_REF_NOT_DONE` are preserved even for IDs that triggered DUPLICATE_DEFINITION, because the done-status logic handles multi-definition cases by design and suppressing those checks would hide real issues. The DUPLICATE_DEFINITION error surfaces first, signaling the user to fix it before interpreting follow-on results — same model as compiler cascading errors.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot workflows: pr-review and pr-status\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyber-pilot PR: 0\nFile: .cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-03-12T20:32:03.813Z\nLearning: Support Cypilot artifacts including: ADR, CODEBASE, DECOMPOSITION, DESIGN, FEATURE, PR-CODE-REVIEW-TEMPLATE, PR-REVIEW, PR-STATUS-REPORT-TEMPLATE, PRD\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:25:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:25:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935724969","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724969"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935724969"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935724969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1033,"original_start_line":1033,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1053,"original_line":1053,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2935616373,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":24,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935743788","pull_request_review_id":3949220039,"id":2935743788,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6u--Us","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,465 @@\n+\"\"\"\n+workspace-init: Initialize a new workspace by scanning nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\n+\"\"\"\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-feature-workspace:p1\n+# @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-helpers\n+import argparse\n+import os\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n+\n+from ..utils.ui import ui\n+\n+\n+def _is_project_dir(entry: Path) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Check if a directory looks like a project (has .git or AGENTS.md with marker).\"\"\"\n+    if (entry / \".git\").exists():\n+        return True\n+    agents_file = entry / \"AGENTS.md\"\n+    if not agents_file.is_file():\n+        return False\n+    try:\n+        head = agents_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")[:512]\n+        return \"<!-- @cpt:root-agents -->\" in head\n+    except OSError:\n+        return False\n+\n+\n+def _find_adapter_path(entry: Path) -> Optional[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Find the adapter path for a project directory.\"\"\"\n+    from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory, _read_cypilot_var\n+\n+    # v3 discovery: read cypilot_path variable from AGENTS.md\n+    cypilot_rel = _read_cypilot_var(entry)\n+    if cypilot_rel:\n+        candidate = (entry / cypilot_rel).resolve()\n+        if candidate.is_dir() and (candidate / \"config\").is_dir():\n+            return cypilot_rel\n+\n+    # Fallback: try find_cypilot_directory for recursive search\n+    found_dir = find_cypilot_directory(entry)\n+    if found_dir is not None:\n+        try:\n+            return str(found_dir.relative_to(entry))\n+        except ValueError:\n+            return str(found_dir)\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _compute_source_path(entry: Path, output_dir: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Compute relative source path from the output location.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        return Path(os.path.relpath(entry, output_dir)).as_posix()\n+    except ValueError:\n+        # Windows: entry and output_dir are on different drives\n+        return entry.resolve().as_posix()\n+# @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-helpers\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1\n+def _infer_role(repo_path: Path) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Best-effort role inference from directory contents.\"\"\"\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    has_src = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"src\", \"lib\", \"app\", \"pkg\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-src\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    has_docs = any((repo_path / d).is_dir() for d in [\"docs\", \"architecture\", \"requirements\"])\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-docs\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+    has_kits = (repo_path / \"kits\").is_dir()\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-check-kits\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-multi\n+    capabilities = sum((has_src, has_docs, has_kits))\n+    if capabilities > 1:\n+        return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-multi\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    if has_kits:\n+        return \"kits\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-kits\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    if has_docs:\n+        return \"artifacts\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-artifacts\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    if has_src:\n+        return \"codebase\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-if-codebase\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+    return \"full\"\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-infer-role:p1:inst-role-return-full\n+\n+\n+def _sanitize_source_name(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Sanitize an auto-discovered source name to safe characters.\"\"\"\n+    import re\n+    # Replace unsafe characters with hyphens\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]\", \"-\", name)\n+    # Strip leading non-alphanumeric characters\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"^[^A-Za-z0-9]+\", \"\", sanitized)\n+    # Collapse consecutive hyphens\n+    sanitized = re.sub(r\"-{2,}\", \"-\", sanitized)\n+    return sanitized or \"source\"\n+\n+\n+def _dedup_source_key(key: str, existing: Dict[str, dict], new_path: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Return a unique source key, warning on collision.\"\"\"\n+    key = _sanitize_source_name(key)\n+    if key not in existing:\n+        return key\n+    n = 2\n+    while f\"{key}-{n}\" in existing:\n+        n += 1\n+    new_key = f\"{key}-{n}\"\n+    print(\n+        f\"Warning: source name '{key}' collision — \"\n+        f\"'{new_path}' conflicts with '{existing[key].get('path', '?')}'; \"\n+        f\"renaming to '{new_key}'\",\n+        file=sys.stderr,\n+    )\n+    return new_key\n+\n+\n+# @cpt-algo:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1\n+def _scan_nested_repos(\n+    scan_root: Path,\n+    output_dir: Path,\n+    max_depth: int = 3,\n+    _current_depth: int = 1,\n+) -> Dict[str, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Scan nested sub-directories for repos with adapters.\"\"\"\n+    discovered: Dict[str, dict] = {}\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-depth\n+    if _current_depth > max_depth:\n+        return discovered\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-depth\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+    try:\n+        entries = sorted(scan_root.iterdir(), key=lambda p: p.name)\n+    except OSError as exc:\n+        print(f\"Warning: cannot scan {scan_root}: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        entries = []\n+    # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-list-entries\n+\n+    # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+    for entry in entries:\n+        if not entry.is_dir() or entry.name.startswith(\".\") or entry.is_symlink():\n+            continue\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-foreach-entry\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+        if not _is_project_dir(entry):\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-check-project\n+            # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+            # Not a project — recurse into subdirectory\n+            nested = _scan_nested_repos(entry, output_dir, max_depth, _current_depth + 1)\n+            for nkey, ninfo in nested.items():\n+                nkey = _dedup_source_key(nkey, discovered, ninfo.get(\"path\", \"?\"))\n+                discovered[nkey] = ninfo\n+            continue\n+            # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-not-project\n+\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        adapter_path = _find_adapter_path(entry)\n+        # @cpt-end:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n+        # @cpt-begin:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n+        if not adapter_path:\n+            continue","path":".bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py","commit_id":"9f1bd09558f424b565e977a1d2160e7304c3390c","original_commit_id":"68de967b4d86a467fa59ff89ded3aac49971aebd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Keep descending when a repo boundary has no adapter.**\n\nOnce a directory matches `_is_project_dir()`, the scan stops treating it as a container. If that repo has no local adapter, this exits the subtree entirely, so deeper repos with adapters are never discovered.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Possible fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         adapter_path = _find_adapter_path(entry)\n         # `@cpt-end`:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-find-adapter\n         # `@cpt-begin`:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n         if not adapter_path:\n-            continue\n+            nested = _scan_nested_repos(entry, output_dir, max_depth, _current_depth + 1)\n+            for nkey, ninfo in nested.items():\n+                nkey = _dedup_source_key(nkey, discovered, ninfo.get(\"path\", \"?\"))\n+                discovered[nkey] = ninfo\n+            continue\n         # `@cpt-end`:cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-discover-nested:p1:inst-disc-if-no-adapter\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py\naround lines 152 - 168, The scan currently stops descending when\n_is_project_dir(entry) is true but _find_adapter_path(entry) returns falsy,\nwhich skips nested repos with adapters; instead, when adapter_path is falsy call\n_scan_nested_repos(entry, output_dir, max_depth, _current_depth + 1) and merge\nits results into discovered using _dedup_source_key (same pattern used above),\nthen continue—leave the existing handling when adapter_path exists intact so\nadapters are still registered.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:44:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:47:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935743788","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935743788"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935743788"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935743788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":152,"original_start_line":152,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":168,"original_line":168,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":168,"position":168,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repo