)` whenever not `--local-only`. This can still inject IDs from other sources in cases where cross-repo resolution is disabled by workspace config.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if not args.local_only and ws_ctx is not None:\n+    if not args.local_only and ws_ctx is not None and ws_ctx.cross_repo and ws_ctx.resolve_remote_ids:\n         artifact_ids.update(ws_ctx.get_all_artifact_ids())\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 517 - 518,\nThe code unconditionally merges workspace artifact IDs when not args.local_only\nby calling ws_ctx.get_all_artifact_ids(), which bypasses workspace traceability\nsettings; change the logic to first check the workspace's\ntraceability/cross-repo resolution flag on ws_ctx (e.g., a property like\nws_ctx.settings.allow_cross_repo_traceability or\nws_ctx.config.allow_cross_repo_resolution) and only call\nws_ctx.get_all_artifact_ids() and update artifact_ids when that flag allows\ncross-repo expansion, otherwise skip expansion; adjust the condition around\nargs.local_only and ws_ctx.get_all_artifact_ids() accordingly and add/update\ntests for both enabled and disabled traceability cases.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-14T19:44:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T19:51:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935743791","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2935743791"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#discussion_r2935743791"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/re