hting/parsing is correct.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`79-90`: **`--source` filter only applies to workspace sources, not primary.**\n\nWhen `--source` is specified but the context is not a `WorkspaceContext`, primary artifacts are still scanned without any indication that the filter had no effect. This could confuse users who expect to see only artifacts from the named source.\n\nConsider either:\n1. Emitting a warning when `--source` is specified but no workspace is active, or\n2. Also filtering primary artifacts when the source name matches the primary repo\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 79 - 90,\nThe --source filter is only applied inside WorkspaceContext, so when args.source\nis provided but ctx is not a WorkspaceContext primary artifacts still get\nscanned; update list_ids.py to detect this case and respond: if args.source is\nset and not isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext) either (a) emit a clear warning\nvia the existing logger/console that the --source filter was ignored because no\nworkspace context is active, or (b) alternatively apply the same name check to\nprimary artifact scanning (filter primary artifacts by args.source matching the\nprimary repo name); add the check near the existing WorkspaceContext branch that\nreferences ctx, args.source, and artifacts_to_scan so behavior is consistent and\nusers are informed when their filter has no effect.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`87-96`: **Duplicate import and redundant iteration.**\n\n`WorkspaceContext` is imported twice in the same function (line 73 and line 89). The second import is unnecessary.\n\nAdditionally, the `path_to_source` mapping iterates over the same workspace sources that were just processed in lines 72-81. These could be combined into a single loop for efficiency.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix: combine loops and remove duplicate import</summary>\n\n```diff\n         # Workspace: also scan artifacts from remote sources\n+        path_to_source: Dict[str, str] = {}\n         from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\n         if isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext):\n             for sc in ctx.sources.values():\n                 if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n                     continue\n                 for art, _sys in sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts():\n                     art_path = (sc.path / art.path).resolve()\n                     if art_path.exists():\n                         artifacts_to_scan.append((art_path, str(art.kind)))\n+                        path_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name\n\n     if not artifacts_to_scan:\n         print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": \"No Cypilot artifacts found in registry\"}, indent=None, ensure_ascii=False))\n         return 1\n\n-    # Build path-to-source mapping for workspace results\n-    path_to_source: Dict[str, str] = {}\n-    from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\n-    if isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext):\n-        for sc in ctx.sources.values():\n-            if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n-                continue\n-            for art, _sys in sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts():\n-                art_path = (sc.path / art.path).resolve()\n-                path_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name\n+    else:\n+        path_to_source = {}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py` around lines 87 - 96,\nRemove the duplicate import of WorkspaceContext and merge the two iterations\nover ctx.sources into one: keep a single import of WorkspaceContext at the top\nand inside the function iterate once over ctx.sources (use the existing loop\nthat checks sc.reachable and sc.meta) to both build the initial results and\npopulate the path_to_source dict; use sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts() within that\nsame loop to compute art_path and set path_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name so\nyou avoid redundant looping and the extra import.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`86-95`: **Duplicate import and redundant iteration (same issue as `where_used.py`).**\n\n`WorkspaceContext` is imported twice (line 72 and line 88), and the `path_to_source` mapping iterates over the same sources that were just processed in lines 71-80.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix: combine loops and remove duplicate import</summary>\n\n```diff\n         # Workspace: also scan artifacts from remote sources\n+        path_to_source: Dict[str, str] = {}\n         from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\n         if isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext):\n             for sc in ctx.sources.values():\n                 if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n                     continue\n                 for art, _sys in sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts():\n                     art_path = (sc.path / art.path).resolve()\n                     if art_path.exists():\n                         artifacts_to_scan.append((art_path, str(art.kind)))\n+                        path_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name\n\n     if not artifacts_to_scan:\n         print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": \"No Cypilot artifacts found in registry\"}, indent=None, ensure_ascii=False))\n         return 1\n\n-    # Build path-to-source mapping for workspace results\n-    path_to_source: Dict[str, str] = {}\n-    from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\n-    if isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext):\n-        for sc in ctx.sources.values():\n-            if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n-                continue\n-            for art, _sys in sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts():\n-                art_path = (sc.path / art.path).resolve()\n-                path_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name\n+    else:\n+        path_to_source = {}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py` around lines 86 -\n95, Remove the duplicate import of WorkspaceContext and merge the second loop\nthat builds path_to_source into the initial iteration over ctx.sources (the same\nloop used earlier) to avoid iterating sources twice; specifically, delete the\nextra \"from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\" and, inside the existing\nloop that visits each sc in ctx.sources (checking sc.reachable and sc.meta),\nalso populate the path_to_source dict by resolving (sc.path /\nart.path).resolve() and mapping str(art_path) to sc.name (using the existing\nsc.meta.iter_all_artifacts() call), keeping the same guards for sc.reachable and\nsc.meta.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py`:\n- Around line 84-90: The code currently swallows all exceptions when\nreading/parsing config_path (PROJECT_CONFIG_FILENAME) and sets existing = {},\nwhich can overwrite a malformed .cypilot-config.json; change the logic in the\nworkspace_add routine to first read raw_text = config_path.read_text(...) if the\nfile exists, attempt json.loads(raw_text) and only fall back to {} on a\nJSONDecodeError while preserving raw_text and raising or returning a structured\nerror instead of silently proceeding; do not overwrite the file when parsing\nfailed. Also wrap the write block that updates existing (the section that writes\nback to config_path) in a try/except that returns a structured JSON error object\non failure (include the exception message and original raw_text when available)\nrather than allowing a silent failure or partial overwrite. Ensure you reference\nconfig_path, PROJECT_CONFIG_FILENAME, existing, and the write routine so\nreviewers can locate the changes.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py`:\n- Around line 31-40: The current branch treating a missing or failed-to-parse\nworkspace the same hides parse errors; update the logic around\nfind_workspace_config (variables ws_cfg and ws_err) so that if ws_cfg is None\nand ws_err is set you emit an error status (e.g., \"WORKSPACE_ERROR\") with the\nws_err message and return a non-zero exit code (1), while preserving the\nexisting \"NO_WORKSPACE\" / exit 0 behavior only when ws_err is None; adjust the\nprinted JSON keys accordingly to include the error message and status.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`:\n- Around line 163-167: When resolving output_path in workspace_init, handle the\ncase where args.output is a directory and guard against write errors: if\nargs.output is provided and Path(args.output).is_dir() then set output_path to\nPath(args.output) / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME (otherwise resolve as before),\nensure parent directories exist (mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)), then\nperform the write inside a try/except catching OSError/IOError and log or print\nthe error and exit with non‑zero status; update the code that calls\noutput_path.write_text to use this guarded write and references to output_path,\nargs.output, scan_root and WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME to locate the changes.\n- Around line 142-147: The current try/except around reading config_path sets\nexisting = {} on any exception which can clobber a real config; change the read\nlogic in workspace_init so you only treat a missing file as {} but treat\nread/parse errors specially: catch specific exceptions (json.JSONDecodeError,\nUnicodeDecodeError, OSError) and set existing = None (or leave it unchanged) and\nemit a warning instead of defaulting to {}. Then ensure subsequent write/merge\nlogic only overwrites the file when isinstance(existing, dict) (or when user\nexplicitly confirms), so unreadable/invalid files are not silently replaced;\nreference the variables config_path and existing and the workspace_init flow\nwhen making this change.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py`:\n- Around line 266-268: The code ignores workspace load errors returned by\nfind_workspace_config(primary_ctx.project_root) by returning None when ws_cfg is\nNone and discarding ws_err; modify the logic around the call to\nfind_workspace_config so that when ws_cfg is None you surface or log ws_err\n(e.g., throw or log an informative error via the module logger or raise an\nexception) instead of silently falling back to single-repo mode; update the\nhandling in the surrounding function (where ws_cfg and ws_err are used) to\npropagate the error or include ws_err in the returned result so callers can\nreact appropriately.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/files.py`:\n- Line 12: The import statement at the top imports an unused symbol\nWORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME; remove WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME from the from\n..constants import list so it only imports ARTIFACTS_REGISTRY_FILENAME and\nPROJECT_CONFIG_FILENAME to eliminate the unused import and linter warning in\nskills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/files.py.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/SKILL.md`:\n- Around line 295-310: Update the SKILL.md command reference lines for the\ncypilot CLI so they list the missing supported flags: modify the workspace-init\nusage example in skills/cypilot/SKILL.md to include the --output <path> option\n(i.e., python3 {cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-init\n[--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--dry-run]) and update the\nworkspace-add-inline example to include the --adapter <path> flag (i.e., python3\n{cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add-inline --name\n<name> --path <path> [--role <role>] [--adapter <path]]), ensuring the command\nlines and surrounding docs reflect these supported options.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py`:\n- Around line 79-90: The --source filter is only applied inside\nWorkspaceContext, so when args.source is provided but ctx is not a\nWorkspaceContext primary artifacts still get scanned; update list_ids.py to\ndetect this case and respond: if args.source is set and not isinstance(ctx,\nWorkspaceContext) either (a) emit a clear warning via the existing\nlogger/console that the --source filter was ignored because no workspace context\nis active, or (b) alternatively apply the same name check to primary artifact\nscanning (filter primary artifacts by args.source matching the primary repo\nname); add the check near the existing WorkspaceContext branch that references\nctx, args.source, and artifacts_to_scan so behavior is consistent and users are\ninformed when their filter has no effect.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py`:\n- Around line 86-95: Remove the duplicate import of WorkspaceContext and merge\nthe second loop that builds path_to_source into the initial iteration over\nctx.sources (the same loop used earlier) to avoid iterating sources twice;\nspecifically, delete the extra \"from ..utils.context import WorkspaceContext\"\nand, inside the existing loop that visits each sc in ctx.sources (checking\nsc.reachable and sc.meta), also populate the path_to_source dict by resolving\n(sc.path / art.path).resolve() and mapping str(art_path) to sc.name (using the\nexisting sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts() call), keeping the same guards for\nsc.reachable and sc.meta.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_used.py`:\n- Around line 87-96: Remove the duplicate import of WorkspaceContext and merge\nthe two iterations over ctx.sources into one: keep a single import of\nWorkspaceContext at the top and inside the function iterate once over\nctx.sources (use the existing loop that checks sc.reachable and sc.meta) to both\nbuild the initial results and populate the path_to_source dict; use\nsc.meta.iter_all_artifacts() within that same loop to compute art_path and set\npath_to_source[str(art_path)] = sc.name so you avoid redundant looping and the\nextra import.\n\nIn `@workflows/workspace.md`:\n- Around line 61-68: Add the missing language specifier \"bash\" to the fenced\ncode blocks that contain shell commands (e.g., the blocks with \"python3\n{cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py adapter-info\" and \"python3\n{cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-init --dry-run\");\nupdate every command block called out in the review (lines noted: 67-68,\n114-116, 121-122, 127-132, 178-179, 189-194) by changing the opening fences from\n``` to ```bash so markdownlint MD040 is satisfied and syntax\nhighlighting/parsing is correct.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between bfc39d03df75003ca91d2193f5bddb938dfbb6d1 and c79f4baa6c5b0f6e29e161f3afdf9e4e2a194769.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (24)</summary>\n\n* `CLISPEC.md`\n* `README.md`\n* `requirements/artifacts-registry.md`\n* `requirements/workspace.md`\n* `schemas/artifacts.schema.json`\n* `schemas/workspace.schema.json`\n* `skills/cypilot/SKILL.md`\n* `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py`\n* `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapt