.\n+\n+**Location**: `.cypilot-workspace.json` or inline in CLI commands\n+\n+**When applicable**: Workspace checks (S.1-S.4) apply only when a workspace is active (workspace config exists or inline workspace provided).\n+\n+### Workspace Config Structure\n+\n+[Add workspace configuration details here]\n+\n+### Inline Workspace\n+\n+Inline workspaces allow workspace configuration to be provided directly via CLI rather than through a configuration file.\n+\n+[Add inline workspace details here]\n+\n+---\n+\n ## Path Resolution\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/artifacts-registry.md around lines 992 -\n1000, Add a new \"Workspace Configuration\" section between the existing\n\"Autodetect\" and \"Path Resolution\" sections that defines the workspace concept\nin Cypilot, documents the `.cypilot-workspace.json` file format, explains the\ndifference between a file-based workspace and an \"inline workspace\" (i.e.,\nworkspace entries embedded directly in artifact/codebase/kit manifests), and\nclarifies when workspace-related checks (like S.2) apply during validation;\nreference the terms \"inline workspace\", \".cypilot-workspace.json\", and the S.2\nchecklist entry so readers can map the explanation to the cross-repo source\nchecks.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`996-999`: **Clarify version numbering to avoid confusion.**\n\nThe checks reference \"v1.2+\" (S.1) and version \"1.2\" (S.4), while the document header states the current schema version is `2.0` (line 71). This could confuse readers about which version applies to what.\n\nConsider adding a brief note in the checklist or in S.4's description clarifying that version 1.2 refers to the artifact/workspace data model version, distinct from the registry schema version (2.0). Alternatively, consistently use a qualifier like \"artifact schema v1.2\" or \"data model v1.2\" to distinguish it from the registry schema version.\n\nMinor: S.4's description uses \"≥ 1.2\" while the table shows \"1.2\" - standardizing to \"1.2+\" or \"≥ 1.2\" would improve consistency.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/artifacts-registry.md around lines 996 -\n999, The checklist entries S.1–S.4 currently use \"v1.2\", \"v1.2+\" and \"1.2\" which\nconflicts with the document header stating registry schema version 2.0; update\nthe table and S.4 description to explicitly qualify the version as the\nartifact/data model version (e.g., \"artifact schema v1.2\" or \"data model v1.2\")\nand standardize the comparison to either \"v1.2+\" or \"≥ 1.2\" (prefer \"v1.2+\" for\nconsistency), and add a one-line clarifying note near the checklist that\nexplains \"artifact/data model v1.2\" is distinct from the registry schema version\n2.0.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`279-317`: **Prefer `cypilot ...` examples over invoking internal script paths.**\n\nUsing `python3 cypilot/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py ...` exposes internal layout and may drift; README should show the public CLI interface (`cypilot workspace-init`, etc.) for stability and portability.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed doc fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- python3 cypilot/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-init\n+ cypilot workspace-init\n...\n- python3 cypilot/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add --name docs --path ../docs-repo --role artifacts\n+ cypilot workspace-add --name docs --path ../docs-repo --role artifacts\n...\n- python3 cypilot/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py validate --local-only\n+ cypilot validate --local-only\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@README.md` around lines 279 - 317, Replace the README examples that call the\ninternal script path \"python3 cypilot/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py\n...\" with the public CLI form using the installable entrypoint \"cypilot\" (e.g.,\nuse \"cypilot workspace-init\", \"cypilot workspace-add --name docs --path\n../docs-repo --role artifacts\", \"cypilot workspace-add-inline --name docs --path\n../docs-repo\", and the cross-repo commands \"cypilot validate\", \"cypilot validate\n--local-only\", \"cypilot where-defined --id ...\", \"cypilot list-ids --source\n...\", \"cypilot workspace-info\"); update the code blocks and any prose that\nreferences the internal script path so examples demonstrate the stable public\nCLI instead of the internal script location.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/CLISPEC.md:\n- Around line 550-556: Update the document's top metadata banner so it matches\nthe Version History entry v1.2: change the current \"Version: 1.0\" banner to\n\"Version: 1.2 (2026-02)\" (and update any adjacent date or revision fields if\npresent) so the header aligns with the Version History section; look for the\nheader block containing the \"Version:\" metadata near the top of CLISPEC.md and\nreplace the version string accordingly.\n- Around line 469-546: The command blocks for workspace-init, workspace-add,\nworkspace-add-inline and workspace-info in CLISPEC.md must be normalized to the\nCLISPEC grammar: replace option type words like \"path/string/boolean\" with\nexplicit angle-bracket types (<path>, <string>, <boolean>), ensure every COMMAND\nblock includes the required ARGUMENTS section (use \"ARGUMENTS: (none)\" if there\nare none), and make OPTIONS 