ace_info) and the CLI identity\n(\"workspace-info\") so automated tooling can map the module to artifacts.\n- Around line 76-85: The current bare except in the block that calls\nload_artifacts_meta hides failures; replace it with handling that captures the\nexception (except Exception as e), logs the error (including found_adapter and\ncontext) via the module logger (or process logger) using logger.exception or\nlogger.error, and surface the failure in the info dict (e.g.,\ninfo[\"artifact_meta_error\"] = str(e) or a boolean flag) instead of silently\npassing; keep using load_artifacts_meta, meta.iter_all_artifacts, and the info\ndictionary so successful metadata still populates artifact_count and\nsystem_count while failures are visible.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`:\n- Around line 11-214: Add unit tests for cmd_workspace_init covering dry-run,\ninline mode, standalone write, and error paths by exercising the\ncmd_workspace_init function; specifically write tests that (1) run with\n--dry-run and assert the DRY_RUN JSON output and return code 0, (2) simulate\ninline mode by mocking _read_cypilot_var to return a cypilot path and\ntoml_utils.load/dump to succeed and assert CREATED output and that\ntoml_utils.dump was called with existing[\"workspace\"], (3) simulate standalone\noutput by running without --inline and mocking toml_utils.dump to succeed and\nassert CREATED and correct workspace file path, and (4) cover error paths: mock\nfind_project_root to return None to assert the \"No project root\" error and code\n1, mock toml_utils.load to raise ValueError to assert parse failure handling,\nand mock toml_utils.dump to raise OSError to assert write failure handling. Use\ntmp_path fixtures and monkeypatch to control filesystem behaviors and to stub\nfind_project_root, _read_cypilot_var, find_cypilot_directory, and\ntoml_utils.load/dump so tests are deterministic and verify JSON outputs and\nreturn codes from cmd_workspace_init.\n