act-scoped mode vs global mode behavior,\n> - `\"source\"` presence/absence in output definitions.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py` around lines 57 -\n> 97, The tests are missing coverage for the new source-attribution mapping path:\n> add focused pytest cases that exercise collect_artifacts_to_scan to return a\n> non-empty path_to_source mapping and verify that where_defined.py's logic (loop\n> over artifacts_to_scan, use of path_to_source.get(...), and emission of \"source\"\n> in each definitions entry) correctly propagates the \"source\" field into the\n> output; include tests for both artifact-scoped vs global modes\n> (artifacts_to_scan with single artifact vs multiple) and assert presence or\n> absence of \"source\" on definitions, targeting the functions/variables\n> scan_cpt_ids, collect_artifacts_to_scan, path_to_source, and the definitions\n> list generation.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`88-89`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Remote scanning should also require `resolve_remote_ids`.**\n\nAt Line 88, checking only `ctx.cross_repo` allows remote scans even when workspace config disables remote ID resolution.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            if is_workspace and ctx.cross_repo:\n+            if is_workspace and ctx.cross_repo and ctx.resolve_remote_ids:\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 88 - 89,\nThe remote scanning branch currently allows remote scans when is_workspace and\nctx.cross_repo are true; update the guard to also require the workspace config\nto permit remote ID resolution by adding ctx.resolve_remote_ids to the condition\n(i.e., change the if that controls the loop over ctx.sources.values() to require\nis_workspace && ctx.cross_repo && ctx.resolve_remote_ids) so remote scanning\nonly runs when resolve_remote_ids is enabled.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`264-293`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Honor `resolve_remote_ids` and stop swallowing scan errors silently.**\n\nLine 280 should require `self.resolve_remote_ids` in addition to `self.cross_repo`. Also, Lines 277 and 291 currently suppress scan failures, which hides partial results and diagnostics.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+        import logging\n+        logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n@@\n-                except Exception:\n-                    continue\n+                except Exception as e:\n+                    logger.warning(\"Failed to scan IDs from %s: %s\", art_path, e, exc_info=True)\n+                    continue\n@@\n-        if self.cross_repo:\n+        if self.cross_repo and self.resolve_remote_ids:\n@@\n-                        except Exception:\n-                            continue\n+                        except Exception as e:\n+                            logger.warning(\"Failed to scan IDs from remote artifact %s: %s\", art_path, e, exc_info=True)\n+                            continue\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 264 - 293,\nget_all_artifact_ids currently ignores the resolve_remote_ids flag and silently\nswallows scan_cpt_ids exceptions; change the remote-source guard to require both\nself.cross_repo and self.resolve_remote_ids before iterating sources (so remote\nresolution honors the flag) and replace the bare \"except Exception: continue\"\nblocks around scan_cpt_ids calls with error reporting that preserves partial\nresults (e.g., log the exception with context including artifact path using the\nclass logger or raise a specific error) while continuing to collect other IDs;\nreferences: get_all_artifact_ids, scan_cpt_ids, resolve_artifact_path,\nself.cross_repo, self.resolve_remote_ids.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`194-447`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add required `@cpt-*` markers to the new workspace-context blocks.**\n\nThe newly introduced workspace structures/flows are missing traceability marker coverage in this file.\n\n \n\nAs per coding guidelines `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 194 - 447, Add\nmissing `@cpt-`* traceability markers around the new workspace-related structures\nand flows: add marker comments at the top of the SourceContext and\nWorkspaceContext class definitions, and add markers inside the WorkspaceContext\nmethods resolve_artifact_path, get_all_artifact_ids, get_all_registered_systems,\nand load; also add markers in the module-level functions ensure_context,\nis_workspace, get_primary_context, and collect_artifacts_to_scan where workspace\nsources/remote artifacts are enumerated (references: SourceContext,\nWorkspaceContext, resolve_artifact_path, get_all_artifact_ids,\nget_all_registered_systems, load, ensure_context, is_workspace,\nget_primary_context, collect_artifacts_to_scan). Use the project convention of\ninline comments like \"# `@cpt-`<purpose>\" (e.g. \"# `@cpt-workspace`\", \"#\n`@cpt-resolve`\", \"# `@cpt-scan`\") to clearly mark each code-to-artifact traceability\nboundary.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`250-262`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Do not resolve to local fallback when `artifact.source` is explicit but unavailable.**\n\nAt Line 262, unresolved/unreachable explicit sources fall back to the primary filesystem root, which can mis-resolve remote artifacts as local ones. Return an unavailable value for that case and let callers skip it.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    def resolve_artifact_path(self, artifact: Union[Artifact, CodebaseEntry, Kit], fallback_root: Path) -> Path:\n+    def resolve_artifact_path(self, artifact: Union[Artifact, CodebaseEntry, Kit], fallback_root: Path) -> Optional[Path]:\n@@\n-        if src_name and src_name in self.sources:\n-            sc = self.sources[src_name]\n-            if sc.reachable:\n-                return (sc.path / artifact.path).resolve()\n-        return (fallback_root / artifact.path).resolve()\n+        if src_name:\n+            sc = self.sources.get(src_name)\n+            if sc and sc.reachable:\n+                return (sc.path / artifact.path).resolve()\n+            return None\n+        return (fallback_root / artifact.path).resolve()\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 250 - 262, The\nfunction resolve_artifact_path currently falls back to fallback_root when\nartifact.source is present but not available; change its behavior to treat an\nexplicit but unavailable source as \"unresolvable\" and return None so callers can\nskip it: update resolve_artifact_path's return type to Optional[Path], check\nsrc_name = getattr(artifact, \"source\", None) and if src_name is truthy then if\nsrc_name in self.sources and self.sources[src_name].reachable return (sc.path /\nartifact.path).resolve(), otherwise return None (do not fall back); only use\n(fallback_root / artifact.path).resolve() when src_name is falsy (no explicit\nsource). Update callers of resolve_artifact_path to handle the Optional return.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>tests/test_workspace.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-485`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add required `@cpt-*` markers to this new Python test module.**\n\nThe new test surface is missing repository traceability markers at module/class scopes.\n\n \n\nAs per coding guidelines `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_workspace.py` around lines 1 - 485, Add repository traceability\nmarkers to this new test module by inserting module-level and class-level `@cpt-`*\ncomment markers: add a module marker near the top of tests/test_workspace.py\n(e.g. a \"# `@cpt`:tests\" comment) and add class markers above each test class\ndeclaration (TestSourceEntry, TestWorkspaceConfig, TestFindWorkspaceConfig,\nTestWorkspaceContext, TestIsWorkspace) as \"# `@cpt`:class-<name>\" (or your repo's\nstandard `@cpt-`* format) so the file and each test class include the required\n`@cpt` markers.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py`:\n- Around line 79-86: The warning about \"--source\" being ignored (when\nis_workspace is False) is printed but the code still enters the else branch and\napplies the source filter; to fix, after printing the warning in the