se error, no-workspace, and reachable/unreachable source branches.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 1 -\n129, The test suite is missing unit tests for workspace_info.py which causes 0%\nper-file coverage; add pytest tests that exercise cmd_workspace_info and helper\npaths: simulate no project root (mock find_project_root to return None),\nsimulate parse/find_workspace_config error (mock find_workspace_config to return\n(None, \"error\")), simulate no workspace (find_workspace_config returns (None,\nNone)), and simulate workspace with reachable and unreachable sources (create a\nfake WorkspaceConfig or mock resolve_source_path, ws_cfg.sources,\nws_cfg.is_inline, ws_cfg.workspace_file, ws_cfg.traceability and test\n_build_source_info with adapters and _enrich_with_artifact_counts via mocking\nload_artifacts_meta), and assert JSON outputs and exit codes from\ncmd_workspace_info; use mocks for get_context/WorkspaceContext to test\ncontext_loaded true/false and reachable counts; focus tests on\ncmd_workspace_info, _build_source_info, _enrich_with_artifact_counts, and\n_probe_source_adapter behaviors.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`1-129`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add required `@cpt-*` markers to this new command module.**\n\nThis new workspace CLI surface lacks the required traceability annotations.\n\n \nAs per coding guidelines `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 1 -\n129, The new workspace-info CLI module is missing the required `@cpt-`*\ntraceability markers; add module-level and symbol-level annotations so the code\nmaps to artifacts: put `@cpt-cli` (or `@cpt-module`) markers in the top-level\ndocstring for this module and add `@cpt-cli-command` for the public entrypoint\nfunction cmd_workspace_info (including the command name \"workspace-info\" and a\nstable artifact id), and add `@cpt-helper/`@cpt-adapter markers on helper\nfunctions _build_source_info and _enrich_with_artifact_counts (and/or\n_probe_source_adapter) to capture their roles; ensure these are plain comment\nmarkers (e.g. # `@cpt-`...) adjacent to the module docstring and function\ndefinitions so the traceability tooling can detect them.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`54-62`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Do not swallow source metadata load failures.**\n\nIf metadata parsing fails, the command currently suppresses it and can report an incomplete but seemingly healthy source status.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    except Exception:\n-        pass\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        info[\"artifact_meta_error\"] = str(e)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 54 -\n62, The try/except around load_artifacts_meta currently swallows all errors (do\nnot pass) so metadata load failures are hidden; change the except to capture the\nexception (except Exception as e) and surface it in the returned info (e.g., set\ninfo[\"artifact_error\"] = str(e) and set info[\"artifact_count\"] = 0 and\ninfo[\"system_count\"] = 0 or remove those keys) so callers can see parsing\nfailures; update the block around load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir) and the\nmeta/err handling accordingly (use the symbols load_artifacts_meta, meta, err,\nand the info dict) instead of a bare pass.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`314-319`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Do not silently suppress scan failures in `_scan_definition_ids`.**\n\nSwallowing all exceptions here hides broken artifact scans and causes incomplete ID sets without diagnostics.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 314 - 319, The\ntry/except in _scan_definition_ids is currently swallowing all exceptions from\nscan_cpt_ids(artifact_path), hiding scan failures and resulting in incomplete\nids; replace the broad silent except with error handling that surfaces the\nfailure: catch exceptions as e (do not use a bare except), log the artifact_path\nand the exception (e) via the module/class logger and then re-raise (or\npropagate) the exception so callers can detect the broken scan; alternatively,\nif you must continue, record a diagnostic entry tied to artifact_path instead of\nsilently passing. Ensure you update the block around scan_cpt_ids,\nartifact_path, and ids in _scan_definition_ids accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`273-275`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Honor `resolve_remote_ids` in all remote-artifact collection paths.**\n\nRemote IDs/artifacts are still collected when only `cross_repo` is true, which bypasses the workspace traceability toggle.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if self.cross_repo:\n+        if self.cross_repo and self.resolve_remote_ids:\n             for sc in self.sources.values():\n                 _collect_source_definition_ids(sc, ids)\n@@\n-    if is_ws and ctx.cross_repo:\n+    if is_ws and ctx.cross_repo and ctx.resolve_remote_ids:\n         _collect_remote_artifacts(ctx, artifacts, path_to_source)\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 463-465\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 273 - 275, The\ncurrent cross-repo collection path calls _collect_source_definition_ids(sc, ids)\nunconditionally, which ignores the resolve_remote_ids toggle; update the\nbranches that iterate self.sources (the one guarded by cross_repo around\n_collect_source_definition_ids and the similar block at the other location) to\nrespect self.resolve_remote_ids: only call the remote-artifact/remote-id\ncollection helper when self.resolve_remote_ids is true, otherwise skip or call\nthe non-remote helper. Specifically, modify the branch that checks\nself.cross_repo and the similar block at lines ~463-465 so they consult\nself.resolve_remote_ids before invoking _collect_source_definition_ids (or any\nremote-id collection helper).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`194-467`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add `@cpt-*` markers on the new workspace-context flows.**\n\nThe newly added workspace branches/helpers are missing required traceability annotations.\n\n \nAs per coding guidelines `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 194 - 467, The\nworkspace-related flows lack the required traceability annotations (`@cpt-`*) —\nadd `@cpt-`* markers as comments on the new workspace entry points and branches so\ntraceability tools can pick them up. Specifically, add markers to\nWorkspaceContext class, its methods resolve_artifact_path and\nget_all_artifact_ids, the load() classmethod, and to helper functions\n_load_source, _load_reachable_source, _collect_source_definition_ids,\n_scan_definition_ids, _collect_remote_artifacts, ensure_context, is_workspace,\nget_primary_context, and collect_artifacts_to_scan (place markers at the start\nof each function/class and at key branch points where workspace vs primary flows\ndiverge, e.g. where ctx.cross_repo or sc.reachable are checked). Ensure markers\nfollow the `@cpt-`* naming convention used in the repository and are added as\nsimple inline comments so static scanners can detect them.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`194-467`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**CI gate remains blocked by per-file coverage (77.73% < 90%).**\n\nPlease add focused tests for unresolved source handling, `resolve_remote_ids=False` behavior, and scan-failure diagnostics in workspace paths.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 194 - 467, Add\nunit tests that cover (1) unresolved source handling by exercising\nWorkspaceContext.load with a workspace config pointing to a non-existent source\nso _load_source returns a SourceContext with reachable=False and error set; (2)\nresolve_remote_ids=False behavior by creating a WorkspaceContext (or mocked\nws_cfg) with traceability.resolve_remote_ids=False and asserting\nget_all_artifact_ids and collect_artifacts_to_scan do not include remote-source\nIDs/paths when resolve_remote_ids is false (use\nresolve_artifact_path/get_all_artifact_ids/collect_artifacts_to_scan to\nvalidate); and (3) scan-failure diagnostics by forcing scan_cpt_ids to raise for\na reachable source artifact and asserting _scan_definition_ids swallows the\nexception but that workspace code still records artifact existence and includes\ndiagnostics (simulate via temp files and monkeypatching scan_cpt_ids and\nload_artifacts_meta/_collect_remote_artifacts). Target tests at\nWorkspaceContext.load, _load_source/_load_reachable_source,\nresolve_artifact_path, get_all_artifact_ids, collect_artifacts_to_scan, and\n_scan_definition_ids so CI per-file coverage covers unresolved sources,\nresolve_remote_ids behavior, and scanning error paths. Ensure tests create\ntemporary directories/files and clean up, and assert SourceContext.reachable/\nerror, absence/presence of IDs, and that failures do not crash the scan.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`250-263`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Do not fall back to local path when `artifact.source` is unresolved.**\n\nWhen `artifact.source` is set but missing/unreachable, local fallback can mis-resolve remote references to local files.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-def resolve_artifact_path(self, artifact: Union[Artifact, CodebaseEntry, Kit], fallback_root: Path) -> Path:\n+def resolve_artifact_path(self, artifact: Union[Artifact, CodebaseEntry, Kit], fallback_root: Path) -> Optional[Path]:\n@@\n-    if src_name and src_name in self.sources:\n-        sc = self.sources[src_name]\n-        if sc.reachable:\n-            return (sc.path / artifact.path).resolve()\n+    if src_name:\n+        sc = self.sources.get(str(src_name))\n+        if sc is None or not sc.reachable:\n+            return None\n+        return (sc.path / artifact.path).resolve()\n     return (fallback_root / artifact.path).resolve()\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py` around lines 250 - 263, The\ncurrent resolve_artifact_path falls back to fallback_root when artifact.source\nis set but missing or unreachable; instead, modify resolve_artifact_path to\ntreat a set but unresolved source as an error: if src_name is present but not in\nself.sources or sc.reachable is False, raise a clear exception (e.g., ValueError\nor a custom ArtifactSourceError) identifying the artifact and source rather than\nreturning (fallback_root / artifact.path). Keep the existing behavior only when\nartifact.source is None/absent (then continue to return (fallback_root /\nartifact.path).resolve()). Ensure references to resolve_artifact_path,\nartifact.source, self.sources and sc.reachable are updated accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-237`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**CI blocker: per-file coverage is still 0% for `workspace_init.py`.**\n\nPlease add tests for dry-run, inline write, standalone write, and error branches to clear the coverage gate.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 1 -\n237, Add unit tests to cover workspace_init.py: write tests that call\ncmd_workspace_init to exercise the dry-run path (pass --dry-run and assert JSON\noutput contains \"DRY_RUN\" and correct sources); the inline write path (mock\nfind_project_root and _read_cypilot_var and toml_utils.dump/load to simulate\nreading/writing, call cmd_workspace_init with --inline and assert _write_inline\npath returns CREATED and toml_utils.dump was invoked); the standalone write path\n(use a temporary scan_root and output file, call cmd_workspace_init and assert\n_write_standalone created the file and returns CREATED); and error branches\n(simulate missing project root via mocking find_project_root returning None,\nsimulate unwritable output by making toml_utils.dump raise OSError to verify\nJSON ERROR responses). Target tests to exercise cmd_workspace_init,\n_write_inline, _write_standalone and _scan_sibling_repos behaviors, using\ntemporary directories and mocks for filesystem and toml_utils to keep tests\nhermetic.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`1-237`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add required `@cpt-*` markers for this new workspace-init flow.**\n\nThe file is missing repository-required code-to-artifact traceability annotations.\n\n \nAs per coding guidelines `**/*.{js,ts,tsx,jsx,py,java,cs,cpp,c,go,rb,php}`: Use `@cpt-`* markers to establish code-to-artifact traceability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 1 -\n237, The workspace-init flow must emit code-to-artifact traceability markers;\nupdate _write_standalone and _write_inline to include an `@cpt`:workspace marker\nin the generated TOML (e.g., a top-level comment or a dedicated metadata field)\nand annotate each source entry with an `@cpt`:source marker (or equivalent key) so\nproduced workspace files and inline core.toml contain the required `@cpt-`*\nmarkers; also ensure cmd_workspace_init’s dry-run JSON includes these markers in\nthe workspace_data so previews match the written output.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`:\n- Around line 204-205: The code computes output_dir as\nPath(args.output).resolve().parent which wrongly treats a directory output as a\nfile and offsets sources[*].path; change the logic in workspace_init.py where\noutput_dir is computed (and similarly at the other occurrence around lines\n233-234) to treat args.output as a directory when it has no file\nsuffix/extension or when the provided string indicates a directory;\nspecifically, compute resolved = Path(args.output).resolve() and set output_dir\n= resolved if resolved.suffix == \"\" (or args.output ends with a path separator)\nelse output_dir = resolved.parent so saved sources[*].path remain relative to\nthe actual workspace file location.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/s