breaks source-owned/workspace codebases; change it to accept an optional base\n> (or detect a workspace root) and in scan_codebase_entry use entry.source /\n> entry.get(\"source\") or a workspace field when present as the base root instead\n> of project_root. Concretely: update resolve_code_path to take a base_root: Path\n> = project_root (or branch on entry.source) and in scan_codebase_entry determine\n> base = getattr(entry, \"source\", None) or entry.get(\"source\") and call\n> resolve_code_path(path, base) (or pass the base into resolve_code_path) so\n> entries with workspace/source are resolved against their workspace root while\n> others still use project_root.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `31-59`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Make `--artifact` workspace-aware.**\n> \n> This branch always reloads `CypilotContext` from the artifact directory. For a workspace artifact in a remote repo that relies on the primary-adapter fallback, `where-defined --artifact ...` can fail as “not initialized” or “not in registry”, and this path never fills the new `source` field. Resolve the owning workspace source before doing registry lookup.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/where_defined.py\n> around lines 31 - 59, When handling args.artifact, resolve the owning\n> workspace/source for the given artifact_path before loading the Cypilot context\n> and doing the registry lookup: instead of always calling\n> CypilotContext.load(artifact_path.parent), determine the workspace root/source\n> that owns artifact_path (falling back to the primary-adapter workspace when\n> appropriate), then call CypilotContext.load with that workspace root so ctx.meta\n> and project_root reflect the correct registry; use\n> meta.get_artifact_by_path(rel_path) as before but when appending to\n> artifacts_to_scan include the artifact_meta.source (or otherwise set the new\n> source field) alongside (artifact_path, str(artifact_meta.kind)) so the scan is\n> workspace-aware and does not miss workspace artifacts.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`618-628`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`resolve_remote_ids` regressed in the shared artifact collector.**\n\nThis helper only checks `cross_repo` before adding remote sources, and the primary loop still resolves source-backed artifacts unconditionally. A workspace with `resolve_remote_ids = false` — or any caller expecting local-only behavior — will keep scanning remote artifacts in `where-defined` / `where-used`.\n \n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     # Primary artifacts\n     is_ws = isinstance(ctx, WorkspaceContext)\n     for artifact_meta, _system_node in ctx.meta.iter_all_artifacts():\n+        if (\n+            is_ws\n+            and getattr(artifact_meta, \"source\", None)\n+            and (not ctx.cross_repo or not ctx.resolve_remote_ids)\n+        ):\n+            continue\n         if is_ws:\n             artifact_path = ctx.resolve_artifact_path(artifact_meta, project_root)\n         else:\n             artifact_path = (project_root / artifact_meta.path).resolve()\n         if artifact_path is not None and artifact_path.exists():\n             artifacts.append((artifact_path, str(artifact_meta.kind)))\n\n     # Remote source artifacts (workspace mode with cross-repo enabled)\n-    if is_ws and ctx.cross_repo:\n+    if is_ws and ctx.cross_repo and ctx.resolve_remote_ids:\n         _collect_remote_artifacts(ctx, artifacts, path_to_source)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 618 - 628, The artifact collection loop currently resolves source-backed\nartifacts unconditionally which ignores the resolve_remote_ids flag; update the\nloop in context.py (the block iterating ctx.meta.iter_all_artifacts that calls\nctx.resolve_artifact_path and then _collect_remote_artifacts) to skip resolving\nor adding artifacts that are remote/source-backed when ctx.resolve_remote_ids\n(or a similarly named flag on ctx) is false, and also only call\n_collect_remote_artifacts when both ctx.cross_repo and ctx.resolve_remote_ids\nare true, so remote sources are only scanned when remote resolution is\nexplicitly enabled.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`349-360`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Mirror the `info` resolver fix here too.**\n\nThis copy has the same `resolve_source_path()` call, so it will keep materializing Git URL sources and hiding resolver failures as `{\"active\": False}` unless the same change is applied here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py` around lines 349 -\n360, The loop in adapter_info.py currently calls\nws_cfg.resolve_source_path(name), which can materialize Git URL sources and\nmasks resolver failures; mirror the earlier \"info\" resolver change by replacing\nresolve_source_path(name) with the non-materializing info resolver used\nelsewhere (the same safe resolve used in the other info path), use that to\ndetermine reachable/is_dir() for each src and ensure resolver errors propagate\n(or are reflected) instead of being swallowed by the outer except; update the\nloop that fills ws_info[\"sources\"] (and related usage of ws_cfg and\nconfig[\"workspace\"]) to use that safe resolver.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`85-99`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--source` should reuse the workspace-aware collector.**\n\nThis branch skips the primary repo and rebuilds paths with `sc.path / art.path`, so it can miss a named primary source and drift from the normal `resolve_artifact_path` / `resolve_remote_ids` behavior. Filtering `collect_artifacts_to_scan(ctx)` would keep `--source` aligned with the unfiltered path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 85 - 99,\nWhen args.source is provided you currently rebuild artifact paths per-source and\nskip the primary repo; instead call collect_artifacts_to_scan(ctx) (the same\nworkspace-aware collector used when no source is passed) and then filter its\nreturned artifacts by the requested source name (using ctx.sources and\nargs.source) so the logic in resolve_artifact_path / resolve_remote_ids is\npreserved; remove the manual sc.path / art.path resolution and ensure\nis_workspace/cross_repo branches still yield the primary source when applicable.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`56-66`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Propagate `load_artifacts_meta()` error returns too.**\n\nThis now exposes exceptions via `metadata_error`, but the common `(None, err)` failure path is still silent. When the loader returns an error string, `workspace-info` presents the source as healthy and drops the reason.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         meta, err = load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir)\n-        if meta and not err:\n+        if err:\n+            info[\"metadata_error\"] = str(err)\n+            return\n+        if meta:\n             info[\"artifact_count\"] = sum(1 for _ in meta.iter_all_artifacts())\n             info[\"system_count\"] = len(meta.systems)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 56 -\n66, _enrich_with_artifact_counts currently only records exceptions in\ninfo[\"metadata_error\"] but ignores the (None, err) failure return from\nload_artifacts_meta; update the function to check the returned err value and,\nwhen err is truthy or meta is None, set info[\"metadata_error\"] = err (or a\nstringified version) and avoid treating the source as healthy; keep the existing\ntry/except to capture unexpected exceptions but ensure the explicit error-path\nfrom load_artifacts_meta (meta, err) is propagated into info[\"metadata_error\"]\nand that artifact_count/system_count are only set when meta is valid.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`30-42`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Invalid source roles are still being widened to `full`.**\n\nA typoed `role` is silently promoted to the most permissive option, and `WorkspaceConfig.validate()` can no longer report it because the original token is discarded here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py` around lines 30 - 42, The\nfrom_dict method in SourceEntry currently coerces any unknown or misspelled role\nto \"full\", discarding the original token so WorkspaceConfig.validate() cannot\nreport it; update from_dict to distinguish between a missing role (use \"full\")\nand a present-but-invalid role (preserve the raw token). Concretely, change how\nraw_role is obtained (use data.get(\"role\", None) so absence is None), compute\nrole = raw_role_str if raw_role_str in VALID_ROLES else (raw_role_str if\nraw_role_str is not None else \"full\"), and pass that role into cls(...) so\ninvalid tokens are preserved for later validation (references: from_dict,\nraw_role, role, VALID_ROLES, WorkspaceConfig.validate).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🟠 Major comments (21)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py-367-395 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`367-395`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Use `sc.adapter_dir` when materializing `adapter_context`.**\n\n`_load_reachable_source()` already resolves and stores an explicit adapter override, but this loader ignores it and starts from `sc.path` instead. For sources whose adapter lives outside the repo root or is only reachable via `adapter = ...`, cross-repo editing will silently fall back to the wrong adapter context.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 367 - 395, The loader currently calls CypilotContext.load(sc.path) which\nignores an explicit adapter override stored on sc.adapter_dir; change the load\ncall to use the resolved adapter directory (sc.adapter_dir) when present so the\nadapter_context is materialized from the actual adapter override (e.g., call\nCypilotContext.load on sc.adapter_dir or its resolved path), then assign the\nresult to sc.adapter_context and set sc._adapter_resolved as done now; keep the\nexisting checks for None/exception but replace references to sc.path with\nsc.adapter_dir for adapter loading.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py-349-360 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`349-360`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Avoid resolving workspace sources from `info`.**\n\n`resolve_source_path()` is the materializing resolver for URL-backed sources, so this read-only command can end up cloning/fetching repos just to compute `reachable`. The blanket fallback to `{\"active\": False}` then turns resolver failures into “no workspace”, which is misleading when the workspace is configured but temporarily unavailable.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py\naround lines 349 - 360, The code currently calls\nws_cfg.resolve_source_path(name) inside the adapter_info workspace loop which\ncan materialize URL-backed sources and hide real workspace configuration by\nfalling back to config[\"workspace\"] = {\"active\": False\"} on any exception;\nremove the call to resolve_source_path(name) and instead populate\nws_info[\"sources\"][name] using only src.path and src.role (set reachable to None\nor False/ \"unknown\" without attempting to fetch), and adjust the exception\nhandling so that an exception does not flip the workspace to inactive—preserve\nworkspace active state when ws_cfg exists and only mark individual source\nreachability as unknown.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py-246-252 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`246-252`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Honor source roles before aggregating remote systems and artifacts.**\n\nThese paths currently treat every reachable source as an artifact source. That means `codebase`-only or `kits`-only entries still add registered systems, definition IDs, and artifact scans to cross-repo commands, which makes the workspace `role` setting effectively informational.\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+def _source_exposes_artifacts(sc: \"SourceContext\") -> bool:\n+    return sc.reachable and sc.meta is not None and sc.role in {\"artifacts\", \"full\"}\n+\n     def get_all_registered_systems(self) -> Set[str]:\n         \"\"\"Get registered systems from primary and all reachable sources.\"\"\"\n         systems = set(self.primary.registered_systems)\n         for sc in self.sources.values():\n-            if sc.reachable and sc.registered_systems:\n+            if _source_exposes_artifacts(sc) and sc.registered_systems:\n                 systems.update(sc.registered_systems)\n         return systems\n...\n def _collect_source_definition_ids(sc: \"SourceContext\", ids: Set[str]) -> None:\n     \"\"\"Collect definition IDs from a single reachable source's artifacts.\"\"\"\n-    if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n+    if not _source_exposes_artifacts(sc):\n         return\n...\n def _collect_remote_artifacts(\n     ctx: \"WorkspaceContext\",\n     artifacts: List[Tuple[Path, str]],\n     path_to_source: Dict[str, str],\n ) -> None:\n     \"\"\"Append artifacts from reachable remote workspace sources.\"\"\"\n     for sc in ctx.sources.values():\n-        if not sc.reachable or sc.meta is None:\n+        if not _source_exposes_artifacts(sc):\n             continue\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 463-470, 546-553\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 246 - 252, get_all_registered_systems currently aggregates systems from\nevery reachable source by checking sc.reachable and sc.registered_systems;\nchange the condition to