r(\n+                f\"Invalid role '{raw_role}' for source '{name}' \"\n+                f\"(valid: {', '.join(sorted(VALID_ROLES))})\"\n+            )\n+        role = raw_role or \"full\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py` around lines 46 - 50, The\ncode in the workspace loader which computes raw_role and then coerces unknown\nvalues to \"full\" (variables raw_role, VALID_ROLES, role) silently widens\npermissions; instead, validate raw_role against VALID_ROLES and raise an\nexplicit error (or propagate an exception) when raw_role is non-empty and not in\nVALID_ROLES so the caller (e.g., WorkspaceConfig.validate) can catch/configure\nthe failure; update the logic in the function that sets role to stop defaulting\ninvalid inputs to \"full\" and surface the invalid role with a clear exception\nmessage that includes the source name and invalid value.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`:\n- Around line 93-96: The current try/except around scan_root.iterdir swallows\nOSError and sets entries = [], which masks filesystem/permission failures and\nyields a NO_SOURCES outcome; change the handler so that when scan_root.iterdir\nraises OSError you propagate that as an ERROR result containing the original\nexception (include the exception message/trace) instead of falling back to an\nempty entries list — update the code around scan_root.iterdir and entries\nassignment so the OSError is not swallowed but returned/raised as an ERROR\nresponse that preserves the underlying exception details.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypi