/workspace.py` around lines 46 - 50, When\nparsing source roles in workspace.py, do not coerce invalid values to \"full\";\ninstead detect an invalid raw_role and raise an error so the misconfiguration\nsurfaces (allowing validate() to report it). Specifically, in the block that\nreads raw_role and compares against VALID_ROLES, if raw_role is non-empty and\nnot in VALID_ROLES, raise a ValueError (include source name, the invalid\nraw_role, and the sorted VALID_ROLES); otherwise set role to raw_role if present\nor default to \"full\" only when no role was provided.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py`:\n- Around line 107-126: The parser currently allows both --path and --url and\nthen manually checks that at least one is present; change this to enforce\nexactly one by creating a mutually exclusive required group on the\nArgumentParser (use p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)) and add\n--path and --url to that group instead of adding them directly to p, then remove\nthe manual \"if not args.path and not args.url\" validation; keep the existing\ninline/URL check that rejects --inline with --url and leave _add_to_standalone()\nand resolve_source_path() unchanged (they will now always receive exactly one of\npath or url).\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py`:\n- Around line 277-286: The standalone branch only writes the workspace manifest\nbut does not register it in core.toml, so subsequent discoverers like\nfind_workspace_config() (used by workspace-add/workspace-info) won't find it;\nafter calling _write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data) update the\nrepository's core.toml to set the workspace key to point at the new workspace\nfile (use a relative path from project_root when possible, falling back to the\nabsolute output_path) so find_workspace_config() can resolve it; modify the code\naround the _write_standalone call to write or merge the workspace = \"<path>\"\nentry into core.toml (preserving other keys) and ensure\nWORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME/args.output logic remains consistent.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`:\n- Around line 345-376: The code currently treats any present but malformed\nws_value as if no workspace was specified and returns (None, None); instead\ndetect when cfg contains \"workspace\" but ws_value is neither a non-empty str nor\na dict and raise a configuration error. Modify the end of find/parse logic in\nworkspace.py (the branch handling ws_value, near WorkspaceConfig.load and\nWorkspaceConfig.from_dict and before the final \"return None, None\") to raise a\nclear exception (e.g. ValueError or a project ConfigError) that includes the bad\nws_value and a message like \"malformed 'workspace' in core.toml\" so callers\nsurface the bad config rather than silently falling back to single-repo mode.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py`:\n- Around line 46-50: When parsing source roles in workspace.py, do not coerce\ninvalid values to \"full\"; instead detect an invalid raw_role and raise an error\nso the misconfiguration surfaces (allowing validate() to report it).\nSpecifically, in the block that reads raw_role and compares against VALID_ROLES,\nif raw_role is non-empty and not in VALID_ROLES, raise a ValueError (include\nsource name, the invalid raw_role, and the sorted VALID_ROLES); otherwise set\nrole to raw_role if present or default to \"full\" only when no role was provided.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `6deab9a5-fc5d-4