60 - 465,\n> scan_codebase_entry and resolve_code_path currently always resolve paths as\n> project_root / entry.path, which ignores CodebaseEntry.source; update resolution\n> to be workspace-aware like the artifact-resolution logic: when entry has a\n> source (e.g., getattr(entry, \"source\", None) or entry.get(\"source\")), resolve\n> the code path against that workspace/repo root instead of project_root, falling\n> back to project_root when no source exists; modify resolve_code_path or\n> call-site in scan_codebase_entry to accept a source parameter (or choose the\n> appropriate workspace root) so that scan_codebase_entry, resolve_code_path, and\n> any uses of project_root correctly incorporate entry.source for cross-repo\n> tracing.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>architecture/specs/cli.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `250-261`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Update the usage lines for the new workspace flags.**\n> \n> Line 251 and Line 308 still show the pre-workspace command shapes, so readers copying the synopsis will miss `--local-only` and `--source`. Keep the usage blocks in sync with the option tables.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested wording</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -cpt validate [--artifact PATH] [--system SYSTEM] [--kind KIND] [--strict]\n> +cpt validate [--artifact PATH] [--system SYSTEM] [--kind KIND] [--strict] [--local-only] [--source SOURCE]\n> \n> -cpt list-ids [--kind KIND] [--pattern PATTERN] [--system SYSTEM] [--format FORMAT]\n> +cpt list-ids [--kind KIND] [--pattern PATTERN] [--system SYSTEM] [--format FORMAT] [--source SOURCE]\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 307-318\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@architecture/specs/cli.md` around lines 250 - 261, Update the synopsis/usage\n> strings for the \"cpt validate\" command so they match the option table by adding\n> the new workspace flags; specifically ensure the usage lines that currently read\n> `cpt validate [--artifact PATH] [--system SYSTEM] [--kind KIND] [--strict]`\n> (appearing in the CLI docs) include `--local-only` and `--source SOURCE` (e.g.,\n> `cpt validate [--artifact PATH] [--system SYSTEM] [--kind KIND] [--strict]\n> [--local-only] [--source SOURCE]`) so all usage blocks are consistent with the\n> option table across the document.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`452-456`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Respect `resolve_remote_ids` before expanding workspace IDs.**\n\nThis block only checks `--local-only`. If the workspace explicitly disables remote ID resolution, validate still pulls in IDs from every workspace source and no longer matches the workspace config. Gate the branch on `getattr(ctx, \"resolve_remote_ids\", True)` as well.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 452 - 456,\nThe current expansion of workspace artifact IDs ignores the workspace's\nresolve_remote_ids setting and only checks args.local_only; update the\nconditional that adds ctx.get_all_artifact_ids() so it also checks getattr(ctx,\n\"resolve_remote_ids\", True) is True (in addition to not args.local_only) and\nstill ensures ctx is a WorkspaceContext before calling get_all_artifact_ids(),\nso remote IDs are only pulled when both flags allow it.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`49-67`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Don't drop the selected source in `--artifact` mode.**\n\nAfter `--source` switches `ctx` to that source's adapter context, the single-artifact branch resolves `args.artifact` from the current cwd and then reloads `CypilotContext` from `artifact_path.parent`. `validate --source repo-b --artifact architecture/PRD.md` therefore stops using `repo-b` entirely and can validate the wrong repository. Resolve relative artifact paths against the selected source root and keep the chosen adapter context when `args.source` is set.\n\n \n\n\nAlso applies to: 131-149\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 49 - 67,\nThe --source branch currently replaces ctx with the adapter context\n(adapter_ctx) but later the single-artifact branch resolves args.artifact\nagainst the current working directory and reloads a CypilotContext from\nartifact_path.parent, which drops the selected adapter context; change the\nartifact resolution logic so that when args.source is set you resolve relative\nartifact_path against the selected source root/adapter context (use\nadapter_ctx.root or the source object sc) instead of cwd, and ensure you do not\noverwrite or replace adapter_ctx/ctx with a new CypilotContext when in\n--artifact mode; apply the same adjustment to the duplicate block referenced\n(lines ~131-149) so both single-artifact flows keep the chosen adapter context\nand resolve relative paths against that source.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`61-64`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Surface `load_artifacts_meta()` return errors.**\n\n`load_artifacts_meta()` reports missing or invalid registries through `err`, not only via exceptions. Right now a source can show `adapter_found: true` with no artifact counts and no `metadata_error`, which hides the actual failure. Set `info[\"metadata_error\"] = err` before the success check.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 61 -\n64, The code currently ignores the returned err from\nload_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir), which can hide registry/metadata problems;\nmodify the block that calls load_artifacts_meta in workspace_info.py to set\ninfo[\"metadata_error\"] = err immediately after the call (using the returned meta\nand err variables), then only populate info[\"artifact_count\"] and\ninfo[\"system_count\"] when meta is truthy and err is falsy (keeping use of\nmeta.iter_all_artifacts() and meta.systems as before) so any load error is\nsurfaced even when artifacts aren't present.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`271-272`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Keep standalone output discoverable from the current project.**\n\nIf `--root` points outside `project_root`, or `--output` writes elsewhere, this path creates a standalone manifest that later commands from the repo root will not find. Either keep the default standalone target under `project_root`, or register external targets in `core.toml` when writing them.\n\n \nBased on learnings `find_workspace_config()` first checks `core.toml.workspace` and only auto-discovers a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root`.\n\n\nAlso applies to: 321-322\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 271 -\n272, The code sets scan_root = Path(args.root).resolve() if args.root else\nproject_root which can create a standalone manifest outside project_root that\nfind_workspace_config() won't auto-discover; change this logic so if args.root\nis provided but is outside project_root, default scan_root to project_root (or,\nwhen intentionally writing outside, add registration of that external path into\ncore.toml.workspace) and apply the same guard for the output path handling\n(related code near where output is computed) so external targets are either kept\nunder project_root or explicitly recorded in core.toml.workspace.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`48-53`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Use a true relative-path calculation here.**\n\n`Path.relative_to()` only works for descendants. When the workspace file lives outside `scan_root` or beside the scanned repos, this falls back to an absolute `sources[*].path`, which makes the generated manifest non-portable.\n\n  \nRun this read-only repro to compare the current behavior with an actual relative path:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os\n\nentry = Path(\"/tmp/repos/service-a\")\noutput_dir = Path(\"/tmp/workspaces\")\n\ntry:\n    print(\"relative_to:\", entry.relative_to(output_dir).as_posix())\nexcept Exception as exc:\n    print(\"relative_to_error:\", type(exc).__name__, exc)\n\nprint(\"relpath:\", Path(os.path.relpath(entry, output_dir)).as_posix())\nPY\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 48 -\n53, The current _compute_source_path uses Path.relative_to which fails for\nnon-descendant paths and falls back to absolute paths; change the fallback to\ncompute a true relative path using os.path.relpath (or\nPath(os.path.relpath(...))). Update _compute_source_path to return\nPath(os.path.relpath(entry, output_dir)).as_posix() in the exception branch (and\nadd an import for os if not present), keeping the function signature and string\nreturn type.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`301-305`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify when a standalone workspace file is auto-discovered.**\n\nThis currently reads like any super-root `.cypilot-workspace.toml` is picked up implicitly. Auto-discovery is limited to `project_root`; external workspace files outside that location need an explicit `workspace = \"...\"` reference in `core.toml`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n **Workspace config** can be:\n-- A standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` file at a super-root directory\n+- A standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` file at the current project root\n - Inline in any repo's `config/core.toml` under the `[workspace]` section\n-- A reference from `core.toml` to an external workspace file\n+- A `workspace = \"...\"` reference in `core.toml` to an external workspace file outside the project root\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` first checks `core.toml`, then only auto-discovers `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root`; there is no parent-directory walk-up.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@README.md` around lines 301 - 305, Clarify README wording to state that a\nstandalone .cypilot-workspace.toml is only auto-discovered at the project_root\n(no parent-directory walk-up) and that external workspace files located outside\nproject_root must be referenced explicitly via workspace = \"...\" in core.toml;\nreference the find_workspace_config() behavior and the order (it first checks\ncore.toml, then only checks project_root for .cypilot-workspace.toml) so readers\nknow how to make a workspace file be picked up.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/cli.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`729-731`: 