n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py:\n- Around line 86-100: When args.source is set we currently populate\nartifacts_to_scan from the matching ctx.sources entry but later code still walks\nctx.meta and ctx.project_root; update the flow so that when args.source is\nprovided (and is_workspace is True) the scanner does not fall back to the\nprimary repo. Concretely: in list_ids.py adjust either collect_artifacts_to_scan\nor the later scanning block that iterates ctx.meta / ctx.project_root to check\nargs.source (or a new local flag) and skip primary-repo scanning, ensuring only\nartifacts in artifacts_to_scan (populated from ctx.sources via\nctx.sources.values() / sc.meta.iter_all_artifacts()) are scanned when\nargs.source is specified.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py:\n- Around line 152-159: The clone target's parent directories may not exist\nbefore calling _clone_or_fetch; ensure the directory hierarchy for local_path is\ncreated first by using the resolve_config.workdir/templated-derived path\n(local_path) and creating its parent directories (e.g., workspace_parent /\nworkdir / templated). Call mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) on\nlocal_path.parent (or equivalent) right before invoking _clone_or_fetch(url,\nlocal_path, branch) so git clone has an existing parent directory.\n- Around line 72-81: The current flow in git_utils.py only runs\n_run_git([\"fetch\", \"--quiet\"]) then checkout, which leaves the worktree on the\nold commit if the branch is already checked out; after fetching you should\nupdate the checked-out files by ensuring the branch is checked out and then\nhard-reset it to the tracked remote branch (or its upstream). Modify the\nbranch-handling path that calls _run_git([\"checkout\", \"--quiet\