ate the flow description to include the standalone\nworkspace fallback: when attempting workspace discovery in the\n`inst-ctx-workspace-upgrade` step (where `WorkspaceContext.load(primary_ctx)` is\ncalled), note that `find_workspace_config()` may discover a standalone\n`.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` even if `core.toml` lacks a\n`workspace` key; therefore the branch that currently only describes discovery\nvia the `core.toml` `workspace` key must be expanded to state that discovery can\nalso succeed via the standalone file and proceed to \"load source contexts,\nresolve reachability, RETURN WorkspaceContext\" in that case (otherwise RETURN\nCypilotContext for single-repo mode).\n\nIn `@architecture/features/workspace.md`:\n- Around line 359-367: The documented flow treats the --source override\n(inst-validate-source-flag) as unreachable because Steps 2-3\n(inst-target-foreach-source, inst-target-if-match, inst-target-return-source,\ninst-target-return-primary) unconditionally return; change the algorithm to\nevaluate the --source flag before performing the longest-prefix scan: if\n--source is present, resolve the named source and its adapter context via\ncpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-resolve-adapter-context and return (source,\nadapter_context) or (source, primary_context) as appropriate, and only if\n--source is absent proceed with the existing longest-prefix iteration and\nfallback; apply the same change to the mirrored\n.bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/workspace.md copy so both docs reflect\nthe corrected ordering.\n- Around line 141-153: The flow currently treats missing workspace config as an\nunconditional error; update the logic so inst-add-if-no-ws only errors when the\n--inline flag is NOT set: in the workspace-add flow (inst-user-workspace-add)\ncall inst-add-find-ws (cpt-cypilot-algo-workspace-find-config) and if no config\nis found, check inst-add-if-inline-flag first — allow writing to core.toml when\n--inline is present and no standalone