8`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **The command metadata tables are already drifting out of sync.**\n> \n> `main()` still dispatches `self-check` and `generate-resources`, but they are absent from `all_commands` and the top-level help sections. Adding workspace commands in several more places extends the same maintenance trap.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py` around lines 188 - 228, The top-level\n> command lists (workspace_commands, all_commands) and help metadata\n> (_cmd_descriptions, _sections) have diverged from the actual dispatcher in\n> main() which still handles \"self-check\" and \"generate-resources\"; fix by\n> centralizing command metadata: create a single canonical command registry (e.g.,\n> COMMAND_REGISTRY dict or list) that maps command names to descriptions and\n> section membership, replace scattered workspace_commands and all_commands with\n> references to that registry, and update main(), _cmd_descriptions, and _sections\n> to build their values from COMMAND_REGISTRY so new commands like \"self-check\"\n> and \"generate-resources\" are always included and the lists (workspace_commands,\n> all_commands, _cmd_descriptions, _sections) stay in sync.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `363-371`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Remove module-qualified name or import the type at module level.**\n> \n> The return annotation `\"cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta.ArtifactsMeta\"` triggers Ruff `F821` (undefined name `cypilot`) because the identifier is not available in module scope. Either import the type at the top of the file (`from cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta import ArtifactsMeta`) and use `\"ArtifactsMeta\"` in the annotation, or remove the module qualifier entirely.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 363 - 371, The return annotation\n> on _bootstrap_kit uses a module-qualified string\n> \"cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta.ArtifactsMeta\" which triggers an unresolved name\n> error; fix this by importing ArtifactsMeta at module scope (from\n> cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta import ArtifactsMeta) and change the annotation to\n> \"ArtifactsMeta\" (or remove the module qualifier entirely), ensuring the function\n> signature def _bootstrap_kit(...) -> \"ArtifactsMeta\": references the type\n> available in module scope.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (16)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/workspace.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`504-506`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify that `workspace-add` auto-detects inline workspaces.**\n\nThe DoD at lines 504-506 states `workspace-add` operates \"on standalone config by default, and on inline config when `--inline` is specified.\" However, line 161-162 describes auto-routing to inline mode when the existing workspace is inline (no `--inline` flag required).\n\nConsider rewording to make the auto-detection behavior explicit:\n\n> `workspace-add` **MUST** operate on standalone config by default, on inline config when `--inline` is specified, **or auto-route to inline mode when an existing inline workspace is detected**.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/workspace.md around lines 504 - 506,\nUpdate the DoD sentence for the workspace-add command to explicitly state\nauto-detection: change the description for `workspace-add` (and its `--inline`\nflag) to read that it \"MUST operate on standalone config by default, on inline\nconfig when `--inline` is specified, or auto-route to inline mode when an\nexisting inline workspace is detected,\" so that `workspace-add`'s behavior\n(including error handling for type mismatches and preservation of existing\nentries) clearly documents automatic inline detection; reference the\n`workspace-add` command and `--inline` flag in the updated wording.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>vulture_whitelist.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-14`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**`WorkspaceConfig.get_reachable_sources` does not exist — this import will fail.**\n\nThe method `get_reachable_sources` is not defined on `WorkspaceConfig`. This will raise an `AttributeError` when the whitelist is imported during vulture linting.\n\nVerify the actual method name on `WorkspaceConfig` (e.g., `get_sources`, `sources`, or similar) and update the reference accordingly.\n\n\n\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for the actual methods defined on WorkspaceConfig\nrg -n \"def (get_.*sources|sources)\" skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py\n# Also check for any property or attribute named reachable\nrg -n \"reachable\" skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@vulture_whitelist.py` around lines 7 - 14, The alias get_reachable_sources\npoints to a non-existent WorkspaceConfig.get_reachable_sources and will raise on\nimport; open the WorkspaceConfig class and confirm the correct API (e.g.,\nget_sources, sources, or a property) and replace get_reachable_sources =\nWorkspaceConfig.get_reachable_sources with the actual member name (or add a\nsmall wrapper alias on WorkspaceConfig if you intend that exact name) so the\nwhitelist references a real symbol.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`371-377`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Remove network I/O from workspace source reachability checks.**\n\nThe loop on lines 371-377 calls `ws_cfg.resolve_source_path(name)` for each source. This method delegates Git URL sources to `resolve_git_source()`, which clones on first access if the repo doesn't already exist locally. This causes the `info` command to perform unexpected network I/O and mutate the workspace cache.\n\nFor Git URL sources without a local checkout, use a non-mutating check (e.g., verify the directory exists without triggering a clone) or report the reachability as false without attempting resolution.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>architecture/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`224-226`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Sync the workspace design text with the API that landed.**\n\nThis paragraph still says `WorkspaceContext` extends `CypilotContext`, only describes discovery via the `core.toml` `workspace` key, and calls the resolve field `namespace_rules`. The implementation in this PR is wrapper-style, uses `resolve.namespace`, and also supports standalone project-root workspace discovery, so this wording points downstream docs and agents at the wrong surface.\n \n\nBased on learnings, `find_workspace_config()` also auto-discovers a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` without requiring a `workspace` key in `core.toml`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@architecture/DESIGN.md` around lines 224 - 226, The DESIGN.md text is out of\nsync with the landed API: update the paragraph to reflect that WorkspaceContext\nis a wrapper (not an extension) around CypilotContext, that workspace discovery\nuses the new find_workspace_config() which also auto-discovers a standalone\n.cypilot-workspace.toml at project_root (not only the core.toml \"workspace\"\nkey), and that the resolver config uses resolve.namespace (not namespace_rules);\nalso mention that inline workspace defs reject url and that path takes\nprecedence when both are present to match the implemented behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/SKILL.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`362-384`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add `--json` to the new workspace command blocks.**\n\nThese are explicit copy-paste commands in an agent-facing SKILL. Without `--json`, an agent following them verbatim drops back to human-formatted stdout and breaks the machine-readable contract set in “Agent-Safe Invocation”.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--force] [--dry-run]\n+python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-init [--root <dir>] [--output <path>] [--inline] [--force] [--dry-run]\n@@\n-python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-add --name <name> (--path <path> | --url <url>) [--branch <branch>] [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>] [--inline]\n+python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-add --name <name> (--path <path> | --url <url>) [--branch <branch>] [--role <role>] [--adapter <path>] [--inline]\n@@\n-python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-info\n+python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-info\n@@\n-python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py workspace-sync [--source <name>] [--dry-run]\n+python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py --json workspace-sync [--source <name>] [--dry-run]\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/SKILL.md` around lines 362 - 384, Update the four agent-facing\ncommand examples to include the --json flag so they emit machine-readable\noutput: modify the workspace-init, workspace-add, workspace-info, and\nworkspace-sync code blocks to append --json to their invocation forms (e.g., add\n--json to the python3 {cypilot_path}/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py\nworkspace-init ... and likewise for workspace-add, workspace-info,\nworkspace-sync) ensuring inline/standalone notes remain unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`68-72`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**Reject checkout templates that escape the workspace root.**\n\n`_apply_template()` only strips a leading slash. A template like `../shared/{repo}` still passes through, and Lines 165-166 then `resolve()` and `mkdir()` that escaped path outside the workspace before clone.\n  \n\nRun this read-only check to confirm the current join + `resolve()` flow escapes the workspace root. The `../...` cases should print `under workspace? False`.\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nsed -n '67,72p;160,166p' skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py\n\npython3 <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nworkspace_parent = Path(\"/tmp/cypilot-workspace\").resolve()\nfor templated in [\"repo\", \"../escape/repo\", \"../../outside/repo\"]:\n    candidate = (workspace_parent / \".workspace-sources\" / templated).resolve()\n    print(f\"{templated!r} -> {candidate} | under workspace? {workspace_parent in candidate.parents}\")\nPY\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _apply_template(template: str, org: str, repo: str) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Apply {org}/{repo} substitution to a namespace template.\"\"\"\n-    result = template.replace(\"{org}\", org).replace(\"{repo}\", repo)\n-    # Strip leading slash that appears when org is empty (\"{org}/{repo}\" → \"/repo\")\n-    return result.lstrip(\"/\")\n+    result = template.replace(\"{org}\", org).replace(\"{repo}\", repo).lstrip(\"/\")\n+    candidate = Path(result)\n+    if candidate.is_absolute() or any(part == \"..\" for part in candidate.parts):\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid workspace checkout template: {template}\")\n+    return candidate.as_posix()\n@@\n-    templated = _apply_template(template, org, repo)\n+    try:\n+        templated = _apply_template(template, org, repo)\n+    except ValueError as exc:\n+        print(f\"Warning: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+        return None\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 163-166\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/git_utils.py` around lines 68 - 72, The\ntemplate substitution currently allows path traversal (e.g., \"../shared/{repo}\")\nand escapes the workspace; update _apply_template to reject templates that\nproduce absolute paths or contain parent-segment components by checking\nPath(result).is_absolute() or any(part == \"..\" for part in Path(result).parts)\nand raising a ValueError with a clear message, and additionally add a guard\nafter the join+resolve step where the code computes (workspace_parent /\n\".workspace-sources\" / templated).resolve() (the same place that calls\nmkdir/clone) to verify the resolved path is inside the workspace_root (e.g.,\nensure workspace_parent in candidate.parents or candidate == workspace_parent)\nand raise if not; this ensures templates cannot escape the workspace even if\nthey attempt traversal.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`596-600`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Persist remote registry load failures on `SourceContext`.**\n\nIf `load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir)` returns `err`, this still emits a reachable source with `meta=None` and `error=None`, so later workspace scans silently skip the source instead of explaining why it vanished. Set `src_error` when `err` is truthy, and mirror the change in `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py`.\n \n<details>\n<summary>Minimal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     if adapter_dir is not None:\n         m, err = load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir)\n         if m and not err:\n             meta = m\n             reg_systems = m.get_all_system_prefixes()\n+        elif err:\n+            src_error = f\"Failed to load artifacts metadata for source '{name}': {err}\"\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 604-614\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 596 - 600, When loading adapter metadata in the SourceContext creation\npath, if load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir) returns an error, populate the\nSourceContext.src_error with that error instead of leaving meta and src_error\nNone; update the block around the call to load_artifacts_meta (and the analogous\nblock at lines ~604-614) so that when m, err = load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir)\nyields err truthy you set src_error = err, otherwise assign meta = m and\nreg_systems = m.get_all_system_prefixes(); ensure you reference the\nSourceContext instance and its src_error field so the error is retained for\ndownstream workspace scans.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`751-772`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Make single-artifact resolution workspace-aware.**\n\nThis helper always loads a plain `CypilotContext` from `artifact_path.parent` and resolves the file through `ctx.project_root`. A workspace artifact routed via `artifact.source` but registered only in the primary workspace manifest will still be rejected here unless the source repo duplicates that entry locally. Resolve against the active workspace registry first, then fall back to local-only lookup. Mirror the fix in `skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 751 - 772, The helper currently loads a local CypilotContext from\nartifact_path.parent and only calls ctx.meta.get_artifact_by_path against\nctx.project_root; change it to resolve against the active workspace registry\nfirst and only then fall back to the local context: attempt to obtain the active\nworkspace context/registry (use the project workspace API or active workspace\nCypilotContext) and call its meta.get_artifact_by_path(rel_path) for the\nartifact_path-derived rel_path; if that returns no result, then load the local\nCypilotContext via CypilotContext.load(artifact_path.parent) and call\nctx.meta.get_artifact_by_path(rel_path) as before (referencing artifact_path,\nrel_path, CypilotContext.load and ctx.meta.get_artifact_by_path when updating\nthe code).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`86-102`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Keep `--include-code` scoped to the selected source.**\n\n`artifacts_to_scan` is narrowed to `args.source`, but the later code-scan path still walks `ctx.meta.iter_all_codebase()` and `ctx.project_root`, which are the primary repo in workspace mode. `list-ids --source X --include-code` will therefore mix one source's artifacts with the primary repo's code references.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py around\nlines 86 - 102, When args.source is set in workspace mode we narrow\nartifacts_to_scan to that remote source but the later --include-code path still\nwalks ctx.meta.iter_all_codebase() and ctx.project_root (the primary repo);\nupdate the code-scan branch to scope code discovery to the selected source\ninstead: when args.source is provided (and is_workspace), use the selected\nsource's expanded meta (the _meta from get_expanded_meta(sc)) and the source\npath (sc.path) as the root when iterating code with iter_all_codebase(), and\navoid using ctx.meta or ctx.project_root so that artifacts_to_scan and the\ncode-scan remain consistent for the chosen source.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`125-147`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Wrap the new workspace dispatch helpers in the existing `@cpt-*` block.**\n\nThese entry points sit between the surrounding traceability markers, so they are currently outside code↔artifact coverage.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+# `@cpt-begin`:cpt-cypilot-algo-core-infra-route-command:p1:inst-route-helpers\n def _cmd_workspace_init(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n     from .commands.workspace_init import cmd_workspace_init\n     return cmd_workspace_init(argv)\n@@\n def _cmd_workspace_sync(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n     from .commands.workspace_sync import cmd_workspace_sync\n     return cmd_workspace_sync(argv)\n+# `@cpt-end`:cpt-cypilot-algo-core-infra-route-command:p1:inst-route-helpers\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines: `Use `@cpt-`* markers for establishing code↔artifact traceability`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/cli.py around lines 125 -\n147, The four workspace dispatch helpers (_cmd_workspace_init,\n_cmd_workspace_add, _cmd_workspace_info, _cmd_workspace_sync) must be enclosed\nwithin the existing code↔artifact traceability markers; move or wrap these\nfunction definitions so they sit between the surrounding `@cpt-`* markers (e.g.\n`@cpt-start` / `@cpt-end` or the project’s existing `@cpt-`... block) so they are\nincluded in the code↔artifact coverage.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-22`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Honor `src.adapter` first, using the same adapter predicate as the writer.**\n\nWhen an explicit adapter path is configured, probing the whole repo first can report `adapter_found: true` from some other nested adapter and hide a broken workspace entry. The explicit-path check is also stricter than `workspace-init`, which records adapters based on a `config/` directory.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _probe_source_adapter(resolved: Path, explicit_adapter: Optional[Path]) -> Optional[Path]:\n     \"\"\"Find the adapter directory for a reachable source.\"\"\"\n     from ..utils.files import find_cypilot_directory\n \n-    found = find_cypilot_directory(resolved)\n-    if found is None and explicit_adapter is not None:\n-        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n-            found = explicit_adapter\n-    return found\n+    if explicit_adapter is not None:\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"config\").is_dir():\n+            return explicit_adapter\n+        return None\n+    return find_cypilot_directory(resolved)\n```\n</details>\n \n\n\nAlso applies to: 48-49\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 14 -\n22, In _probe_source_adapter, prefer the explicit_adapter (src.adapter) first\nand validate it using the same predicate the writer uses (i.e., check\nexplicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists()) before\nfalling back to find_cypilot_directory(resolved); if explicit_adapter passes the\npredicate return it immediately to avoid picking up a nested repo's adapter, and\napply the same change to the other probe usage referenced around the second\noccurrence (lines 48-49) where explicit_adapter is currently ignored or checked\nafter find_cypilot_directory.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`31-46`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Keep unreachable source payloads schema-stable and actionable.**\n\nThe early return omits `adapter_found`, and URL-only sources can still emit `Source directory not reachable: None`. Initialize `adapter_found` to `False` up front and build the warning from the best available identifier.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     info: dict = {\n         \"name\": name,\n         \"path\": src.path,\n         \"resolved_path\": str(resolved) if resolved else None,\n         \"role\": src.role,\n         \"adapter\": src.adapter,\n         \"reachable\": reachable,\n+        \"adapter_found\": False,\n     }\n@@\n     if not reachable:\n-        info[\"warning\"] = f\"Source directory not reachable: {src.path}\"\n+        info[\"warning\"] = f\"Source directory not reachable: {src.url or src.path or name}\"\n         return info\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 31 -\n46, Initialize and include \"adapter_found\": False in the info dict before the\nreachable check so unreachable payloads remain schema-stable; when reachable is\nFalse, set info[\"warning\"] to a message built from the best available identifier\n(prefer src.path, fall back to src.url, then src.name) instead of embedding\n\"None\"; keep the early return but ensure info always contains the adapter_found\nkey and the constructed warning.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`167-181`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Resolve the final standalone output file once and reuse it everywhere.**\n\nDirectory-style `--output` targets are still handled in two different ways: `_write_standalone()` may convert a directory into `<dir>/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, but `cmd_workspace_init()` keeps using the original `output_path` for relative-path computation and the manual-registration hint. That makes the copied `workspace = \"...\"` hint wrong for directory targets and still leaves not-yet-created directories ambiguous.\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed direction</summary>\n\n```diff\n+def _resolve_output_target(args: argparse.Namespace, scan_root: Path) -> Path:\n+    from ..constants import WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+\n+    if not args.output:\n+        return scan_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME\n+\n+    raw = Path(args.output).resolve()\n+    looks_like_dir = (\n+        args.output.endswith((os.sep, \"/\"))\n+        or raw.is_dir()\n+        or (not raw.exists() and raw.suffix == \"\")\n+    )\n+    return raw / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME if looks_like_dir else raw\n+\n+\n def _resolve_output_dir(args: argparse.Namespace, scan_root: Path, project_root: Path) -> Path:\n     \"\"\"Compute the output directory used for relative path computation.\"\"\"\n     if args.inline:\n         return project_root\n-    if args.output:\n-        _out_resolved = Path(args.output).resolve()\n-        return _out_resolved if _out_resolved.is_dir() else _out_resolved.parent\n-    return scan_root\n+    return _resolve_output_target(args, scan_root).parent\n@@\n-        output_path = Path(args.output).resolve() if args.output else (scan_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n+        output_path = _resolve_output_target(args, scan_root)\n         exit_code, data = _write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data)\n```\n</details>\n \n\n\nAlso applies to: 196-203, 329-336\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 167 -\n181, The output path is resolved differently between _write_standalone and\ncmd_workspace_init causing wrong \"workspace = ...\" hints for directory targets;\nupdate _write_standalone to compute the final file path once (if\noutput_path.is_dir() set output_path = output_path / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME),\npersist that resolved path in the function result (e.g., return it in the result\ndict or as part of the Tuple), and ensure toml_utils.dump writes to that\nresolved path; then modify cmd_workspace_init to consume the resolved output\npath returned from _write_standalone when computing relative paths and composing\nthe manual-registration/workspace hint so both code paths use the exact same\nfinal file location (refer to symbols: _write_standalone, cmd_workspace_init,\nWORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME, toml_utils.dump, and the\nmanual-registration/workspace hint generation).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`224-224`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Document the standalone workspace-file fallback too.**\n\nThis paragraph currently implies that workspace config is discovered only from `core.toml`, but the implementation also auto-discovers `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root` when no `workspace` key is present. The docs should mention that second step so the discovery model matches runtime behavior.\n \n\nBased on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step discovery order with auto-discovery of standalone workspace files at project_root as an intentional fallback.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/DESIGN.md at line 224, Update the DESIGN.md\nparagraph describing workspace config discovery to include the standalone\nfallback file: state that WorkspaceContext.load() (via find_workspace_config())\nfirst checks the core.toml `workspace` key (string path or inline dict) and, if\nabsent, auto-discovers a standalone .cypilot-workspace.toml at project_root as a\nfallback; ensure the doc mentions the two-step discovery order and that this\nmatches the runtime behavior used by find_workspace_config().\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2999-3005`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Restore JSON mode after forcing human output.**\n\nThese tests flip the module-global UI state to human mode and never restore it, so later command tests in the same module can become order-dependent. Add a cleanup right after each `set_json_mode(False)` call.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n from cypilot.utils.ui import set_json_mode\n set_json_mode(False)\n+self.addCleanup(set_json_mode, True)\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 3012-3019, 3027-3031, 3038-3046, 3053-3059, 3067-3071, 3079-3087, 3094-3098, 3105-3109, 3130-3134\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 2999 - 3005, The test forces\nglobal UI state to human mode by calling set_json_mode(False) (near uses with\n_human_validate) but never restores it, causing later tests to be\norder-dependent; after each set_json_mode(False) call add a cleanup to reset\nstate (e.g., call set_json_mode(True) or use try/finally to restore) immediately\nafter the block so the module-global UI mode is returned to JSON mode for\nsubsequent tests; locate all occurrences of set_json_mode(False) in this file\n(including the blocks around _human_validate) and ensure each has a matching\nrestoration to JSON mode.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`2809-2830`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Split the remaining compressed statements onto separate lines.**\n\nRuff is still going to fail on these new blocks with `E702` (`multiple statements on one line`). The earlier cleanup did not cover all of the newly added helpers/tests.\n  \n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\npython3 -m pip install ruff -q\nruff check tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py --select E702 -n\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 2883-2893, 2901-2901, 2992-2992, 3021-3021, 3061-3061, 3073-3073, 3171-3173, 3190-3191\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 2809 - 2830, Several helper/test\nclass definitions contain multiple statements on one line causing Ruff E702\n(e.g., in classes _FakeMeta, _FakeInnerCtx, _FakePrimary and the test setup\ncreating ws_ctx, TemporaryDirectory, art, inner); split each compressed\nstatement onto its own line: replace single-line multiple assignments like\n\"systems = []; kits = {}\" with two lines, move inline method definitions and\nreturns onto separate lines (e.g., def get_artifact_by_path(self, _rel): return\nNone → def get_artifact_by_path(self, _rel):\\n    return None), and ensure\nobject instantiations and attribute assignments such as \"ws_ctx =\nWorkspaceContext(primary=_FakePrimary(), sources={})\" and \"inner =\n_FakeInnerCtx(); inner.project_root = Path(td)\" are each on their own line so no\nline contains more than one statement (apply same fix to the other reported\nblocks at the noted locations).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/schemas/workspace.schema.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-3`: **Consider updating the `$id` to use an actual domain.**\n\nThe schema uses `https://example.com/cypilot/workspace.schema.json` as a placeholder. If this schema will be published or referenced externally, consider updating to a real domain (e.g., `https://cyberfabric.github.io/cyber-pilot/schemas/workspace.schema.json`).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/schemas/workspace.schema.json at line 3, Update the JSON\nSchema $id to a real, stable URL instead of the example placeholder; locate the\n$id field in workspace.schema.json and replace\n\"https://example.com/cypilot/workspace.schema.json\" with your published schema\nURL (e.g.,\n\"https://cyberfabric.github.io/cyber-pilot/schemas/workspace.schema.json\" or\nanother canonical domain you control) so external references and publishing\nresolve correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>requirements/workspace.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`128-131`: **Table entry for `path` could be more precise.**\n\nLine 130 states paths are \"resolved relative to workspace file location,\" but this only applies to standalone workspace files. For inline `[workspace]` in `core.toml`, paths resolve relative to the project root (as correctly documented in lines 165-168).\n\nConsider updating the table description for consistency:\n\n```diff\n-| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path, resolved relative to workspace file location. Takes precedence over `url` when both set. |\n+| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path. Resolved relative to workspace file (standalone) or project root (inline). Takes precedence over `url` when both set. |\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@requirements/workspace.md` around lines 128 - 131, Update the table entry for\nthe `path` field to clarify how resolution differs between standalone workspace\nfiles and inline workspace configs: state that when `path` is used in a\nstandalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` it is resolved relative to the workspace\nfile location, and when `path` is used in an inline `[workspace]` in `core.toml`\nit is resolved relative to the project root; reference the `path` field, the\ninline `[workspace]` section, and `core.toml` so readers can cross-check the\nlater docs (lines describing project-root resolution).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/cli.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`74-75`: **Minor: Duplicate horizontal rule.**\n\nThere are two consecutive `---` separators. One can be removed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n <!-- /toc -->\n\n ---\n-\n----\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/cli.md around lines 74 - 75, Remove the\nduplicate horizontal rule in the file by deleting one of the consecutive '---'\nseparators so there is only a single '---' divider present; locate the two\nadjacent '---' lines and remove one to eliminate the duplicate.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`730-731`: **Add language specifiers to fenced code blocks.**\n\nPer markdownlint, fenced code blocks should have a language specified. These command syntax blocks could use `text` or leave them as-is for plain command notation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Example fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n-cpt workspace-init [--root DIR] [--output PATH] [--inline] [--force] [--dry-run]\n-```\n+```text\n+cpt workspace-init