or\": str(exc)} for\nknown, recoverable errors, and add a final \"except Exception:\" that re-raises\nthe exception (or remove the catch) so programming errors aren't silently\nswallowed; update the block around the workspace processing where config is\nassigned to use these specific exception handlers.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`113-142`: **Kind inference uses primary-only system set.**\n\n`_match_system_prefix()` reads from `ctx.registered_systems`, which on `WorkspaceContext` contains only primary systems. When `--source` filters to a remote source, IDs from that source may have `kind=None` because their system prefixes aren't in the primary's registered set.\n\nConsider using `ctx.get_all_registered_systems()` when `is_workspace` is true to enable accurate kind inference for cross-repo IDs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested approach</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    registered_systems = set((ctx.registered_systems or set()) if ctx else set())\n+    if is_workspace and hasattr(ctx, 'get_all_registered_systems'):\n+        registered_systems = set(ctx.get_all_registered_systems() or set())\n+    else:\n+        registered_systems = set((ctx.registered_systems or set()) if ctx else set())\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py` around lines 113 - 142,\nThe system-prefix matching currently uses ctx.registered_systems (in\n_match_system_prefix), which only contains primary systems for a\nWorkspaceContext; update the logic to use ctx.get_all_registered_systems() when\nctx is a workspace (e.g., if ctx and getattr(ctx, \"is_workspace\", False):\nregistered_systems = set(ctx.get_all_registered_systems() or []) else:\nregistered_systems = set((ctx.registered_systems or set()) if ctx else set()))\nso _match_system_prefix and _infer_kind see all registered systems across\nsources and correctly infer kinds for cross-repo IDs; keep known_kinds handling\nas-is.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_sync.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-126`: **Extract source selection and sync execution into helpers.**\n\n`cmd_workspace_sync()` is already over the repo's complexity threshold, and the named-source validation, dry-run, base resolution, and aggregation branches are getting hard to evolve consistently. Splitting this into small helpers would make the exit-code behavior easier to preserve and test.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_sync.py` around lines 14 -\n126, The function cmd_workspace_sync is too large; split responsibilities into\nsmall helpers: implement get_git_sources(ws_cfg, source_name) to perform\nnamed-source lookup, validation (including URL check) and return the git_sources\ndict or error payload; implement dry_run_report(git_sources) to call ui.result\nwith the DRY_RUN payload using _human_workspace_sync; implement\ncompute_base_and_resolve(ws_cfg, project_root) to return (resolve_cfg, base)\nhonoring ws_cfg.resolve and resolution_base; and implement\nrun_sync_on_sources(git_sources, resolve_cfg, base) to call sync_git_source for\neach source, collect results, count synced/failed, and return (results, synced,\nfailed). Replace the corresponding blocks in cmd_workspace_sync to call these\nhelpers and preserve the existing ui.result payloads and final exit-code logic\n(status calculation and return value) exactly; keep references to ResolveConfig,\nsync_git_source, _human_workspace_sync, and ui.result unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<