":\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 366 - 374, The return annotation\n> for _bootstrap_kit uses a fully-qualified string\n> \"cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta.ArtifactsMeta\" which triggers F821 because cypilot\n> isn't defined at module scope; change the annotation to the short forward-ref\n> \"ArtifactsMeta\" and add a conditional import under TYPE_CHECKING: from\n> cypilot.utils.artifacts_meta import ArtifactsMeta (ensure TYPE_CHECKING is\n> imported from typing and place the import inside an if TYPE_CHECKING: block).\n> Update the function signature's return type to \"ArtifactsMeta\".\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (15)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>requirements/workspace.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`131-134`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Make the `path` row describe both resolution modes.**\n\nThe summary table still says `path` resolves relative to the workspace file, but the later Path Resolution section says inline `[workspace]` sources resolve relative to the project root. This row should describe both standalone and inline behavior.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path, resolved relative to workspace file location. Takes precedence over `url` when both set. |\n+| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path. In standalone workspace files it resolves relative to the workspace file; in inline `[workspace]` config it resolves relative to the project root. |\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@requirements/workspace.md` around lines 131 - 134, Update the `path` table\nrow to describe both resolution behaviors: state that when used in a standalone\n.cypilot-workspace.toml the `path` is resolved relative to the workspace file\nlocation, and when used as an inline `[workspace]` source it is resolved\nrelative to the project root; keep the note that `path` takes precedence over\n`url` when both are set and retain required/default metadata. Reference the\n`path` field and the inline `[workspace]` source behavior described in the Path\nResolution section to ensure wording matches both contexts.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`81-103`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--source` still doesn't scope `--include-code`.**\n\nThis branch narrows `artifacts_to_scan`, but the later `args.include_code` path still walks `ctx.meta.iter_all_codebase()` under `ctx.project_root`. `list-ids --source <name> --include-code` will still mix the selected source's artifacts with code references from the primary repo.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/list_ids.py around\nlines 81 - 103, When args.source is provided we currently narrow\nartifacts_to_scan but still run the include-code path over\nctx.meta/ctx.project_root; change the include-code handling so that when\nargs.source is set you resolve the matching source (the same loop that calls\n_get_expanded_meta(sc)) and use that source's expanded meta to iterate its\ncodebase (call _get_expanded_meta(sc) and then use its iter_all_codebase() or\nequivalent) instead of ctx.meta.iter_all_codebase() or walking ctx.project_root;\nensure this uses the same reachable/meta checks and appends only code files\nunder that source to artifacts_to_scan so --source correctly scopes\n--include-code.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`230-230`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Document the standalone workspace fallback in discovery flow.**\n\nLine 230 currently describes only `core.toml`-key discovery; it should also mention fallback auto-discovery of `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at project root.\n \n\nBased on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` uses a two-step order—`core.toml` `workspace` key first, then standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/DESIGN.md at line 230, The DESIGN.md text only\ndocuments discovery from the core.toml workspace key but omits the fallback to a\nstandalone .cypilot-workspace.toml; update the paragraph around\nWorkspaceContext.load() / find_workspace_config() to state the two-step\ndiscovery order: first honor the core.toml `workspace` key (string path or\ninline dict), then if absent attempt auto-discovery of a standalone\n`.cypilot-workspace.toml` at the project root, and clarify that this fallback is\nused when no core.toml workspace key is present so behavior matches the\nfind_workspace_config() implementation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`125-133`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Preserve workspace config errors in `--artifact` mode.**\n\nLine 215 resets `ctx_errors` and drops workspace config errors collected at Lines 125-133, so invalid workspace config can be silently hidden for artifact-scoped validation.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    # Surface context-level load errors (e.g., invalid constraints.toml) as validation errors.\n-    ctx_errors = list(getattr(ctx, \"_errors\", []) or [])\n+    # Surface context-level load errors (e.g., invalid constraints.toml) as validation errors.\n+    ctx_errors = list(getattr(ctx, \"_errors\", []) or [])\n+    ws_config_errors: List[Dict[str, object]] = []\n\n     # Validate workspace config if present\n     if ws_ctx is not None:\n         from ..utils.workspace import find_workspace_config as _find_ws\n         _ws_cfg, _ = _find_ws(ws_ctx.project_root)\n         if _ws_cfg is not None:\n             for ws_err in _ws_cfg.validate():\n-                ctx_errors.append(constraints_error(\n+                ws_config_errors.append(constraints_error(\n                     \"workspace\", ws_err, path=str(_ws_cfg.workspace_file),\n                 ))\n+    ctx_errors.extend(ws_config_errors)\n@@\n-        # Refresh context-level errors for this context.\n-        ctx_errors = list(getattr(ctx, \"_errors\", []) or [])\n+        # Refresh context-level errors for this context, but keep workspace-level config errors.\n+        ctx_errors = list(getattr(ctx, \"_errors\", []) or [])\n+        ctx_errors.extend(ws_config_errors)\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 214-216\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py around\nlines 125 - 133, Previously collected workspace validation errors from ws_ctx\n(found via _find_ws and stored as ctx_errors entries for _ws_cfg.validate()) are\nbeing lost when ctx_errors is later reset for --artifact mode; preserve them by\nsaving the workspace-specific errors before the reset and re-appending them\nafterward (or merge instead of overwriting). Concretely: when using ws_ctx and\n_ws_cfg to produce workspace errors, collect those into a temporary list (e.g.,\nworkspace_errors) rather than directly appending to ctx_errors, then after the\ncode path that resets ctx_errors for artifact-scoped validation, extend/merge\nctx_errors with workspace_errors so workspace config errors from\n_ws_cfg.validate() are not dropped. Ensure the logic touches the same symbols\n(_find_ws, _ws_cfg, ws_ctx, ctx_errors) so the workspace errors are preserved\nacross the artifact-mode reset.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`133-133`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify inline `path` resolution in this table row.**\n\nLine 133 currently documents only standalone behavior. Inline `[workspace]` source paths resolve relative to project root (as documented in Line 170-Line 171), so this row should mention both modes.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path, resolved relative to workspace file location. Takes precedence over `url` when both set. |\n+| `path`   | string | Yes (unless `url` is set)         | —           | Local filesystem path. In standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml`, resolve relative to the workspace file location; in inline `core.toml` workspace config, resolve relative to project root. Takes precedence over `url` when both set. |\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/requirements/workspace.md at line 133, Update the table row\nfor `path` to clarify both resolution modes: state that when `path` is used in a\nstandalone workspace file it is resolved relative to the workspace file location\n(and takes precedence over `url`), and when used as an inline `[workspace]`\nsource path it is resolved relative to the project root (matching the behavior\ndocumented around lines 170–171); keep the existing precedence note for `url`\nand ensure the wording explicitly contrasts the two modes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>architecture/PRD.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1014-1025`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**UC-015 still states two different contracts for local paths.**\n\nStep 3 says a local source path must already be a directory, while the alternative flow says unreachable paths are accepted and checked later. `workspace_add.py` implements the latter, so this use case should describe that behavior consistently.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@architecture/PRD.md` around lines 1014 - 1025, Update UC-015 to make the\ncontract for local source paths consistent with workspace_add.py: change Step 3\nto state that local source paths may be any path (they are accepted even if not\ncurrently reachable) and that existence/reachability is deferred to runtime\nchecks by the commands workspace-info and validate; also update the alternative\nflow \"Source path unreachable\" to match (remove the contradiction about\nrequiring an existing directory) and reference workspace_add.py as the\nauthoritative implementation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`308-315`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Build the discovery hint from the manifest that was actually written.**\n\nWhen `--output` is a directory, `_write_standalone()` writes `<dir>/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, but this hint still suggests `workspace = \"<dir>\"`. It also fires for `--output <project_root>`, even though that manifest is auto-discovered there. Derive the hint from `data[\"config_path\"]` and skip it when the written file is the project-root default.\n \n\nBased on learnings project-root `.cypilot-workspace.toml` is auto-discovered by `find_workspace_config()`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 308 -\n315, The hint logic should use the actual path written by _write_standalone\n(data[\"config_path\"]) instead of the original output_arg: after calling\n_write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data), read written_path =\nPath(data[\"config_path\"]).resolve(), and if written_path is not equal to\n(project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve() then compute rel =\nwritten_path.relative_to(project_root) if\nwritten_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else written_path and set data[\"hint\"]\nto the discovery hint using rel; otherwise do not set the hint (skip when the\nmanifest equals the project-root default, which is auto-discovered by\nfind_workspace_config()).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/cli.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`731-733`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add `bash` to the workspace command fences.**\n\nThese four blocks still trigger MD040 and keep docs lint noisy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```bash\n cpt workspace-init [--root DIR] [--output PATH] [--inline] [--force] [--max-depth N] [--dry-run]\n ```\n@@\n-```\n+```bash\n cpt workspace-add --name NAME (--path PATH | --url URL) [--branch BRANCH] [--role ROLE] [--adapter PATH] [--inline] [--force]\n ```\n@@\n-```\n+```bash\n cpt workspace-info\n ```\n@@\n-```\n+```bash\n cpt workspace-sync [--source NAME] [--dry-run] [--force]\n ```\n```\n</details>\n \n\n\nAlso applies to: 777-779, 825-827, 906-908\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/architecture/specs/cli.md around lines 731 - 733, Update\nthe Markdown fenced code blocks for the CLI commands to include the bash\nlanguage tag so they stop triggering MD040: add \"bash\" to the opening fences for\nthe blocks that show the commands cpt workspace-init, cpt workspace-add, cpt\nworkspace-info, and cpt workspace-sync (and the other occurrences noted at lines\naround 777-779, 825-827, 906-908) by replacing the triple-backtick fences with\ntriple-backtick + bash for those command examples.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`21-24`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Accept explicit adapter roots that have `config/`.**\n\nConfigured adapters like `.bootstrap` are valid when the directory itself is the Cypilot root, but this gate rejects them unless that root also contains `AGENTS.md`. Those sources will be reported as having no adapter and never get artifact counts.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     if explicit_adapter is not None:\n-        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"config\").is_dir():\n             return explicit_adapter\n         return None  # explicit path declared but invalid\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py\naround lines 21 - 24, The explicit_adapter check in workspace_info.py currently\nonly accepts a directory if it contains \"AGENTS.md\", causing valid adapter roots\nlike \".bootstrap\" (which have a \"config/\" subdirectory) to be rejected; update\nthe conditional around explicit_adapter to return the explicit_adapter when\nexplicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists() OR\n(explicit_adapter / \"config\").is_dir(), and otherwise return None, so adapters\nthat are Cypilot roots via a config/ directory are treated as valid.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`308-315`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Only emit the custom-output hint for truly non-default manifest paths.**\n\nAny explicit `--output` currently gets the “not discoverable automatically” hint. That is wrong when the written file is exactly `{project_root}/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, and if `--output` is a directory the suggested `workspace = \"...\"` value still points at the directory instead of the manifest file.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     output_path = Path(output_arg).resolve() if output_arg else (scan_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n     exit_code, data = _write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data)\n     if output_arg and exit_code == 0:\n-        rel = output_path.relative_to(project_root) if output_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else output_path\n-        data[\"hint\"] = (\n-            f\"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n-            f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n-        )\n+        written_path = Path(data[\"config_path\"]).resolve()\n+        default_path = (project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME).resolve()\n+        if written_path != default_path:\n+            rel = written_path.relative_to(project_root) if written_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else written_path\n+            data[\"hint\"] = (\n+                f\"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n+                f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n+            )\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py\naround lines 308 - 315, The hint is being emitted whenever --output is provided\neven if it points to the default manifest file or to a directory; change the\nlogic in the block around output_path/_write_standalone so you first compute the\ncanonical default manifest path (default_path = scan_root /\nWORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME), normalize the intended manifest file path (if\noutput_arg is a directory, treat the intended path as output_path /\nWORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME; otherwise use output_path), then compare the\nnormalized intended path to default_path (using resolved/absolute forms) and\nonly add the \"not discoverable\" hint when they differ; when building rel for the\nhint, use the normalized manifest file path (not the directory) and call\n.relative_to(project_root) only if that succeeds, otherwise use the absolute\nnormalized path.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2809-2829`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Split the remaining semicolon-chained statements onto separate lines.**\n\nRuff still reports E702 on these changed blocks, so the test module won't pass lint as-is.\n\n  \n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nruff check tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py --select E702 -n\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 2882-2900, 2991-2991, 3020-3020, 3060-3060, 3072-3072, 3170-3190\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 2809 - 2829, Several statements\nin the test (e.g., in class _FakeMeta and classes _FakeInnerCtx/_FakePrimary)\nuse semicolon-chained statements like \"systems = []; kits = {}\" and\n\"registered_systems = set(); kits = {}; _errors = []\" which triggers Ruff E702;\nsplit each semicolon-separated assignment or statement into its own line so each\nassignment (systems = [], kits = {}, registered_systems = set(), _errors = [],\nand method definitions) is on a separate line in the definitions for _FakeMeta,\n_FakeInnerCtx, and _FakePrimary, and apply the same split to the other cited\nblocks (around lines 2882-2900, 2991, 3020, 3060, 3072, 3170-3190) to eliminate\nE702.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`2998-3130`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Restore JSON mode after each formatter test.**\n\n`set_json_mode(False)` mutates module-global state and these tests never unwind it. Later direct-command tests in this module still parse JSON from stdout, so the suite becomes order-dependent.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Minimal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        from cypilot.utils.ui import set_json_mode\n-        set_json_mode(False)\n+        from cypilot.utils.ui import is_json_mode, set_json_mode\n+        prev_json_mode = is_json_mode()\n+        set_json_mode(False)\n+        self.addCleanup(set_json_mode, prev_json_mode)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tests/test_cli_py_coverage.py` around lines 2998 - 3130, Each formatter test\ncalls set_json_mode(False) and never restores it, making global JSON mode\npersist across tests; update each test that calls set_json_mode(False) (e.g.,\ntest_human_validate_formatter_pass,\ntest_human_validate_formatter_fail_truncation,\ntest_human_validate_formatter_other_status, test_format_issue_*, etc.) to\nrestore the previous mode after the test by capturing the original value and\nresetting it in a finally block (orig = set_json_mode(False) is not valid—call\nset_json_mode to set and read current mode first if available, otherwise call\nset_json_mode(False) inside a try/finally and call set_json_mode(True) in\nfinally) or use a context manager/fixture that sets JSON mode to False for the\nduration and then resets it; ensure you reference set_json_mode when making the\nchange so JSON mode is always returned to its prior state after each test.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`621-641`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Honor an explicit workspace adapter path without a root `AGENTS.md`.**\n\nThis guard rejects a configured `workspace.sources.<name>.adapter` directory unless `AGENTS.md` exists at its root, then silently falls back to `find_cypilot_directory(resolved_path)`. That can load a different adapter than the workspace config explicitly selected.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Minimal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    adapter_dir = None\n-    if explicit_adapter is not None and explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"AGENTS.md\").exists():\n-        adapter_dir = explicit_adapter\n-    else:\n-        # Fallback: auto-discover adapter from source root\n-        adapter_dir = find_cypilot_directory(resolved_path)\n-\n-    meta = None\n-    reg_systems: Set[str] = set()\n-    src_error = None\n+    adapter_dir = None\n+    src_error = None\n+    if explicit_adapter is not None:\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir():\n+            adapter_dir = explicit_adapter\n+        else:\n+            src_error = f\"Configured adapter path not found for source '{name}': {explicit_adapter}\"\n+    else:\n+        # Fallback: auto-discover adapter from source root\n+        adapter_dir = find_cypilot_directory(resolved_path)\n+\n+    meta = None\n+    reg_systems: Set[str] = set()\n@@\n-    elif src_entry.adapter is not None:\n+    elif src_entry.adapter is not None and src_error is None:\n         src_error = f\"Adapter not found for source '{name}' at {resolved_path}\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 621 - 641, The code currently rejects an explicitly configured adapter\ndirectory unless an AGENTS.md file exists, causing a silent fallback to\nfind_cypilot_directory; change the logic so that when explicit_adapter is\nprovided and is_dir() we accept it as adapter_dir (set adapter_dir =\nexplicit_adapter) and then call load_artifacts_meta(adapter_dir); if AGENTS.md\nis missing, emit a warning/log but do not ignore the explicit_adapter; keep the\nfind_cypilot_directory(resolved_path) fallback only when explicit_adapter is\nNone or not a directory. Ensure references to explicit_adapter, adapter_dir,\nAGENTS.md, load_artifacts_meta, and find_cypilot_directory are updated\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`184-205`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--source` is still bypassable for single-artifact validation.**\n\nLine 185 resolves relative artifact paths from the workspace cwd, not the selected source root, and Lines 199-204 only reject mismatches when `matched_sc` is set. `validate --source foo --artifact architecture/PRD.md` can still validate the primary repo or miss the intended remote file entirely.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Minimal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        artifact_path = Path(args.artifact).resolve()\n+        artifact_path = Path(args.artifact)\n+        if not artifact_path.is_absolute():\n+            base_root = project_root if args.source else Path.cwd()\n+            artifact_path = (base_root / artifact_path).resolve()\n+        else:\n+            artifact_path = artifact_path.resolve()\n@@\n-            if args.source and matched_sc is not None and matched_sc.name != args.source:\n+            if args.source:\n+                selected_root = project_root\n+                if getattr(matched_ctx, \"project_root\", None) != selected_root:\n+                    actual = matched_sc.name if matched_sc is not None else \"primary\"\n                     ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": (\n-                    f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{matched_sc.name}', \"\n+                    f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{actual}', \"\n                     f\"not '{args.source}'.\"\n                 )})\n                 return 1\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 184 - 205,\nThe artifact path is resolved against the workspace cwd and the code only\nrejects a source mismatch when determine_target_source returns matched_sc; fix\nby resolving args.artifact relative to the selected source root when args.source\nis provided (use workspace context to get the source root) before calling\ndetermine_target_source, and tighten the mismatch logic so that if args.source\nis set you error when either matched_sc is None or matched_sc.name !=\nargs.source; update the block that imports determine_target_source /\nCypilotContext and the conditional that sets ctx to enforce the source selection\nfor validate --artifact.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`15-16`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Import the forward-referenced context types explicitly.**\n\nRuff is still flagging `WorkspaceContext` / `CypilotContext` as undefined here, so this file won't pass lint as written. The same `TYPE_CHECKING` block can also cover `SystemNode` for Line 579 later in the file.\n\n  \n\n<details>\n<summary>Minimal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n+\n+if TYPE_CHECKING:\n+    from ..utils.artifacts_meta import SystemNode\n+    from ..utils.context import CypilotContext, WorkspaceContext\n```\n</details>\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nruff check skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py --select F821 -n\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 42-45\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 15 - 16,\nAdd explicit forward-type imports so Ruff doesn't flag\nWorkspaceContext/CypilotContext (and SystemNode later) as undefined: import\nTYPE_CHECKING from typing and inside an if TYPE_CHECKING: block add the needed\nimports for WorkspaceContext and CypilotContext (used by\n_resolve_source_context) and SystemNode (used later), so the names are available\nfor type checking without affecting runtime.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`394-395`: **Avoid blanket exception capture in workspace assembly.**\n\nLine 394 catches all exceptions and can hide unexpected regressions behind `{\"active\": false, \"error\": ...}`. Prefer narrowing this to expected failure classes so true coding errors still surface during development.\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Narrowed exception handling (example)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    except Exception as exc:\n+    except (ImportError, OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n         config[\"workspace\"] = {\"active\": False, \"error\": str(exc)}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/adapter_info.py` around lines 394 -\n395, The broad \"except Exception as exc:\" around the workspace assembly (where\nconfig[\"workspace\"] is set) should be narrowed to only the expected failure\ntypes so real bugs still surface; change the except to catch a specific tuple of\nexceptions (e.g., ValueError, KeyError, OSError or your domain-specific\nWorkspaceError) and set config[\"workspace\"] = {\"active\": False, \"error\":\nstr(exc)} there, and for any other exceptions re-raise them (or let them\npropagate) so unexpected errors in adapter_info.py aren't swallowed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`253-254`: **Use a `URL` label for Git sources in the human formatter.**\n\nFor `workspace-add --url ...`, this branch renders the remote under `Path`, which makes the success output slightly misleading. Switching the label based on whether `source[\"url\"]` or `source[\"path\"]` is present would keep the human formatter aligned with the payload.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_add.py` around lines 253 -\n254, The human-readable output shows remote Git repositories under the \"Path\"\nlabel; change the formatter to display \"URL\" when the source contains a \"url\"\nkey (i.e., when source.get(\"url\") is truthy) and keep \"Path\" when\nsource.get(\"path\") is present; locate the two ui.detail calls that render Source\nand Path (using ui.detail and source.get) and replace the second call with a\nconditional that uses the label \"URL\" for URL-based sources and \"Path\" for\nfilesystem sources so the label matches the payload.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`156-163`: **Expose `SourceContext.error` next to the affected source.**\n\nThis block only publishes aggregate context counts, so a reachable source that failed during `WorkspaceContext` construction has no per-source explanation in `workspace-info`. Merging `sc.error` back into the matching source entry would make the command much more actionable.\n\n\nBased on learnings `_load_reachable_source` already stores source-level failures in `SourceContext.error`, but that field is currently never surfaced to users.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_info.py` around lines 156 -\n163, The workspace-info handler currently only emits aggregate counts from\nget_context()/WorkspaceContext; include per-source errors by merging\nSourceContext.error into each source entry so users see failures recorded by\n_load_reachable_source. Locate the ctx.sources mapping (used in the block around\nget_context/WorkspaceContext and where reachable_count is computed) and when\nbuilding the result[\"sources\"] or per-source dicts, add an \"error\" field\npopulated with sc.error (or null/None if absent) for each SourceContext; keep\nthe existing reachable_count and total_registered_systems logic intact.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/workspace.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`511-523`: **Consider sorting `__all__` alphabetically.**\n\nRuff flags that `__all__` is not sorted. While not critical, sorting improves maintainability.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested sorted order</summary>\n\n```diff\n __all__ = [\n+    \"NamespaceRule\",\n+    \"ResolveConfig\",\n+    \"SourceEntry\",\n+    \"TraceabilityConfig\",\n     \"VALID_ROLES\",\n+    \"WorkspaceConfig\",\n+    \"find_workspace_config\",\n+    \"load_inline_config\",\n+    \"require_project_root\",\n     \"validate_source_name\",\n-    \"SourceEntry\",\n-    \"TraceabilityConfig\",\n-    \"NamespaceRule\",\n-    \"ResolveConfig\",\n-    \"WorkspaceConfig\",\n-    \"find_workspace_config\",\n-    \"require_project_root\",\n-\n-    \"load_inline_config\",\n ]\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summ