ot-workspace.md\n* .bootstrap/.core/architecture/features/traceability-validation.md\n* .bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_sync.py\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#pullrequestreview-3949119923","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/81#pullrequestreview-3949119923"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/81"}},"submitted_at":"2026-03-14T18:19:57Z","commit_id":"ed70b29788f350969c136e1d46992d66e4a85eb0"},{"id":3949220039,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOQ7VXwc7rZFDH","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 4**\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`310-317`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Non-default standalone output is still easy to make undiscoverable.**\n\nThe default standalone path is derived from `scan_root`, so `workspace-init --root ..` writes a manifest that later commands will not auto-discover. The hint also uses the pre-write `output_path`, so directory targets suggest `workspace = \"<dir>\"` instead of the actual file. Base this on `data[\"config_path\"]`, and handle every written path that differs from `project_root/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, not just explicit `--output` cases.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>💡 Possible fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    output_path = Path(output_arg).resolve() if output_arg else (scan_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n+    output_path = Path(output_arg).resolve() if output_arg else (project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n     exit_code, data = _write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data)\n-    if output_arg and exit_code == 0:\n-        rel = output_path.relative_to(project_root) if output_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else output_path\n-        data[\"hint\"] = (\n-            f\"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n-            f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n-        )\n+    if exit_code == 0:\n+        written_path = Path(data[\"config_path\"])\n+        if written_path != project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME:\n+            rel = written_path.relative_to(project_root) if written_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else written_path\n+            data[\"hint\"] = (\n+                \"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n+                f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n+            )\n```\n</details>\nBased on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` first checks the `workspace` key in `core.toml` and otherwise only auto-discovers a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py` around lines 310 -\n317, The hint logic currently checks only output_arg and uses the pre-write\noutput_path, which can produce incorrect/unhelpful hints; update the post-write\nlogic after calling _write_standalone to base discovery hints on\ndata[\"config_path\"] (the actual path written) and not just on output_arg, and if\ndata[\"config_path\"] is not equal to project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME set\ndata[\"hint\"] to instruct adding workspace = \"<relative path to\ndata['config_path']>\" to config/core.toml (use project_root-relative path when\npossible); ensure you treat cases where config_path points to a directory vs the\nactual file so the hint references the actual config file name.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`310-317`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Non-default standalone output is still easy to make undiscoverable.**\n\nThe default standalone path is derived from `scan_root`, so `workspace-init --root ..` writes a manifest that later commands will not auto-discover. The hint also uses the pre-write `output_path`, so directory targets suggest `workspace = \"<dir>\"` instead of the actual file. Base this on `data[\"config_path\"]`, and handle every written path that differs from `project_root/.cypilot-workspace.toml`, not just explicit `--output` cases.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>💡 Possible fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    output_path = Path(output_arg).resolve() if output_arg else (scan_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n+    output_path = Path(output_arg).resolve() if output_arg else (project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME)\n     exit_code, data = _write_standalone(output_path, workspace_data)\n-    if output_arg and exit_code == 0:\n-        rel = output_path.relative_to(project_root) if output_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else output_path\n-        data[\"hint\"] = (\n-            f\"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n-            f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n-        )\n+    if exit_code == 0:\n+        written_path = Path(data[\"config_path\"])\n+        if written_path != project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME:\n+            rel = written_path.relative_to(project_root) if written_path.is_relative_to(project_root) else written_path\n+            data[\"hint\"] = (\n+                \"Custom output path used. Other commands will not discover this file automatically. \"\n+                f'Add \\'workspace = \"{rel}\"\\' to config/core.toml to enable discovery.'\n+            )\n```\n</details>\nBased on learnings: `find_workspace_config()` first checks the `workspace` key in `core.toml` and otherwise only auto-discovers a standalone `.cypilot-workspace.toml` at `project_root`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py\naround lines 310 - 317, The current logic only warns when --output is passed and\nuses the pre-write output_path which can be a directory and may not reflect the\nactual written file; change the check after calling _write_standalone to compare\ndata[\"config_path\"] (the actual path written by _write_standalone) against the\ndefault (project_root / WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME) and, if different, compute\nrel = Path(data[\"config_path\"]).relative_to(project_root) when possible\n(otherwise use the absolute path) and set data[\"hint\"] to instruct adding\nworkspace = \"<rel>\" to config/core.toml; update references in workspace_init.py\n(output_path, _write_standalone, data[\"config_path\"], WORKSPACE_CONFIG_FILENAME,\nproject_root, scan_root) so the hint is based on the post-write config_path for\nall non-default writes, not only when output_arg is provided.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-17`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Resolve annotation symbols to clear Ruff F821.**\n\nLine 16 and Line 43 still trigger undefined-name checks for `WorkspaceContext` / `CypilotContext`. Add a type-only import block so lint passes consistently.\n\n  \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n+\n+if TYPE_CHECKING:\n+    from ..utils.artifacts_meta import SystemNode\n+    from ..utils.context import CypilotContext, WorkspaceContext\n```\n</details>\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify unresolved names in annotations are gone.\nruff check skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py --select F821 -n\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 42-45\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 15 - 17,\nThe undefined-name lint errors for WorkspaceContext and CypilotContext in the\n_resolve_source_context function annotations are caused by runtime name\nresolution; fix by adding a type-only import block (using typing.TYPE_CHECKING)\nthat imports WorkspaceContext and CypilotContext only for type checking, or\nenable postponed evaluation of annotations (from __future__ import annotations)\nat the top of the module; update the file to import these symbols in a\nTYPE_CHECKING guard so the annotations on _resolve_source_context (and other\nlines around 42-45) resolve for Ruff F821 without affecting runtime.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`194-205`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--source` enforcement still bypasses primary-context matches.**\n\nAt Line 199, mismatch rejection only runs when `matched_sc is not None`. If the artifact resolves to primary, `--source` can still be bypassed.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if ws_ctx is not None:\n+            selected_root = getattr(ctx, \"project_root\", None) if args.source else None\n             matched_sc, matched_ctx = determine_target_source(artifact_path, ws_ctx)\n             if matched_ctx is None:\n                 ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": f\"Cannot resolve context for artifact: {artifact_path}\"})\n                 return 1\n-            if args.source and matched_sc is not None and matched_sc.name != args.source:\n-                ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": (\n-                    f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{matched_sc.name}', \"\n-                    f\"not '{args.source}'.\"\n-                )})\n-                return 1\n+            if args.source:\n+                if selected_root is None or getattr(matched_ctx, \"project_root\", None) != selected_root:\n+                    actual = matched_sc.name if matched_sc is not None else \"primary\"\n+                    ui.result({\"status\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": (\n+                        f\"Artifact '{args.artifact}' belongs to source '{actual}', \"\n+                        f\"not '{args.source}'.\"\n+                    )})\n+                    return 1\n             ctx = matched_ctx\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/validate.py` around lines 194 - 205,\nThe current check only rejects a --source mismatch when matched_sc is not None,\nallowing artifacts resolved to the workspace primary to bypass --source; update\nthe logic after determine_target_source to compute the resolved source name (use\nmatched_sc.name if matched_sc is present, otherwise derive the workspace primary\nsource name from ws_ctx, e.g. ws_ctx.primary.name or the appropriate primary\nsource property), then if args.source is provided and does not equal that\nresolved source name, call ui.result with the error and return 1; keep the\nmatched_ctx assignment to ctx as before.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`621-628`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Explicit `adapter` can still be silently ignored and replaced.**\n\nLine 623 requires a `config/` subdir before honoring `explicit_adapter`; otherwise it falls back to auto-discovery. That can mask a configured adapter and load a different one.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    adapter_dir = None\n-    if explicit_adapter is not None and explicit_adapter.is_dir() and (explicit_adapter / \"config\").is_dir():\n-        adapter_dir = explicit_adapter\n-    else:\n-        # Fallback: auto-discover adapter from source root\n-        adapter_dir = find_cypilot_directory(resolved_path)\n+    adapter_dir = None\n+    src_error = None\n+    if explicit_adapter is not None:\n+        if explicit_adapter.is_dir():\n+            # Respect explicit adapter path; loader will validate structure.\n+            adapter_dir = explicit_adapter\n+        else:\n+            src_error = f\"Configured adapter path not found for source '{name}': {explicit_adapter}\"\n+    if adapter_dir is None and explicit_adapter is None:\n+        # Fallback only when no explicit adapter is configured\n+        adapter_dir = find_cypilot_directory(resolved_path)\n \n     meta = None\n     reg_systems: Set[str] = set()\n-    src_error = None\n@@\n-    elif src_entry.adapter is not None:\n+    elif src_entry.adapter is not None and src_error is None:\n         src_error = f\"Adapter not found for source '{name}' at {resolved_path}\"\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 640-642\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/utils/context.py around\nlines 621 - 628, The code currently ignores a provided explicit_adapter unless\nit contains a \"config\" subdir, which can silently replace a user-configured\nadapter with one found by find_cypilot_directory; change the logic in the\nadapter selection so explicit_adapter is honored if it exists and is a directory\n(explicit_adapter.is_dir()) and only fall back to find_cypilot_directory when\nexplicit_adapter is None or not a directory; if you still need the config/\ncheck, emit a warning or log when explicit_adapter lacks \"config\" rather than\nsilently falling back. Apply the same fix to the similar check referenced around\nlines 640-642 (the other explicit_adapter/config check) so both use the same\nexistence-first policy and log on missing config.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.bootstrap/.core/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot/commands/workspace_init.py:\n- Around line 152-168: The scan currently stops descending when\n_is_project_dir(entry) is true but _find_adapter_path(entry) returns falsy,\nwhich skips nested repos with adapters; instead, when adapter_path is falsy call\n_scan_nested_repos(entry, output_dir, max_depth, _current_depth + 1) and merge\nits results into discovered using _dedup_source_k