ata. No other changes.|\n|**Design examples** <br> `kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/examples/example.md`|Updated Example.md Date from 2025-01-15 to 2026-01-15. No content changes.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~1 minute\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I nudged the dates with gentle hops,  \n> From twenty‑twenty‑five to twenty‑twenty‑six,  \n> The docs keep pace, no other stops,  \n> A tiny tweak, no trick or mix,  \n> — Sincerely, your hare with calendar tricks ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n### ❌ Failed checks (1 warning)\n\n|  Check name | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Resolution                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| :---------: | :--------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Title check | ⚠️ Warning | The PR title describes a date correction in an ADR, but the changeset also includes unrelated date updates in multiple other documentation files (DESIGN.md, decomposition checklist/rules, and example.md), making the title incomplete and partially misleading. | Update the title to reflect all changes, such as 'docs: Update documentation dates from 2025 to 2026' 