itly list \"actors\", \"problems\",\n\"functional requirements (FR)\", \"non-functional requirements (NFR)\", \"use\ncases\", and \"success criteria\" so the PRD definition aligns with the SDLC kit\nexpectations (e.g., update the PRD — Product Requirements Document entry to read\nthat it documents product intent including actors, problems, FR, NFR, use cases,\nand success criteria).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`54-56`: **DESIGN definition misses required scope details.**\n\nThe DESIGN definition doesn’t mention boundaries, interfaces, drivers, or principles/constraints, which are required in DESIGN artifacts. Consider updating the sentence to include those elements explicitly.  \nBased on learnings: “Applies to kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/*.md : DESIGN artifacts must document system blueprint including architecture, components, boundaries, interfaces, drivers, and principles/constraints”.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@README.md` around lines 54 - 56, Update the \"DESIGN — Technical Design\nDocument\" description to explicitly list the required scope items: architecture,\ncomponents, boundaries, interfaces, drivers, and principles/constraints;\nspecifically edit the line labeled \"DESIGN — Technical Design Document\" so it\nreads something like \"Describes system architecture, components, boundaries,\ninterfaces, drivers, and principles/constraints, plus implementation approach\"\nto ensure DESIGN artifacts follow the kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/*.md\nrequirement.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Around line 48-50: Expand the PRD bullet description to include the required\nartifact contents: explicitly list \"actors\"