sted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>.cypilot/requirements/adapter-structure.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `937-940`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Duplicate note paragraphs.**\n> \n> Lines 937-939 contain two nearly identical \"Note\" paragraphs about artifact paths. One mentions `specs/` subdirectory, the other mentions `features/` subdirectory. Consolidate into a single comprehensive note.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>♻️ Proposed consolidation</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`specs/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n> -\n> -**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`features/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n> +**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`features/`, `ADR/`, etc.) are defined by the kit.\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.cypilot/requirements/adapter-structure.md around lines 937 - 940, There are\n> two near-duplicate \"Note\" paragraphs about artifact paths (one referencing a\n> specs/ subdirectory and the other a features/ subdirectory); consolidate them\n> into a single comprehensive Note that mentions both possible subdirectories\n> (specs/ and features/), merges any differing details, removes duplication, and\n> ensures the final paragraph reads clearly and unambiguously about artifact path\n> resolution and usage.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>.cypilot-adapter/artifacts.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `82-82`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Fix placeholder syntax in `system_root`: `$system` should be `{system}`.**\n> \n> Line 82 uses `$system`, but the artifacts-registry.md specification (line 461) and all other codebase usages define `{system}` as the placeholder format. This inconsistency will cause autodetect to fail.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -          \"system_root\": \"{project_root}/examples/$system\",\n> +          \"system_root\": \"{project_root}/examples/{system}\",\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.cypilot-adapter/artifacts.json at line 82, Replace the incorrect\n> placeholder in the artifacts JSON so autodetect matches the registry spec:\n> locate the \"system_root\" entry and change its value from using the $system\n> placeholder to the brace-style placeholder used across the codebase (i.e.,\n> replace \"$system\" with \"{system}\") so the \"system_root\" key uses \"{system}\" as\n> the placeholder format.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🟡 Minor comments (34)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/CLISPEC.md-269-269 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`269-269`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix spaces inside code span.**\n\nMD038 flags spaces inside the inline code span. Remove inner spaces so the code span is tight.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/CLISPEC.md at line 269, The inline code span \" `$ ` \" contains\ninner spaces that trigger MD038; replace it with a tight code span by removing\nthe inner space (e.g., change the code span from `$ ` to `$`) in the statement\n\"✅ Examples must start with `$ `\", ensuring the backticks enclose the exact `$`\ncharacter with no surrounding spaces.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/CLISPEC.md-31-53 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`31-53`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks.**\n\nmarkdownlint reports MD040 for multiple code fences lacking a language. Please annotate these fences (e.g., `text`, `markdown`, `bash`, `python`) to satisfy MD040.  \n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 64-108, 113-123, 143-147, 165-179, 194-205, 209-212, 218-248, 327-347\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/CLISPEC.md around lines 31 - 53, Multiple fenced code blocks (e.g.,\nthe block starting with ``` containing \"COMMAND <command-name> ... EXAMPLE: $\n<example-usage>\" and other similar blocks that show CLI examples or specs) lack\nlanguage identifiers and trigger markdownlint MD040; update each triple-backtick\nfence in .cypilot/CLISPEC.md to include an appropriate language tag (for example\nuse \"text\" or \"markdown\" for spec blocks, \"bash\" for shell examples like\n\"EXAMPLE: $ <example-usage>\", or \"json\"/\"yaml\"/\"python\" where applicable) across\nthe affected sections (the initial COMMAND block and the other fenced blocks\nwith ARGUMENTS/OPTIONS/EXIT CODES/RELATED or example snippets) so every code\nfence includes a language identifier.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md-937-940 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`937-940`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Duplicate note paragraphs.**\n\nLines 937-939 contain two nearly identical \"Note\" paragraphs. This appears to be copy-paste duplication. Remove one.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n **Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`specs/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n-\n-**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`features/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md around lines 937 - 940, Remove\nthe duplicated \"Note\" paragraph that begins \"Note: Artifact paths are FULL paths\nrelative to `project_root`...\" so only a single copy remains; search for the two\nadjacent identical notes in .cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md (the\nlines containing the text about `artifacts_dir` and subdirectories like\n`specs/`/`features/` and `ADR/`) and delete one of them to eliminate the\ncopy-paste duplication.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/README.md-22-54 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`22-54`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Structure diagram shows outdated path.**\n\nThe structure diagram at line 23 shows `kits/sdlc/` but this PR relocates the kit to `.cypilot/kits/sdlc/`. Update the diagram to reflect the actual path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ```text\n-kits/sdlc/\n+.cypilot/kits/sdlc/\n ├── README.md           # This file\n ├── artifacts/\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/README.md around lines 22 - 54, Update the\nASCII structure diagram in README.md to reflect the relocated kit path by\nreplacing the top-level \"kits/sdlc/\" entry with \".cypilot/kits/sdlc/\" (the\nREADME.md file and the fenced code block containing the tree should be updated\nso the tree now starts with \".cypilot/kits/sdlc/\" and retains the existing child\nentries like artifacts/, codebase/, and their files).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/README.md-64-68 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`64-68`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Usage paths also reference outdated location.**\n\nThe path resolution examples reference `kits/sdlc/artifacts/...` but should use `.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/...` to match the relocated structure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ```text\n-template:  kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/template.md\n-checklist: kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/checklist.md\n-example:   kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/examples/example.md\n+template:  .cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/template.md\n+checklist: .cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/checklist.md\n+example:   .cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/examples/example.md\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/README.md around lines 64 - 68, Update the\nthree path entries (template, checklist, example) in the README so they\nreference the relocated directory by prefixing each path with \".cypilot/\";\nchange the values for the keys \"template\", \"checklist\", and \"example\" from\n\"kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/...\" to \".cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/{KIND}/...\" to\nmatch the new structure.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md-245-245 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`245-245`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove trailing spaces inside code spans (MD038).**\nUse a visible space marker or remove the trailing space in the examples.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n-- If the heading is numbered, the numbering prefix is parsed as `^<num>(\\.<num>)*\\s+` (e.g. `1 `, `1.2 `, `2.10.3 `).\n+- If the heading is numbered, the numbering prefix is parsed as `^<num>(\\.<num>)*\\s+` (e.g. `1␠`, `1.2␠`, `2.10.3␠`).\n@@\n-- ``- `cpt-my-system-fr-login` ``\n-- ``* `cpt-my-system-fr-login` ``\n+- ``- `cpt-my-system-fr-login``\n+- ``* `cpt-my-system-fr-login``\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 388-392\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md at line 245, Remove the trailing\nspace characters inside inline code spans in the examples (e.g. change \"`1 `\" to\n\"`1`\" and \"`1.2 `\" to \"`1.2`\") so the regex example `^<num>(\\.<num>)*\\s+` no\nlonger contains code spans with trailing spaces; apply the same removal to the\nother occurrences mentioned (lines 388-392) to satisfy MD038.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/codebase/rules.md-96-107 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`96-107`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language tags to fenced blocks to satisfy MD040.**\nSeveral fenced blocks omit a language; `text` is sufficient for these pseudo-code/outputs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix (apply to each fenced block)</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n-```\n+```text\n CODE markers exist\n     ↓\n FEATURE: flow/algo/state/dod IDs → [x]\n     ↓\n FEATURE: ALL IDs [x] → mark feature entry [x] in DECOMPOSITION\n     ↓\n DECOMPOSITION: feature entry [x] → referenced PRD/DESIGN IDs (fr, principle, component, etc.) → [x]\n     ↓\n PRD: fr/nfr IDs [x] when ALL downstream refs [x]\n DESIGN: principle/constraint/component/seq/dbtable IDs [x] when ALL refs [x]\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 236-242, 411-428, 484-504\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each findin