(or equivalent)\nabove the \"Phase 3: Cypilot Markers\" heading to restore valid navigation; apply\nthe same fix for the similar entry mentioned at lines 248-249.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/constraints.md-3-3 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-3`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update the constraints source path to the new .cypilot location.**\nThis now lives under `.cypilot/kits/sdlc`; the current path is misleading.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-Source: `kits/sdlc/constraints.json`\n+Source: `../constraints.json`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/constraints.md at line 3, Update the Source path\nin the constraints guide so it points to the new repository location: replace\nthe existing \"Source: `kits/sdlc/constraints.json`\" entry in\n.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/constraints.md with \"Source:\n`.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json`\" (and update any identical \"Source\"\nreferences in that file), ensuring the Source line now references the new\n.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json path.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/README.md-41-51 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`41-51`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Heading says “6‑Layer” but the table lists seven artifacts.**\nThe list includes BRD, PRD, ADR, DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, FEATURE, and CODE. Align the heading with the actual count.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-## The 6-Layer SDLC Pipeline\n+## The 7-Layer SDLC Pipeline\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/README.md around lines 41 - 51, The heading \"The 6-Layer\nSDLC Pipeline\" is inconsistent with the seven artifacts listed (BRD, PRD, ADR,\nDESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, FEATURE, CODE); update the heading text \"The 6-Layer SDLC\nPipeline\" to \"The 7-Layer SDLC Pipeline\" (or alternatively remove or consolidate\nan artifact if you intend six layers) so it matches the listed artifacts and\nkeep all artifact names (BRD, PRD, ADR, DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, FEATURE, CODE)\nunchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json-1014-1019 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1014-1019`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove the duplicate example entry.**\n`cpt-cypilot-status-overall` appears twice in the status examples list.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n         \"examples\": [\n           \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\",\n           \"cpt-overwork-alert-status-overall\",\n-          \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"\n+          \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"\n         ],\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json around lines 1014 - 1019, In the\n\"examples\" array for the template \"cpt-{system}-status-overall\" remove the\nduplicate string \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\" so each example is unique; locate\nthe examples array under the template key and delete the repeated entry, keeping\nonly one \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\" alongside the other examples.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/codebase/rules.md-76-79 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`76-79`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clean up the nested code span around `inst-*`.**\nThe current inline code span embeds backticks and trips MD038; a single code span renders cleanly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [ ] If Mode ON: every implemented CDSL instruction (`[x] ... `inst-*``) has a paired `@cpt-begin/.../@cpt-end` block marker in code\n+- [ ] If Mode ON: every implemented CDSL instruction (`[x] ... inst-*`) has a paired `@cpt-begin/.../@cpt-end` block marker in code\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/codebase/rules.md around lines 76 - 79, The inline code\nspan for the CDSL instruction is nested and contains extra backticks (the\nfragment \"[x] ... `inst-*``\"), which trips MD038; update the bullet so the\ninstruction token is a single, normal code span: replace the nested/back-to-back\nbackticks with `inst-*` and adjust the surrounding text to remove the extra\nbackticks so the line reads e.g. \"If Mode ON: every implemented CDSL instruction\n(`[x] ... inst-*`) has a paired `@cpt-begin/.../@cpt-end` block marker in code\"\n(target the line containing inst-*).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md-421-427 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`421-427`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add a language tag to the fenced “ignored” example (MD040).**\nThe inner fence is unlabeled; `text` is sufficient here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n ```markdown\n-```\n+```text\n ...ignored...\n ```\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md around lines 421 - 427, The inner\nfenced code block in the markdown snippet is missing a language tag (MD040);\nupdate the unlabeled inner fence to include a simple tag such as text (change\n``` to ```text) so the example is properly labeled and satisfies the linter\nrule.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/CDSL.md-365-416 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`365-416`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Specify a language for the fenced error-message examples.**\nmarkdownlint flags the error snippets; adding `text` keeps the examples readable and lint-clean.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix (apply to each error snippet)</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n-```\n+```text\n ⚠️ Invalid CDSL syntax detected: {description}\n → Location: {file}:{line}\n → Found: {prohibited element}\n → Fix: Replace with plain English description\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/CDSL.md around lines 365 - 416, Add a language tag\n(use text) to each fenced code-block showing error-message examples in\n.cypilot/requirements/CDSL.md so they are lint-clean; update the three‑backtick\nfences that surround the \"Invalid CDSL syntax detected: {description}\" example\nand all other examples under \"Missing Required Tokens\", \"Duplicate Instruction\nIDs\", \"Unbalanced Cypilot Markers in Code\", and \"Empty Cypilot Block in Code\" to\nstart with ```text (not plain ```), leaving the content unchanged and keeping\ntokens like cpt-begin/cpt-end, inst-{id}, and the example messages intact.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/agent-compliance.md-18-20 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-20`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix TOC anchor for emoji heading.**\n\nThe TOC entry for “Agent Anti-Patterns” uses `#-agent-anti-patterns`, which won’t match the generated heading ID.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [Agent Anti-Patterns](`#-agent-anti-patterns`)\n+- [Agent Anti-Patterns](`#agent-anti-patterns`)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/agent-compliance.md around lines 18 - 20, The TOC\nentry uses the incorrect anchor \"#-agent-anti-patterns\" for the \"Agent\nAnti-Patterns\" heading; update the link to the correct generated anchor (remove\nthe leading dash) by replacing \"#-agent-anti-patterns\" with\n\"#agent-anti-patterns\" in the table of contents so it matches the \"Agent\nAnti-Patterns\" heading ID.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md-17-22 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`17-22`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix TOC anchors for emoji headings.**\n\nThe TOC links use `#-...` but the actual heading IDs for emoji-prefixed titles typically resolve without the leading hyphen. This likely breaks in-page navigation.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [Execution Protocol Violations](`#-execution-protocol-violations`)\n-- [Compaction Recovery](`#-compaction-recovery`)\n+- [Execution Protocol Violations](`#execution-protocol-violations`)\n+- [Compaction Recovery](`#compaction-recovery`)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md around lines 17 - 22, The TOC\nentries for emoji-prefixed headings use anchors with a leading hyphen (e.g.\n`#-execution-protocol-violations`, `#-compaction-recovery`) which don't match\nthe generated heading IDs; update the TOC to use the actual IDs (remove the\nleading hyphen and use the slugified text) for \"Execution Protocol Violations\",\n\"Compaction Recovery\", and any other emoji-prefixed titles so links point to\n`#execution-protocol-violations`, `#compaction-recovery`, etc., matching the\nheadings in the document.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/template.md-3-8 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-8`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Normalize placeholder names for feature IDs.**\n\nThe template mixes `{feature-slug}` and `{slug}` for feature IDs, which can produce mismatched identifiers.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-{system}-featstatus-{feature-slug}`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-{system}-featstatus-{feature-slug}`\n\n- [ ] `p2` - `cpt-{system}-feature-{slug}`\n+ [ ] `p2` - `cpt-{system}-feature-{feature-slug}`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/template.md around lines 3 - 8, The\ntemplate mixes two different placeholder names for feature identifiers (e.g.,\n`cpt-{system}-featstatus-{feature-slug}` vs `cpt-{system}-feature-{slug}`),\ncausing inconsistent IDs; update the template so both checklist entries use the\nsame placeholder name (choose either `{feature-slug}` or `{slug}`) and replace\nall occurrences (notably the `p1` line `cpt-{system}-featstatus-{feature-slug}`\nand the `p2` line `cpt-{system}-feature-{slug}`) to the single normalized\nplaceholder to ensure consistent generated IDs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/rules.md-239-285 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`239-285`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks (markdownlint MD040).**\n\nmarkdownlint reports missing languages on multiple fenced blocks; adding `text` keeps them valid and quiets warnings.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n DECOMPOSITION Validation Report\n ═══════════════════════════════\n \n Structural: PASS/FAIL\n Decomposition Quality: PASS/FAIL (N issues)\n \n Issues:\n - [SEVERITY] CHECKLIST-ID: Description\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n ⚠ Template not found: kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/template.md\n → Verify Cypilot installation is complete\n → STOP — cannot proceed without template\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n ⚠ DESIGN not found or not readable\n → Ask user for DESIGN location\n → Cannot decompose without DESIGN artifact\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n ⚠ Coverage gap: {design element} not assigned to any feature\n → Add design element to appropriate feature\n → Or document intentional exclusion with reasoning\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n ⚠ Scope overlap: {design element} appears in multiple features: {feature1}, {feature2}\n → Assign to single feature\n → Or document intentional sharing with reasoning\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/rules.md around lines 239 - 285,\nSeveral fenced code blocks in the DECOMPOSITION rules (the \"DECOMPOSITION\nValidation Report\" block and each error-handling example beginning with \"⚠\nTemplate not found:\", \"⚠ DESIGN not found or not readable\", \"⚠ Coverage gap:\"\nand \"⚠ Scope overlap:\") lack language identifiers, triggering markdownlint\nMD040; add a language tag (e.g., text) to each opening ``` so the blocks become\n```text and ensure all closing fences remain ``` to silence the warnings and\nkeep rendering unchanged.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/PRD/template.md-147-153 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`147-153`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix heading level jump in Use Cases.**\n\nLine 151 uses an H4 immediately under an H2, which violates MD001 and makes the outline inconsistent. Prefer an H3 here (or add a missing H3 section header first).  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-#### {Use Case Name}\n+### {Use Case Name}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifac