ound lines 170 - 179, The\nmarkdown fenced code blocks in the PRD validation sections (e.g., the \"PRD\nValidation Report\" block and the subsequent\nwarning/template/checklist/example/adapter blocks) are missing language\nidentifiers which triggers MD040; update every triple-backtick fence in\n.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/PRD/rules.md that surrounds those blocks to declare\na language (use \"text\") so they become ```text ... ```; ensure you update all\nrepeated occurrences referenced in the review (the main report block and the\nwarning/template/checklist/example/adapter blocks) so linting passes.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/examples/example.md-115-116 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`115-116`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix dependency inconsistency in “Feature Dependencies.”**\n\nThe global section states “None,” but Notifications depends on `cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`. This can mislead validation and readers.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-## 3. Feature Dependencies\n-\n-None.\n+## 3. Feature Dependencies\n+\n+- `cpt-taskflow-feature-notifications` depends on `cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on learnings, DECOMPOSITION artifacts must provide an executable plan with FEATURE list, ordering, dependencies, and coverage links back to PRD and DESIGN.\n\n\nAlso applies to: 178-181\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/examples/example.md around lines\n115 - 116, The \"Feature Dependencies\" section is inconsistent: the global\ndependencies claim \"None\" while the Notifications feature lists\n`cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`; update the example so globals and per-feature\ndependencies match by either adding `cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud` to the\nglobal dependency list or removing it from the Notifications feature, and ensure\nthe Notifications entry in \"Feature Dependencies\" (and the repeated block at\nlines ~178-181) includes explicit dependency links and coverage references back\nto PRD and DESIGN (i.e., update the FEATURE list, ordering, dependency entries,\nand coverage links so the artifact provides an executable plan).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/identifiers.md-35-38 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`35-38`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add fenced code languages to satisfy MD040.**\n\nThese examples should declare a language for markdownlint compliance.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n - [ ] **ID**: `cpt-myapp-fr-must-authenticate`\n - [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-myapp-flow-login`\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n - `cpt-myapp-fr-must-authenticate`\n - [x] `p1` - `cpt-myapp-flow-login`\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n **ID**: `cpt-myapp-fr-must-authenticate`\n - [ ] **ID**: `cpt-myapp-actor-admin-user`\n - [x] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-myapp-core-comp-api-gateway`\n `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-myapp-core-auth-flow-login`\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n `cpt-myapp-fr-must-authenticate`\n [ ] `cpt-myapp-core-comp-api-gateway`\n [x] `p1` - `cpt-myapp-core-auth-flow-login`\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cpt-{hierarchy-prefix}-{kind}-{slug}\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 41-44, 79-84, 100-104, 126-128\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/identifiers.md around lines 35 - 38, Add a language\ntag to each fenced code block to satisfy MD040: update the opening backticks for\nthe blocks that contain the identifier lists (e.g. the blocks showing\n`cpt-myapp-fr-must-authenticate`, `cpt-myapp-flow-login`,\n`cpt-myapp-core-comp-api-gateway`, `cpt-myapp-core-auth-flow-login`, and the\ntemplate `cpt-{hierarchy-prefix}-{kind}-{slug}`) to include a language like\n\"text\" (e.g. change ``` to ```text) and do the same for the other blocks noted\nin the review (the other occurrences around the same identifier groups). Ensure\nevery fenced block opening has a language specifier and keep the existing\nclosing ``` unchanged.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/BROWNFIELD.md-42-48 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`42-48`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add fenced code languages to satisfy MD040.**\n\nThese example blocks should declare a language (e.g., `text`) for markdownlint compliance.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n 1. cypilot reverse FEATURE from src/auth/     → Creates FEATURE from code\n 2. cypilot reverse FEATURE from src/billing/  → Creates another FEATURE from code\n 3. cypilot decompose from features            → Creates DECOMPOSITION from FEATUREs\n 4. cypilot make DESIGN from DECOMPOSITION     → Creates DESIGN from structure\n 5. cypilot make PRD from DESIGN               → (optional) Creates PRD from DESIGN\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n 1. cypilot reverse DESIGN from codebase       → Extracts architecture from code\n 2. cypilot decompose                          → Creates feature breakdown\n 3. cypilot make FEATURE for {slug}            → Creates detailed features\n 4. cypilot implement {slug}                   → Implements with traceability markers\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n 1. cypilot reverse PRD from codebase          → Extracts requirements\n 2. cypilot make DESIGN from PRD               → Creates architecture\n 3. cypilot decompose                          → Creates feature breakdown\n 4. cypilot make FEATURE for {slug}            → Creates detailed features\n 5. cypilot implement {slug}                   → Implements with traceability markers\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Week 1: cypilot implement {slug}              → Code-only, with checklist\n Week 2: cypilot make FEATURE for {slug}       → Add features for complex work\n Week 3: cypilot decompose                     → Organize features\n Later:  cypilot make DESIGN                   → Document architecture\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot make DESIGN\n Context:\n - Source of truth: code\n - Code areas: src/api/, src/domain/\n - Existing docs: docs/architecture.md (may be outdated)\n - Constraints: do not break public API\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot reverse PRD from codebase\n Context:\n - Source of truth: code\n - Code entry points: src/routes/, src/controllers/\n - Existing docs: docs/api.md (partial)\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot reverse DESIGN from codebase\n Context:\n - Source of truth: code\n - Existing features: docs/openapi.yaml, docs/db-schema.md\n - Constraints: do not break public API\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot decompose from codebase\n Context:\n - Group features by modules: billing, auth, reporting\n - Code structure: src/modules/\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot make FEATURE for notifications\n Context:\n - Include scenarios: retries, rate limits, provider outage\n - Code boundaries: src/notifications/\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot implement notifications\n Context:\n - Where to implement: src/notifications/\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot update PRD\n cypilot validate PRD\n cypilot propagate PRD changes to DESIGN\n cypilot validate DESIGN\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot update DESIGN\n cypilot validate DESIGN\n cypilot propagate DESIGN changes to FEATURE {slug}\n cypilot validate FEATURE {slug}\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot update FEATURE {slug}\n cypilot validate FEATURE {slug}\n cypilot sync code with FEATURE {slug}\n cypilot validate code for {slug}\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot compare FEATURE {slug} to code\n cypilot sync FEATURE {slug} from code\n cypilot validate FEATURE {slug}\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: