.cypilot/requirements/prompt-engineering.md around lines 528 - 569, Several\nfenced code blocks in the \"### 8.3.1 Refinement Support\" through \"## 9.2\nImprovement Recommendations\" / \"Layer 9: Improvement Synthesis\" sections lack\nlanguage identifiers (triggering markdownlint MD040); update every\ntriple-backtick fenced block in those sections to include the appropriate\nlanguage tag (e.g., ```markdown, ```bash) so they render correctly and satisfy\nlinting, and ensure any suggested example blocks in the \"🔧 Suggested updates\"\ndetails also include explicit language tags.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/BROWNFIELD.md-42-48 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`42-48`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks (MD040).**  \nmarkdownlint flags multiple code fences without a language; add a language like `text` for prompt blocks.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Example fix pattern (apply to all flagged blocks)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n 1. cypilot reverse FEATURE from src/auth/     → Creates FEATURE from code\n 2. cypilot reverse FEATURE from src/billing/  → Creates another FEATURE from code\n 3. cypilot decompose from features            → Creates DECOMPOSITION from FEATUREs\n 4. cypilot make DESIGN from DECOMPOSITION     → Creates DESIGN from structure\n 5. cypilot make PRD from DESIGN               → (optional) Creates PRD from DESIGN\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 56-61, 70-76, 84-89, 118-125, 165-171, 220-226, 262-267, 319-324, 373-377, 437-441, 446-451, 455-460, 464-468\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/BROWNFIELD.md around lines 42 - 48, Multiple\nfenced code blocks in BROWNFIELD.md lack language identifiers (MD040); update\neach fenced block that contains prompt-like listings (for example the block\nstarting with \"1. cypilot reverse FEATURE from src/auth/\") and all other flagged\nblocks (lines referenced in the review) to use a language tag such as text by\nchanging ``` to ```text so markdownlint stops flagging them; ensure you apply\nthe same change to every similar fenced block (e.g., the blocks at the other\nflagged ranges) so all prompt/code fences include a language identifier.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/QUICKSTART.md-281-281 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`281-281`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Consider a stronger adjective than “Deep.”**  \nLanguageTool flagged this wording; a clearer alternative (e.g., “comprehensive” or “thorough”) can improve clarity.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Proposed wording tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `cypilot review PRD` | Deep review with 300+ criteria |\n+| `cypilot review PRD` | Comprehensive review with 300+ criteria |\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/QUICKSTART.md at line 281, Replace the adjective\n\"Deep\" in the table row containing the command text \"`cypilot review PRD` | Deep\nreview with 300+ criteria\" with a stronger, clearer word such as \"Comprehensive\"\nor \"Thorough\" (e.g., \"`cypilot review PRD` | Comprehensive review with 300+\ncriteria\") so the wording reads more precise; update that single table cell in\nQUICKSTART.md accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/BROWNFIELD.md-11-20 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-20`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify “Start Anywhere” vs required pipeline order.**  \nThe guide says brownfield has no required order, but the SDLC rules require the PRD → ADR + DESIGN → DECOMPOSITION → FEATURE → CODE order for deterministic validation/traceability. Consider adding a note that adoption can start anywhere, but validation/traceability still conforms to the canonical pipeline order.  \n\n\nBased on learnings: Follow the SDLC pipeline order: PRD → ADR + DESIGN → DECOMPOSITION → FEATURE → CODE with templates, checklists, and rules.md for deterministic validation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/BROWNFIELD.md around lines 11 - 20, Update the\n\"Start Anywhere\" section to explicitly state that while adoption and work can\nbegin from any artifact (PRD, DESIGN, FEATURE, or CODE) and Cypilot supports\ncode-only mode and uses the code-checklist for guidance, the project’s\nvalidation and traceability must still follow the canonical SDLC pipeline order\n(PRD → ADR + DESIGN → DECOMPOSITION → FEATURE → CODE); add a concise sentence\nreferencing the pipeline and that templates, checklists, and rules.md are used\nto ensure deterministic validation/traceability.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md-18-19 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-19`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix TOC link fragment for \"Execution Protocol Violations\".**\n\nThe link fragment `#-execution-protocol-violations` includes a leading dash that won't match the heading anchor. The heading \"## ⚠️ Execution Protocol Violations\" will generate an anchor without the emoji, typically `#execution-protocol-violations` or similar.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [Execution Protocol Violations](`#-execution-protocol-violations`)\n+- [Execution Protocol Violations](`#execution-protocol-violations`)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md around lines 18 - 19, The TOC\nentry uses a wrong fragment with a leading dash; update the link under the TOC\nthat currently reads `[- Execution Protocol\nViolations](`#-execution-protocol-violations`)` (or similar) to match the\ngenerated anchor for the heading `## ⚠️ Execution Protocol Violations`—e.g.,\nchange the fragment to `#execution-protocol-violations` (or the exact slug your\nmarkdown renderer produces) so the link resolves properly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md-937-940 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`937-940`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove duplicate note.**\n\nLines 937-940 contain two nearly identical notes about artifact paths and `artifacts_dir`. The second note (line 939-940) appears to be a copy-paste artifact with only a minor variation (`specs/` vs `features/`).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`specs/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n-\n-**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`features/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n+**Note**: Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to `project_root`. The `artifacts_dir` defines the default base directory for NEW artifacts — subdirectories for specific kinds (`features/`, `ADR/`) are defined by the kit.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md around lines 937 - 940, There is\na duplicated explanatory note about artifact paths and artifacts_dir (the two\nconsecutive lines mentioning \"Artifact paths are FULL paths relative to\n`project_root`\" and `artifacts_dir`) — remove the duplicate so only one clear\nnote remains and ensure it uses the correct subdirectory examples (e.g.,\n`features/` or `specs/`) as intended; locate the repeated text referencing\n`artifacts_dir` and `project_root` and delete the redundant copy, keeping the\nsingle canonical note with the desired subdirectory wording.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json-1015-1019 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1015-1019`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove duplicate example.**\n\nThe `status` identifier has a duplicate example value `\"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"` in the examples array.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"examples\": [\n           \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\",\n-          \"cpt-overwork-alert-status-overall\",\n-          \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"\n+          \"cpt-overwork-alert-status-overall\"\n         ],\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json around lines 1015 - 1019, The examples\narray for the status identifier contains a duplicate string\n\"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"; remove the repeated entry from the \"examples\"\narray (leave each example value only once) so the array under the status\nconstraint contains unique example values and update any ordering if needed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md-357-358 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`357-358`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove duplicate separator.**\n\nThere are two consecutive `---` separators at lines 357-358. This appears to be a copy-paste artifact.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ---\n-\n----\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/execution-protocol.md around lines 357 - 358, Remove\nthe duplicate markdown separator by deleting one of the consecutive '---' lines\nso there's only a single horizontal rule; locate the two consecutive '---'\nentries around the mentioned section and remove the redundant line to eliminate\nthe copy-paste artifact.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md-16-16 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`16-16`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Broken ToC link: \"Checkbox Management\" section does not exist.**\n\nThe Table of Contents references `#checkbox-management` at line 16, but there is no \"Checkbox Management\" heading in this document. Either remove this ToC entry or add the missing section.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix: remove orphan ToC entry</summary>\n\n```diff\n    - [Semantic Requirements](`#semantic-requirements`)\n    - [DESIGN Scope Guidelines](`#design-scope-guidelines`)\n    - [Upstream Traceability](`#upstream-traceability`)\n-   - [Checkbox Management](`#checkbox-management`)\n 2. [Tasks](`#tasks`)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md at line 16, The Table of\nContents contains an orphan entry \"[Checkbox Management](`#checkbox-management`)\"\nthat has no corresponding \"Checkbox Management\" heading; fix by either removing\nthat ToC line or adding a matching heading \"## Checkbox Management\" (and\nappropriate content) so the anchor resolves; update the ToC entry text if you\nchoose a different heading name to keep the link consistent with the heading.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/PRD/rules.md-170-179 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`170-179`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add languages to fenced code blocks.**\n\nMarkdownlint MD040 is triggered on multiple fences; add `text`/`markdown` to each block.  \nLine 170, Line 188, Line 195, Line 202, Line 210.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Example fix pattern</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n ...\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 188-214\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/PRD/rules.md around lines 170 - 179, Update the\nfenced code blocks in the \"PRD Validation Report\" section so each\ntriple-backtick fence includes a language tag (e.g., replace ``` with ```text or\n```markdown) to satisfy markdownlint MD040; specifically edit the code fences\nthat render the report block and any subsequent fenced examples (the multi-line\nblocks shown under the \"PRD Validation Report\" header and the example fix\npattern) so they all use a language identifier like text/markdown.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md-245-246 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`245-246`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove trailing spaces inside inline code spans.**\n\nMD038 flags code spans like `` `1 ` `` and similar examples. Remove trailing spaces or represent them explicitly (e.g., `1␠` or `1<space>`).  \nLine 245, Line 392.  \n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 389-393\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md around lines 245 - 246, The inline\ncode spans in the constraints doc contain trailing spaces (e.g., `1 `) which\ntrigger MD038; locate the occurrences referenced (the numbering regex example\n`^<num>(\\.<num>)*\\s+`, the sentence referencing `raw title` and `pattern`, and\nthe examples around lines 245, 389–393) and remove the trailing space inside the\nbackticks or replace it with an explicit visible marker such as `␠` or `<space>`\n(e.g., change `1 ` to `1␠` or `1<space>`) so the inline code spans no longer end\nwith a literal trailing space.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/rules.md-238-245 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`238-245`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add languages to fenced code blocks.**\n\nMarkdownlint MD040 is triggered on multiple fences; add `text`/`markdown` to each.  \nLine 238, Line 248, Line 258, Line 296, Line 368.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Example fix pattern</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n ...\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 248-255, 258-264, 296-303, 368-378\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/rules.md around lines 238 - 245, Update\nthe fenced code blocks in .cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/rules.md so each\ntriple-backtick fence includes a language label (e.g., text or markdown) to\nsatisfy MD040; specifically add a language token to the fence containing the \"⚠\nDECOMPOSITION not found\" block and the other fences referenced (blocks around\nlines noted in the review: the fences covering ranges 238-245, 248-255, 258-264,\n296-303, and 368-378); keep the content unchanged, only change the opening ```\nto ```text (or ```markdown) for each affected block so markdownlint stops\nflagging MD040.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/code-checklist.md-608-617 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`608-617`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add languages to fenced code blocks.**\n\nMarkdownlint reports missing languages for multiple fences. Add `markdown` (or `text`) to each block so lint passes.  \nLine 608, Line 631.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Example fix pattern</summary>\n\n`