301, 312), preserving content\nand fence placement so the blocks render correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/GREENFIELD.md-47-214 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`47-214`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language specifiers to context example blocks.**\n\nMultiple context example blocks lack language specifiers. Based on static analysis feedback. These should use `text` or `markdown` to improve readability.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix for context examples</summary>\n\n```diff\n **Example format:**\n-```\n+```text\n cypilot make DESIGN for taskman\n Context:\n - Repo: taskman - task management CLI tool\n```\n\nApply similar fixes to code blocks at lines 83, 136, 178, 214.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/GREENFIELD.md around lines 47 - 214, The fenced\nexample code blocks (e.g., the one starting with \"cypilot make DESIGN for\ntaskman\" and similar blocks containing \"cypilot make PRD for taskman\", \"cypilot\nmake DESIGN\", and the other context examples) are missing language specifiers;\nupdate each triple-backtick fence to include a language tag (use \"text\" or\n\"markdown\") so they render correctly (for example change ``` to ```text) for\nevery example block in GREENFIELD.md containing those command/context snippets.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/CLISPEC.md-187-213 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`187-213`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**The linking syntax is documented but secondary to the production traceability system.**\n\nThe `@CLI.command-name`, `@Workflow.name`, `@Feature.slug`, and `@DomainModel.TypeName` syntax are documented in CLISPEC.md and guides/ADAPTER.md with examples. However, the actual production traceability system used throughout the codebase is the `@cpt-*` marker system with formal specifications in requirements/traceability.md.\n\nThe `@cpt-*` format (`@cpt-{hierarchy-prefix}-{kind}-{slug}`) has comprehensive tooling support:\n- Deterministic validation via `requirements/traceability.md` (paired `@cpt-begin`/`@cpt-end` markers, phase numbers, instance IDs)\n- CLI commands: `cypilot validate-code`, `list-ids`, `where-defined`, `where-used`\n- Adopted across FEATURE→CODE implementation per AGENTS.md\n\nClarify whether the `@CLI`/`@Workflow`/`@Feature` syntax is intended for documentation-level cross-references only, or if tooling support for resolution is required. If the latter, consider aligning with the `@cpt-*` marker system which already has validation infrastructure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/CLISPEC.md around lines 187 - 213, Update the Linking Syntax\nsection to state explicitly whether `@CLI.command-name`, `@Workflow.name`,\n`@Feature.slug` and `@DomainModel.TypeName` are documentation-only cross-reference\nformats or must be supported by tooling; if tooling resolution is required,\nchange the spec to require using the existing `@cpt-`* marker system (the\n`@cpt-`{hierarchy-prefix}-{kind}-{slug} convention with paired\n`@cpt-begin/`@cpt-end, phase numbers and instance IDs) and reference the\ntraceability validation and CLI tooling that support it so implementers use the\ndeterministic `@cpt-`* markers instead of the ad-hoc `@CLI/`@Workflow/@Feature\nformats.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md-1-13 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-13`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify placeholder references and actual paths in the prompt.**\n\nThe \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" section exists in the checklist and aligns well with the review guidance. However, the adr-review.md prompt uses generic placeholders (`{existing_artifacts}`, `{template}`, `{checklist}`) while the actual checklist references concrete paths (`docs/adrs/`, `docs/spec-templates/ADR.md`). Either document the placeholder-to-path mapping in the prompt or replace placeholders with the actual paths from the checklist to avoid ambiguity during review execution.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md around lines 1 - 13, The prompt uses\ngeneric placeholders {existing_artifacts}, {template}, and {checklist} which are\nambiguous; update the prompt text in .cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md to either\n(a) replace these placeholders with the concrete paths used by the checklist\n(docs/adrs/, docs/spec-templates/ADR.md, and the actual checklist path/name) or\n(b) add a short explicit mapping line that declares \"{existing_artifacts} =>\ndocs/adrs/, {template} => docs/spec-templates/ADR.md, {checklist} =>\n<checklist-path>\" so reviewers receive unambiguous references; edit the prompt\nstring containing those placeholders to include the mapping or replacements and\nensure the \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" reference remains unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md-536-605 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`536-605`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add comprehensive unit tests for the system slug detection algorithm.**\n\nThe algorithm implementation in `artifacts_meta.py` is complete and handles documented edge cases correctly, but the test file `tests/test_artifacts_meta.py` is empty. Add unit tests covering:\n\n- System slug with kind token as substring (e.g., `my-db-service` with kind `db`)\n- Empty parent prefix handling\n- System with no definition IDs (folder-based slug preserved)\n- Conflicting slugs from different IDs (error case)\n- Ambiguous ID detection (all IDs contain multiple kind tokens)\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/artifacts-registry.md around lines 536 - 605, Add\ncomprehensive unit tests in tests/test_artifacts_meta.py that exercise the\nslug-detection routine implemented in artifacts_meta.py (call the public\nfunction that resolves an autodetected child system slug — e.g., the module's\nslug-detection function used by the validator). Create tests for: (1) a system\nwhose folder slug contains a kind token substring (e.g., system \"my-db-service\"\nwith kind tokens including \"db\") and verify the function picks the full\n\"my-db-service\" slug (unambiguous IDs present); (2) empty parent prefix behavior\n(IDs without a parent prefix) to ensure detection works when parent prefix = \"\";\n(3) no definition IDs — verify the folder-based slug is preserved; (4)\nconflicting slugs produced by different unambiguous IDs — assert the function\nraises an error containing \"Inconsistent system slugs in IDs\"; and (5) all IDs\nambiguous (every ID yields multiple candidates) — assert the function raises an\nerror containing \"Cannot determine system slug from IDs\". Use isolated inputs\n(lists of definition IDs, parent prefix, and known kind token set) and explicit\nassertions for returned slug or expected exception messages.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/identifiers.md-71-71 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`71-71`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify version discrepancy.**\n\nThe frontmatter specifies `version: 1.3`, but line 71 states \"**Supported Version**: `1.0`\". It's unclear what \"Supported Version\" refers to—perhaps an ID format version distinct from the document version?\n\nConsider clarifying what \"Supported Version: 1.0\" represents (e.g., \"ID Format Version\" or \"Scanner Version\").\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/identifiers.md at line 71, The \"Supported Version:\n`1.0`\" line conflicts with the frontmatter `version: 1.3`; update the markdown\nto clarify what 1.0 refers to (for example change the heading text from\n\"Supported Version\" to \"ID Format Version\" or \"Scanner Supported Version\") and\nadd a short parenthetical or sentence stating that the document's frontmatter\n`version: 1.3` is the document schema version while `1.0` denotes the ID\nformat/scanner version (refer to the lines showing \"Supported Version: `1.0`\"\nand the frontmatter `version: 1.3` to locate where to change the label and add\nthe clarifying note).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json-1015-1019 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1015-1019`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Duplicate example in status identifier.**\n\nThe `examples` array contains a duplicate entry `\"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Fix duplicate example</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"examples\": [\n           \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\",\n           \"cpt-overwork-alert-status-overall\",\n-          \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"\n+          \"cpt-todo-app-status-overall\"\n         ],\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/constraints.json around lines 1015 - 1019, The examples\narray for the status identifier contains a duplicated value\n\"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\"; remove the duplicate from the \"examples\" array so\neach entry is unique (keep one \"cpt-cypilot-status-overall\" and preserve the\nother entries like \"cpt-overwork-alert-status-overall\"), updating the JSON in\nthe constraints.json snippet that defines \"examples\".\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md-167-192 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`167-192`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Example heading constraint includes undocumented `identifiers` field.**\n\nThe example at lines 167-192 shows heading constraints with an `identifiers` field (e.g., `\"identifiers\": [\"fr\"]`), but this field is not documented in the Heading Constraint Entry schema at lines 72-91. The note at lines 92-94 mentions that scoping is done via `identifiers[<kind>].headings`, not via a heading's `identifiers` field.\n\nEither remove the `identifiers` field from the example or document it in the schema section.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Option 1: Remove undocumented field from example</summary>\n\n```diff\n       {\n         \"level\": 2,\n         \"pattern\": \"Functional Requirements\",\n         \"required\": true,\n         \"multiple\": \"prohibited\",\n-        \"numbered\": \"allow\",\n-        \"identifiers\": [\"fr\"]\n+        \"numbered\": \"allow\"\n       },\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/kit-constraints.md around lines 167 - 192, The example\nunder \"headings\" includes an undocumented \"identifiers\" field (e.g.,\n\"identifiers\": [\"fr\"]) that conflicts with the Heading Constraint Entry schema;\nupdate the example or the schema: either remove all \"identifiers\" occurrences\nfrom the example entries in the \"headings\" array, or add documentation to the\nHeading Constraint Entry schema (the schema described around \"Heading Constraint\nEntry\") to declare the \"identifiers\" property, its type (array of strings), and\nits intended use so it matches the note about scoping via\nidentifiers[<kind>].headings; modify whichever section you choose (the\n\"headings\" example or the Heading Constraint Entry schema) so both the example\nand the schema are consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/requirements/adapter-triggers.md-92-95 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`92-95`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update DESIGN.md section references to use correct heading paths.**\n\nThe trigger checks reference non-existent sections like \"DESIGN.md Section C.2 (Domain Model)\" and \"Section C.3 (API Contracts)\". The actual DESIGN template structure uses numeric headings (Section 3: Technical Architecture with subsections 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, etc.). References should instead use:\n- \"Technical Architecture > Domain Model\" (or Section 3.1)\n- \"Technical Architecture > API Contracts\" (or Section 3.3)\n\nAlso note that references to \"Section B (Actor Flows)\", \"Section C (Algorithms)\", and \"Section E (Technical Details)\" appear to conflate FEATURE template sections with DESIGN. Clarify whether these checks apply to FEATURE documents instead, or update to match the actual DESIGN structure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/requirements/adapter-triggers.md around lines 92 - 95, Update the\nincorrect DESIGN.md section references in the trigger definitions: replace\noccurrences of \"DESIGN.md Section C.2 (Domain Model)\" and \"Section C.3 (API\nContracts)\" with \"Technical Architecture > Domain Model (Section 3.1)\" and\n\"Technical Architecture > API Contracts (Section 3.3)\" respectively, and update\nthe trigger messages that reference \"Section B (Actor Flows)\", \"Section C\n(Algorithms)\", and \"Section E (Technical Details)\" to either target the FEATURE\ntemplate (if the checks belong to FEATURE) or map them to the correct DESIGN\nheadings (e.g., map Actor Flows/Algorithms/Technical Details to their equivalent\nDESIGN sections), ensuring the trigger strings and any explanatory text use the\nexact new heading paths (\"Technical Architecture > ...\") so the checks point to\nexisting sections.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/examples/example.md-227-280 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`227-280`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix section numbering (3.6/3.7 duplicated).**\n\nAfter 3.7 “Database schemas & tables”, the optional sections restart at 3.6/3.7. Renumbering keeps references consistent.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔢 Suggested renumbering</summary>\n\n```diff\n-### 3.6: Topology (optional)\n+### 3.8: Topology (optional)\n...\n-### 3.7: Tech stack (optional)\n+### 3.9: Tech stack (optional)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/examples/example.md around lines 227 -\n280, The document has duplicated section numbers: \"### 3.7 Database schemas &\ntables\" is followed by \"### 3.6: Topology (optional)\" and \"### 3.7: Tech stack\n(optional)\"; rename those headings to continue the sequence (e.g., change \"3.6:\nTopology (optional)\" -> \"3.8: Topology (optional)\" and \"3.7: Tech stack\n(optional)\" -> \"3.9: Tech stack (optional)\") and update any in-document\nreferences or IDs that rely on those numbers (e.g., headings\n\"cpt-taskflow-topology-local\" and the Tech stack status line) so numbering and\nreferences stay consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/examples/example.md-75-79 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`75-79`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix broken spec link to point to correct FEATURE artifact.**\n\nThe link `../specs/task-crud/DESIGN.md` is broken—no `specs/task-crud/` directory exists. The task-crud specification is located at `kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/examples/task-crud.md`. Update the link to `../../FEATURE/examples/task-crud.md`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Link correction</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [`cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`](../specs/task-crud/DESIGN.md) — Spec implementing task persistence\n+- [`cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`](../../FEATURE/examples/task-crud.md) — Spec implementing task persistence\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/examples/example.md around lines 75 - 79,\nReplace the broken markdown link \"`../specs/task-crud/DESIGN.md`\" in the More\nInformation section with the correct FEATURE artifact path\n\"`../../FEATURE/examples/task-crud.md`\" so the `cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud`\nreference points to the actual task-crud spec; update the link target only\n(leave link text `cpt-taskflow-feature-task-crud` unchanged).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md-134-151 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`134-151`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language tags to fenced code blocks.**\n\nMarkdownlint flags code fences without language identifiers (MD040). Tag them as `text` or `markdown` for consistency.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Example fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- ```\n+ ```text\n  ⚠ Parent PRD not found or incomplete\n  → Option 1: Run /cypilot-generate PRD first (recommended)\n  ...\n- ```\n+ ```\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 176-183, 232-241\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md around lines 134 - 151, Several\nfenced code blocks in the DESIGN rules lack language tags (triggering MD040);\nlocate the blocks beginning with the text \"⚠ Parent PRD not found or incomplete\"\nand \"⚠ PRD may be outdated (last modified: {date})\" (and the other similar\nblocks referenced in the comment) and add a language identifier to each opening\ntriple-backtick (e.g., ```text or ```markdown) so markdownlint no longer flags\nthem; ensure every fenced block in the file (including the examples around those\npassages) is updated consistently.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md-10-17 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-17`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Table of Contents links to a non-existent section.**\n\n`Checkbox Management` appears in the ToC but has no matching heading. Either add the section or remove the entry to satisfy MD051.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Proposed fix (remove ToC entry)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-   - [Checkbox Management](`#checkbox-management`)\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 98-103\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md around lines 10 - 17, The Table\nof Contents includes a dead link \"Checkbox Management\" causing MD051; remove the\nToC entry \"- [Checkbox Management](`#checkbox-management`)\" (and any duplicate ToC\nreferences) or alternatively add a matching heading \"## Checkbox Management\"\nwith content; for this PR follow the proposed fix and delete the ToC line so the\nToC and headings are consistent and MD051 is resolved.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/checklist.md-508-514 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`508-514`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Hyphenate compound adjective in checklist item.**\n\n“Rate limiting handling” should be hyphenated when used as a compound modifier.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- - [ ] Rate limiting handling documented\n+ - [ ] Rate-limiting handling documented\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/FEATURE/checklist.md around lin