vs FEATURE if both terms must coexist\nso readers know which term is authoritative.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/MONOLITH.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`30-44`: **Add language specifiers to hierarchy example code blocks.**\n\nThe hierarchy diagrams at lines 30-44 and 46-60 should have language specifiers for consistency.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Add language specifier</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n System: E-Commerce Platform\n ├── Subsystem: Storefront\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/guides/MONOLITH.md around lines 30 - 44, Add a language\nspecifier to the ASCII hierarchy code blocks so Markdown renders them\nconsistently: update the opening triple-backtick fence for the code block that\nstarts with \"System: E-Commerce Platform\" (the hierarchy diagram in the snippet\ncontaining \"Subsystem: Storefront\" / \"Component: Catalog\" etc.) and the second\nsimilar diagram later in the file to use a language tag (e.g., ```text) while\nkeeping the existing closing triple-backtick fences unchanged.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/checklist.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`593-599`: **Hyphenate “rate-limiting” in INT-DESIGN-002.**\n\nSmall readability tweak for the compound adjective.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested edit</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [ ] Rate limiting handling documented\n+- [ ] Rate-limiting handling documented\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.cypilot/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/checklist.md around lines 593 - 599,\nUpdate the checklist entry for INT-DESIGN-002 to hyphenate the compound\nadjective: change the item text \"Rate limiting handl