summary>\n\n```\nIn `@skills/scripts/pr.py` around lines 581 - 585, The summary table label is\ninaccurate: the variable n_code_unresolved counts code_threads (unreplied\nthreads) but the header displays \"unresolved\". Update the report to either (A)\nchange the label in the f-string to \"unreplied\" to match n_code_unresolved, or\n(B) recompute the value using len(unresolved_threads) and keep the \"unresolved\"\nlabel; locate the f-string constructing the table (the lines using\nn_code_unresolved / n_code_resolved) and adjust the label or the variable\naccordingly (refer to n_code_unresolved, code_threads, and unresolved_threads).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:17:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:17:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794508410","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794508410"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794508410"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794508410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":625,"original_start_line":581,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":629,"original_line":585,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":585,"position":629,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794665951","pull_request_review_id":3786339284,"id":2794665951,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mkzff","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Architecture Decision Record Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR changes against ADR best practices.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Ensure this problem is module/system scoped, not generic and repeatable\n+- Compliance with /docs/spec-templates/ADR.md template\n+- Ensure this problem is not already solved by other existing ADRs in docs/adrs/\n+- Alternatives are genuinely different approaches (not straw men)\n+- Decision rationale is concrete and traceable to project constraints\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/ADR.md` as the structured review guide.\n+Pay attention to the \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" section at the end of the checklist.","path":"prompts/pr/adr-review.md","commit_id":"a1ce6b83e73c88a16432f8e269c4ee77cb0e3858","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed. review again","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:52:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:52:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794665951","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794665951"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794665951"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794665951/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":13,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146917,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794666414","pull_request_review_id":3786339789,"id":2794666414,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mkzmu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Code Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR code changes.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Correctness and edge cases\n+- Code style and idiomatic patterns\n+- Performance implications\n+- Test coverage\n+- Security vulnerabilities\n+- Cargo, clippy, dylint, and rustfmt conformance\n+- New code has unit tests and end to end tests in testing/ folder\n+- Mistakes and potential misbehaviors\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/CODE.md` as the structured review guide when available.\n+Refer to `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` for Rust-specific conventions.\n+Refer to `guidelines/SECURITY.md` for security requirements.\n+Refer to `clippy.toml` and `Cargo.toml` workspace lints for lint rules.","path":"prompts/pr/code-review.md","commit_id":"df59d93a7ecdf2f706e69152f32000604878d4da","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","