1,13 @@\n+# Architecture Decision Record Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR changes against ADR best practices.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Ensure this problem is module/system scoped, not generic and repeatable\n+- Compliance with /docs/spec-templates/ADR.md template\n+- Ensure this problem is not already solved by other existing ADRs in docs/adrs/\n+- Alternatives are genuinely different approaches (not straw men)\n+- Decision rationale is concrete and traceable to project constraints\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/ADR.md` as the structured review guide.\n+Pay attention to the \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" section at the end of the checklist.","path":"prompts/pr/adr-review.md","commit_id":"a1ce6b83e73c88a16432f8e269c4ee77cb0e3858","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### **Ask**❓\nfixed. review again\n\n### **Answer:**\nRe-reviewed `prompts/pr/adr-review.md` against the earlier CodeRabbit finding.\n\n✅ **The specific “missing docs paths” issue appears fixed** in the PR diff you shared:\n- The prompt no longer hard-codes repo-specific paths like `/docs/spec-templates/ADR.md`, `docs/adrs/`, or `docs/checklists/ADR.md`.\n- Instead it correctly uses placeholders:\n  - `{template}` (for the ADR template path)\n  - `{existing_artifacts}` (for the ADR inventory/search scope)\n  - `{checklist}` (for the checklist path/content)\n- This matches the design of the PR review system described elsewhere in the PR (prompts resolved via `{cypilot_adapter_path}/pr-review.json → prompts[]`).\n\n⚠️ **Follow-ups to ensure it won’t regress at runtime**\n1. **Confirm `pr-review.json` provides these placeholders for the ADR prompt**  \n   The workflow says placeholders are resolved from the matched prompt entry. Make sure the ADR entry includes keys for:\n   - `template`\n   - `existing_artifacts`\n   - `checklist`\n   Otherwise the prompt will still be “broken”, just later (placeholder not substituted / left literal).\n\n2. **Consistency between prompt copy and workflow copy**  \n   The ADR prompt ends with “Pay attention to the ‘PR Review Focus (ADR)’ section…”. Ensure the checklist referenced by `{checklist}` actually contains that section; if not, either update the checklist or soften the wording.\n\n3. **Optional improvement: make the ADR prompt explicitly mention placeholders**  \n   Consider slightly rewording bullets so it’s clear they are variables (e.g., “Ensure compliance with the ADR template at `{template}`” and “Check against existing ADRs in `{existing_artifacts}`”). The current text is fine, but that wording reduces confusion when reading raw prompt files.\n\nNet: the earlier critical complaint about referencing non-existent repo paths is addressed by parameterizing the references.\n\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/