","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794669976","pull_request_review_id":3786343545,"id":2794669976,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk0eY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Code Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR code changes.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Correctness and edge cases\n+- Code style and idiomatic patterns\n+- Performance implications\n+- Test coverage\n+- Security vulnerabilities\n+- Cargo, clippy, dylint, and rustfmt conformance\n+- New code has unit tests and end to end tests in testing/ folder\n+- Mistakes and potential misbehaviors\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/CODE.md` as the structured review guide when available.\n+Refer to `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` for Rust-specific conventions.\n+Refer to `guidelines/SECURITY.md` for security requirements.\n+Refer to `clippy.toml` and `Cargo.toml` workspace lints for lint rules.","path":"prompts/pr/code-review.md","commit_id":"df59d93a7ecdf2f706e69152f32000604878d4da","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### **Ask**❓\nfixed. review again\n\n### **Answer:**\nRe-reviewed the PR additions (primarily `skills/scripts/pr.py`, new prompts/templates, and workflow routing in `SKILL.md`). Overall, the workflow design is coherent and the script provides a solid “fetch → status report → reorder” loop. That said, there are still a few correctness and robustness issues worth addressing before relying on it heavily.\n\n## ✅ What looks good\n- **Root detection**: `_find_project_root()` via `git rev-parse` with a fallback is sensible for running inside/outside a git worktree.\n- **Config resolution**: Reading `.cypilot/.cypilot-config.json` for `cypilotAdapterPath`, then loading `{adapter}/pr-review.json` is a good pattern.\n- **Status report structure**: Generated `status.md` matches the added template closely, and the output is actionable (reviewers, action items, unreplied sections).\n- **Review thread capture**: Using GraphQL `reviewThreads` to get `isResolved` is the right approach; REST review comments provide `diff_hunk` for context.\n- **Reorder feature**: Sorting “unreplied” blocks by severity is useful and implemented simply.\n\n## ⚠️ Issues / improvements to consider\n\n### 1) `status ALL` likely crashes if `.prs/` doesn’t exist\nIn `main()` for `status` with `ALL`, you do `os.listdir(PRS_DIR)` without ensuring `PRS_DIR` exists. On a fresh repo, this raises `FileNotFoundError`.\n- Fix: `os.makedirs(PRS_DIR, exist_ok=True)` before listing (same for other commands that assume it exists).\n\n### 2) `.prs/config.yaml` parsing is very brittle\n`_load_exclude_list()` is a minimal line-based parser and will fail on common YAML patterns:\n- inline lists (`exclude_prs: [1, 2]`)\n- indentation variations\n- comments on same line\n- non-string numeric PRs (it currently coerces to string, which is fine, but YAML parsing would handle it more reliably)\nIf you want to keep “no dependencies”, consider documenting the supported format strictly. Otherwise, use `yaml.safe_load` (PyYAML) when available, with a graceful fallback.\n\n### 3) “Replied PR comments” heuristic is weak / can misclassify\n`_detect_pr_replies()` only marks a comment as replied-to if the PR author later posts a comment quoting some of the original text with `>` and matching substring.\n- Many real replies don’t quote (especially on GitHub).\n- It also scans PR-level `meta.json` `comments`, not review threads; that’s fine for PR comments, but the heuristic will likely undercount replies.\nSuggestions:\n- Consider treating a PR author comment that includes an `@reviewer` mention (of the original author) within some time window as a reply signal.\n- Or mark “replied” when the PR author posts *any* later comment in the same PR discussion, and link them by `inReplyToId` if available (GraphQL for issue comments may help).\n\n### 4) Reviewers table may be missing “latest review wins” nuance\n`_reviewer_table()` overwrites reviewer state with the last iterated entry from `meta[\"reviews\"]`, but ordering isn’t guaranteed unless `gh` returns in chronological order.\n- If reviews are unsorted, “last state wins” becomes nondeterministic.\n- Fix: sort reviews by `submittedAt` (if available via `--json`) or by `createdAt` if present, then apply “last wins”.\n\n### 5) `statusCheckRollup` shape assumptions\n`_ci_summary()` assumes `meta[\"statusCheckRollup\"]` is iterable with `conclusion/state/status`. In GH’s GraphQL types, `statusCheckRollup` can be `null`, or include different node types.\n- You already guard `if not checks: return \"—\"`, good.\n- But if it’s not a list (e.g., dict with `contexts`), it may misbehave.\nSuggestion: add a type check:\n- if `isinstance(checks, dict)` and `contexts` in it, use that list\n- else if list, proceed\n- else return \"—\"\n\n### 6) `reorder()` section parsing is regex-fragile\nThe regex-based section extraction will break if headings change slightly, or if content contains similar heading text.\n- It also splits blocks by `\\n---\\n`, but the generator writes `---` surrounded by blank lines in some places. You tried to normalize with `re.split(r\"\\n---\\n\", ...)`, but some blocks are `\\n---\\n\\n`.\nSuggestion:\n- Split on `\\n---\\n` *and* `\\n---\\n\\n` via a regex like `r\"\\n---\\n(?:\\n)?\"`\n- Or parse as markdown headings + horizontal rules more explicitly.\n\n### 7) “Suspicious” counts are hardcoded to 0 in header\nThe status header prints:\n- `0 suspicious` for code comments and PR comments always\nbut the workflow later instructs the LLM to update suspicious counts.\n- If the intent is “LLM updates after audit”, consider leaving placeholders like `{N suspicious}` or compute it from the file during reorder (or provide a helper command to recompute counts).\n\n## Minor polish\n- `fetch()` says it “overwrites” but it currently writes files anew; that’s fine, but consider explicitly truncating/overwriting (current `open(...,\"w\")` already does).\n- `BOTS` list is helpful; consider normalizing logins to lowercase in `_is_bot()` just in case.\n- In `_format_conversation()`, quoting bodies with `>` is readable, but it can get noisy; consider trimming very long comments.\n\n## Net assessment\nThe PR is in good shape conceptually and will work in many repos, but I’d recommend fixing the `.prs/` existence crash for `status ALL` and tightening the reply/CI/review ordering assumptions to reduce false “unreplied” and flaky reviewer status results.\n\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794669976","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794669976"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794669976"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794669976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":15,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146927,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":18,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670152","pull_request_review_id":3786343687,"id":2794670152,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk0hI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Code Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR code changes.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Correctness and edge cases\n+- Code style and idiomatic patterns\n+- Performance implications\n+- Test coverage\n+- Security vulnerabilities\n+- Cargo, clippy, dylint, and rustfmt conformance\n+- New code has unit tests and end to end tests in testing/ folder\n+- Mistakes and potential misbehaviors\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/CODE.md` as the structured review guide when available.\n+Refer to `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` for Rust-specific conventions.\n+Refer to `guidelines/SECURITY.md` for security requirements.\n+Refer to `clippy.toml` and `Cargo.toml` workspace lints for lint rules.","path":"prompts/pr/code-review.md","commit_id":"df59d93a7ecdf2f706e69152f32000604878d4da","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check the current content of the code review prompt file\necho \"=== Current content of prompts/pr/code-review.md ===\"\ncat prompts/pr/code-review.md\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Checking for referenced files ===\"\necho \"Searching for CODE.md:\"\nfind . -name \"CODE.md\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\nSearching for RUST.md:\"\nfind . -name \"RUST.md\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\nSearching for SECURITY.md:\"\nfind . -name \"SECURITY.md\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\nSearching for clippy.toml:\"\nfind . -name \"clippy.toml\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\nSearching for Cargo.toml:\"\nfind . -name \"Cargo.toml\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Checking commit ff04555 ===\"\ngit show ff04555:prompts/pr/code-review.md 2>/dev/null || echo \"Could not find commit or file in that commit\"\n```\n\nLength of output: 1182\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer` Great fix! ✅ \n\nThe updated prompt now uses generic placeholders (`{checklist}`, `{coding_guidelines}`, `{security_guidelines}`) instead of hardcoded file paths. This approach is much better because:\n\n1. **No broken references** - eliminates the issue of pointing to non-existent files\n2. **More flexible** - the placeholders can be dynamically populated by your workflow scripts\n3. **Language-agnostic** - no longer tied to Rust-specific configs\n\nI also noticed you improved the first focus point to include \"error handling\" alongside correctness and edge cases. Nice enhancement!\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794670152","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670152"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794670152"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":15,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146927,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":18,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670317","pull_request_review_id":3786343853,"id":2794670317,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk0jt","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Architecture Decision Record Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR changes against ADR best practices.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Ensure this problem is module/system scoped, not generic and repeatable\n+- Compliance with /docs/spec-templates/ADR.md template\n+- Ensure this problem is not already solved by other existing ADRs in docs/adrs/\n+- Alternatives are genuinely different approaches (not straw men)\n+- Decision rationale is concrete and traceable to project constraints\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/ADR.md` as the structured review guide.\n+Pay attention to the \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" section at the end of the checklist.","path":"prompts/pr/adr-review.md","commit_id":"a1ce6b83e73c88a16432f8e269c4ee77cb0e3858","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify the ADR documentation files now exist\n\necho \"=== Checking for ADR template ===\"\nif [ -f \"docs/spec-templates/ADR.md\" ]; then\n    echo \"✓ docs/spec-templates/ADR.md exists\"\n    echo \"File size: $(wc -l < docs/spec-templates/ADR.md) lines\"\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"First 20 lines:\"\n    head -20 docs/spec-templates/ADR.md\nelse\n    echo \"✗ docs/spec-templates/ADR.md does NOT exist\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking for ADRs directory ===\"\nif [ -d \"docs/adrs\" ]; then\n    echo \"✓ docs/adrs/ directory exists\"\n    echo \"Contents:\"\n    ls -la docs/adrs/\nelse\n    echo \"✗ docs/adrs/ directory does NOT exist\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking for ADR checklist ===\"\nif [ -f \"docs/checklists/ADR.md\" ]; then\n    echo \"✓ docs/checklists/ADR.md exists\"\n    echo \"File size: $(wc -l < docs/checklists/ADR.md) lines\"\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"Checking for 'PR Review Focus (ADR)' section...\"\n    grep -n \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" docs/checklists/ADR.md || echo \"Section not found\"\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"First 30 lines:\"\n    head -30 docs/checklists/ADR.md\nelse\n    echo \"✗ docs/checklists/ADR.md does NOT exist\"\nfi\n```\n\nLength of output: 228\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer`, I've checked the repository and unfortunately the ADR documentation files are still missing. The verification shows:\n\n❌ **Still not found:**\n- `docs/spec-templates/ADR.md`\n- `docs/adrs/` directory\n- `docs/checklists/ADR.md`\n\n**To resolve this issue, you need to:**\n\n1. Create the ADR template at `docs/spec-templates/ADR.md` with the structure/template for writing ADRs\n2. Create the `docs/adrs/` directory (can be empty or with example ADRs)\n3. Create the ADR checklist at `docs/checklists/ADR.md` with a \"PR Review Focus (ADR)\" section at the end\n\nPlease ensure these files are committed and pushed to the `cypilot-pr-workflow` branch. If you've created them locally, they may not be pushed yet, or they might be in a different branch.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794670317","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670317"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794670317"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":13,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146917,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794670628","pull_request_review_id":3786344169,"id":2794670628,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk0ok","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Code Review Prompt\n+\n+Review the following PR code changes.\n+\n+Focus on:\n+- Correctness and edge cases\n+- Code style and idiomatic patterns\n+- Performance implications\n+- Test coverage\n+- Security vulnerabilities\n+- Cargo, clippy, dylint, and rustfmt conformance\n+- New code has unit tests and end to end tests in testing/ folder\n+- Mistakes and potential misbehaviors\n+\n+Use `docs/checklists/CODE.md` as the structured review guide when available.\n+Refer to `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` for Rust-specific conventions.\n+Refer to `guidelines/SECURITY.md` for security requirements.\n+Refer to `clippy.toml` and `Cargo.toml` workspace lints for lint rules.","path":"prompts/pr/code-review.md","commit_id":"df59d93a7ecdf2f706e69152f32000604878d4da","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers