ments/2794685103"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794685103"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794685103/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":162,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146955,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794689348","pull_request_review_id":3786365315,"id":2794689348,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk5NE","diff_hunk":"@@ -159,6 +159,8 @@ ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py init --yes`\n \n ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py agents --agent <name>` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot agents <name>`\n \n+ALWAYS run `python3 {project_root}/.cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py list` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot list PRs` or any PR listing intent — NEVER use `gh pr list`","path":"skills/cypilot/SKILL.md","commit_id":"ff045550d1b7901cfe9e839b3471ba3d72ee35f9","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### **Ask**❓\nfixed, please review again\n\n### **Answer:**\nReviewed the updated additions (notably `skills/scripts/pr.py`, the PR prompts/templates, and the SKILL/workflow routing). Overall this is a solid, cohesive PR: the script fetches the right artifacts, the workflows enforce “refetch each time”, and the templates are consistent with the generated outputs.\n\nThat said, there are still a few correctness/robustness issues and some “paper cut” improvements I’d recommend before merging.\n\n## ✅ What looks good now\n- **Project-root resolution**: `_find_project_root()` using `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` with a fallback is practical.\n- **Config resolution**: `_load_pr_config()` correctly reads `.cypilot/.cypilot-config.json` and falls back to `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json`.\n- **Fetching strategy**: `status()` calling `fetch()` ensures freshness (matches the workflow contract).\n- **Good data coverage**: saving `meta.json`, `diff.patch`, REST review comments (for `diff_hunk`), plus GraphQL threads (for `isResolved`) is a good combination.\n- **Exclude list support**: `.prs/config.yaml` parsing is simple but effective for the intended use.\n- **Reorder**: severity-based reorder is a nice utility for the status workflow.\n\n## ⚠️ Remaining issues / risks\n\n### 1) `status ALL` can crash if `.prs/` doesn’t exist\nIn `main()` → `elif cmd == \"status\":` and `arg.upper() == \"ALL\"`:\n- It does `os.listdir(PRS_DIR)` without ensuring `PRS_DIR` exists.\n- In a fresh repo run, `.prs/` may not exist yet, causing `FileNotFoundError`.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- Create the directory (or gracefully handle missing):\n  - `os.makedirs(PRS_DIR, exist_ok=True)` before `listdir`\n  - or if missing, print guidance: “No fetched PRs yet; run `pr.py fetch ALL` or `pr.py status <PR>`”.\n\n### 2) `status ALL` only processes already-fetched PR folders (not actually “ALL open PRs”)\nCurrent behavior for `status ALL`:\n- It iterates directories under `.prs/` and calls `status(d)` only if `.prs/{d}/meta.json` exists.\n- This does **not** necessarily match “ALL open PRs” unless the user fetched all open PRs previously.\n\nYour workflow docs say: `pr.py status ALL` “auto-fetches the latest PR data … for each PR”. That reads like “all open PRs”, not “all local folders”.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- For `status ALL`, consider calling `_list_open_prs()` and iterating PR numbers (respecting exclude list), similar to `fetch ALL`. This would align with the workflow description and avoid surprises.\n\n### 3) Potential GraphQL pagination truncation for review threads\n`_REVIEW_THREADS_QUERY` requests `reviewThreads(first:100)` with no pagination. Large PRs can exceed 100 threads, and the report would silently omit the remainder.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- Either:\n  - Implement pagination (`pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }`), loop until done, or\n  - Explicitly document the limit and warn in the report header when `hasNextPage == true`.\n\n### 4) PR-comment “replied” heuristic is likely to misclassify\n`_detect_pr_replies()` marks a comment as “replied” only if a later author comment **quotes** part of the original (`>` lines).\n- In practice, many replies don’t quote; they just respond conversationally.\n- That means many “replied” threads will still show as “unreplied” action items.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- Consider expanding heuristics:\n  - If PR author posts a later PR-level comment within N minutes/hours and mentions the commenter `@login`, treat as reply.\n  - Or if GitHub provides `inReplyToId` / thread linkage (not sure for PR conversation comments), prefer that.\n\n### 5) Inconsistent URL fields between REST review comments and GraphQL thread comment URLs\n`_load_diff_hunks()` builds a lookup by `html_url`.\nIn status generation, it later looks up hunks using `first.get(\"url\", \"\")` from GraphQL, which is a GitHub URL string but may not match `html_url` formatting from REST (or could be API URL vs HTML URL depending on source).\n\n**Impact**\n- Diff hunks may not appear even when available, because keys don’t match.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- Normalize on one canonical key:\n  - Prefer HTML URL everywhere if possible.\n  - Or store hunks by comment `id` (REST has `id`; GraphQL has `id`) and match by `id` instead of URL.\n\n### 6) “Suspicious Resolutions” counts are hardcoded to 0\nThe header table always prints `0 suspicious` for code comments and PR comments:\n```python\nf\"| **Code comments** | {unresolved} ... / 0 suspicious |\"\n```\nBut your `pr-status` workflow explicitly instructs the LLM to move suspicious entries and “update the suspicious counts in the header table accordingly.”\n\n**Suggestion**\n- Either:\n  - Make `pr.py reorder` (or a new command) recompute and update those counts from the markdown, or\n  - Have `status()` compute suspicious entries (if present) by parsing existing report (but status() rewrites from scratch right now), or\n  - Clarify in workflow that the LLM must update those counts manually and `reorder` won’t touch them.\n\n### 7) YAML parsing for excludes is intentionally simplistic but brittle\n`_load_exclude_list()` only supports:\n- exact line `exclude_prs:`\n- list items `- 123`\n- stops on “any other non-empty non-comment line”\n\nThis is probably fine, but it will break on:\n- indentation differences, inline comments, or quoted YAML arrays.\n\n**Suggestion**\n- If you want minimal deps, keep it; but consider tolerating indentation and inline comments (split on `#` before parsing).\n- If deps are acceptable, use `PyYAML` (but I understand you may want zero dependencies).\n\n## Minor polish suggestions\n- `_run(...)`: printing stderr and exiting only when `check=True` is OK, but a few calls manually check return codes; consider consistent usage (either always `check=True` or return-based).\n- `_quote()`: quoting long PR descriptions works; you might want to preserve blank lines more explicitly (currently it will include them as `> ` which is fine).\n- `BOTS`: good list; `login.endswith(\"[bot]\")` covers most anyway—list is fine as overrides.\n\n## Summary recommendation\n- **Approve directionally**, but I’d address at least:\n  1) `PRS_DIR` existence crash,\n  2) `status ALL` semantics mismatch,\n  3) URL/id mismatch for diff hunks (so code context reliably shows),\n  4) GraphQL thread pagination (or at least warn on truncation).\n\nIf you want, I can propose concrete patch snippets for (1), (2), and (5) that are small and low-risk.\n\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:58:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:58:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794689348","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794689348"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pull/64#discussion_r2794689348"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/64"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794689348/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":162,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794146955,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-constructor/pulls/comments/2794689913","pull_request_review_id":3786366012,"id":2794689913,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQ7VXwc6mk5V5","diff_hunk":"@@ -159,6 +159,8 @@ ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py init --yes`\n \n ALWAYS run `python3 {cypilot_path}/skills/cypilot/scripts/cypilot.py agents --agent <name>` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot agents <name>`\n \n+ALWAYS run `python3 {project_root}/.cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py list` directly WHEN user invokes `cypilot list PRs` or any PR listing intent — NEVER use `gh pr list`","path":"skills/cypilot/SKILL.md","commit_id":"ff045550d1b7901cfe9e839b3471ba3d72ee35f9","original_commit_id":"e4e64c42967ff9f20d952d2def8a69f4d21e1e43","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Skipped: comment is from another GitHub bot.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T17:58:3